{"pair": "sigir-20153__NCT01444612", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a cancer diagnosis or a primary inpatient discharge diagnosis of cancer in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a cancer-related surgery; the only surgery mentioned is a right total hip replacement, which is not cancer-related.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of anticoagulant treatment or thromboprophylaxis therapy in relation to a cancer-related surgery.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient receiving any injectable anticoagulant, so cannot confirm this exclusion criterion is met.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient receiving anticoagulant therapy prior to any index anticoagulant.\n  - [not met] The patient presents with symptoms suggestive of PE or DVT (shortness of breath, tachypnea, chest pain, right calf pain), but there is no explicit diagnosis of DVT, PE, or major bleed in the note.\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note of a prior outpatient visit with a diagnosis of DVT or PE in the last 6 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being transferred from another facility.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT02133911", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has severe segmental left ventricular dysfunction and mildly impaired systolic function, but there is no explicit mention of a diagnosis of non-ischemic dilated cardiomyopathy. Coronary an\n  - [not met] Ejection fraction (EF) is not explicitly reported. The note states 'overall left ventricular systolic function was mildly impaired,' which typically suggests EF > 35%.\n  - [not met] NYHA functional class is not specified. The patient presented with chest pain and shortness of breath, but this is an acute episode and does not necessarily reflect chronic NYHA class II-IV symptoms.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the duration or optimization of medical management.\n  - [not met] The patient is 82 years old, which is above the inclusion age range (<75 years).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information about hypersensitivity to the medication.\n  - [not met] The patient is 82 years old, which is >75 years and meets the exclusion criterion.\n  - [not met] EF is not explicitly reported, but 'mildly impaired' systolic function suggests EF > 35%.\n  - [not met] The patient has chronic renal insufficiency, but GFR is not reported. Renal-artery stenosis and chronic renal insufficiency suggest possible GFR < 30, but this is not certain.\n  - [met] No information about liver dysfunction or liver test results.\n  - [met] No mention of LQT syndrome.\n  - [met] No mention of drugs affecting CYP3A4 metabolism.\n  - [not met] The patient has dementia, which is an exclusion criterion.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT01076738", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of an uncomplicated myocardial infarction (2 years ago) and a transient ischemic attack (6 months ago), both of which are documented acute coronary syndromes or ischemic stro\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no explicit mention of previously known symptomatic or asymptomatic PAD confirmed by diagnostic methods or interventions in the note. The patient has symptoms suggestive of PAD (calf pain on \n  - [met] No mention of non-invasive or invasive vascular diagnostic tools (ABI, Toe-brachial index, Duplex ultrasound, etc.) being used or documented in the patient's medical record.\n  - [met] No evidence of previous related intervention (angioplasty, stenting, atherectomy, bypass graft, amputation, etc.) in the clinical note.\n  - [met] No information suggesting that ABI cannot be measured accurately; no mention of conditions like severe arterial calcification or other factors that would prevent ABI measurement.\n  - [met] No mention of the patient being enrolled in a clinical trial or product registry.\n  - [met] No indication that the patient is currently hospitalized; the note describes outpatient symptoms and examination.\n  - [met] This is a general statement and not a specific exclusion criterion; it does not apply to the assessment.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT01911702", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has an acute abdomen (tenderness, guarding, rebound, no bowel sounds) after trauma and is likely to require emergency abdominal surgery. However, there is no explicit mention of surgery or\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic renal failure or dialysis treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of acute coronary syndrome, NYHA class, or significant cardiac history.\n  - [met] The patient is fully awake, alert, and there is no mention of being judged not subject to resuscitative measures.\n  - [met] There is no mention of massive hemorrhage or need for >5 units of blood products.\n  - [met] There is no mention of orthotopic liver transplantation.\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT01384370", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the clinical note that the patient attended a colposcopy visit. The note only states she came to discuss lab results from a pap smear.\n  - [not met] The note does not specify whether the referral Pap sample had a valid APTIMA HPV Assay result. It only mentions 'cytology negative, HPV positive' without specifying the assay used.\n  - [not met] The note states the Pap was 'HPV positive', but does not specify if this was from an APTIMA HPV Assay. Therefore, it is unclear if this criterion is met.\n  - [not met] There is no information about an APTIMA HPV Assay negative result or any histology results such as CIN2 or more severe.\n  - [not met] There is no information about an APTIMA HPV Assay negative result, histology results, or random selection for inclusion.\n  - [not met] The note states the Pap was 'HPV positive', but does not specify if this was from an APTIMA HPV Assay. Therefore, it is unclear if this criterion is met.\n  - [not met] There is no information about an APTIMA HPV Assay negative result or any histology results such as CIN2+.\n  - [not met] There is no information about an APTIMA HPV Assay negative result, histology results, or random selection for inclusion.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 0}
{"pair": "sigir-201527__NCT01700426", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 15 years old, which is much older than the 9-24 months age range required.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's birth weight.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's gestational age at birth.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information about infant formula consumption in the past 3 months. However, the patient is 15 years old, so it is extremely unlikely.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any of the listed diseases or conditions. The anemia appears related to iron deficiency (low Hb, low MCV, low serum iron, low ferritin).\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous diagnosis of iron deficiency or iron deficiency anemia; this appears to be a new evaluation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous treatment for iron deficiency or iron deficiency anemia.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
