{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT02126683", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms suggestive of hypothyroidism (cold intolerance, fatigue, constipation, hyporeflexia, dry skin, slow movements), which are consistent with Hashimoto's thyroiditis. However, the\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's thyroid function tests (free T4 or TSH), so euthyroid state cannot be confirmed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 56-year-old female, but there is no mention of pregnancy, plans for pregnancy, or lactation.\n  - [met] No information is provided about renal or liver function.\n  - [met] No mention of hematologic diseases such as anemia, agranulocytosis, or thrombocytopenia.\n  - [met] No mention of G6PD deficiency or porphyria cutanea tarda.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to 4-aminoquinoline compounds.\n  - [met] No mention of retinopathy or visual field defects.\n  - [met] No mention of current immunosuppression therapy.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201413__NCT02355548", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of pulmonary embolism by CTA or high probability VQ scan in the clinical note. The patient presents with shortness of breath, tachypnea, and tachycardia, but no imag\n  - [met] PESI score is not explicitly calculated, but the patient is 30 years old, has no history of cancer, heart failure, or chronic lung disease, is not hypotensive, and has oxygen saturation of 92%. Based \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of massive PE or hypotension with right heart strain. BP is 110/70, and no mention of right heart strain on imaging.\n  - [met] Systolic BP is 110 mmHg, and no mention of sustained SBP <95 mmHg during ED or observation stay.\n  - [met] Patient is 30 years old.\n  - [met] Patient gave birth 3 weeks ago, so she is not currently pregnant.\n  - [met] No mention of renal insufficiency or abnormal creatinine clearance.\n  - [met] No mention of hepatic dysfunction; CBC and chest x-ray are normal, but liver function tests are not reported.\n  - [met] No mention of unreliable social situation or inability to follow up.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to enoxaparin, warfarin, or rivaroxaban.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT01018238", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has clinical features (malar rash, arthralgias, alopecia, anemia, thrombocytopenia, positive ANA and anti-dsDNA, proteinuria, RBC casts) consistent with a diagnosis of systemic lupus eryth\n  - [not met] There is no information about the duration of the disease; the note only describes current presentation.\n  - [not met] The patient has active SLE with multiple organ involvement (skin, joints, kidneys), but the severity is not clearly described as mild to moderate. The presence of proteinuria and RBC casts suggests po\n  - [not met] There is no information about current or prior maintenance therapy.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has proteinuria and RBC casts, which are indicative of significant lupus nephritis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active CNS disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of arterial or venous thrombosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of body weight, but nothing suggests the patient weighs 120 kg or more.\n  - [met] There is no mention of alcohol or substance abuse.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of cancer.\n  - [met] There is no mention of infections.\n  - [met] There is no mention of viral infections such as HIV, Hepatitis B or C, EBV, CMV, VZV, or HSV.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201512__NCT02467309", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has sudden onset of fever and nuchal rigidity (neck stiffness), which are clinical manifestations consistent with probable bacterial meningitis. However, there is no mention of cerebrospin\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about cerebrospinal fluid appearance, leukocyte count, protein, or glucose levels.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of laboratory confirmation (culture, Gram stain, or antigen detection) of a bacterial pathogen in CSF or blood.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence or mention of congenital immunodeficiency in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no evidence or mention of HIV in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no evidence or mention of long-term corticosteroid treatment in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no evidence or mention of disorders in adrenal gland, pituitary gland, or hypothalamus in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no evidence or mention of tuberculosis in the clinical note.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201529__NCT02359643", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a child with persistent fever, strawberry tongue, red/cracked lips, bilateral non-purulent conjunctivitis, erythematous rash, and swollen red hands, which fulfill the American Heart Ass\n  - [met] The patient has fever >5 days and at least 4 of the 5 principal symptoms: (1) bilateral non-purulent conjunctivitis, (2) oral mucosal changes (strawberry tongue, cracked lips), (3) peripheral extremit\n  - [met] Diffuse mucosal inflammation is present as evidenced by strawberry tongue and red, cracked lips.\n  - [met] The patient has bilateral red eyes with no discharge, consistent with bilateral non-purulent conjunctivitis.\n  - [met] The patient has an erythematous rash on the trunk, which qualifies as a dysmorphous skin rash.\n  - [met] The patient has swollen red hands, which is consistent with indurative angioedema over the hands and feet.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of cervical lymphadenopathy or IVIG treatment in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient fulfills the Kawasaki Disease criteria.\n  - [met] The patient has had fever for more than 5 days but less than 10 days.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the completeness of follow-up data.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about IVIG treatment at another hospital.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about corticosteroid treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of another disease known to mimic Kawasaki disease.\n  - [met] No mention of previous diagnosis of Kawasaki disease.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to take aspirin.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201518__NCT01671995", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 65-year-old male, which is above the threshold of 60 years.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms consistent with heart failure (shortness of breath on exertion, orthopnea, bibasilar crackles, pitting edema, jugular venous distension). These findings are consistent with NY\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about left ventricular ejection fraction or echocardiography results.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of acute myocardial infarction or unstable angina pectoris within the last three months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of valvular stenosis in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of dementia or cognitive impairment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe concomitant disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of refusal to participate.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT02281123", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 31 years old, which is less than 45 years.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the location of consultation or whether it was at the University Hospital of Fort-de-France.\n  - [met] The patient has fever and sudden onset of joint pain affecting the ankle and knees, which is suggestive of suspected chikungunya infection.\n  - [not met] The duration of symptoms is 2 weeks (14 days), which is more than 10 days.\n  - [met] The patient currently has pain, swelling, and stiffness in multiple joints, indicating presence of joint pain on the day of inclusion.\n  - [met] The patient has no previous medical problems, suggesting no history of inflammatory arthritis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of steroidal or non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug use in the past two weeks.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to participate for 12 months.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, so age at onset of symptoms is <45 years.\n  - [met] Duration of symptoms is 2 weeks (14 days), which is more than 10 days.\n  - [not met] The patient has joint pain on the day of inclusion.\n  - [met] The patient has no history of inflammatory arthritis and no mention of NSAID use.\n  - [met] No mention of taking NSAIDs or steroids in the two weeks preceding inclusion.\n  - [not met] No information about inability to participate for 12 months.\n  - [not met] No information about social health care affiliation.\n  - [not met] No information about refusal to participate or sign consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT01410526", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 48 years old, which is greater than 18.\n  - [met] The patient has severe abdominal sepsis (ruptured liver abscess, fever, hypotension, tachycardia, ICU admission), fitting the study group. The criterion is about group assignment, not an individual re\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Manheim Peritonitis Score is not provided. Cannot determine if it is <29.\n  - [not met] Pre-operative SOFA score is not provided. Cannot determine if it is <6.\n  - [met] No mention of other temporary abdominal closure systems being used.\n  - [met] The patient survived surgery and was taken to the ICU, so did not die before the first VAC dressing change.\n  - [met] No mention of participation in another clinical trial.\n  - [not met] The patient has common variable immunodeficiency (CVID), which is an immune deficiency.\n  - [met] No mention of HIV/AIDS.\n  - [met] No mention of steroid treatment.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-201519__NCT01636401", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms and signs highly suggestive of moderate to severe COPD (chronic cough, progressive dyspnea, barrel chest, wheezing, significant smoking history). However, there is no spiromet\n  - [met] The patient has smoked 1 to 2 packs per day for 47 years, which is at least 47 pack-years, well above the 10 pack-year threshold.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history or current diagnosis of asthma in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hospitalization for an acute COPD exacerbation within the past 3 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a respiratory tract infection or COPD exacerbation in the 6 weeks prior to the visit.\n  - [met] No other clinically significant respiratory conditions besides COPD are mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201422__NCT02137603", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl, which falls within the pediatric age range of 5-18.\n  - [not met] The patient has a diagnosis of appendicitis based on clinical presentation and ultrasound findings. However, there is no information about being scheduled for appendectomy or the timing (0600-1800).\n  - [not met] There is no mention of intraoperative findings or confirmation of suppurative appendicitis; only imaging findings are described.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient denies sexual activity and has regular menses, making pregnancy highly unlikely.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a complex medical history; the patient appears otherwise healthy.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT02451631", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 64 years old, which is within the 20-80 years age range.\n  - [not met] Patient has type 2 diabetes. However, she is not compliant with her diabetes medication or exercise, and there is no evidence she has been stably taking oral diabetic drugs or insulin and doing lifest\n  - [not met] No information provided about insulin treatment or regimen. Cannot assess.\n  - [not met] Patient has persistently elevated HbA1c, but the exact value is not provided. Cannot confirm if it is between 7.0% and 10.0%.\n  - [not met] No information about patient's ability to understand and use smartphone application.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has type 2 diabetes and no mention of insulin pump use.\n  - [met] No mention of severe complications such as stage IV/V chronic kidney failure, diabetic foot complications, unstable angina, MI, stroke, or recent surgical procedures. The patient has a painful skin le\n  - [met] No mention of uncontrolled hypertension.\n  - [met] Patient is a 64-year-old female; no mention of pregnancy or contraception status.\n  - [met] No information about ability to use application during treatment.\n  - [met] No mention of medications that can affect glucose level other than diabetes medication.\n  - [met] No mention of alcohol abuse or dependency.\n  - [met] No mention of liver enzyme levels.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201415__NCT02152696", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is female and presents with 12 weeks of amenorrhea and a negative pregnancy test. There is no clear evidence of a persisting pregnancy of unknown location, as the pregnancy test is negativ\n  - [not met] Pregnancy of unknown location requires a positive pregnancy test, but the patient's test is negative. No definitive signs of intrauterine or ectopic pregnancy are seen on ultrasound.\n  - [not met] No serial hCG values are provided; only a single negative test is mentioned. Cannot assess persistence of hCG.\n  - [met] The patient is hemodynamically stable (no mention of instability) and blood counts are normal, suggesting hemoglobin >10 mg/dL.\n  - [met] The patient is 36 years old, which is greater than 18.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of hemodynamic instability or need for acute treatment is described.\n  - [met] The most recent hCG is negative (below 25 mIU/mL), well below 5000 mIU/mL.\n  - [met] No mention of recent delivery or abortion; the patient presents with amenorrhea and symptoms, not post-pregnancy care.\n  - [not met] Gestational trophoblastic disease (vesicular mole) is in the differential diagnosis, but not confirmed. Uncertain if this is the diagnosis.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about willingness or ability to comply with study procedures.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about hypersensitivity to MTX.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about contraindications to MTX.\n  - [met] No mention of prior medical or surgical management of this gestation.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201526__NCT01601964", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is admitted for a non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy, which means she is a confirmed case (and thus also suspected at some point).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of hemodynamic instability (e.g., hypotension, tachycardia, shock). The patient is being considered for laparoscopic treatment, which suggests stability.\n  - [met] The patient has an ectopic pregnancy and a low beta HCG (100 mIU) at 8 weeks LMP, which is not consistent with a healthy intrauterine pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of missed abortion; the diagnosis is ectopic pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of incomplete abortion; the diagnosis is ectopic pregnancy.\n  - [met] The patient is being considered for laparoscopic treatment, but there is no indication that immediate surgery is required (e.g., no rupture, no instability). The attending is concerned about obesity a", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20141__NCT02001545", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note regarding provision of informed consent.\n  - [not met] The patient presents with chest pain and EKG shows nonspecific changes, but there is no explicit diagnosis of STEMI or NSTEMI.\n  - [not met] The patient presented to the ER within 2 days of symptom onset, but it is not clear if she was hospitalized within 24 hours of onset. The latest episode ended half an hour prior to arrival, suggesting\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence that the chest pain or possible MI was precipitated by surgery, trauma, GI bleeding, or post-PCI.\n  - [met] The patient presented to the ER with new symptoms, not while already hospitalized for another reason.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any condition or circumstance that would limit follow-up (e.g., language barrier, psychiatric disturbance).", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT02458495", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 64-year-old female, which confirms she is an adult over 18 years old.\n  - [met] The note states the patient has a diagnosis of diabetes mellitus. While it does not specify type 2, the context (adult, obesity, oral/injectable medication) strongly suggests type 2 diabetes.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about enrollment in the Vanderbilt APPC or Eskind Diabetes Clinic.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about registration as a My Health at Vanderbilt user.\n  - [met] The note mentions 'persistently elevated HbA1c', which suggests an A1c of 7.0 or greater, but does not provide a specific value.\n  - [met] The patient is described as 'not compliant with her diabetes medication', which implies she is prescribed diabetes medication and is currently being treated, even if not taking it as directed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note is written in English and there is no mention of language barriers.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hearing or visual impairment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of delirium or severe cognitive impairment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a caregiver administering diabetes medications.\n  - [not met] There is no information about access to a mobile phone or computer with internet.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness or ability to provide written informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT00305201", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is currently presenting with symptoms and findings consistent with acute Kawasaki disease (fever, conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue, extremity changes, lymphadenopathy, coronary artery inv\n  - [not met] The patient is described as a 2-year-old boy, which is younger than 8 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of diabetes mellitus in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypertension or uncontrolled blood pressure in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of treatment with drugs that modify endothelial function (ACE inhibitors, ARBs, calcium channel blockers).\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy, so it is extremely unlikely he is a smoker, and there is no mention of smoking.\n  - [met] There is no mention of total cholesterol levels in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of triglyceride levels in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic statin treatment in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic renal insufficiency or creatinine levels in the clinical note.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201410__NCT00533156", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient underwent cardiac catheterization, which is a coronary diagnostic or interventional procedure.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient cannot undergo emergent vascular surgery if needed.\n  - [not met] The note states the procedure was via the right femoral artery, but does not specify the size (7F) or exact location (common femoral artery).\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the femoral artery lumen diameter.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The procedure was performed via the right femoral artery only.\n  - [met] No mention of prior closure or manual compression within 30 days.\n  - [met] No history of bleeding or platelet disorders is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of acute ST-elevation myocardial infarction within 48 hours prior.\n  - [met] No information about hypertension status at time of vessel closure.\n  - [met] No information about activated clotting time.\n  - [met] No information suggesting ineligibility for in-catheterization lab introducer sheath removal.\n  - [met] No mention of concurrent participation in another trial.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 26}
