{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT02111057", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, which is greater than 18.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient undergoing total joint replacement surgery.\n  - [not met] The patient has 2 weeks of joint pain, swelling, and stiffness in multiple joints, but there is no explicit diagnosis of RA or confirmation that ACR/EULAR or 1987 criteria are met. Duration is less th\n  - [not met] There is no mention of OA, SLE, or other inflammatory arthritis diagnosis. The patient is not described as a control subject.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no diagnosis of any other systemic rheumatic disease mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of crystalline arthropathy (e.g., gout, pseudogout).\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's language abilities, but there is no evidence to suggest inability to understand or read English.\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's ability to follow the study protocol, but there is no evidence to suggest inability.\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, which is between 18 and 75.\n  - [not met] This is an explanation, not a criterion.\n  - [not met] This is a heading, not a criterion.\n  - [not met] There is mention of joint stiffness, but not specifically morning stiffness lasting at least 1 hour.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 26}
{"pair": "sigir-201412__NCT00535561", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms suggestive of hypothyroidism (fatigue, weight gain, cold intolerance, hair loss, change in voice, anterior cervical mass possibly indicating goiter), but there is no mention o\n  - [met] There is no mention of swallowing difficulties. The patient complains of fatigue and other symptoms, but nothing suggests inability to swallow tablets.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of multifactorial anemia or anemia due to other reasons. In fact, anemia is not mentioned at all.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of iron deficiency anemia requiring urgent intervention, nor any mention of cardiac ischemia, severe anemia, GI/GU losses, or acute/subacute blood loss.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior thyroid disorder or treatment history. The symptoms appear to be new and presenting for the first time.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any other co-morbid disease such as renal insufficiency, coronary heart disease, hypertension, diabetes, or other endocrine diseases.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT02114099", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a clinical diagnosis consistent with Kawasaki Disease (fever, conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue, extremity changes, lymphadenopathy, desquamation) and echocardiogram shows moderate dil\n  - [not met] The patient is 2 years old, which is younger than 10 years old.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient ever receiving coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) surgery.\n  - [not met] The patient has elevated alanine aminotransferase and enlarged liver, which may indicate active hepatitis or persistent abnormal liver function.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a past history of rhabdomyolysis.\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy, so is not female and cannot be pregnant or planning child-bearing.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
