{"pair": "sigir-201411__NCT01682096", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of arrhythmia or irregular heart rhythm. Tachycardia is present, but sinus rhythm is likely unless otherwise specified.\n  - [not met] The patient presents with excruciating pain in her right arm, not chest pain. No chest pain is reported.\n  - [not met] No information is provided regarding pre-test probability of coronary artery disease. The patient has no past medical history and is 40 years old, which may suggest low probability, but this is not ex\n  - [not met] No ECG findings are described in the note, so absence of ischemic changes cannot be confirmed.\n  - [not met] No troponin results are provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to iodinated contrast.\n  - [met] No mention of renal insufficiency or creatinine levels.\n  - [met] No history of coronary artery disease or prior myocardial revascularization; patient has no past medical history.\n  - [not met] Patient is hemodynamically unstable (BP 80/60 mm Hg, which is <100 mm Hg systolic).\n  - [met] No mention of cardiac arrhythmia; only tachycardia is noted.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to perform exercise test.\n  - [met] No mention of incapacity to provide informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT00880347", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No explicit mention of AD diagnosis; patient has progressive memory loss and severe cognitive deficits, but also jerking movements and EEG with periodic sharp waves, which are more suggestive of Creut\n  - [met] Patient is a 62-year-old male, which meets the age and sex requirement.\n  - [not met] No mention of clinical diagnosis of probable AD according to DSM-IV TR or NINCDS-ADRDA criteria; findings are more consistent with CJD.\n  - [not met] No information about written informed consent.\n  - [not met] Brain imaging (neuroimaging studies) was performed and showed cerebral atrophy, but no explicit statement that results are compatible with AD diagnosis.\n  - [not met] Neurological exam confirms severe cognitive deficits and memory dysfunction, and jerking movements (myoclonus), which are focal signs likely related to other conditions than AD.\n  - [not met] No information about compliance with study procedures.\n  - [met] Patient does not belong to the AD group, so may be considered for non-AD demented group.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] AD group: Not applicable, as patient does not meet AD group criteria.\n  - [met] AD group: Not applicable.\n  - [met] No mention of drug or alcohol abuse or dependence.\n  - [met] Patient has severe cognitive deficits and memory dysfunction, not mild cognitive impairment.", "n_inc_assessed": 26, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201415__NCT00237965", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 36-year-old woman, which means she is above age 18. No ethnicity restriction is mentioned in the note, but none is required for this criterion.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any significant skin disease in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no information about the patient's language proficiency, but the note is in English and there is no indication that the patient is a non-English speaker.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any severe co-morbidity that would prevent the patient from performing a SSE (self skin examination).\n  - [met] There is no mention of cognitive impairment or inability to give informed consent or understand instructions.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
