{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT02232022", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient had a recent cryptogenic stroke (hospitalized two weeks ago). However, CT was negative for brain hemorrhage, but no explicit mention of brain infarction on imaging. Since thrombolytic therapy \n  - [met] No history or finding of atrial fibrillation is reported. ECG shows normal sinus rhythm. No mention of atrial fibrillation on inpatient monitoring.\n  - [not met] No presumed stroke etiology is identified; the stroke is described as cryptogenic and extensive workup found no abnormalities. Therefore, this criterion is not met.\n  - [met] CHADS2 score: Age \u226575 (0), Hypertension (1), Diabetes (1), Stroke (2). Patient is 72, so age does not count. Total: 1 (HTN) + 1 (DM) + 2 (stroke) = 4. Therefore, CHADS2 \u22653.\n  - [not met] Patient has hypertension and type 2 diabetes, but none of the listed comorbidities (OSA, CAD, COPD, hyperthyroidism, BMI>30, prior MI, prolonged PR, renal impairment) are mentioned. Therefore, does no\n  - [not met] No information about consent is provided in the note.\n  - [met] Patient is 72 years old.\n  - [not met] Patient had stroke two weeks ago; device must be implanted within 7 days of event. Therefore, this criterion is not met.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No documented history of AF or atrial flutter.\n  - [met] No evidence of high-risk cardiac source of embolism; TEE and MRA found no abnormalities.\n  - [met] No mention of untreated hyperthyroidism.\n  - [met] No mention of recent MI or CABG.\n  - [met] No mention of valvular disease requiring immediate surgery.\n  - [met] No mention of permanent indication for anticoagulation.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to oral anticoagulation.\n  - [met] No mention of participation in another clinical trial.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
