{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT01017081", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old (within 1-12 years), presents with acute symptoms (fever, cough, dyspnea for 2 days), and chest x-ray shows bilateral lung infiltrates, consistent with acute community-acqui\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note states the patient presents to the ER and is in respiratory distress, but there is no mention of ICU admission or hospitalization in intensive care units.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pleural effusion or chest drainage in the clinical note.\n  - [met] A chest x-ray shows bilateral lung infiltrates, but there is no mention of atelectasis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior pneumonia or pleural effusion in the previous six months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of other pulmonary underlying disease, heart disease, cerebral palsy, or immune deficiency.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201415__NCT01826045", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 36-year-old woman, which is between 20 and 49 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of cervical intraepithelial neoplasia 1 (CIN1) in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of HPV status in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The note states that the complete blood count and biochemical profile are normal, which strongly suggests WBC, hemoglobin, platelet, and ANC are within normal limits.\n  - [not met] There is no information about AST or ALT levels in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about EKG or chest X-ray in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of malignant tumor in any organ other than possible vesicular mole or fibroid degeneration, which are not confirmed malignancies.\n  - [met] No evidence of active liver disease, immune disorder, or severe renal failure is mentioned; blood and biochemical profiles are normal.\n  - [met] No mention of leukemia, collagenosis, sclerosis, autoimmune disease, or significant allergic disease.\n  - [met] No mention of diagnosed diabetes.\n  - [met] No mention of taking medications or supplements affecting immunological reaction.\n  - [met] The patient presents with 12 weeks of amenorrhea and an enlarged uterus, but the pregnancy test is negative. The differential includes vesicular mole (which can present with high hCG but here is negat\n  - [met] No mention of registration in other clinical trials.\n  - [met] No information to suggest the investigator considers the patient inappropriate.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201523__NCT00473135", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with acute illness (high fever, chills, epistaxis, severe headache, joint pain, leukopenia, increased hematocrit, thrombocytopenia), which does not indicate good general health.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's availability for the duration of the study.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about willingness to use contraception.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of chronic neurologic, heart, lung, liver, rheumatologic, autoimmune, or kidney disease. The current illness appears acute.\n  - [met] No mention of behavioral, cognitive, or psychiatric disease.\n  - [not met] The patient has significant laboratory abnormalities (leukopenia, thrombocytopenia, increased hematocrit).\n  - [met] No mention of alcohol or illegal drug use problems.\n  - [met] No history of severe allergic reaction or anaphylaxis is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of severe asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of HIV-1 infection.\n  - [met] No mention of Hepatitis C infection.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 21}
