{"pair": "sigir-201415__NCT00486863", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information provided about screening by a study midwife.\n  - [met] Patient is a 36-year-old woman.\n  - [not met] Patient presents to the emergency department, not specifically to a study midwife with suspected pregnancy.\n  - [not met] No information about residence in a study village.\n  - [not met] No specific information about main study inclusion.\n  - [not met] No information about S. japonicum infection.\n  - [not met] Urine pregnancy test is negative, so pregnancy is not confirmed by test.\n  - [met] Patient is 36 years old.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient has significant acute illness (abdominal pain, vaginal bleeding, abnormal uterus, possible vesicular mole or fibroid degeneration).\n  - [met] No history of seizures, neurologic disorder, or chronic medical problem mentioned.\n  - [met] Laboratory results are normal.\n  - [not met] Ultrasound shows enlarged uterus with multiple cystic areas; differential includes fibroid degeneration, but no explicit mention of myoma >5 cm or submucosal myoma.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital anomalies of the reproductive tract.\n  - [not met] Patient has acute symptoms (pain, bleeding, nausea, vomiting) that may significantly alter daily activities.\n  - [met] No mention of cysts in the eye or neurocysticercosis.\n  - [met] No mention of regular medication use for chronic condition.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
