{"pair": "sigir-20149__NCT02160626", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 43 years old, which is over 18.\n  - [not met] Lesions are described as small, soft, pedunculated, and on the neck. No explicit diagnosis of seborrheic keratosis is given, and the description is more typical of skin tags (acrochordons) than seborr\n  - [not met] Patient has multiple lesions, but it is not specified that there are 4 appropriate seborrheic keratosis lesions on the trunk/extremities. Lesions are on the neck.\n  - [not met] Lesions are described as clinically typical for their type, but not specified as seborrheic keratosis.\n  - [met] No mention of prior treatment; likely treatment na\u00efve.\n  - [not met] No Physician Lesion Assessment (PLA) score is provided.\n  - [not met] Largest lesion is 4 mm in diameter, which is less than the required \u22657mm.\n  - [not met] No information on the perpendicular dimension, but largest lesion is only 4 mm, so cannot be \u22657mm.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of atypical or rapidly growing lesions.\n  - [met] Multiple lesions are present, but no mention of eruptive onset or Sign of Leser-Trelat.\n  - [met] No mention of systemic malignancy.\n  - [met] No mention of keloid or hypertrophic scarring history.\n  - [met] No mention of systemic therapy use.\n  - [met] No mention of retinoid use.\n  - [met] No mention of glucocorticosteroid use.\n  - [met] No mention of anti-metabolite use.", "n_inc_assessed": 19, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT02605122", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has a documented fever with temperature 103.4\u00b0F (39.7\u00b0C), which is above 38\u00b0C.\n  - [met] No chest radiograph is mentioned, but the patient is an outpatient starting on oral therapy, so a radiograph is not required.\n  - [met] Patient has at least 2 symptoms: productive cough, chest pain, fever, chills, and worsening cough.\n  - [not met] No mention of difficulty breathing.\n  - [met] Patient has a productive cough, which suggests production of purulent sputum.\n  - [met] Patient reports chest pain.\n  - [not met] No mention of grunting.\n  - [not met] Blood pressure is 120/80, which is normal. No hypotension.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of ventilator-associated or hospital-acquired pneumonia; patient is outpatient.\n  - [met] No mention of prior antibacterial therapy.\n  - [met] No evidence or suspicion of bacterial meningitis.\n  - [met] Patient is male.\n  - [met] Patient is male.", "n_inc_assessed": 22, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT02564237", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 31-year-old woman, which is within the 18-50 age range.\n  - [not met] Patient has no previous medical problems, but currently presents with joint pain, fatigue, fevers, and chest pain, which may indicate an acute illness. General health is not clearly 'good' at this tim\n  - [not met] No information is provided about use of birth control.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient reports intermittent fevers (38.2 to 39.4\u00b0C) and symptoms suggestive of acute illness.\n  - [met] Patient has no previous medical problems and no chronic illness is mentioned.\n  - [met] No evidence or mention of immunodeficiency.\n  - [met] No history of cardiac pathology is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of congenital malformation syndromes is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of autoimmune or systemic diseases is mentioned.\n  - [not met] Patient has undiagnosed acute self-limiting polyarthritis (joint pain, swelling, and stiffness in multiple joints over 2 weeks). This matches the exclusion criterion.\n  - [met] No previous echocardiogram or findings are mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 22}
{"pair": "sigir-20159__NCT02612896", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note does not mention willingness or ability to participate in all aspects of the study, such as providing samples, participating in surveys, or taking oral anthelmintic tablets.\n  - [not met] The note does not mention willingness or ability to provide informed consent or assent for minors with parental consent.\n  - [not met] The note does not specify whether the patient lives in, attends school in, or regularly visits the bore holes present in the study communities.\n  - [met] The patient is 10 years old, which is older than five years.\n  - [met] There is no mention of epilepsy in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note does not mention unwillingness or inability to participate in study activities.\n  - [met] The note does not mention unwillingness or inability to provide informed consent or assent.\n  - [met] The note does not specify that the patient lives outside of, or does not regularly visit or attend school in, the study communities.\n  - [met] The patient is 10 years old, not four years or younger.\n  - [met] There is no mention of epilepsy in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] The patient is acutely ill (cyanosis, neck stiffness, periorbital edema, high WBC, tachycardia, hypotension, tachypnea), and likely unable to engage in normal activities of daily living without assist", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
