{"pair": "sigir-20143__NCT00894569", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note mentions a lung mass and a solitary brain mass, but does not specify histologic or cytologic confirmation, nor does it state that the carcinoma is of unknown primary or non-resectable.\n  - [met] The patient has measurable lesions (lung mass and brain mass) as seen on imaging, which likely meet RECIST criteria.\n  - [met] The patient is described as having only mild exertional dyspnea and occasional cough, otherwise asymptomatic, suggesting a WHO performance status of 0 or 1.\n  - [not met] This is a study-specific criterion and cannot be determined from the clinical note.\n  - [not met] No information about informed consent is provided.\n  - [met] The patient is 58 years old.\n  - [not met] No information about contraception or risk of conception is provided.\n  - [not met] No laboratory data is provided to assess bone marrow function.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information about prior exposure to EGFR-targeting therapy.\n  - [met] No information about prior chemotherapy.\n  - [met] No information about recent radiotherapy or major surgery.\n  - [met] No information about concurrent systemic therapies.\n  - [met] No information about investigational agents or recent clinical trial participation.\n  - [met] No information about coronary disease or recent MI.\n  - [met] The patient has a solitary brain mass and a lung mass, which are unlikely to be curable by local treatment, but this is not explicitly stated.\n  - [met] No mention of axillary node metastasis.", "n_inc_assessed": 15, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201514__NCT02158195", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has evidence of hemolytic anemia (anemia, elevated LDH, elevated reticulocyte count, hemosiderinuria, polychromasia, anisocytosis, poikilocytosis), but the DAT (direct antiglobulin test) i\n  - [not met] There is no mention of secondary causes of AIHA such as infections, hematological diseases, or systemic diseases. The patient is pregnant, which can be associated with secondary AIHA, but this is not \n  - [met] The patient is already receiving iron supplementation for iron deficiency, but there is no mention of prior treatment for hemolytic anemia. It is likely she is naive to hemolytic anemia treatment.\n  - [met] The patient is 27 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no information about language comprehension.\n  - [not met] There is no information about written informed consent.\n  - [met] The patient does not have a known autoimmune disease, cancer, or active infection.\n  - [met] Duplicate of inclusion_criteria_3; patient is 27 years old.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence of cold agglutinin disease (no agglutination, negative DAT).\n  - [not met] The patient is pregnant (11 weeks gestation).\n  - [not met] There is no information about national health insurance status.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT00300872", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, which is below the required age range of 20 to 80 years.\n  - [not met] The clinical note describes symptoms suggestive of OSA (nighttime snoring, pauses in breathing, excessive sleepiness), but there is no mention of an Apnea Hypopnea Index (AHI) or results from a Polyso\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the Epworth Sleepiness Scale (ESS) score.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of hypertension or anti-hypertensive medications in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence that the patient has problems staying awake during driving or shift work. The patient is a child and likely does not drive or do shift work.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a recent myocardial infarction.\n  - [met] There is no mention of unstable angina.\n  - [met] There is no mention of underlying malignancy.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT00273962", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient does not have a known history of asthma; the note specifically states he has a history of allergic rhinitis but no history of wheezing. This is his first episode of wheezing.\n  - [met] The patient is a 4 year old boy, which is within the 2 to 10 years age range.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about informed consent being signed by parents or legal guardians.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypersensitivity to study drugs.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any medical condition that would contraindicate the use of beta2-adrenergic or anticholinergic medications.\n  - [not met] This is the patient's first wheezing episode, as stated in the note.\n  - [met] There is no history of prior intubation for asthma.\n  - [met] There is no mention of ipratropium use within six hours prior to consultation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of concurrent stridor or possible intra-thoracic foreign body. Wheezing is localized to the mid-right chest, but no evidence of foreign body or stridor is described.\n  - [met] There is no mention of diseases known to have chronic effect on respiratory function (e.g., cystic fibrosis or cardiac disease).\n  - [met] The patient is playful, well-appearing, and has O2 sats of 100% on room air, so does not require immediate resuscitation or airway intervention.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-20143__NCT00124761", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a solitary mass in the right frontal lobe on CT scan, but there is no mention of a contrast MRI scan within two weeks before treatment.\n  - [not met] The patient has a left lung mass, but there is no histological or cytological diagnosis of systemic cancer provided.\n  - [met] The patient is 58 years old, which is >= 18.\n  - [not met] There is no information about suitability for both S and RS by neurosurgeon and radiation oncologist.\n  - [not met] No information about agreement to adjuvant WBRT.\n  - [not met] No Karnofsky Performance Status (KPS) or RTOG RPA class is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about KPS or whether poor performance status is due to the metastasis.\n  - [not met] No information about accessibility for treatment and follow-up.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No previous history of brain metastases is mentioned.\n  - [met] No indication that surgery is required to relieve life-threatening raised intracranial pressure or for tissue diagnosis. Neurologic exam is unremarkable.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to surgery by site or comorbidities.\n  - [met] No mention of leptomeningeal disease.\n  - [met] Primary cancer is presumed to be lung, but not specified as small cell. No evidence of germ cell tumor, lymphoma, leukemia, or myeloma.\n  - [met] No mention of prior cranial radiotherapy.\n  - [met] Patient is a 58-year-old female, but no mention of pregnancy. Given age and context, unlikely to be pregnant.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT00386022", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 31 years old, which is outside the required age ranges of 45-55 or 70-80 years old.\n  - [not met] The patient has had amenorrhea for 7 months, which is less than the 12 months required to define natural menopause. There is no mention of surgical menopause or FSH level.\n  - [met] The patient is currently taking no medications, which includes hormonal medications, herbal supplements, or over-the-counter menopause therapy.\n  - [not met] TSH is normal, prolactin is elevated, and there is no information about factor V Leiden, CBC, BUN, or creatinine.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's BMI.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of smoking status.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of contraindications to estrogen or mammogram results.\n  - [met] There is no history of coronary artery disease mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient is not on any medications, so is not on medications that act on the GnRH pulse generator.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypersensitivity or allergy to the listed drugs.\n  - [met] There is no prior history of breast cancer or blood clots mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT01458405", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presented with typical ischemic symptoms (chest pain radiating to left shoulder and jaw), ST-segment elevations on EKG, and elevated troponin and CK-MB. Imaging (ventriculography and echoc\n  - [not met] No history of percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) or stent placement is mentioned.\n  - [not met] Left ventricular systolic function is described as 'mildly impaired,' but no quantitative LVEF value is provided. Severe segmental dysfunction is noted, but without a specific LVEF \u22640.45, this cannot \n  - [not met] No information about post-reperfusion assessment after a recent MI is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about chronic MI or timing post-reperfusion is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about screening or randomization timing relative to MI is provided.\n  - [not met] No MRI data or infarct size is provided. However, there is evidence of segmental wall motion abnormalities (akinesis, hypokinesis), but the percentage of LV mass is not specified.\n  - [met] Coronary angiography showed no stenosis or clinically significant disease, suggesting no further revascularization is indicated.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No history of coronary artery bypass surgery or grafts is mentioned.\n  - [met] No diagnosis or suspicion of myocarditis is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history or evidence of cardiac tumor is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No history of acute coronary syndrome in the 4 weeks prior to study infusion is mentioned, but the current event may be an acute coronary syndrome. However, since the timing of study infusion is not s\n  - [met] No history of previous stem cell therapy is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of radiation treatment to the thorax is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of systemic autoimmune or connective tissue disease is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of immunosuppressive or anti-inflammatory treatment is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 20}
{"pair": "sigir-201526__NCT02152696", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a female with a positive pregnancy test (Beta HCG is 100 mIU) and is admitted for a non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy. However, the diagnosis is not 'pregnancy of unknown location' but rat\n  - [not met] The patient has a diagnosed ectopic pregnancy, not a pregnancy of unknown location. There is no mention of ultrasound findings, but the diagnosis of ectopic pregnancy implies a location has been ident\n  - [not met] There is only one Beta HCG value (100 mIU) provided, and no serial values or trends are described.\n  - [met] The patient is admitted for a non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy and there is no mention of hemodynamic instability or low hemoglobin. It is likely she is stable, but hemoglobin is not explicitly stated.\n  - [met] The patient is 28 years old.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of hemodynamic instability or need for acute treatment. The ectopic pregnancy is non-ruptured.\n  - [met] Most recent hCG is 100 mIU/mL, which is well below 5000 mIU/mL.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recent delivery or abortion; the patient is currently pregnant.\n  - [met] There is no mention of gestational trophoblastic disease.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is unwilling or unable to comply with study procedures.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypersensitivity to MTX.\n  - [met] There is no mention of clinical contraindications to MTX, though the attending is concerned about obesity and adhesions, but these are not absolute contraindications.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior medical or surgical management of this gestation. The patient has had prior laparoscopy for adhesions, but not for this pregnancy.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT01569698", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 6-month-old male infant, which is less than 18 years old, including newborns.\n  - [not met] The patient has acute kidney injury: urine output <0.2 mL/kg/hr, elevated BUN and creatinine, generalized edema, and urinalysis findings (granular casts, RBCs). However, the note does not explicitly s\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of terminal renal failure or treatment by extra renal replacement therapy for terminal renal failure.\n  - [met] There is no history of renal transplantation mentioned in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inborn errors of metabolism or extra renal replacement therapy for such conditions without acute renal failure.\n  - [met] There is no mention of drug intoxication or extra renal replacement therapy in that context without acute renal failure.\n  - [met] There is no mention of treatment by MARS (Molecular Adsorbent Recirculating System).\n  - [met] There is no mention of modified ultrafiltration during surgery.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20149__NCT02432118", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient having had a stereotactic or ultrasound-guided biopsy with marker placement.\n  - [not met] There is no information about a lesion or biopsy marker being visible under ultrasound.\n  - [not met] There is no information about a surgical target or its distance from the skin.\n  - [not met] The patient has multiple discreet lesions, but it is not clear if there is a single discreet surgical target.\n  - [not met] The lesions are described, but it is not specified if the center/focal area is defined.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability or willingness to sign informed consent.\n  - [met] ECOG/Karnofsky status is not used as an inclusion criterion, so this is not applicable.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability or willingness to sign informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the need for more than one localization needle.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous open surgical biopsy, lumpectomy, or mastectomy in the operative breast.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a prosthesis/implant in the operative breast.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a cardiac pacemaker or defibrillator device.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is contraindicated for surgery.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT01631916", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is an 8-year-old presenting to the ER with fever, dyspnea, cough, and bilateral lung infiltrates on chest x-ray, consistent with community-acquired pneumonia. The note implies hospitalizat\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old, which is within the 2-18 years old range.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any pulmonary chronic disease, including asthma, in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of immunodeficiency or related conditions in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of diseases requiring corticosteroid therapy, such as rheumatic diseases.\n  - [met] The note does not mention wheezing; it describes bronchial respiratory sounds, which are not the same as wheezing.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous hospitalization within 14 days prior to admission.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pleural effusion on admission; chest x-ray shows bilateral lung infiltrates, but no effusion is described.\n  - [met] There is no mention of malnutrition in the clinical note.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT01050881", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about the patient's blood donor status or whether they are a deferred blood donor.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of deferral due to positive routine blood tests for HIV, hepatitis B, hepatitis C, HTLV, or being at risk of vCJD.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the timing of any blood donor deferral.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about registration at NHSBT centres or the English Blood Service.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note that the patient is a blood donor; this criterion may be met by default.\n  - [met] No record of notification is mentioned in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] No information about Armed Forces membership or other professions is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about the timing of deferral is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about deferral due to non-routine tests or syphilis infection only.\n  - [not met] No information about registration with or notification by Welsh, Scottish, or Northern Irish Blood Services.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201512__NCT00162578", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 44-year-old adult (age > 18). He presents with symptoms highly suggestive of meningitis (severe headache, fever, nuchal rigidity) following a skull fracture and clear fluid dripping f\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention in the clinical note of any allergy to antibiotics used in the study.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT02212496", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient was hospitalized for cryptogenic stroke two weeks ago. The note does not specify if she presented within 7 days from symptom onset, only that hospitalization was two weeks ago. Timing of p\n  - [not met] There is no information about embolic infarction outside the perforator territory or diffusion-weighted imaging results in the note.\n  - [met] The patient had a cryptogenic stroke, meaning the cause was undetermined after initial evaluation including electrocardiogram and brain imaging. This matches the criterion.\n  - [not met] The patient had brain MRI, MR angiography, 12-lead ECG, and transesophageal echocardiogram. There is no mention of agitated saline injection, 24-hour Holter, or telemonitoring, so not all required tes\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of single subcortical infarction; the stroke is described as cryptogenic and no abnormalities were found on imaging.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a primary brain tumor in the note.\n  - [met] The patient was able to perform comprehensive studies including MRI, MRA, ECG, and echocardiogram.\n  - [met] There is no mention of refusal or withdrawal of consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT02593643", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent.\n  - [not met] Patient has symptoms consistent with depression (fatigue, increased sleep/appetite, anhedonia, guilt, difficulty concentrating), but no explicit diagnosis of MDD or confirmation by DSM-IV/MINI.\n  - [not met] No evidence or mention of bipolar disorder.\n  - [met] Patient is a 20-year-old female, within the 18-65 age range.\n  - [not met] No mention of inpatient status; likely outpatient.\n  - [not met] No information about pregnancy status, contraception, or hCG test.\n  - [met] Patient is a college student, able to report symptoms and history, suggesting ability to understand and comply, but no explicit statement.\n  - [not met] No mention of suicidal ideation or attempts.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of current or past psychotic symptoms.\n  - [met] No mention of substance or alcohol dependence.\n  - [met] No mention of recent drug abuse.\n  - [met] No evidence of pervasive developmental disorder.\n  - [met] No evidence of dementia.\n  - [met] No mention of intolerance or hypersensitivity to ketamine or midazolam.\n  - [met] Physical exam and labs are normal; no significant medical conditions reported.\n  - [met] No evidence of medical conditions affecting drug metabolism.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT00000520", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy presenting with 5 days of high fever and irritability. He has conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue, inflammation and desquamation of the hands and feet, and cervical lymph\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 0}
{"pair": "sigir-201519__NCT00757120", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to read and write English.\n  - [met] Patient has smoked 1 to 2 packs per day for 47 years, which is at least a 47 pack-year history, exceeding the 30 pack-year requirement.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to participate in the informed consent process.\n  - [not met] Patient presents with recent, progressive shortness of breath and is in moderate respiratory distress, suggesting unstable clinical status in the past six weeks.\n  - [not met] Patient has symptoms and signs consistent with moderate to severe COPD (chronic cough, barrel chest, wheezing, significant smoking history), but no spirometry data is provided to confirm GOLD class II\n  - [not met] No chest CT scan results are provided, so the presence of more than minimal emphysema cannot be confirmed.\n  - [not met] No spirometry data is provided to confirm GOLD class I or 0.\n  - [not met] No chest CT scan results are provided, so the presence or absence of emphysema cannot be confirmed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 66-year-old female, but there is no mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] No information suggests the patient is a prisoner.\n  - [met] No information suggests the patient is part of a vulnerable population (other than age, but 66 is not considered vulnerable by default).\n  - [not met] Patient has recent, progressive shortness of breath and is in moderate respiratory distress, which may indicate a recent illness or exacerbation within the past six weeks.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic inflammatory disease, collagen vascular disease, immunodeficiency, non-cutaneous malignancy, melanoma, or organ transplant.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital lung abnormalities or previous lung surgery.\n  - [met] No mention of hepatitis B, hepatitis C, or HIV/AIDS.\n  - [not met] No CT scan results are provided, so cannot assess fo", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-20147__NCT00883493", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of bipolar disorder and is currently experiencing depressive symptoms (feeling depressed, difficulty sleeping, anxiety, agitation, suicidal thoughts, irritability). The note \n  - [not met] The HAM-D score is not provided. The patient has significant depressive symptoms, but without a formal HAM-D score, this cannot be confirmed.\n  - [not met] The YMRS score is not provided. The patient is described as fidgety and agitated, but there is no evidence of mania or a formal YMRS score.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has bipolar disorder and depressive symptoms. There is no mention of any other Axis I disorder within the past 6 months. However, the patient has current suicidal thoughts, which may pose \n  - [not met] The patient is taking lithium carbonate and zolpidem. There is no information about drugs that induce or inhibit hepatic metabolizing enzymes within 14 days before randomisation.\n  - [not met] The patient is currently taking lithium carbonate (a mood stabilizer) and zolpidem (a psychoactive medication). There is no indication that she is able to discontinue these medications prior to random", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201429__NCT01440803", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 51-year-old woman who is postmenopausal (documented by LH and FSH levels). This criterion requires premenopausal women aged 20-45 with regular menses and no secondary cause of osteopo\n  - [not met] There is no mention of any adult fractures, low-trauma or otherwise, in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about willingness to use contraception.\n  - [not met] The patient is postmenopausal and over age 35. This criterion is for premenopausal women ages 20-35 with a major osteoporotic fracture and low BMD. She does not meet the age or menopausal status requi\n  - [not met] This criterion is for premenopausal women above age 35 with a history of fracture and/or low BMD. The patient is postmenopausal and there is no mention of fracture or low BMD.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any condition that increases the risk of osteosarcoma.\n  - [met] No information about early follicular phase serum is provided, but as the patient is postmenopausal, this is not applicable.\n  - [met] No disorders of mineral metabolism are mentioned.\n  - [met] No suspicion of osteomalacia is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of vitamin D deficiency.\n  - [met] No mention of pregnancy or lactation within the past 12 months; patient is postmenopausal.\n  - [met] Prolonged amenorrhea during reproductive years is not mentioned; patient is postmenopausal.\n  - [met] No history of eating disorder is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 18}
{"pair": "sigir-201523__NCT01983553", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note indicating that the patient is participating in study CYD23.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of assent or informed consent forms being signed by the participant, parent, or witnesses.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the participant's or parent's ability to attend scheduled visits or comply with study procedures.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is planning to participate in another dengue clinical trial.\n  - [met] There is no information indicating the patient is deprived of freedom, in an emergency setting, or hospitalized involuntarily.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20159__NCT00367627", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is described as a 10 year old child, which is outside the 2-5 years old range.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any serious chronic illness in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about a stool test or its result for STH (soil-transmitted helminths).\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient having taken any antehelminthic drug in the previous six months.\n  - [not met] There is no information about parental/guardian consent for participation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 10 years old, which is more than 5 years old, so this exclusion criterion is met (should NOT have age <2 or >5).\n  - [not met] There is no information about stool test results for intestinal helminths.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any serious chronic illness.\n  - [not met] There is no information about parental/guardian consent or refusal.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient receiving any antehelminthic drug after survey but before study interventions.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT01084239", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presented with chest pain radiating to the left shoulder and jaw, and shortness of breath, which are cardiac equivalents. The episode occurred in the morning and led to ED presentation, su\n  - [met] The patient has hypertension and hypercholesterolemia (hyperlipidemia), which are two cardiac risk factors.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to provide written informed consent. The patient has dementia, which may impair consent capacity.\n  - [not met] The patient is 82 years old, which is older than 75.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's ability to hold their breath for 10 seconds.\n  - [met] The EKG showed sinus regular tachycardia, which is a sinus rhythm.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The EKG showed ST-segment elevations up to 3 mm in V1, V2, and V3 (more than two anatomically adjacent leads), which meets the exclusion criterion for new diagnostic ischemic ECG changes.\n  - [met] Coronary angiography showed no stenosis or clinically significant disease. There is no documented or self-reported history of CAD, MI, PCI, or CABG.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the time since ED presentation.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about BMI.\n  - [not met] The patient has chronic renal insufficiency, but no serum creatinine value is provided. However, chronic renal insufficiency suggests likely impaired renal function.\n  - [not met] Troponin T is 0.40 ng/ml, which is above the exclusion threshold (>0.09 ng/ml).\n  - [met] The patient is hypertensive (BP 199/108 mm Hg), but there is no evidence of hemodynamic instability (systolic BP <80 mm Hg, arrhythmias, or persistent chest pain despite therapy).\n  - [not met] No information about allergy to iodinated contrast agent.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT02442999", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 31-year-old woman, which falls within the 18-50 years old range.\n  - [met] The patient is seen in clinic for amenorrhea and desires pregnancy, suggesting she is likely being seen by an OB/GYN or reproductive endocrinology specialist, but this is not explicitly stated.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of polycystic ovarian syndrome or the modified Rotterdam criteria being met. The patient's amenorrhea and galactorrhea are more consistent with hyperprolactinemia.\n  - [met] The note is in English and there is no indication of language barrier or inability to consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of late onset congenital adrenal hyperplasia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of Cushing's disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of androgen-secreting tumors.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.\n  - [met] The patient is currently taking no medications, including sleep medications.\n  - [met] The patient is not taking any medications, including Unisom, Ambien, or Lunesta.\n  - [met] This criterion is about not excluding patients taking non-prescribed herbal medications for sleep. The patient is not taking any medications, so this does not apply.\n  - [met] Thyroid stimulating hormone (TSH) is normal, so there is no untreated thyroid disease.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT02494232", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as 'fully awake and alert,' which strongly suggests a Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) of 15, as this corresponds to being fully conscious and oriented.\n  - [met] Vital signs are reported as blood pressure 134/74 mm Hg and pulse 87/min, both within normal ranges. No evidence of shock or instability is mentioned.\n  - [met] The note states the patient is 'admitted to the ER following a car accident,' but does not specify the exact time since injury. However, ER admission after trauma typically occurs within hours, so it \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being assigned to an 'urgent' or 'urgent triage category.' She is stable and alert, which suggests she is not in the most urgent triage category.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201423__NCT01248507", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about informed consent being signed.\n  - [met] The patient is 63 years old.\n  - [met] The patient has a history of heavy smoking, chronic respiratory symptoms (cough, dyspnea), physical findings (barrel chest, cyanosis, tachypnea, rales), and chest x-ray with hyperinflation, all consis\n  - [met] The patient is described as a heavy smoker, which strongly suggests at least 10 pack-years.\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute worsening of respiratory symptoms (increased cough, purulent sputum, increased dyspnea) requiring increased oxygen use, consistent with an acute exacerbation of COPD (A\n  - [met] The patient was admitted to the hospital due to worsening respiratory symptoms consistent with AECOPD.\n  - [not met] There is no information about treatment with oral corticosteroids or antibiotics, or confirmation at GP setting.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a heavy smoker.\n  - [met] The patient has COPD, but there is no mention of other active long-term respiratory diseases such as asthma, cystic fibrosis, severe bronchiectasis, malignancy, or restrictive lung disease.\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note that the exacerbation is due to pneumothorax or acute decompensated heart failure.\n  - [met] There is no mention of communication difficulties.\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note to suggest a life expectancy less than one year.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201410__NCT00471289", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information about written informed consent is provided.\n  - [met] Patient is 67 years old, which is >18 years.\n  - [met] Patient is female and 67 years old; likely postmenopausal and not of childbearing potential, but pregnancy status and birth control use are not specified.\n  - [not met] No information about willingness or ability to comply with follow-up evaluation.\n  - [not met] Patient has loss of distal pulses and a cool right foot, which may indicate critical limb ischemia, but there is no explicit mention of rest pain, ulcers, or gangrene.\n  - [not met] No information about stenosis or occlusion of infrapopliteal arteries or lesion length.\n  - [not met] No information about artery diameter.\n  - [not met] No information about patency of common iliac, external iliac, superficial femoral, or popliteal artery.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient has loss of distal pulses and a cool foot after catheterization, which may suggest acute limb ischemia, but the note does not explicitly state 'acute limb ischemia.'\n  - [met] No mention of subacute limb ischemia or need for thrombolysis.\n  - [met] No mention of active bleeding or bleeding diathesis.\n  - [met] No mention of recent hemorrhagic stroke or CNS abnormality.\n  - [met] No mention of gastrointestinal or genitourinary bleeding.\n  - [not met] Patient has a pulsatile mass in the right groin, which is suggestive of an aneurysm in the common femoral artery.\n  - [not met] Patient underwent cardiac catheterization via the right femoral artery earlier in the morning, which may be considered revascularization involving the same limb within 30 days prior to the index proce\n  - [met] No mention of previous implanted stent at the index site.", "n_inc_assessed": 9, "n_exc_assessed": 20}
{"pair": "sigir-20151__NCT02150941", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presented with multiple bouts of vomiting with a 'coffee ground' appearance, which is consistent with coffee ground emesis.\n  - [not met] The patient is hypotensive (BP 70/40 mmHg, systolic < 90) and tachycardic (HR 135 bpm, >110). However, there is no mention of hematochezia (passage of fresh blood per rectum).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about endoscopy findings or whether a bleeding source was identified within 5 minutes. Cannot determine from the note.\n  - [met] The patient is 44 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of an endoscopy being performed in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a previous endoscopy for the current episode of UGIB.\n  - [not met] The patient has decreased mental status, but there is no information about consent or the presence/absence of a substitute decision maker.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT00957021", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, which is younger than the required age range of 21-80 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention that the patient requires a primary cemented total knee replacement.\n  - [not met] The patient has an osteolytic lesion, but there is no diagnosis of osteoarthritis, traumatic arthritis, or avascular necrosis.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the status of the collateral ligaments.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient or guardian signing an IRB approved consent form.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness or ability to comply with postoperative evaluations and rehabilitation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of inflammatory arthritis.\n  - [met] There is no information about the patient's BMI or morbid obesity.\n  - [met] There is no history of total or unicompartmental reconstruction of the affected joint mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a high tibial osteotomy or femoral osteotomy.\n  - [met] Sensation and motor tone were normal, and there is no mention of neuromuscular or neurosensory deficiency.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a systemic or metabolic disorder leading to progressive bone deterioration.\n  - [met] There is no mention of immunosuppression or chronic steroid use.\n  - [not met] The patient has an osteolytic lesion, which may compromise bone stock, but it is not explicitly stated that the bone cannot provide adequate support/fixation.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201530__NCT00586365", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 47 years old, which is greater than 18 years.\n  - [not met] The note does not specify whether operative treatment is planned or performed, only that the patient presents with a dislocation.\n  - [met] The patient has an elbow dislocation (ulna and radius dislocated from humerus).\n  - [not met] There is no mention of an olecranon fracture-dislocation or simple olecranon fracture.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a distal humerus fracture.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No existing diagnosis of any exclusionary conditions is mentioned.\n  - [met] No injury to the central nervous system, thorax, or abdomen is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of a fracture of any long bone; only dislocations are described.\n  - [met] No history of gastritis, peptic ulcer disease, or upper GI bleeding is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of impaired renal function, hypovolemia, heart failure, high blood pressure, fluid retention, asthma, liver dysfunction, or coagulation disorder.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to NSAIDs.\n  - [met] No mention of asthma, nasal polyps, urticaria, or hypotension associated with NSAIDs.\n  - [met] No mention of considerable dehydration.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 22}
{"pair": "sigir-201527__NCT01221844", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl. There is no mention of pregnancy or genetic thrombophilia markers such as factor V Leiden, prothrombin 20210A mutation, antiphospholipid antibodies, hyperhomocystein\n  - [not met] The patient is not described as pregnant, nor is there mention of hypertension (HT). She does have iron deficiency anemia, but the criterion specifically requires pregnant women with HT.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of pregnancy or trimester of pregnancy.\n  - [not met] No history of miscarriage is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No history of preterm delivery is mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient has Hb 4.2 g/dL (\u226411), MCV 61.8 fL (microcytic), serum iron <1.8 umol/L (very low), ferritin 2 ng/mL (\u226412). The number of red blood cells is not provided, but all other criteria for iron d\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has iron deficiency anemia as evidenced by low Hb, low MCV, low serum iron, and low ferritin.\n  - [met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl, not described as pregnant.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy, so the concept of 'uncomplicated pregnancies' does not apply.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about informed consent.\n  - [met] No mention of other iron supplementation treatments.\n  - [met] No mention of recent blood transfusion.\n  - [met] No other concomitant diseases are mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to milk proteins or iron products.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-20153__NCT01164046", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient does not have a history of cancer, and there is no mention of confirmed PE or DVT, nor of having been treated for 6-12 months with anticoagulants.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about written informed consent.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of an indication for long-term anticoagulant therapy such as metastasized disease or chemotherapy.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is above the minimum age of 18.\n  - [met] There is no mention of indications for anticoagulant therapy other than DVT or PE.\n  - [not met] There is no information about contraindications to LMWH or VKA.\n  - [met] The patient is a 65-year-old male, so childbearing potential, pregnancy, or breastfeeding do not apply.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a life expectancy less than 3 months.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201413__NCT01828697", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 30 years old, which is 18 years or older.\n  - [not met] The patient gave birth 3 weeks ago, so she is not currently pregnant. No mention of a positive urinary pregnancy test.\n  - [not met] The patient is postpartum, not currently pregnant, so gestational age < 14 weeks does not apply.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of previous objectively confirmed VTE (venous thromboembolism) in the patient's history.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous VTE related to a major provoking risk factor.\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient is currently on or requires therapeutic dose anticoagulant therapy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability to provide informed consent; the patient is described as apprehensive but alert.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any contraindication to LMWH in the note.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT00206375", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient does not have clinical or biochemical evidence of hypothyroidism. Her TSH is normal, and there is no mention of low T4 or fT4. She presents with amenorrhea and elevated prolactin, not hypo\n  - [not met] The patient is a 31-year-old woman, which is outside the age range of 8 to 16 years for females.\n  - [not met] The patient is female, not male.\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note of any chronic medical conditions. Amenorrhea and hyperprolactinemia are not necessarily chronic diseases affecting overall health.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the availability of a parent or guardian to attend study visits.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is not taking any medications, including those that affect growth.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of health problems or conditions that affect growth rate such as growth hormone deficiency, Cushing Syndrome, rickets, or chronic diseases.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any contraindications for GH or GNRHa therapy such as active tumor, impaired glucose tolerance, neurofibromatosis, or sleep apnea.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about moving to a new location.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about willingness to continue with the study.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT01554527", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, which falls within the 5-12 years old range.\n  - [not met] The note describes symptoms of sleep apnea (nighttime snoring, pauses in breathing, excessive sleepiness), but does not state that the patient is scheduled for an adenotonsillectomy.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the child can or will provide assent.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the parent's or guardian's language ability or willingness to agree to the study.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information about whether the patient has siblings already enrolled in the study.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient expecting to have another surgery during the study period.\n  - [met] There is no mention of neurological, psychiatric, or other medical conditions, or social factors that would interfere with the study.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking medications that affect sleepiness or alertness.\n  - [met] There is no mention of stimulant use (e.g., Ritalin, Adderall, Concerta).\n  - [met] There is no mention of sleep aide use (e.g., Melatonin, Ambien, Ativan).\n  - [met] There is no mention of sedating medicine use (e.g., Benadryl, Klonopin, Xanax, Valerian).", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201411__NCT00990262", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with excruciating pain in her right arm, not chest pain. There is no mention of chest pain or admission to rule out acute coronary syndrome.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about initial troponin or CK-MB tests.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of diagnostic ECG changes.\n  - [not met] The patient is hemodynamically unstable (BP 80/60).\n  - [not met] No information about creatinine clearance.\n  - [not met] No information about allergy to iodinated contrast agents.\n  - [not met] No information about metformin therapy.\n  - [not met] No information about asthma or reactive airway disease.\n  - [not met] No information about atrial fibrillation.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT01499134", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 72-year-old man, which meets the age and sex requirements.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is unable to give informed consent or complete scheduled visits.\n  - [met] The patient has increasing calf pain when walking uphill (claudication) for 3 months, with diminished pulses and cool extremities, suggesting peripheral arterial disease. However, there is no ABI meas\n  - [met] The patient has a history of hypertension. At the visit, BP is 151/91 mmHg and pulse is 67/min. He is currently prescribed a beta-blocker (propranolol previously, but not currently; currently on isoso\n  - [met] The patient has a history of myocardial infarction and transient ischemic attack, both of which indicate at least moderate risk for CAD.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information about participation in another clinical trial.\n  - [met] No evidence of ongoing resting limb pain or ulceration. No ABI <0.6 is reported.\n  - [met] No history of limb or digit amputation is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of peripheral revascularization within the last 6 months.\n  - [met] Blood pressure is 151/91 mmHg, which is below the exclusion threshold of 160/100 mmHg.\n  - [met] No contraindication or allergy to beta-blockers is mentioned. The patient was previously on propranolol.\n  - [met] The patient had a TIA 6 months ago, which is exactly at the cutoff. Myocardial infarction was 2 years ago. No coronary revascularization is mentioned. This is borderline, but technically meets the cri\n  - [met] No mention of angina symptoms.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-20149__NCT00937690", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a volunteer with or without a history of melanoma. There is no mention of melanoma history, but the criterion is met regardless of history.\n  - [met] The patient has multiple palpable skin lesions on her neck, as described in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a tissue diagnosis by cytologic or histologic evaluation.\n  - [not met] There is no mention that a tissue diagnosis will be obtained.\n  - [met] A clinical diagnosis of skin tags is strongly suggested by the description: small, soft, pedunculated lesions, flesh colored to slightly hyperpigmented. This matches the example of skin tags given in \n  - [met] The patient is 43 years old, which meets the age requirement. Willingness and ability to give informed consent is not explicitly stated, but there is no evidence to suggest otherwise.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy to adhesive skin markers or water-soluble ink.\n  - [met] There is no mention of very fragile skin.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any medical contraindication or potential problem in complying with the protocol.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
