{"pair": "sigir-201419__NCT00727376", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 52 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's willingness or ability to provide informed consent.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's willingness to comply with follow-up requirements.\n  - [not met] The patient has progressive dysphagia and weight loss, which are suggestive of esophageal cancer, but there is no mention of a biopsy-confirmed diagnosis, histology, or clinical stage.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the patient is indicated for chemotherapy and/or radiation therapy.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the ability to dilate the stricture to 15mm diameter.\n  - [not met] There is no information about placement of a PolyFlex stent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is contraindicated for endoscopy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior esophageal stent placements.\n  - [met] There is no information about the clinical stage of disease, so advanced stage cannot be confirmed.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT01550588", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient had a cryptogenic stroke two weeks ago, which is within the previous 3 months, and it was radiologically verified (CT scan performed).\n  - [not met] No mention of a Patent Foramen Ovale (PFO) diagnosis or echocardiographic verification. TEE was performed but found no evidence of abnormalities.\n  - [not met] No explicit statement about willingness to participate in follow-up visits. This information is not available.\n  - [met] Absence of other potential causes of stroke is implied by 'cryptogenic stroke' and negative findings on imaging and echocardiogram.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No identifiable cause of thromboembolic event other than PFO; in fact, no PFO was found. Stroke was cryptogenic.\n  - [met] No evidence of intracardiac thrombus, tumor, dilated cardiomyopathy, prosthetic heart valve, mitral stenosis, or endocarditis based on TEE and clinical note.\n  - [met] No mention of significant atherosclerosis, aortic dissection, collagen vascular disease, arteritis, vasculitis, or coagulopathy.\n  - [met] No history of acute or recent myocardial infarction or unstable angina is mentioned.\n  - [met] CT scan was negative for brain hemorrhage and stroke was cryptogenic, indicating vascular origin of neurological symptoms.\n  - [met] No history of intracranial bleeding, AVM, aneurysm, or uncontrolled coagulopathy is mentioned.\n  - [met] No pre-existing neurological disorders or intracranial disease (e.g., multiple sclerosis) are mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of left ventricular aneurysm or akinesis.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT00954031", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with symptoms suggestive of a severe throat infection (progressively worsening dysphagia, drooling, fever, muffled 'hot potato' voice, toxic appearance, leaning forward), which ar\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of neoplastic disease of the throat, hematologic disease with tonsillar localization, or history of tonsillectomy in the clinical note. The patient is a 5-year-old boy with no rele", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201412__NCT02548715", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a biopsy or a diagnosis of head and neck cancer. The patient has a cervical mass, but its nature is not specified.\n  - [not met] There is no information about treatment with surgery or location (Edmonton, Alberta).\n  - [not met] There is no information about treatment intent or any treatment at all.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of sub-clinical hypothyroidism or lab values (TSH, free T4). The patient has symptoms suggestive of hypothyroidism, but no labs or diagnosis are provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a cervical mass at the midline, which could be thyroid in origin, but there is no confirmed diagnosis of head and neck cancer of the thyroid gland or other subsite involving the thyroi\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous treatment for a different head and neck cancer.\n  - [met] There is no mention of history of radiation therapy or chemotherapy to the head and neck.\n  - [met] There is no explicit history of thyroid disease, but the patient has symptoms suggestive of hypothyroidism and a cervical mass possibly related to the thyroid. However, no formal diagnosis is stated.\n  - [met] The patient has symptoms suggestive of hypothyroidism (fatigue, weight gain, cold intolerance, hair loss, voice change), but no formal diagnosis is stated.\n  - [met] There is no mention or symptoms of hyperthyroidism.\n  - [met] There is no mention of autoimmune thyroid disease, Grave's disease, or Hashimoto's thyroiditis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of thyroiditis.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT00774137", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient underwent major surgery, but it is not specified as 'emergent'.\n  - [not met] Baseline serum creatinine is not provided, but current serum creatinine is 1.3 mg/dL, which is less than 2 mg/dL.\n  - [not met] No information about ejection fraction is provided.\n  - [not met] The patient is 6 months old, not 70 years old.\n  - [not met] No mention of diabetes mellitus.\n  - [not met] No mention of combined CABG and valve surgery.\n  - [not met] No mention of repeat CABG or valve surgery.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is an infant, not an adult.\n  - [met] No evidence of pre-operative acute kidney injury; kidney impairment is described post-operatively.\n  - [met] No mention of enrollment in a conflicting research study.\n  - [met] No mention of prior kidney transplantation.\n  - [met] Serum creatinine is 1.3 mg/dL, which is less than 4.5 mg/dL.\n  - [met] No mention of nephrotoxic drugs administered pre-operatively.\n  - [met] No mention of surgery for only left ventricular assist device.\n  - [met] No mention of undergoing open heart surgery; only 'major surgery' is specified.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT02568124", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note states that the patient had a normal head CT 3 weeks ago. There is no mention of a new CT scan or evidence of a subdural hematoma, chronic or otherwise.\n  - [not met] There is no diagnosis of subdural hematoma or any other specific diagnosis within the last 14 days mentioned in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence of an acute subdural hematoma with no chronic component; in fact, there is no evidence of any subdural hematoma.\n  - [met] No mention of any active thrombotic, thromboembolic, or atheroembolic disease.\n  - [met] No history of unprovoked DVT or idiopathic pulmonary embolism is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of hereditary thrombophilia.\n  - [met] No mention of atrial fibrillation.\n  - [met] No mention of a metallic heart valve.\n  - [met] No mention of vascular stenting procedure within the last year.\n  - [met] No mention of cardiac or vascular surgical procedure within the last 6 months.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT00119509", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient had a routine Pap smear with cytology negative, HPV positive. The criterion requires ONLY certain results, but does not specify if cytology negative, HPV positive is included. The note doe\n  - [not met] There is no mention of low grade epithelial abnormality in the Pap smear results. The result was cytology negative.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of minor changes in squamous cells. The Pap smear was cytology negative.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of minor changes in squamous cells with appearances consistent with Papillomavirus. The result was cytology negative, HPV positive.\n  - [met] The patient is a 32 year old female, which is within the 18-70 years age range.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy or plans to become pregnant. The patient reports no complaints and is in general good health.\n  - [met] The patient has no previous medical history and there is no mention of previous Pap smear abnormalities for 2 years.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT00002444", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No specific condition is described; this is a header.\n  - [not met] No mention of AIDS diagnosis or HIV status in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] No information about CD4 count or cryptosporidiosis duration; patient does not have documented AIDS.\n  - [not met] No mention of cryptosporidial diarrhea; stool findings are consistent with Giardia lamblia, not Cryptosporidium.\n  - [not met] Stool findings are consistent with Giardia lamblia (ellipsoidal cysts with 2+ nuclei), not Cryptosporidium oocytes. No mention of chronic diarrhea duration or frequency.\n  - [met] No evidence of life-threatening illness; likely has life expectancy >1 month.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to tolerate food; symptoms are GI but not severe enough to preclude oral intake.\n  - [not met] No information about prior medication.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No specific co-existing condition described; this is a header.\n  - [met] No specific symptoms or conditions listed; this is a header.\n  - [met] No mention of grade 3 or 4 toxicity; patient appears stable.\n  - [met] No prior conditions listed; this is a header.\n  - [not met] Stool findings are consistent with Giardia lamblia (ellipsoidal cysts with 2+ nuclei), which is specifically listed as an exclusion. Therefore, patient has Giardia lamblia in stool.\n  - [met] No history of intestinal Mycobacterium avium intracellular infection or intestinal Kaposi's sarcoma mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of Cytomegalovirus colitis mentioned.\n  - [met] No information about prior medication.", "n_inc_assessed": 13, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT02063087", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a child (8-year-old boy) seeking care with his parents implied.\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old, which is less than 18.\n  - [met] The child had blunt trauma above the eyebrows (struck his left temple on the pavement).\n  - [met] The patient is positive for at least one PECARN predictor (vomiting, GCS < 15, altered mental status).\n  - [not met] This criterion is for children < 2 years of age; the patient is 8 years old.\n  - [not met] This criterion is for children < 2 years of age; the patient is 8 years old.\n  - [met] This criterion is for children 2-18 years of age; the patient is 8 years old.\n  - [met] The patient meets several PECARN predictors for 2-18 years: vomiting, GCS < 15, altered mental status.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [not met] The patient has a GCS of 6 (< 15), so this exclusion criterion is NOT met.\n  - [met] No evidence of penetrating trauma, basilar skull fracture, or depressed skull fracture is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of brain tumors.\n  - [met] No mention of ventricular shunts.\n  - [met] No mention of bleeding disorder.\n  - [met] No mention of pre-existing neurological disorders.\n  - [met] No neuroimaging at an outside hospital before transfer is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT01228383", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 28-year-old female, which is within the age range of 18 to 55 years.\n  - [not met] The patient presented with neck and shoulder pain, paresthesias, tremors, spasticity, and later developed severe symptoms including hydrophobia and agitation, suggesting an acute and possibly severe i\n  - [not met] No information about the patient's body mass index is provided.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about sexual activity or contraception use.\n  - [met] This criterion is not applicable as the patient is female.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information is provided about prior rabies immunization.\n  - [not met] The patient developed acute illness with symptoms such as agitation, hydrophobia, and malaise, but there is no mention of fever \u226538\u00b0C within 2 weeks before dosing. However, the acute illness is clinic\n  - [met] No information is provided about immunodeficiency or auto-immune disease history.\n  - [met] No information is provided about planned immunization with live vaccines.\n  - [met] No information is provided about chronic administration of immunosuppressants or immune-modifying drugs.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201514__NCT01232387", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 27-year-old woman at 11 weeks gestation. Inclusion requires admission for term delivery (37 0/7 to 41 6/7 weeks gestation). The patient is only at 11 weeks gestation, so she does not \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the fetus having a known anomaly in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the woman is unable to complete the consent process due to precipitous delivery, severe labor discomfort, or fetal distress requiring immediate intervention.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT02147470", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 6-month-old infant, which is less than 18 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of cirrhosis of the liver in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the location of hospitalization.\n  - [met] The patient has oliguria, elevated BUN and creatinine, and granular casts, all consistent with acute kidney injury by AKIN criteria.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a right to left intracardiac shunt.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pulmonary hypertension or portopulmonary hypertension.\n  - [met] The patient is a 6-month-old male infant, so pregnancy or lactation is not possible.\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergies to Definity\u00ae.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of liver or kidney transplant.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is on hemodialysis.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT02190214", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The clinical note states the patient is a 56-year old female, which is clearly above 18 years old.\n  - [not met] The clinical note describes the patient as a 'Caucasian female' but does not mention citizenship. Being Caucasian does not preclude Malaysian citizenship, but there is no explicit evidence provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note regarding consent. Absence of evidence means we cannot confirm lack of consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-20156__NCT01204359", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with typical clinical symptoms of Graves disease: weight loss, sweating, insomnia, diarrhea, increased appetite, palpitations, warm and sweaty hands, tachycardia, hyperreflexia, a\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information in the note indicating the presence of 131I treatment contraindications, lack of informed consent, failure to complete treatment/follow-up, or unsuitability for radionuclide th", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201429__NCT01141972", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is documented to be in menopause within the last year, which qualifies as early menopause.\n  - [met] Patient is 51 years old, which is within the 40-55 age range.\n  - [not met] No information about BMI or weight is provided.\n  - [not met] No mention of menopausal symptoms (e.g., hot flashes, night sweats, etc.) in the note.\n  - [not met] No information about menstrual cycle changes or skipped cycles is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about pregnancy test results is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about vitamin D levels is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about weight stability is provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has been in menopause within the last year, so has not had >12 months without a period.\n  - [met] No mention of hormone use in the last 3 months.\n  - [met] No mention of hysterectomy.\n  - [met] No mention of abnormal blood tests.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic renal insufficiency, elevated calcium, sarcoidosis, lymphoma, or tuberculosis.\n  - [met] No history of osteoporosis or baseline DXA results are mentioned.\n  - [met] No information about vitamin D deficiency.\n  - [met] No information about vitamin D supplementation.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT02592434", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is 31 years old, which is outside the 2 to <18 years age range.\n  - [not met] No mention of meeting ILAR JIA diagnostic criteria; patient is an adult and not described as having JIA.\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of extended oligoarthritis is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of polyarthritis (RF+) is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of polyarthritis (RF-) is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of systemic JIA; patient is an adult.\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of psoriatic arthritis is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of polyarticular course JIA; patient is an adult.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [met] No information about previous JIA treatment with tofacitinib.\n  - [met] No diagnosis of systemic JIA.\n  - [met] No diagnosis of persistent oligoarthritis.\n  - [met] No diagnosis of undifferentiated JIA.\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic infections.", "n_inc_assessed": 23, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT00222742", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient's Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) is 6/15, which is less than or equal to 8.\n  - [met] The Glasgow Motor Score is not explicitly stated, but the patient has impaired movement of the right upper and lower extremities and a GCS of 6/15. It is likely the motor score is less than 6.\n  - [met] The injury was caused by a fall striking the left temple, with no mention of a penetrating injury. This is consistent with a closed head injury.\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old, which is between 0 and 18 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no indication that cooling could not be initiated within 6 hours. The patient was transferred and treated promptly.\n  - [met] The patient's GCS is 6, not 3.\n  - [met] No CT scan was performed, so there is no evidence of a normal CT scan. The criterion is met by default.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a penetrating brain injury; the injury is described as a fall with impact to the temple.\n  - [met] The mechanism of injury is clearly described (fall from bike, struck temple).\n  - [met] The time of injury is known (half an hour after the fall, symptoms developed).\n  - [met] No mention of uncorrectable coagulopathy or abnormal PT/PTT/INR.\n  - [met] The patient's blood pressure is elevated (155/98), not hypotensive.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-20147__NCT02129790", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of bipolar disorder, which satisfies the requirement for a diagnosis of Bipolar Disorder I, II, or Not Otherwise Specified.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about the patient's living situation or parental involvement.\n  - [not met] The patient reports recent suicidal thoughts, but the note does not specify if these occurred for at least 1 week in the prior 3 months or if there was a suicidal event.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness to be treated pharmacologically by a psychiatrist in the UCLA CHAMP clinic.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has suicidal thoughts but there is no indication that immediate hospitalization is required.\n  - [met] There is no mention of borderline personality disorder, schizophrenia, or schizoaffective disorder.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current substance dependence disorder.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20141__NCT00990262", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient had episodic chest pain that began two days earlier, with the latest episode ending half an hour prior to arrival. The pain started while walking, radiated to the back, and was accompanied\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of positive initial troponin or CK-MB tests in the note.\n  - [met] The EKG shows nonspecific changes, not diagnostic ECG changes such as ST-segment elevation or horizontal ST-segment depression in more than two contiguous leads.\n  - [met] The patient is not described as hemodynamically unstable, having ventricular tachycardia, or persistent chest pain despite therapy. Physical examination is normal.\n  - [met] There is no mention of creatinine clearance or renal dysfunction.\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy to iodinated contrast agents.\n  - [met] The patient is not on any medications, including metformin.\n  - [met] There is no mention of asthma or reactive airway disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of atrial fibrillation.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT02447614", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy (within 3-12 years) with habitual snoring and symptoms suggestive of sleep-disordered breathing. While the note does not explicitly state he was scheduled for an overn\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any chronic medical or psychiatric condition in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an acute respiratory infection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe craniofacial deformities.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cardiopulmonary diseases.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a genetic syndrome affecting cognitive abilities or use of medications that interfere with memory, sleep onset, or heart rate.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT02014896", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 72 years old, which is >18 years.\n  - [met] Patient was hospitalized for cryptogenic stroke (suggestive of AIS) and reports symptoms such as palpitations, shortness of breath, and chest pain.\n  - [not met] Criterion is incomplete ('One of the following') and does not specify what is required. Unable to assess.\n  - [not met] Patient was hospitalized two weeks ago for stroke, but timing of arrival relative to symptom onset is not specified.\n  - [not met] Patient was hospitalized two weeks ago for stroke, but timing of arrival relative to symptom onset is not specified.\n  - [met] CT was negative for brain hemorrhage; MRI and echocardiogram found no abnormalities. This suggests other pathologies were ruled out.\n  - [not met] No information about informed consent in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of CNS infection (meningitis or encephalitis) in past 30 days.\n  - [not met] Patient had a stroke two weeks ago, which is within the past 30 days.\n  - [met] No mention of primary or metastatic cancer involving the brain.\n  - [met] No mention of active cancer or recent cancer treatment.\n  - [met] No mention of autoimmune diseases such as lupus, rheumatoid arthritis, Crohn's disease, or ulcerative colitis.\n  - [met] No mention of active infectious diseases (HIV/AIDS, hepatitis C).\n  - [met] No mention of underlying medical condition prohibiting informed consent.\n  - [met] No mention of major surgery within three months prior to the index event.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201413__NCT01274637", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No evidence in the note that the patient is at high risk for thromboembolism for any of the specified reasons.\n  - [not met] No mention of known low risk thrombophilia or prior testing; per protocol, assumed not to have thrombophilia.\n  - [not met] No evidence of immobilization; patient presented with acute shortness of breath but no mention of prolonged bed rest.\n  - [not met] No evidence that the patient meets any two of the listed risk factors.\n  - [not met] No mention of postpartum infection, fever, or elevated neutrophil count.\n  - [not met] No mention of postpartum hemorrhage or estimated blood loss.\n  - [not met] No information about pre-pregnancy BMI.\n  - [not met] No mention of emergency cesarean birth; only that she gave birth 3 weeks ago.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient gave birth 3 weeks (21 days) ago, which is more than 36 hours since delivery.\n  - [not met] No mention of need for anticoagulation as judged by investigator.\n  - [not met] No personal history of previous VTE (DVT or PE) mentioned.\n  - [not met] No mention of LMWH use in the antenatal period.\n  - [not met] No mention of mechanical heart valve.\n  - [not met] No mention of high-risk thrombophilia; per protocol, assumed not to have it if not previously tested.\n  - [not met] No mention of contraindication to heparin therapy.\n  - [not met] No history of heparin induced thrombocytopenia (HIT) mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 19}
{"pair": "sigir-201415__NCT02348541", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the clinical note of a diagnosis of intrauterine adhesions or eligibility for hysteroscopic adhesiolysis. The main findings are amenorrhea, enlarged uterus with cystic areas, an\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's willingness to use additional contraception throughout the study.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is not pregnant (negative pregnancy test) but has a suspected molar pregnancy, which is specifically mentioned in the exclusion criterion. Therefore, the exclusion criterion is NOT met (i.\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note that the patient has suffered or currently suffers from a gynecological malignancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous hysteroscopic surgery or removal of fibroids.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201422__NCT02467959", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presented with abdominal pain that localized to the right lower quadrant.\n  - [met] The clinical presentation (right lower quadrant pain, rebound tenderness, edematous appendix on ultrasound) is highly suggestive of acute appendicitis.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of flank pain in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous appendectomy; the ultrasound shows an edematous appendix, indicating the appendix is present.\n  - [met] The patient denies sexual activity and has regular menses, making pregnancy highly unlikely.\n  - [met] There is no mention of unstable vital signs in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of frank peritonitis; only localized rebound tenderness is described.\n  - [met] The sequence of events is not explicitly stated, but it is likely that the ultrasound was performed after the examination, as the exam findings are described before the ultrasound result.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT01339702", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is an 8-year-old boy (child) who suffered physical trauma (fall from bike, striking head). He was transferred to the emergency department (likely a trauma center) after the incident. The c\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note of non-mechanical mechanisms (e.g., drowning), choking, asphyxiation, environmental injury, poisoning, non-traumatic intracranial hemorrhage, or other non-traumatic ac", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201419__NCT00907543", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The clinical note describes progressive dysphagia and weight loss, suggestive of esophageal cancer, but there is no mention of histological confirmation or specific cancer type (squamous cell carcinom\n  - [not met] There is no mention of distant metastases (M0) or M1 status in the note.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about clinical nodal status (N0 vs N1) or surgeon stratification.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of tumor spread into the gastric cardia or findings from esophagogastroscopy.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about mediastinal nodes or their resectability.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior chemotherapy for this malignancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior radiotherapy.\n  - [met] No mention of other malignancies.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The location of the tumor is described as at the lower end of the sternum, which is consistent with thoracic esophagus (>20 cm from incisors), not cervical esophagus (<20 cm).\n  - [met] No information about tumor spread into the gastric cardia or >3 cm spread into the stomach.\n  - [met] No mention of biopsy-proven metastatic supraclavicular nodes.\n  - [met] No mention of biopsy-proven metastatic celiac nodes.", "n_inc_assessed": 9, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT02046135", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 6-month-old male infant, which is less than or equal to 18 years of age.\n  - [not met] The patient underwent major surgery, but the note does not specify that it was cardiac surgery with cardiopulmonary bypass.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient's serum creatinine is 1.3 mg/dL, but there is insufficient information (height, Schwartz formula calculation) to determine creatinine clearance. Cannot confirm abnormal clearance.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cystic kidney disease or posterior ureteral valves in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a known metabolic disorder in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The patient is 6 months old, so not a premature infant <30 weeks gestation and <30 days old.\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe cardiogenic shock or use of ECMO/LVAD post-operatively.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT02381184", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, which is between 18-35 years.\n  - [not met] The patient has had amenorrhea for 7 months, which is less than 2 years of infertility.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's FSH level.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of clomiphene citrate (CC) resistance or treatment history.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about tubal patency or partner's semen analysis.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has hyperprolactinemia (elevated prolactin), which is a cause of infertility other than CC-resistant PCOS.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about BMI.\n  - [met] The patient is not taking any medications currently, and there is no mention of recent use of metformin, gonadotropins, hormonal contraception, or diet regimen.\n  - [not met] The patient has hyperprolactinemia (elevated prolactin), which is an exclusion criterion.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about hypersensitivity or contraindications to Letrozole or clomiphene.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about previous laparoscopic ovarian drilling (LOD).", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT00705952", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a diagnosis of diabetes mellitus, but the note does not specify whether this is new onset or Type 2. Given her age (64) and obesity, it is likely Type 2, but 'new onset' is not confirm\n  - [met] The patient is described as obese, which strongly suggests a BMI >25kg/m2.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is not compliant with her diabetes medication, indicating she is prescribed oral hypoglycaemic medications. This criterion requires the patient NOT to have such medications, so it is NOT m\n  - [met] The patient is a 64-year-old female; there is no mention of pregnancy and it is highly unlikely at this age.\n  - [met] The note is written in English and there is no indication that the patient cannot converse competently in English.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient attending another weight management programme.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient would be unable to attend all programme sessions for medical or other reasons.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about groups listed in A24, so cannot assess.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT00132951", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header criterion. Assessment is based on the following criteria.\n  - [met] Patient is a 31-year-old male outpatient with symptoms consistent with CAP (community-acquired pneumonia): fever, cough, chest pain, egophony.\n  - [met] Patient is male; criterion about female reproductive status does not apply.\n  - [not met] No information about informed consent in the note.\n  - [met] Patient has a clinical diagnosis consistent with CAP (fever, cough, chest pain, egophony).\n  - [not met] Patient is 31 years old, which is less than 35.\n  - [not met] No history of chronic bronchitis or FEV1/FVC data provided.\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of AECB (acute exacerbation of chronic bronchitis); patient has no history of chronic bronchitis.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header criterion. Assessment is based on the following criteria.\n  - [met] No history of congenital long-QTc syndrome mentioned.\n  - [met] Patient is male, not pregnant or breastfeeding.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to relevant antibiotics.\n  - [met] No mention of treatment with listed drugs.\n  - [met] No mention of treatment with listed drugs.\n  - [met] No mention of previous participation in this study.\n  - [met] No history of myasthenia gravis mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 20, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-20145__NCT00740883", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note describes a patient with symptoms suggestive of pulmonary embolism (shortness of breath, malaise, elevated D-dimer, decreased breath sounds), but there is no explicit diagnosis of idiopathic \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 56 years old, which is above 18.\n  - [met] There is no mention of warfarin hypersensitivity.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness or ability to give consent.\n  - [not met] The patient has right calf tenderness, which could suggest DVT, but there is no confirmed diagnosis of distal or proximal DVT.\n  - [not met] The pulmonary embolism (if present) would be provoked by recent surgery (mastectomy 20 days ago and bed rest), which is a reversible major risk factor.\n  - [met] No mention of major thrombophilia.\n  - [met] No mention of previous DVT or PE.\n  - [met] No mention of other indications for anticoagulation.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-201411__NCT02357212", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 40-year-old woman, which is age 18 or older.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of chest discomfort; the patient presents with right arm pain. No evidence of non-ST-elevation acute coronary syndrome is provided.\n  - [not met] No laboratory values are provided for troponin T.\n  - [not met] No laboratory values are provided for creatinine kinase MB-isoenzyme.\n  - [not met] No laboratory values are provided for NT-pro-BNP.\n  - [not met] No ECG findings are provided, so ST-segment depression cannot be assessed.\n  - [not met] No information is provided to calculate the TIMI risk score.\n  - [not met] No mention of recent non-cardiac surgery or elevated cardiac enzymes.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of ST-elevation myocardial infarction is provided.\n  - [met] No evidence of cardiogenic shock is provided.\n  - [met] No evidence of congestive heart failure is provided.\n  - [not met] The patient is hypotensive (BP 80/60), which suggests hemodynamic instability.\n  - [met] No mention of fibrinolytic therapy in the last 96 hours.\n  - [met] No mention of current bleeding or bleeding disorder.\n  - [met] No mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to study medications.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT02260934", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has progressive arthralgias, malaise, alopecia, malar rash, purpura, swelling/tenderness of joints, normocytic anemia, thrombocytopenia, positive ANA and anti-dsDNA, and proteinuria with RBC c\n  - [met] ANA and anti-dsDNA are both positive in labs.\n  - [not met] Patient has proteinuria and RBC casts, suggesting active lupus nephritis, but biopsy information is not provided.\n  - [not met] No kidney biopsy documentation is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No kidney biopsy documentation is mentioned, but active urinary sediment (RBC casts) is present.\n  - [not met] Urine is positive for RBC casts, but specific RBC/hpf count is not provided.\n  - [not met] No mention of WBC/hpf in urine.\n  - [met] Cellular casts (RBC casts) are present in urine.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information about prior treatment for lupus nephritis.\n  - [met] No mention of neutropenia.\n  - [met] Patient has thrombocytopenia, but platelet count is not specified. Severe thrombocytopenia (<50,000/mm^3) is not confirmed.\n  - [met] Patient has normocytic anemia, but hemoglobin value is not provided. Moderately severe anemia (< mg/dL) cannot be confirmed.\n  - [met] No mention of hypogammaglobulinemia.\n  - [met] No mention of TB test results.\n  - [met] No mention of pulmonary fibrotic changes.\n  - [met] No mention of active infection.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 20}
{"pair": "sigir-201528__NCT01859130", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old, which is below the required age range of 18-75 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention that the patient qualifies for primary total knee arthroplasty or has severe knee pain and disability due to the listed causes. The patient has knee pain and swelling, but not in t\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of rheumatoid arthritis, osteoarthritis, traumatic arthritis, or polyarthritis is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No mention of collagen disorders or avascular necrosis.\n  - [not met] No evidence of post-traumatic loss of joint configuration or patellofemoral issues.\n  - [not met] No mention of moderate valgus, varus, or flexion deformities.\n  - [not met] No history of previous failed surgical attempts.\n  - [not met] No information about participation in an informed consent process.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of participation in other surgical or pain management studies.\n  - [met] No previous history of infection in the affected joint is mentioned, but the current presentation could be infectious. However, the criterion is about previous history, not current infection.\n  - [met] No mention of insufficient bone stock.\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old and therefore skeletally immature.\n  - [met] No mention of neuropathic arthropathy.\n  - [met] No mention of osteoporosis, loss of musculature, or neuromuscular disease.\n  - [met] No mention of stable, painless arthrodesis.\n  - [met] No mention of severe instability due to absence of collateral ligament integrity.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-20143__NCT00771563", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has a left lung mass and a solitary brain mass, which is consistent with metastatic disease (stage IV NSCLC).\n  - [not met] There is no mention of candidacy for radical combined modality treatments or high-dose radiation therapy. This is not specified in the note.\n  - [met] Patient has at least two measurable lesions: a left lung mass and a solitary brain mass.\n  - [met] Patient is described as otherwise asymptomatic with only mild exertional dyspnea and occasional cough, suggesting good performance status.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about haematological, renal, or liver function.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of previous chemotherapy for NSCLC.\n  - [not met] Patient has a solitary mass in the right frontal lobe, consistent with brain metastasis.\n  - [met] No history of cerebral haemorrhage, recent neurosurgery, or recent surgery is mentioned.\n  - [met] No indication for anticoagulant, thrombolytic, or antiplatelet therapy is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of concomitant therapy with an anti-angiogenesis agent.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication for LMWH.\n  - [met] No mention of limited life expectancy; patient is otherwise asymptomatic except for mild symptoms.\n  - [met] No mention of serious concomitant systemic disease, uncontrolled hypertension, peptic ulcer, or other conditions precluding study participation.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-20143__NCT00946712", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a left lung mass and a solitary brain mass, which is consistent with possible stage IV non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) with brain metastasis. However, there is no histological or cy\n  - [not met] A CT scan of the head was performed and showed a solitary mass in the right frontal lobe. There is no mention of prior treatment for brain metastasis or control status, nor information about corticost\n  - [met] The patient has measurable disease (lung mass and brain mass) documented by CT. However, there is no information about timing of assessment or documentation on a Baseline Tumor Assessment Form.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about tumor tissue availability or agreement to submit specimens for EGFR FISH testing or other studies.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about prior chemotherapy, platinum-based therapy, EGFR-targeted agents, VEGF-related agents, or monoclonal antibody therapy.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about prior radiation or recovery from associated toxicities.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about timing from surgical or biopsy procedures or plans for bevacizumab.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about major surgery, recovery, or plans for bevacizumab.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):", "n_inc_assessed": 30, "n_exc_assessed": 0}
{"pair": "sigir-20152__NCT01376778", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 62-year-old male, not a pregnant woman. The criterion requires diagnosis of primary maternal CMV infection, which is not applicable.\n  - [not met] No information about CMV IgM or IgG antibody screens is provided, and the patient is not maternal.\n  - [not met] No evidence of maternal seroconversion or CMV IgG antibody development is described.\n  - [not met] The patient is a 62-year-old male, not pregnant. Gestational age criteria are not applicable.\n  - [not met] The patient is not pregnant, so singleton pregnancy criteria are not applicable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is not maternal, so maternal CMV infection pre-dating pregnancy is not applicable.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to plasma or plasma derived products.\n  - [met] No mention of planned termination of pregnancy; patient is not pregnant.\n  - [met] No mention of fetal anomalies or demise; patient is not pregnant.\n  - [met] No mention of IgA deficiency.\n  - [met] No mention of planned use of immune globulin, ganciclovir, or valganciclovir.\n  - [met] No mention of maternal renal disease; patient is not maternal.\n  - [not met] The patient is on immunosuppressive medications, including prednisone, which indicates immune impairment (e.g., organ transplant or other causes).", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT02012478", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 64-year-old female, which is clearly age 18 or older.\n  - [met] The patient has a diagnosis of diabetes mellitus. While the type is not explicitly stated, the patient is obese and older, which strongly suggests type II diabetes.\n  - [met] The patient has 'persistently elevated HbA1c' and is non-compliant with medication, suggesting poorly controlled diabetes. The exact values and number of measurements are not provided, but the descrip\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 64-year-old female. There is no mention of pregnancy, and at this age, pregnancy is highly unlikely.\n  - [met] The clinical note is in English and there is no indication that the patient is non-English speaking or reading.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT02380352", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 8 years old (within 6 months to 10 years). Presents with symptoms consistent with CAP (fever, cough, dyspnea, respiratory distress, chest x-ray with infiltrates).\n  - [met] Fever up to 39 C reported in the ER, which meets the fever threshold (>37.5 C axillary, >37.7 C oral, or >38 C rectal).\n  - [met] Patient must meet at least one of the following: tachypnoea, cough, increased work of breathing, or auscultatory findings consistent with pneumonia.\n  - [not met] Tachypnoea is not explicitly documented (no respiratory rate given), so cannot confirm.\n  - [met] Cough is reported by history.\n  - [met] Patient is in respiratory distress, which indicates increased work of breathing.\n  - [met] Bronchial respiratory sounds on the left are auscultatory findings consistent with pneumonia.\n  - [met] Chest x-ray shows bilateral lung infiltrates, consistent with bacterial CAP. No explicit mention of ED physician's judgment, but findings are typical.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of any exclusion conditions (cystic fibrosis, anatomic lung disease, bronchiectasis, congenital heart disease, repeated aspiration, malignancy, immunodeficiency, advanced HIV, recent prolon", "n_inc_assessed": 9, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT02064959", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient suffered a traumatic brain injury from a fall, with no mention of a penetrating injury. The mechanism (fall from bike, struck temple) is consistent with non-penetrating TBI.\n  - [met] The patient's GCS is 6/15. Since the GCS motor score is part of the total GCS, and the patient is not following commands (as evidenced by impaired movement and low GCS), it is likely the motor score i\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old, which is outside the required age range of 22-65 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of acute subdural hematoma or a need for emergent craniotomy. The neurosurgical team deferred CT scan, so this cannot be confirmed.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's temperature or time to reach 35\u00b0C.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient's GCS is 6, not 3, and pupils were initially symmetrical and reactive, later asymmetrical but not described as bilaterally fixed and dilated.\n  - [met] There is no evidence the patient followed commands after an initial period of coma. The patient became drowsy and had impaired movement, but no mention of following commands.\n  - [met] No history of pre-existing neurological deficit is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of concomitant spinal cord injury.\n  - [met] No temperature is provided, so hypothermia (<35\u00b0C) cannot be confirmed.\n  - [met] Blood pressure is 155/98, heart rate 52/min. No evidence of MAP <60 mmHg for 30 minutes.\n  - [met] No mention of active cardiac dysrhythmia or hemodynamic instability.\n  - [met] The patient is an 8-year-old boy, so pregnancy is not possible.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201419__NCT01366833", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 52-year-old man, which is \u226518 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a confirmed diagnosis of esophageal or GEJ cancer on biopsy. The symptoms are suggestive, but confirmation is lacking.\n  - [met] The patient has progressive dysphagia, now including liquids, which typically corresponds to a dysphagia score \u22652 (score 2: able to swallow soft foods only; score 3: liquids only).\n  - [not met] There is no information about stage IV cancer or metastatic disease in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of expected life expectancy <3 months. The patient is experiencing weight loss but no explicit prognosis.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting inability to undergo stent insertion.\n  - [met] There is no mention of Siewert Type III GEJ cancer. The type is not specified.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an esophageal-airway fistula.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20141__NCT01653587", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with new-onset chest pain at rest/minimal exertion, lasting more than 10 minutes, with associated symptoms (nausea, diaphoresis, mild dyspnea). EKG shows nonspecific changes, but \n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the intention to submit the patient to early invasive strategy (coronary angiography/PCI within 72 hours).\n  - [not met] There is no mention of signed informed consent in the note.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about eligibility for transradial/transfemoral access, Allen test, operator familiarity, or agreement.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 58 years old, which is above 18.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy, but the patient is 58 years old, making pregnancy highly unlikely.\n  - [met] The patient is not on any medications, so is not on chronic anticoagulants.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to antiplatelet/anticoagulant drugs.\n  - [met] No evidence of active bleeding, severe liver failure, peptic ulcer, renal failure, or thrombocytopenia.\n  - [met] The patient has hypertension, but there is no mention of it being uncontrolled.\n  - [met] No evidence of cardiogenic shock; physical exam is normal.\n  - [met] No history of previous myocardial revascularization surgery.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT00997100", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 21 years old, which is >18 years.\n  - [met] Patient has at least 4 ACR criteria for SLE: malar rash, alopecia, arthritis, hematologic disorder (anemia, thrombocytopenia), positive ANA, positive anti-dsDNA, renal disorder (proteinuria, RBC casts\n  - [met] Patient presents with active SLE symptoms: arthritis, rash, hematologic and renal involvement.\n  - [met] Patient has arthritis (>2 joints with swelling/tenderness) and inflammatory-type skin rash (malar rash, purpura).\n  - [not met] Laboratory values are described (anemia, thrombocytopenia, proteinuria, RBC casts), but not all values (e.g., neutrophil count, bilirubin, AST/ALT) are provided.\n  - [not met] Hemoglobin is described as 'normocytic anemia', but no value is given. Cannot confirm if \u2265100 g/L.\n  - [not met] No information on absolute neutrophil count.\n  - [not met] No information on bilirubin.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No evidence of CNS lupus, systemic vasculitis, pericarditis, pleuritis, or peritonitis. However, patient has proteinuria and RBC casts, which may indicate active renal lupus.\n  - [not met] No information on GFR or renal function beyond proteinuria/RBC casts.\n  - [not met] No information on corticosteroid use.\n  - [not met] No information on intravenous corticosteroid use.\n  - [not met] No information on intravenous cyclophosphamide use.\n  - [not met] No information on anti-rheumatic/immunosuppressive drug use.\n  - [not met] No information on B-cell depletion therapy.\n  - [not met] No information on CYP3A4 inhibitor/inducer use.", "n_inc_assessed": 12, "n_exc_assessed": 18}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT00610506", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 20-year-old female, which is within the 18 to 65 years age range.\n  - [met] The patient reports fatigue, increased sleep and appetite, difficulty concentrating, anhedonia, and guilt, which are consistent with major depression with atypical features. There is no mention of psy\n  - [not met] No HAM-D score is provided in the note.\n  - [met] The patient is a college student, alert, and able to provide history, suggesting ability to give informed consent. She is of child-bearing potential.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current or recent psychotropic medication use.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of bipolar disorder or manic/hypomanic symptoms.\n  - [met] There is no mention of psychotic symptoms or diagnosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of suicidal ideation or suicide risk.\n  - [met] There is no mention of substance abuse history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypersensitivity to these medications.\n  - [met] The patient has no significant past medical history and normal physical exam and labs.\n  - [met] There is no mention of psychotherapy initiation or termination.\n  - [met] There is no mention of ECT treatment.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT00703521", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 28-year-old female, not a 12-18 month old toddler.\n  - [not met] The patient is not in good health at time of entry, presenting with neck and shoulder pain, paresthesias, tremors, spasticity, agitation, hydrophobia, and was hospitalized.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about availability for all scheduled visits.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent signed by parents.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of a history of rabies immunization.\n  - [met] No mention of Japanese encephalitis immunization or disease.\n  - [not met] The patient appears to have a significant acute infectious disease (possible rabies), as evidenced by hydrophobia, agitation, and hospitalization.\n  - [not met] No mention of fever or recent systemic antibiotic/antiviral therapy, but the patient is acutely ill and hospitalized.\n  - [met] No mention of corticosteroids, immunosuppressive drugs, anti-inflammatory drugs, or chloroquine use.\n  - [met] No mention of any vaccine administration within the past 14 days.\n  - [met] No mention of known immunodeficiency or autoimmune disease.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to neomycin, tetracycline, or amphotericin-B.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT02564471", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about informed consent being provided.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness to comply with study procedures or availability for the study duration.\n  - [met] The patient is a 28-year-old female, which is within the age range (\u226518 to \u226460 years).\n  - [not met] The patient initially had an unremarkable physical exam except for slight tremors and spasticity, but later developed severe symptoms (spastic arm movements, agitation, hydrophobia, difficulty swallow\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a female of childbearing potential, but there is no information about pregnancy, lactation, or contraception status.\n  - [met] There is no information about participation in other clinical trials.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous history of receiving the rabies vaccine.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous history of receiving rabies immune globulin.\n  - [met] The patient has increasing agitation and anxiety, but there is no evidence of a major psychiatric disorder such as severe depression, psychosis, or seizures. The anxiety appears to be acute and relate", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT01978288", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the mother's age.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the mother's (or father's) history of asthma, atopy, or treatment for asthma.\n  - [not met] The child is 5 years old and not being enrolled during the first week of life.\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention of signed informed consent from parent(s) or legal guardian(s).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No history of wheezing or underlying lung disease is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of respiratory complications at birth.\n  - [met] No mention of prematurity; gestational age at birth is not provided.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital heart defects.\n  - [met] No mention of underlying neuromuscular disease.\n  - [not met] The patient has severe upper airway symptoms (drooling, muffled voice, leaning forward), which are classic for severe upper airway obstruction (e.g., epiglottitis).\n  - [met] No mention of hydrocephalus.\n  - [met] No mention of history of seizures.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201512__NCT01730690", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The clinical note describes symptoms suggestive of meningitis (headache, fever, nuchal rigidity, clear fluid from nose after skull fracture), but does not mention any CSF culture results or soluble an\n  - [not met] There is no mention of PCR testing in CSF in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] Purpura fulminant is not mentioned in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of PCR in blood, positive blood culture, or CSF cell reaction in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 44 years old, which is above the exclusion threshold of 18 years.\n  - [met] There is no mention of refusal to participate in the clinical note.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT00929721", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 31 years old, which is younger than 50 years of age.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the patient's residence or whether they reside in the surveillance area.\n  - [met] The patient presents to a healthcare facility with symptoms (productive cough, fever, chest pain, abnormal lung exam) that are consistent with community-acquired pneumonia (CAP), and the treating phys\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient was transferred from another facility or that they were previously hospitalized.\n  - [met] There is no evidence that the pneumonia was acquired in the hospital; symptoms developed at home.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201413__NCT01318174", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of COPD or any suspicion of COPD in the patient's history or current presentation. She is described as generally healthy with no prior health problems except for 2 natural abortion\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a COPD exacerbation. The patient has no known history of COPD and her current symptoms (shortness of breath, tachypnea, tachycardia) are not attributed to COPD.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with acute shortness of breath, but there is no clear diagnosis provided. However, since she does NOT have COPD and her symptoms could be due to other causes (e.g., postpartum sta\n  - [met] There is no mention of contrast allergy or pregnancy. She is postpartum (gave birth 3 weeks ago), so she is NOT pregnant. No evidence she is unable to perform CT pulmonary angio.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting she has already been included in the study.\n  - [met] There is no mention of anticoagulant use in the clinical note.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201412__NCT01739972", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 25 years old, which is within the 18-65 age range. She has symptoms suggestive of hypothyroidism (fatigue, weight gain, cold intolerance, hair loss, voice change, anterior cervical mass\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note of any of the listed exclusion conditions (e.g., pregnancy, cardiac disease, lung disease, GI surgeries, renal/liver dysfunction, cancer, psychosis, medication use, et\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is scheduled for deployment.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT02016053", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 6-month-old male infant with AKI (urine output <0.2 mL/kg/hr, elevated BUN and creatinine, granular casts, high FENa). However, there is no mention of cirrhosis or baseline renal func\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 6 months old, which is less than 18 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of preexisting chronic renal disease; the AKI appears to be acute post-surgery.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of obstructive uropathy.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of cirrhosis or HCC.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of advanced cardiopulmonary disease.\n  - [met] The patient is a 6-month-old male infant, so pregnancy is not possible.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of extrahepatic malignancy.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT01917149", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No explicit diagnosis of dilated cardiomyopathy is mentioned. The patient has segmental left ventricular dysfunction, but this is not the same as dilated cardiomyopathy.\n  - [not met] Left ventricular systolic function is described as 'mildly impaired.' No ejection fraction value is given, but 'mildly impaired' usually does not correspond to <35%.\n  - [not met] NYHA class is not specified. The patient has symptoms (chest pain, shortness of breath), but these may be acute and not chronic heart failure symptoms. Insufficient information.\n  - [not met] No information about symptom stability or rapid deterioration in the month prior to presentation.\n  - [not met] No mention of signed informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of contradictions or intolerance to studied drugs.\n  - [met] Supine systolic blood pressure is 199 mmHg, well above 90 mmHg.\n  - [not met] Patient has renal artery stenosis, but degree (>50%) is not specified.\n  - [met] Patient is an 82-year-old woman; no mention of pregnancy or lactation.\n  - [not met] Patient has chronic renal insufficiency, but no GFR value is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about liver function or bilirubin levels.\n  - [not met] No information about AST or ALT levels.\n  - [not met] No information about hemoglobin or potassium levels.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 19}
{"pair": "sigir-20141__NCT01701453", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 58 years old, which is \u2265 20 years.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to verbally confirm understanding or provide written informed consent.\n  - [not met] There is no information about a culprit lesion in a native coronary artery with significant stenosis (>50%) eligible for stent implantation.\n  - [not met] The patient presents with episodic chest pain, nausea, diaphoresis, and mild dyspnea, but the EKG shows nonspecific changes and there is no mention of elevated biomarkers or specific ECG findings for \n  - [not met] There is no information about the diameter of the target lesion(s) in a native coronary artery.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the target lesion(s) are amenable for percutaneous coronary intervention.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypersensitivity or contraindication to any of the listed medications or contrast media.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active pathologic bleeding.\n  - [met] There is no mention of gastrointestinal or genitourinary bleeding within the prior 3 months, or major surgery within 2 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of systemic Biolimus, everolimus, or zotarolimus use within 12 months.\n  - [met] The patient is a 58-year-old woman, but there is no information about childbearing potential or pregnancy plans.\n  - [met] There is no mention of history of bleeding diathesis, known coagulopathy, or refusal of blood transfusions.\n  - [met] The patient has hypertension and obesity, but there is no mention of noncardiac comorbid conditions with life expectancy <1 year or protocol noncompliance.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an elective surgical procedure planned that would necessitate interruption of clopidogrel.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-20147__NCT00422331", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The clinical note states the patient has a history of bipolar disorder. However, it does not specify whether this is Bipolar 1 Disorder. Bipolar 1 is characterized by manic episodes, but the note does\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the note of the patient being hospitalized or in the process of being hospitalized for a manic or mixed episode. The patient is experiencing depressive and anxious symptoms, but\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of rapid cycling in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The patient is currently taking lithium carbonate, which suggests no history of hypersensitivity or adverse reaction to lithium.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201423__NCT00883701", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of heavy smoking, chronic respiratory symptoms (cough, shortness of breath), barrel-shaped chest, diffuse rales, and hyperinflation on chest x-ray, all strongly suggestive of\n  - [met] The patient is a COPD patient seeking medical assistance for exacerbation-related symptoms. The note does not specify clinic vs hospital, but he is seeking care for these symptoms.\n  - [met] COPD diagnosis according to GOLD Consensus Statement is not explicitly stated, but clinical features (smoking, barrel chest, hyperinflation, chronic symptoms) are highly suggestive.\n  - [not met] Symptoms began about a week prior to admission, which is more than 72 hours ago.\n  - [met] It is unclear if the patient has abstained from any new therapeutic intervention; he has used home oxygen, but no mention of new medications or treatments.\n  - [not met] The patient is cyanotic, tachypneic, and required home oxygen, which are signs of severe exacerbation. He was admitted, suggesting hospitalization was required.\n  - [not met] This is for control subjects, not applicable as patient has COPD.\n  - [not met] Patient sought medical assistance for symptoms suggesting acute bronchitis (dyspnea, sputum production, purulence, cough), but he has COPD, so not a control subject.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient does not have asthma, but does have COPD (a respiratory disease). The exclusion criterion excludes patients with asthma or other respiratory disease, so this patient is excluded.", "n_inc_assessed": 12, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201526__NCT00967746", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 28-year-old female, but she is currently admitted for a non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy, not for contraception. There is no evidence she is healthy or in need of contraception.\n  - [not met] The patient is 28 years old, which is within the 18-40 age range, but there is no evidence she is in need of contraception; she is currently pregnant (ectopic).\n  - [not met] The patient is G1P0A0, meaning she has never given birth to a child (parity = 0).\n  - [not met] There is no information about the measured length of the uterus from external os to fundus.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is currently pregnant (ectopic pregnancy). Therefore, she does NOT meet the exclusion criterion (should not be pregnant).\n  - [not met] The patient is currently experiencing an ectopic pregnancy and has a history of infertility and right Fallopian tube adhesions, which are predisposing factors.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any history or presence of malignancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of premalignant disease of the uterus or cervix, including endometrial hyperplasia or other sex-steroid sensitive premalignancies.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active venous thromboembolic disorder.\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe hepatic disease or abnormal AST/ALT levels.\n  - [met] There is no mention of congenital or acquired malformations or distortions of the uterus or cervix.\n  - [met] There is no mention of uterine fibromyomata.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT02010294", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 5-year-old boy, which is \u22651 month and <15 years.\n  - [not met] The patient is hospitalized (in the emergency department) for a severe infection, but the note does not specify if it is invasive GAS (Group A Streptococcus) infection.\n  - [met] No known risk factors for invasive infection are described (parents deny trauma, foreign body ingestion, and no mention of immunosuppression or recent surgery).\n  - [not met] No known risk factors for invasive infection are described, so this subgroup is not met.\n  - [not met] GAS invasive infection definition requires evidence of S. pyogenes infection from a sterile site or clinical syndrome consistent with invasive GAS. The note does not provide bacteriological confirmati\n  - [not met] No bacteriological isolation of S. pyogenes from a sterile site is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No mention of bacteriological isolation from a non-sterile site or extensive soft tissue necrosis.\n  - [not met] No mention of bacteriological isolation from a non-sterile site or evocative shock syndrome.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No known immune deficiency is described.\n  - [met] No known immune deficiency is described.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20159__NCT01521403", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is 10 years old, which is less than 18 years.\n  - [not met] Patient had abdominal pain and diarrhea two weeks ago, but duration is not specified as more than 10 days.\n  - [not met] No mention of B. hominis in stool specimens.\n  - [not met] No mention of any pathogenic micro-organism identified, but also no evidence that none were found.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient has a fever of 39.5\u00b0C, which is above 37.5\u00b0C.\n  - [met] No mention of bloody diarrhoea.\n  - [met] No mention of weight loss.\n  - [not met] Patient has significant symptoms (cyanosis, periorbital edema, high fever, tachycardia, hypotension), indicating significant decrease of general condition.\n  - [met] No mention of oncological diseases.\n  - [met] No mention of immune deficiencies.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic intestinal diseases.\n  - [met] No mention of anti-protozoan drug use in the last 2 weeks.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201527__NCT02441439", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl. There is no mention of pregnancy in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The patient has very low hemoglobin (4.2 g/dL), low MCV (61.8 fL), extremely low serum iron (<1.8 umol/L), and low ferritin (2 ng/mL), all consistent with iron deficiency anemia.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about intolerance or low compliance for oral iron.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any allergy to iron supplements.\n  - [met] The anemia is due to iron deficiency, as evidenced by low iron, low ferritin, and low MCV.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any acute infection in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of liver failure or viral hepatitis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of thalassemia or hemoglobinopathies. The findings are consistent with iron deficiency anemia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of asthma.\n  - [met] The patient is not pregnant, so multiple pregnancy does not apply.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT00851487", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, which is older than the specified age range of 2 to 59 months (approximately 0.2 to 5 years).\n  - [not met] There is no mention of WHO defined non-severe pneumonia. The patient presents with knee pain, fever, and an osteolytic lesion, not respiratory symptoms.\n  - [not met] There is no information about accessibility for follow-up in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of written informed consent by a parent or legal guardian.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of pneumonia, lower chest wall retraction, or wheezing.\n  - [met] Oxygen saturation is 97%, and there is no mention of cyanosis.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to drink.\n  - [met] No mention of convulsions.\n  - [not met] The patient is described as 'increasingly lethargic,' which may indicate abnormal sleepiness or difficulty to wake.\n  - [met] No mention of severe malnutrition or oedema as defined.\n  - [met] No mention of history of wheeze or asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital heart disease, cyanosis, congestive heart failure, or cardiomegaly.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT00572715", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 6-month-old infant. There is no explicit mention of birthweight, but at 6 months of age, it is highly likely that the birthweight was >1500g, as this is below the threshold for most t\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention in the clinical note of a prenatal renal ultrasound diagnosis of severe hydronephrosis or other known renal abnormalities. The note focuses on acute kidney injury after surgery, no", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201413__NCT01604538", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with acute onset shortness of breath, tachypnea, tachycardia, and hypoxemia (O2 saturation 92%) 3 weeks postpartum, which are suggestive of possible pulmonary embolism. However, t\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 30 years old, which is above 18 years.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201523__NCT00089908", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's willingness to be followed for the duration of the study.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's willingness to use acceptable methods of contraception.\n  - [not met] The patient presents with acute illness (high fever, chills, epistaxis, severe headache, joint pain, leukopenia, increased hematocrit, thrombocytopenia), which does not indicate good general health.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of chronic clinically significant neurologic, cardiac, pulmonary, hepatic, rheumatologic, autoimmune, or renal disease is mentioned. The current illness appears acute.\n  - [met] No behavioral, cognitive, or psychiatric disease is mentioned.\n  - [not met] The patient has hematologic abnormalities (leukopenia, thrombocytopenia, increased hematocrit), which may indicate hematologic disease.\n  - [met] No mention of alcohol or drug abuse.\n  - [met] No history of severe allergic reaction or anaphylaxis is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of asthma or recent ER visit/hospitalization for asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of HIV-1 infection.\n  - [met] No mention of HCV infection.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 21}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT00948272", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is described as a 28-year-old female, which is within the 18 to 60 years age range.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about informed consent.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about ability to attend scheduled visits or comply with trial procedures.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about contraception or pregnancy avoidance.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about entitlement to national social security.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of pregnancy or positive urine pregnancy test.\n  - [met] No mention of breast-feeding.\n  - [met] No mention of participation in another clinical trial in the past 4 weeks.\n  - [met] No mention of planned participation in another clinical trial.\n  - [met] No mention of immunodeficiency, immunosuppressive therapy, chemotherapy, radiation, or corticosteroids.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to vaccine components or history of life-threatening reaction to vaccines.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic illness at a stage that could interfere with trial conduct or completion. The patient has acute symptoms but no chronic illness is described.\n  - [met] No mention of alcohol abuse or drug addiction.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 18}
{"pair": "sigir-201527__NCT02086838", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl, not a mother aged 20-35 years old.\n  - [not met] The patient is not pregnant; there is no mention of pregnancy, let alone a singleton pregnancy between 16-24 weeks.\n  - [not met] The patient has iron deficiency anemia (Hb 4.2 g/dL, MCV 61.8 fL, serum iron < 1.8 umol/L, ferritin 2 ng/mL), but her hemoglobin is below the required range (7-9 g%).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 15 years old, which is less than 20 years old and thus considered an extreme of reproductive age.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of multiple pregnancies; the patient is not pregnant.\n  - [met] The anemia is linked to iron deficiency (low Hb, low MCV, low serum iron, low ferritin).\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy to iron derivatives.\n  - [met] No evidence of diabetes, TB, hepatitis, cirrhosis, cardiovascular disease (other than anemia-related murmur), renal disease, autoimmune disease, infection, or cancer.\n  - [met] No mention of prior parenteral iron treatment.\n  - [met] No mention of obstetric complications; the patient is not pregnant.\n  - [met] No history of chronic blood loss is mentioned; fecal occult blood is negative.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT01978288", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note does not specify the mother's age, but it is reasonable to assume the mother is at least 14 years old given the context.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the mother having a physician diagnosis of asthma or being treated for asthma, nor is there information about parental atopy status.\n  - [not met] The child is 4 years old and is not being enrolled during the first week of life.\n  - [met] There is no explicit mention of signed informed consent, but the mother brought the child to the ED and is involved in care, so it is likely consent could be obtained.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note states the child has no history of wheezing or underlying lung disease.\n  - [met] No mention of respiratory complications at birth.\n  - [met] No mention of prematurity or being born before 37 weeks gestation.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital heart defects.\n  - [met] No mention of underlying neuromuscular disease.\n  - [met] No mention of severe upper airway obstruction, sleep apnea, tracheomalacia, or laryngomalacia.\n  - [met] No mention of hydrocephalus.\n  - [met] No mention of history of seizures.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT02034344", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a malar rash, alopecia, arthralgias, anemia, thrombocytopenia, positive ANA and anti-dsDNA, and renal involvement (proteinuria, RBC casts), all consistent with SLE. However, there is n\n  - [not met] There is no mention of DLE or SCLE, nor confirmation by histology. The patient appears to have SLE with a malar rash, not DLE or SCLE.\n  - [not met] The patient meets the American College of Rheumatology criteria for SLE (malar rash, hematologic disorder, renal disorder, positive ANA, positive anti-dsDNA, arthritis). She also has current positive \n  - [met] The patient has a malar rash and non-palpable purpura, which are active skin lesions that could potentially be biopsied. However, these are not specified as DLE or SCLE lesions, but as lupus erythemat\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention or suggestion of drug-induced lupus. The clinical features and serology are consistent with idiopathic SLE.\n  - [met] The patient's skin disease (malar rash, purpura) is a manifestation of lupus erythematosus.\n  - [not met] The patient has a malar rash (acute cutaneous lupus) and purpura, but no evidence of DLE or SCLE. The criterion excludes patients with ONLY acute cutaneous lupus rash. The patient does not have DLE or\n  - [not met] There is no information about anti-malarial therapy or its dosing stability.\n  - [not met] There is no information about prednisone or steroid use.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of HIV, hepatitis B, or hepatitis C serology.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201514__NCT01134432", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 27 years old, which is over 18.\n  - [met] The patient has anemia (Hb 9.0 and 8.9 g/dL), elevated LDH, elevated reticulocyte count, anisocytosis, poikilocytosis, polychromasia, and hemosiderinuria, all of which are clinical and biochemical sig\n  - [not met] The patient has a negative DAT (Coombs test), so this criterion is not met.\n  - [not met] The patient is pregnant and there is no mention of contraceptive measures. In fact, pregnancy precludes the use of contraceptives during this period.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information is provided about performance status, but there is no indication of significant functional impairment.\n  - [met] No mention of previous treatment with Rituximab.\n  - [met] No mention of other immune suppressive or anti-neoplastic treatment including prednisolone within 3 months.\n  - [met] No mention of a prior diagnosis of autoimmune haemolytic anaemia within 6 months.\n  - [met] No other serious disease is mentioned.\n  - [not met] The patient is currently pregnant, which directly meets the exclusion criterion.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication for Rituximab or hypersensitivity/allergy to murine proteins.\n  - [met] No mention of active infection requiring antibiotic treatment.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT00932425", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 72 years old, which is greater than 18 years.\n  - [met] The patient was hospitalized for cryptogenic stroke. The note does not specify the hospital, but the context suggests this is a UCSF patient.\n  - [met] The stroke occurred two weeks ago, which is within the previous 60 days.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No definite small-vessel etiology is mentioned by history or imaging; stroke is described as cryptogenic.\n  - [met] Vascular imaging (magnetic resonance angiogram) found no evidence of abnormalities or source.\n  - [met] Transesophageal echocardiogram found no evidence of abnormalities or source.\n  - [met] There is no history of atrial fibrillation reported; only occasional palpitations are mentioned.\n  - [met] Admission ECG shows normal sinus rhythm, not atrial fibrillation.\n  - [met] No atrial fibrillation detected by inpatient cardiac telemetry is mentioned; only normal sinus rhythm is reported.\n  - [met] No obvious culpable systemic illness such as endocarditis is mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability to provide written, informed consent. The patient is described as presenting and reporting symptoms, suggesting capacity.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201510__NCT01541241", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is described as having heavy, irregular periods and occasional spotting, indicating she is menstruating, but her periods are not regular.\n  - [not met] The patient is 38 years old, which is above the specified age range of 18-35 years.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hormonal treatment being taken in the last two months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of NSAID use in the last 24 hours.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient is currently pregnant.\n  - [met] The patient has pelvic pain and a history of ectopic pregnancy, but there is no mention of ovarian cysts, endometriosis, polyps, or fibrosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of present or past pelvic inflammatory disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hormonal treatment in the last two months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of NSAID use in the last 24 hours.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT00001081", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Criterion is incomplete and not assessable as written.\n  - [not met] No mention of documented HIV infection in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] No mention of intestinal cryptosporidiosis. The stool findings (ellipsoidal cysts with 2+ nuclei) are more consistent with giardiasis, not cryptosporidiosis.\n  - [not met] No information about willingness to undergo a washout phase or antidiarrheal regimen.\n  - [not met] No information about stool frequency or duration provided.\n  - [not met] Criterion is incomplete and not assessable as written.\n  - [not met] No information about average stool frequency during the 5-day screening period.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Criterion is incomplete and not assessable as written.\n  - [not met] Criterion is incomplete and not assessable as written.\n  - [met] No evidence of inability to tolerate oral medications.\n  - [met] No evidence of life expectancy less than 3 months.\n  - [not met] Patient likely has giardiasis (based on stool findings and exposure history), which is listed as an exclusion. No evidence of cryptosporidiosis.\n  - [met] No evidence of MAC disease or microsporidiosis.\n  - [not met] Criterion is incomplete and not assessable as written.\n  - [not met] No information about diary recording of medication use or bowel movements.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 19}
