{"pair": "sigir-20143__NCT00465907", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note mentions a lung mass but does not specify a histological or cytological diagnosis of non-small cell lung cancer.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of malignant pleural effusion or cytological examination of pleural fluid.\n  - [not met] No mention of stage IIIB or IV disease or malignant pleural effusion.\n  - [met] The patient is a nonsmoker, and there is no mention of secondhand smoke exposure. She fits the non-smoker, no secondhand exposure group.\n  - [met] The patient is described as having mild exertional dyspnea and is otherwise asymptomatic. This suggests ECOG PS 0-2.\n  - [met] There is a measurable left lung mass and a solitary brain mass, but no mention of malignant pleural effusion.\n  - [met] No mention of prior chemotherapy for metastatic or recurrent disease.\n  - [not met] No laboratory values are provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is mildly symptomatic and otherwise asymptomatic, suggesting ECOG PS better than 3.\n  - [met] No mention of prior chemotherapy for metastatic or recurrent disease.\n  - [met] Patient has measurable disease (lung and brain masses).\n  - [not met] No laboratory values are provided.\n  - [not met] No laboratory values are provided.\n  - [not met] No laboratory values are provided.\n  - [not met] No laboratory values are provided.\n  - [met] No history of heart failure, MI, or arrhythmia is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 14, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201419__NCT00826813", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note describes progressive dysphagia and risk factors (smoking, drinking), but does NOT mention histologically confirmed esophageal cancer.\n  - [not met] Dysphagia is present and likely caused by esophageal cancer given risk factors and symptom progression, but cancer is not explicitly confirmed.\n  - [met] There is no mention of esophageal fistulas in the note.\n  - [not met] The note does not specify inpatient status.\n  - [not met] Life expectancy is not discussed in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of esophageal fistulas.\n  - [met] No mention of tracheal compression or related symptoms.\n  - [not met] No lab values provided; cannot assess WBC or platelet count.\n  - [met] No mention of concurrent therapies after stenting.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT02390596", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy (age \u2265 3 months, weight likely \u2265 5 kg). He has had fever for 5 days and exhibits \u2265 4 of 5 main clinical signs: modification of extremities (inflammation, desquamation),\n  - [not met] No information is provided about prior treatment with IV Ig or response to standard therapy. Cannot assess.\n  - [met] The patient is 2 years old; typical weight for this age is well above 5 kg.\n  - [not met] No information about written informed consent from parent or guardian.\n  - [not met] No information about health insurance status.\n  - [met] Patient is a 2-year-old boy; contraception is not relevant for this age.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is not a preterm or neonate, and is not pregnant.\n  - [met] No evidence or suspicion of another diagnosis; clinical picture is consistent with KD.\n  - [met] Urine shows leukocytes but no bacteria; no overt bacterial infection is described.\n  - [met] No mention of prior biotherapy treatment.\n  - [met] No evidence of immunodeficiency or cancer in the note.\n  - [met] No mention of increased risk of TB infection.\n  - [met] No mention of recent or active TB infection.\n  - [met] No mention of close contact with TB patient.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
