{"pair": "sigir-201514__NCT02612558", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has anemia with elevated LDH, elevated reticulocyte count, presence of hemosiderin in urine, negative DAT, and polychromasia. These findings are suggestive of hemolytic anemia, likely auto\n  - [not met] The patient is already receiving iron supplementation for mild iron deficiency, but there is no explicit mention of prior AIHA-specific treatments (e.g., steroids, rituximab, etc.) or failure of such \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note of cold antibody AIHA, cold agglutinin syndrome, mixed type AIHA, or paroxysmal cold hemoglobinuria. The findings are more consistent with warm AIHA.\n  - [met] The patient's platelet count is 119 x 10^9/L (119,000/\u03bcL) and later 108 x 10^9/L (108,000/\u03bcL), both well above the exclusion threshold of 30,000/\u03bcL.\n  - [met] There is no mention of AIHA secondary to autoimmune disease (such as SLE) or lymphoid malignancy. The patient is pregnant, but no underlying autoimmune or lymphoid disease is described.\n  - [met] There is no information provided about the patient's blood pressure or hypertension status.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
