{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT00315042", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 5-year-old boy, which is within the age range of 6 months to less than 13 years.\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention of a clinical diagnosis of acute tonsillitis/pharyngitis caused by Streptococcus pyogenes. The symptoms described (dysphagia, drooling, fever, muffled voice, toxic appeara\n  - [not met] No information is provided about rapid detection throat swab test results or submission of a throat swab specimen.\n  - [not met] The patient has dysphagia and pain on swallowing, but the note does not specify a sore or scratchy throat. He does have at least two clinical signs (drooling, muffled voice, fever, toxic appearance), \n  - [not met] No mention of tonsil or pharyngeal erythema or exudate in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of cervical adenopathy.\n  - [not met] No mention of uvular edema.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient does not have symptoms suggestive of laryngitis, coryza, conjunctivitis, diarrhea, or cough. His symptoms are more severe and suggest a deep tissue infection.\n  - [met] No history of positive throat culture for Streptococcus pyogenes in the absence of clinical signs and symptoms of T/P is mentioned.\n  - [not met] The patient's presentation (drooling, muffled voice, toxic appearance, leaning forward) is highly suggestive of epiglottitis, which is an infection of the deep tissues of the upper respiratory tract a\n  - [met] No history of rheumatic heart disease is mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient is a 5-year-old boy, not a female of childbearing potential.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital prolonged QT syndrome.\n  - [met] No mention of hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, or bradycardia.\n  - [met] No mention of myasthenia gravis.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-20156__NCT01611896", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 46 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms and signs highly suggestive of active Graves' hyperthyroidism (weight loss, sweating, diarrhea, increased appetite, tachycardia, hyperreflexia, exophthalmia), but there is no \n  - [not met] There is no information about written informed consent in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any major co-morbidity.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous treatment with radioactive iodine.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current ATD (antithyroid drug) treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of treatment with immunomodulatory drugs.\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy to selenium or placebo pill components.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy or breastfeeding, but the patient is a woman of reproductive age.\n  - [met] There is no mention of selenium supplementation.\n  - [met] There is no information about the patient's ability to read or understand Danish.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
