{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT00416169", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has progressive memory loss, severe cognitive deficits, and memory dysfunction. However, there is no mention of a clinical diagnosis of Frontotemporal Dementia or Pick Complex, nor is ther\n  - [not met] Neuroimaging shows moderately advanced cerebral atrophy, but it does not specify frontotemporal lobar atrophy or confirm consistency with Frontotemporal Dementia or Pick Complex.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's opportunity to perform activities of daily living as described in the Alzheimer's Disease Cooperative Study -- Activities of Daily Living Inventory.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's living situation or caregiver support.\n  - [not met] No Mini Mental State Examination score or information about ability to complete baseline neuropsychometric testing is provided.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's ability to see, hear, communicate, or willingness to complete serial neuropsychometric tests.\n  - [met] The patient is a 62-year-old man, so this criterion is not applicable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a neurodegenerative disorder with severe cognitive deficits and memory dysfunction. There is no evidence of acute cerebral injuries, cerebrovascular disease, hypoxic cerebral damage, v\n  - [not met] The patient has primary memory disturbance and an amnestic syndrome, which is more compatible with Alzheimer's disease or other primary degenerative dementia, not FTD.\n  - [met] There is no mention of uncontrolled epilepsy, psychiatric disease, cardiovascular, hepatic, renal, pulmonary, metabolic, or endocrine disturbances, active peptic ulcer, or urinary outflow obstruction.\n  - [met] No information is provided about the use of agents for the treatment of dementia or cognitive impairment.\n  - [met] No information is provided about drug allergy or hypersensitivity to choli", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT00539799", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 21-year-old female, which is at least 18 years old.\n  - [met] The patient has progressive arthralgias, malaise, alopecia, malar rash, purpura, swelling and tenderness of wrists and ankles, normocytic anemia, thrombocytopenia, positive ANA and anti-dsDNA, and pro\n  - [not met] The patient has proteinuria and RBC casts, which are suggestive of active lupus nephritis, but the ISN/RPS class (III or IV) is not specified. There is no biopsy or explicit mention of proliferative l\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about current medications, including prednisolone use or dosage.\n  - [not met] There is no information about remission status or duration.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of end-stage renal failure; the patient has proteinuria and RBC casts, but no evidence of ESRD.\n  - [met] There is no information about corticosteroid use or other indications for corticosteroids.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
