{"pair": "sigir-20159__NCT00002191", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about concurrent medications other than OTC medications for viral illness. No evidence of concurrent medication relevant to study.\n  - [not met] No specific requirement is described in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] No mention of coincident enteric pathogens or treatment regimen.\n  - [not met] No information provided about allowed medications or conditions.\n  - [not met] Patient was prescribed OTC medications for viral illness, but no specific mention of antidiarrheal medications or regimen duration.\n  - [not met] No mention of concomitant medications or antiretrovirals.\n  - [not met] No specific condition is described here; unclear criterion.\n  - [not met] No mention of HIV status in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No specific co-existing conditions are described.\n  - [met] No evidence of the listed symptoms or conditions in the note.\n  - [met] WBC is elevated (25,000), no evidence of neutropenia.\n  - [met] No mention of liver disease.\n  - [met] No mention of C. difficile toxin analysis.\n  - [met] No mention of microscopic examination or positive findings for these pathogens.\n  - [met] No mention of positive cultures for these pathogens.\n  - [met] No mention of Cryptosporidium testing.", "n_inc_assessed": 12, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-20152__NCT01646645", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient must satisfy at least one of the following inclusion criteria. The patient has evidence of CMV infection (owl's eye inclusion bodies in BAL fluid), which is consistent with CMV tissue invasion\n  - [met] Patient has interstitial pneumonia (non-productive cough, fever, BAL performed), and is immunosuppressed. Owl's eye inclusion bodies are classic for CMV infection. This is a clinically documented cond\n  - [met] Owl's eye inclusion bodies in BAL fluid are microbiological evidence of CMV tissue invasion.\n  - [not met] Patient must satisfy at least one of the following additional criteria. The note does not provide information about progression, viremia, antiviral therapy, or T-cell availability.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about progression of CMV infection or viremia despite induction therapy.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about CMV viremia while receiving prophylactic antiviral drugs post-transplant.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about inability to sustain antiviral treatment due to toxicities or about CMV-specific T-cells from donor.\n  - [met] No information is provided about blood pressure or pressor support, but absence of mention of instability suggests likely stable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is on prednisone (immunosuppressive), but dose is not specified. No evidence patient is moribund or has other life-threatening conditions unrelated to CMV.\n  - [met] This criterion is about donors, not patients.\n  - [met] This criterion is about donors, not patients.\n  - [met] This criterion is about donors, not patients.\n  - [met] This criterion is about donors, not patients.\n  - [met] This criterion is about donors, not patients.\n  - [met] This criterion is about donors, not patients.\n  - [met] This criterion is about donors, not patients.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT01828749", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old (within 3-60 years) and is fully awake and alert (GCS >14 implied). She was evaluated for blunt trauma (car accident).\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention of a CT abdomen and pelvis being ordered in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is fully awake and alert, with no evidence of intubation or neurological injury.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of intoxication.\n  - [met] The patient's blood pressure is 134/74 mm Hg, which is not hypotensive for her age.\n  - [met] There is no mention of exploratory laparotomy or transfusion during ED evaluation.\n  - [met] The patient is fully awake, alert, and verbal.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a FAST exam or its results.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recent abdominal trauma or surgery in the last month.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT02263235", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about written informed consent by the patient or a trusted person.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's membership or beneficiary status in a social security system.\n  - [not met] No specific criteria for group 1 and 2B are described or referenced in the note.\n  - [not met] The patient is 89 years old, which is above the upper age limit of 85 years.\n  - [met] The patient has progressive cognitive and personality changes, with symptoms consistent with a neurodegenerative disease such as frontotemporal dementia or Alzheimer's disease.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of chronic adult hydrocephalus or need for depletion lumbar puncture.\n  - [not met] No information about specific criteria for group 2A.\n  - [not met] No evidence the patient is an adult requiring neurosurgery with CSF shunt or removal of shunt.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence the patient is deprived of liberty by judicial or administrative decision.\n  - [met] No evidence the patient is a major protected by law.\n  - [met] The patient is an 89-year-old man, so not pregnant, not a woman of childbearing age, and not breast-feeding.\n  - [met] No mention of transmissible viral diseases (HIV, hepatitis B or C).\n  - [met] No mention of inclusion in a clinical trial.\n  - [met] No evidence of inadequate cardiac, hepatic, or severe renal dysfunction. Cardiac rhythm is irregular but no mention of dysfunction.\n  - [met] No evidence of disease of amino acid metabolism (e.g., Leucinose).", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
