{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT01147640", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 48-year-old male, which is within the 18 to 90 years age range.\n  - [met] Patient has a ruptured liver abscess, which is an intraabdominal abscess (including liver) with evidence of intraperitoneal infection.\n  - [met] Patient underwent exploratory laparotomy and surgical drainage of the abscess, which is a surgical intervention.\n  - [not met] No information about preoperative enrollment or preoperative radiographic evidence; patient had ultrasound and surgery, but not clear if enrolled preoperatively.\n  - [not met] No information about prior antibacterial treatment or culture results.\n  - [not met] No information about willingness or ability to comply with study procedures.\n  - [not met] No information about willingness or ability to provide written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is male.\n  - [met] Patient does not have abdominal wall abscess, small bowel obstruction, ischemic bowel disease without perforation, or other listed conditions. Primary etiology is infectious (liver abscess).\n  - [met] Patient does not have simple cholecystitis, gangrenous cholecystitis without rupture, simple appendicitis, cholangitis, or pancreatitis.\n  - [met] No evidence that cIAI is managed by staged abdominal repair, open abdomen, or that source control is not likely to be achieved. Surgical drainage was performed.\n  - [not met] No information about pathogen resistance to meropenem.\n  - [met] No explicit statement about likelihood of survival, but no evidence suggesting imminent death.\n  - [met] Patient is acutely ill (hypotension, tachycardia, ICU admission), but no explicit diagnosis of rapidly-progressing disease or immediately life-threatening illness such as acute hepatic failure, respir\n  - [not met] No information about need for concomitant systemic antibacterial agents.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 23}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT01131312", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient had a pap smear with cytology negative and HPV positive. There is no mention of ASCUS or LSIL diagnosis.\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old.\n  - [met] The patient is alert, oriented, and presents to clinic to discuss results, suggesting ability to give informed consent and likelihood of follow-up.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous hysterectomy and the patient is undergoing pap smears, which suggests an intact cervix.\n  - [met] There is no history of excisional or ablative treatment of the cervix mentioned, and the patient has no previous medical history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy and the patient reports no complaints.\n  - [met] There is no mention of HIV positivity and the patient has no previous medical history.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
