{"pair": "sigir-201423__NCT00531791", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of heavy smoking, chronic cough, shortness of breath, barrel-shaped chest, cyanosis, and hyperinflation on chest x-ray, all of which are classic features of COPD. Although th\n  - [met] The patient is described as a heavy smoker. While the exact pack-year history is not provided, 'heavy smoking' in a 63-year-old man is likely to meet the 15 pack-year threshold.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of spirometry or previous respiratory tests showing irreversible obstruction (FEV1/FVC, FEV1, or bronchodilator response).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no history of asthma or atopy mentioned in the note.\n  - [not met] The patient is being assessed at admission, suggesting hospitalization is required.\n  - [met] There is no mention of oral or intravenous steroid use within the preceding 30 days.\n  - [not met] The patient has diabetes, which is explicitly listed as an exclusion criterion.\n  - [not met] The patient is using home oxygen, indicating oxygen-dependent COPD.\n  - [met] There is no mention of high-dose Advair or Symbicort use.\n  - [met] There is no mention of known cardiac arrhythmia.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201510__NCT01840124", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as having severe premenstrual and menstrual pelvic pain, heavy, irregular periods and occasional spotting between periods, indicating she is premenopausal and has had at least\n  - [met] The patient is 38 years old, which is older than 21 years.\n  - [not met] The patient has heavy, irregular periods and pelvic pain, which are symptoms associated with fibroids, but there is no explicit mention of fibroids in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's desire for surgical management of fibroids.\n  - [not met] There is no information about uterine size.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the size or number of fibroids or imaging results.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the number of fibroids or imaging results.\n  - [not met] There is no information about Pap smear history.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of infertility treatment but there is no mention of planned treatment for infertility.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pedunculated fibroids.\n  - [met] There is no mention of intracavitary (FIGO Type 0) fibroids.\n  - [met] There is no mention of symptomatic fibroids being only FIGO Type 1.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a planned concomitant surgical procedure.\n  - [met] There is no mention of Essure or any other metallic, implantable device within the pelvis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pelvic infection within the last 3 months.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201427__NCT01725490", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 21 years old and has a strong family history of multiple colonic adenomas, with siblings diagnosed with hundreds of colonic adenomas and undergoing proctocolectomy. The patient himself \n  - [met] The patient has FAP (based on family history and his own findings) and is found to have dozens of colonic polyps (adenomas) on sigmoidoscopy.\n  - [met] The patient has dozens of small colonic polyps, which implies at least five or more polyps of 2mm or more in diameter on endoscopic examination.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient has had a colectomy or is scheduled for one. Only his siblings have had proctocolectomy.\n  - [met] There is no evidence or mention of malignant disease or colorectal cancer in the patient. All biopsied polyps were benign adenomas.\n  - [met] There is no mention of NSAID or aspirin use, diabetes mellitus, pregnancy, abnormal lab results, or significant infectious/respiratory diseases. The note does not provide this information, but there i", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT02328872", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 32-year-old female (within 25-69 age range) with a cervix (implied by pap smear), attending for routine cervical screening. No explicit mention of Australian residency or birth date, \n  - [met] No information is provided about previous enrollment in the Compass Pilot or follow-up management for a previous abnormality. However, the patient is attending for routine screening and there is no in\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous total hysterectomy. The patient had a pap smear, which implies the presence of a cervix.\n  - [met] The patient reports no complaints and is in general good health. There are no symptoms or signs for which cervical cancer must be excluded.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cervical cancer or current treatment for it.\n  - [met] There is no information indicating the patient is currently enrolled in the Compass Pilot Study.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT00979199", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is an 82-year-old woman with chest pain and ST-segment elevations, but coronary angiography showed no stenosis or clinically significant disease. She has risk factors (hypertension, hyperc\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 82 years old, which is older than 75 years.\n  - [met] No evidence or mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] Echocardiogram shows 'mildly impaired' LV systolic function, not LVEF < 35%.\n  - [met] Probability of CAD is not explicitly stated, but angiography showed no significant disease. However, the patient has multiple risk factors and symptoms. The probability is likely not low or high, but \n  - [not met] Presentation is consistent with possible acute coronary syndrome (chest pain, ST elevations, elevated troponin), but angiography showed no CAD. However, the diagnosis of ACS cannot be excluded.\n  - [met] Duration of chest pain is not specified.\n  - [met] No mention of de novo or accelerated angina.\n  - [met] No evidence of hemodynamic or electrical instability; BP is high but stable, EKG shows sinus tachycardia.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 26}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT00313365", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has had knee pain for 4 days, which is less than or equal to two weeks.\n  - [met] The infection involves the knee, which is one of the specified joints.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a positive gram stain or culture of synovial fluid, nor is there a synovial fluid WBC count provided.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of synovial fluid or blood cultures, nor of prior antibiotic therapy.\n  - [met] Only the right knee is involved, indicating monoarticular arthritis.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of gonococcal infection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a prosthetic joint.\n  - [met] There is an osteolytic lesion, which may suggest osteomyelitis, but it is not stated that osteomyelitis preceded the joint infection. The timeline and presentation suggest acute joint symptoms first.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a fatal illness or that septic arthritis is incidental in such a context.\n  - [not met] The patient is 10 years old, which is 17 years or less.\n  - [met] Only the right knee is involved, so this is not polyarticular arthritis.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201528__NCT00339157", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of SO-JIA (systemic onset juvenile idiopathic arthritis) is mentioned. The patient presents with fever, joint pain, and swelling, but there is no explicit diagnosis or mention of corticos\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of SO-JIA (Edmonton's revision) is mentioned. The symptoms could be consistent with SO-JIA, but there is no explicit diagnosis.\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old, which is within the required age range (2-20 years).\n  - [not met] Disease duration is not specified as at least 6 months; symptoms have been present for only two days.\n  - [not met] No information about corticosteroid treatment or failure/requirement is provided.\n  - [not met] There is evidence of active arthritis (tender, swollen knee, fever, elevated WBC and SRP), but insufficient detail to confirm at least 3 of Giannini's core-set items. Number of affected joints and spe\n  - [not met] CRP and ESR are mentioned as elevated, but it is not clear if this is in the absence of disease-related fever. The patient currently has fever.\n  - [not met] No information about polyarthritis (at least 5 joints) or radiological evidence of joint damage.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of previous treatment with IL-1Ra.\n  - [met] No mention of intra-articular injection or recent changes in NSAIDs/corticosteroids.\n  - [met] No mention of treatment with other immunosuppressive or disease-modifying drugs.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to anakinra, ongoing infection (other than possible joint infection), or allergy.\n  - [met] No history of malignancy or heart insufficiency is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of need for urgent therapeutic intervention.\n  - [met] No laboratory values are provided that would indicate abnormal counts or liver/renal function.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-20151__NCT00152399", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 44-year-old male (at least 18 years old). He is suspected to have a bleeding episode, likely from peptic ulcer (PU), given the 'coffee ground' vomiting, which is classic for upper GI \n  - [met] The patient has haematemesis ('coffee ground' vomiting) observed by the clinical team in the emergency room.\n  - [met] The patient has documented signs of hypovolemia: tachycardia (HR 135), hypotension (BP 70/40), decreased mental status, and cool extremities.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of treatment with somatostatin, its analogues, vasoactive drugs, or endoscopic therapy for the present bleeding episode.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any treatment with PPIs (IV or oral) within the last 48 hours preceding randomisation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of treatment (endotherapy or pharmacotherapy) for upper GI ulcer bleeding in the last 30 days.\n  - [not met] There is no information about platelet count, INR, prothrombin time, or aPTT. Cannot assess.\n  - [met] There is no mention of anticoagulant therapy (vitamin K antagonists or heparin including LMW heparins).\n  - [met] There is no mention of terminal stage illness or contraindication to endoscopy.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20143__NCT01421316", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a solitary mass in the right frontal lobe on CT scan, which is likely a brain metastasis given the context of a lung mass. However, the note does not explicitly state that the brain ma\n  - [met] The patient is 58 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note regarding informed consent.\n  - [not met] RPA class is not specified. RPA class III typically refers to patients with poor performance status (KPS < 70). The patient is described as otherwise asymptomatic with unremarkable neurologic exam, su\n  - [not met] The patient likely fits RPA class I-II (good performance status), but only has a solitary brain mass, not >3 brain metastases.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of small cell lung cancer or prophylactic WBRT. The lung mass is not specified as small cell.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous whole brain radiotherapy in the note.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201512__NCT00619203", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 44-year-old man, not a child. The inclusion criterion specifies 'all children aged \u2265 2 months'. Therefore, the patient does not meet this criterion.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 44 years old, which is much older than two months. Therefore, he does NOT have age less than two months.\n  - [not met] The patient was recently in an automobile accident and sustained a skull fracture, which is trauma. Therefore, he DOES have trauma.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an intracranial shunt, previous neurological disease, cerebral palsy, or Down's syndrome in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous permanent hearing loss in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of immunosuppression (except HIV infection) in the note.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201518__NCT00523757", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has shortness of breath on exertion, orthopnea (difficulty breathing when lying flat), uses extra pillows at night, and has physical findings of bibasilar crackles, pitting edema, and jugu\n  - [not met] There is no mention of any hospital admission for heart failure in the provided note.\n  - [met] The patient has symptoms with exertion and orthopnea, which is consistent with at least NYHA Class II or III.\n  - [not met] No echocardiographic data is provided in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information about renal function or creatinine clearance is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about potassium levels is provided.\n  - [met] No mention of recent acute coronary syndrome.\n  - [met] No mention of any planned procedures.\n  - [met] No mention of previous intolerance to aldosterone antagonists.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT00015626", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as obese and is 64 years old, which is well above 5 years of age. Adult obesity is defined as BMI > 27, and the note explicitly states 'obese.'\n  - [met] The patient has diabetes mellitus, which is a complication of insulin resistance. However, the note does not mention specific complications such as acanthosis nigricans, dyslipidemia, elevated blood p\n  - [not met] There is no information about siblings or parents, nor about documented insulin resistance in the index subject via OGTT/IVGTT. The patient herself has diabetes, but this criterion is about including \n  - [not met] There is no mention of family history of type II diabetes in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence the patient is critically ill, or has congestive heart failure, renal or liver insufficiency.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability to give consent. The patient is described as reluctant and non-compliant, but not unable to consent.\n  - [not met] The patient is described as 'not compliant with her diabetes medication or exercise,' which is a history of poor compliance with physician's recommendations.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT00002191", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information about concurrent medication is provided.\n  - [not met] No specific required criteria are described in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of coincident enteric pathogens or their treatment.\n  - [not met] No information about allowed medications.\n  - [not met] No mention of antidiarrheal medication use or regimen stability.\n  - [not met] No mention of other concomitant medications or regimen stability.\n  - [not met] No specific requirements listed; unclear.\n  - [not met] No mention of HIV status in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of co-existing conditions.\n  - [met] No mention of listed symptoms or conditions.\n  - [met] No mention of grade 4 neutropenia.\n  - [met] No mention of decompensated liver disease.\n  - [met] No mention of C. difficile toxin analysis.\n  - [not met] Microscopic examination revealed cysts consistent with Giardia lamblia (ellipsoidal cysts with 2+ nuclei), so patient likely has Giardia lamblia.\n  - [met] No mention of positive cultures for Shigella, Salmonella, Yersinia, or Campylobacter.\n  - [met] No mention of Cryptosporidium fluorescent antibody test.", "n_inc_assessed": 12, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT02387281", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No evidence in the note of a diagnosis of Parkinson's Disease (PD) by United Kingdom Brain Bank criteria. The described symptoms (progressive memory loss, jerking movements, severe cognitive deficits,\n  - [not met] No mention of Hoehn & Yahr stage or PD diagnosis. The patient does not appear to have PD.\n  - [not met] No mention of levodopa treatment or response. The patient does not appear to have PD.\n  - [not met] No information about dopaminergic medication or ability to manage 12 hours off it.\n  - [met] Patient is 62 years old, which is within the 18-85 years range.\n  - [not met] No mention of freezing of gait (FOG) by history or exam. Jerking movements are described, but not FOG.\n  - [not met] No information about ability to sign consent or willingness to participate.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindications for MRI (e.g., pacemaker, claustrophobia).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] This is a header criterion for PD subjects with FOG. The patient does not have PD or FOG.\n  - [not met] Patient has severe cognitive deficits and memory dysfunction, likely amounting to dementia that would preclude completing study protocol.\n  - [met] No evidence of PD or Hoehn & Yahr stage V. The patient does not have PD.\n  - [met] No history of FOG described.\n  - [met] No evidence of atypical parkinsonism (PSP, MSA, CBD, Vascular Parkinsonism). The findings are more consistent with a prion disease or other neurodegenerative disorder.\n  - [met] No mention of treatment with medications that cause parkinsonism.\n  - [not met] Jerking movements may interfere with gait, but no explicit mention of a neurological or orthopedic disorder interfering with gait.\n  - [met] No mention of treatment with medications that interfere with NET-PET ligand binding.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 19}
{"pair": "sigir-20149__NCT00358761", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about enrollment in protocol 02-I-0055.\n  - [met] The patient is 43 years old, which is above the minimum age of 14.\n  - [not met] The patient has multiple small, soft, pedunculated lesions on the neck, largest 4 mm, described as flesh colored to slightly hyperpigmented. There is no mention of an acute annular, erythematous, expa\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a tick bite, tick exposure, or relevant travel history.\n  - [not met] There is no information about consent to storage of biologic samples.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is at increased risk from skin biopsy or has immunodeficiency.\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [met] The lesions are on the neck, which would exclude the patient from the skin biopsy portion if the patient otherwise met the case definition. However, the patient does not meet the case definition for E", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT00461760", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 32 year old female, which is within the 25-65 age range. She is attending a clinic for routine cervical screening (pap smear). There is no explicit mention of registration with Medica\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The patient has no previous medical history, and there is no mention of invasive cervical cancer.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient having had a hysterectomy or not having a cervix. She had a pap smear, which implies presence of a cervix.\n  - [met] There is no mention of HIV positivity or immunosuppressive treatments, and the patient is described as in general good health with no previous medical history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability or unwillingness to give informed consent.\n  - [met] There is no mention of treatment for moderate or greater dysplasia within the last 5 years, and the patient has no previous medical history.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT01533285", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The clinical note does not provide information about the patient's height or weight, so BMI cannot be calculated. However, the patient is described as a young female college student with no significan\n  - [not met] The patient is a 20-year-old female. The inclusion criteria require female participants to be 25-45 years old for young healthy or remitted MDD patients, or \u226565 years old for elderly healthy participa\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any DSM-IV axis I diagnosis other than MDD. The patient has symptoms suggestive of depression but no other psychiatric diagnoses are described.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any recent psychosocial stressor within the past 6 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of acute symptoms of suicidality.\n  - [met] There is no mention of substance abuse or dependence within the past 6 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of exposure to experimental medication or medical device within 90 days before screening.\n  - [met] Laboratory tests are described as within normal limits, and there is no mention of positive serology for hepatitis B, C, or HIV.\n  - [met] There is no mention of exposure to typhoid or typhoid vaccine within 5 years before screening.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior exposure to the Trier Social Stress Test (TSST).", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-20153__NCT02258958", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is over 18.\n  - [met] The patient is male. Either gender is allowed.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of lung cancer or metastatic lung disease in the note.\n  - [not met] The patient underwent a right total hip replacement, not any of the listed lung surgeries.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's competence to consent.\n  - [met] The note is about a patient.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of allergy or anaphylactic reaction to contrast dye, heparin, or LMWH.\n  - [met] No mention of current anticoagulation therapy.\n  - [met] No mention of renal impairment or creatinine clearance.\n  - [met] No mention of liver disease, ascites, or peritoneal tapping.\n  - [met] The patient is male, so cannot be pregnant.\n  - [met] No mention of VTE diagnosis or treatment in the past 3 months prior to surgery.\n  - [met] No mention of increased risk of hemorrhage.\n  - [met] No mention of history of heparin induced thrombocytopenia.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201422__NCT01925014", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents to the ER with abdominal pain, localized to the right lower quadrant, with rebound tenderness and ultrasound findings of an edematous appendix. These are classic symptoms and sign\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the note of a request for intravenous contrast-enhanced CT examination. Only an abdominal ultrasound is described.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about willingness to provide telephone or cell phone numbers for follow-up.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about signed informed consent prior to study entry.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The only imaging test mentioned is an abdominal ultrasound. There is no mention of prior cross-sectional imaging tests (such as CT or MRI) to evaluate the presenting symptoms.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a prior history of surgical removal of the appendix. The ultrasound shows an edematous appendix, which would not be present if the appendix had been removed.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20159__NCT02105714", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old child (aged 1-18 years) who had abdominal pain and diarrhea for at least two weeks prior to presentation, as described in the note. The abdominal pain and diarrhea were pe\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about written informed consent being provided. This cannot be determined from the available data.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is tachycardic, hypotensive, and tachypneic, with cyanosis and marked periorbital edema, which may indicate severe illness. However, there is no explicit mention of immediate intensive or \n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's or guardian's willingness or ability to provide written informed consent. This cannot be determined from the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of clinical jaundice or observation of the conjunctivae in the physical exam findings. Therefore, this exclusion criterion is met.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is unable to comply with study requirements. This cannot be determined from the note, but there is no evidence against compliance.\n  - [met] There is no mention of participation in other diagnostic studies or clinical trials.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT02284984", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 21 years old, which is >= 18 years.\n  - [met] Patient has clinical features (malar rash, arthralgias, anemia, thrombocytopenia, positive ANA and anti-dsDNA, proteinuria, RBC casts) consistent with ACR criteria for SLE.\n  - [met] Patient has nephritis (proteinuria, RBC casts) and thrombocytopenia, which are considered severe SLE flares.\n  - [met] SLEDAI score is not explicitly provided, but the presence of nephritis, thrombocytopenia, and other symptoms likely results in a SLEDAI >= 12.\n  - [met] Patient has nephritis (proteinuria, RBC casts) and thrombocytopenia, both of which are new or worse SLE-related activity of major organs.\n  - [not met] No information about prior immunosuppressive treatment or refractory disease.\n  - [not met] No information about failure of initial induction treatment or switching therapy.\n  - [not met] No information about intolerance or contraindication for cyclophosphamide or MMF.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of active pregnancy or positive beta-HCG.\n  - [met] No information about B-cell counts.\n  - [met] No information about IgG levels.\n  - [met] No information about recent live vaccine immunization.\n  - [met] No mention of active infection.\n  - [met] No mention of recent hospitalization for infection.\n  - [met] No mention of recent parenteral antibiotics.", "n_inc_assessed": 22, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT00163774", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient suffered a traumatic brain injury (fall with head strike) and has a Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) of 6/15, which is less than 9, indicating a severe head injury.\n  - [not met] The patient has a GCS < 9, but there is no mention of an intracranial pressure monitor in situ or CT scan evidence of the listed findings. In fact, CT scan was deferred. Therefore, this criterion is n\n  - [met] The patient was transferred to the emergency department within half an hour after the fall, indicating enrollment within the first 48 hours after trauma.\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old, which is younger than the required age range of 17-70 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note that the patient had a cardiac arrest at or after the trauma scene.\n  - [met] On arrival, the patient's pupils were asymmetrical, not fixed bilaterally and dilated >4mm, and GCS is 6 (not 3).\n  - [met] There is no mention of coagulopathy or contraindication to surgery.\n  - [met] There is no statement that there is no chance of survival; immediate treatment was initiated.\n  - [met] There is no mention of lower limb or pelvic trauma.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201410__NCT00667381", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 67-year-old woman, which is over 18 years old.\n  - [met] The patient underwent cardiac catheterization via the right femoral artery, which is consistent with a retrograde femoral approach for left heart catheterization or peripheral arterial angiography.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's willingness or ability to sign a consent form.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the procedure was performed by an operator trained in the ultrasound technique.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Access was via the right femoral artery, which is the common femoral artery site.\n  - [met] The patient has loss of distal pulses, but the note does not specify whether the femoral pulses themselves are nonpalpable. The access site is the femoral artery, and a pulsatile mass is present in th\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's creatinine or dialysis status.\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient is a prisoner.\n  - [met] The patient is a 67-year-old woman, but there is no information about pregnancy. Given the age, pregnancy is highly unlikely.\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's ability or willingness to sign a consent form.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient underwent emergent cardiac catheterization for ST segment elevation myocardial infarction or unstable acute coronary syndrome.\n  - [met] No information is provided about equipment availability.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT00656097", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is not free of obvious health problems; she has neck and shoulder pain, paresthesias, tremors, spasticity, and later developed severe symptoms including spastic arm movements, agitation, h\n  - [met] The patient is a 28-year-old female, which falls within the age range of 19 to 65 years.\n  - [not met] BMI is not mentioned in the clinical note. Cannot assess.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior history of rabies immunization (active or passive).\n  - [not met] The patient has clinically significant acute illness (severe neurological symptoms, hydrophobia, hospitalization) within the past 2 weeks.\n  - [met] No history or family history of immunodeficiency or autoimmune disease is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of anaphylaxis or hypersensitivity reaction is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic administration of immunosuppressants or immune-modifying drugs.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT00451620", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a diagnosis of diabetes mellitus with persistently elevated HbA1c, which strongly suggests type 2 diabetes of more than 3 months duration, as type 1 would likely be specified and the a\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 64-year-old obese female, so she is female.\n  - [not met] The patient is 64 years old, which is not over 65.\n  - [not met] The patient is not compliant with her diabetes medication, which implies she has been prescribed medication and is not diet controlled only.\n  - [not met] The patient has persistently elevated HbA1c, but the exact value is not given. However, 'persistently elevated' suggests it is likely above 8.5%.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is not compliant with her diabetes medication, which means she has been prescribed oral hypoglycemic agents or insulin. This meets the exclusion criterion.\n  - [met] There is no mention of anemia or hemoglobin levels in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking medications known to interfere with glucose metabolism.\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy to glyburide, sulfa drugs, GlucoNorm, or impaired liver function.\n  - [met] There is no mention of impaired renal function or serum creatinine levels.\n  - [met] There is no mention of participation in another clinical trial within the past 30 days.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201526__NCT00260091", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 28-year-old female with a 3-year history of infertility (failure to conceive after one year of unprotected intercourse).\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the male partner's semen analysis.\n  - [not met] Patient has at least one ovary and had minor right Fallopian tube adhesions cauterized. No explicit confirmation of a patent tube, but laparoscopy was performed and no mention of hydrosalpinx or previ\n  - [not met] No mention of endometriosis.\n  - [not met] No information about uterine cavity evaluation.\n  - [not met] No information about ovulatory status or response to ovulation induction medications.\n  - [not met] No information about ovarian reserve labs (FSH, E2, TSH, prolactin).\n  - [not met] Patient is described as obese, but no BMI value is given. Cannot confirm BMI \u2264 38.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient had pelvic laparoscopy with minor adhesions cauterized; no evidence that pelvis was not restored to functional.\n  - [met] No mention of hydrosalpinx.\n  - [met] Laparoscopy showed minor adhesions, which were cauterized. No mention of endometriosis or inability to restore pelvis to normal.\n  - [met] Current admission is for non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy. No mention of prior ectopic pregnancies or nonfunctional tubes.\n  - [not met] No information about male factor infertility or semen analysis.\n  - [met] No mention of previous IUI, IVF, or gonadotropin treatment.\n  - [not met] No information about FSH or estradiol levels.\n  - [met] No mention of GIFT, ZIFT, or TET procedures.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT01911702", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presented with acute abdominal pain, underwent emergency abdominal surgery (exploratory laparotomy for ruptured liver abscess), and upon arrival in ICU had signs of bad perfusion (dehydrat\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic renal failure or dialysis treatment in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of Acute Coronary Syndrome within the past 12 months or NYHA class > 3.\n  - [met] The patient was taken to the ICU after surgery, implying resuscitative measures are being provided. There is no indication that the patient was judged not subject to resuscitative measures.\n  - [met] There is no mention of massive hemorrhage or transfusion of >5 units of erythrocyte concentrates in the operative or perioperative period.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is scheduled for orthotopic liver transplantation.\n  - [met] The patient is 48 years old, which is older than 18 years.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT00851487", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is 8 years old, which is outside the specified age range of 2 to 59 months (approximately 0.16 to 4.9 years).\n  - [not met] Patient presents with respiratory distress and bilateral lung infiltrates, which may indicate severe pneumonia rather than non-severe pneumonia per WHO definitions.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about accessibility for follow-up.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent by a parent or legal guardian.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is in respiratory distress, which may indicate severe pneumonia, but there is no mention of lower chest wall retraction or wheezing.\n  - [met] No mention of cyanosis in the clinical note.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to drink.\n  - [met] No mention of convulsions.\n  - [met] No mention of abnormal sleepiness or difficulty waking.\n  - [met] No mention of severe malnutrition or oedema.\n  - [met] No mention of previous history of 3 or more episodes of wheeze or asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital heart disease, cyanosis, congestive heart failure, or cardiomegaly.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT02317913", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has 5 days of high fever, bilateral conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue (oral changes), inflammation and desquamation of hands and feet (changes of peripheral extremities), and cervical lymp\n  - [met] The patient has had a high fever for 5 days.\n  - [met] Physical exam reveals conjunctivitis, which is likely bilateral as per typical KD presentation, though not explicitly stated.\n  - [met] The patient has a strawberry tongue, which is a change of lips and oral cavity.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of polymorphous exanthema (rash) in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The patient has inflammation of the hands and feet and desquamation of the skin of the fingers and toes, which are changes of peripheral extremities.\n  - [met] The patient has acute nonpurulent cervical lymphadenopathy with the smallest node at 1.5 cm.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient meets the recruited criteria as described above.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201527__NCT00535561", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has clinical and laboratory evidence of iron deficiency anemia: Hb 4.2 g/dL (very low), MCV 61.8 fL (microcytic), serum iron < 1.8 umol/L, ferritin 2 ng/mL (all consistent with iron defici\n  - [met] There is no mention of swallowing difficulties or inability to swallow tablets. The patient is a 15-year-old girl with no reported issues that would prevent tablet swallowing.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The anemia is described as iron deficiency anemia with no evidence of other causes (multifactorial or other reasons). Fecal occult blood is negative, and no other etiology is mentioned.\n  - [met] Although the anemia is severe (Hb 4.2 g/dL), there is no mention of cardiac ischemia, acute/subacute blood loss, or GI/GU malignancy. The patient is symptomatic but stable, so urgent intervention for \n  - [met] There is no mention of prior thyroid disorder or treatment history in the note.\n  - [met] No other co-morbid diseases (renal insufficiency, coronary heart disease, hypertension, diabetes, or other endocrine diseases) are mentioned. The only findings are related to anemia.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT02449928", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute abdominal pain, fever, dehydration, hypotension (BP 80/40), tachycardia (HR 132), and a ruptured liver abscess. These findings are consistent with septic shock (infecti\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 48-year-old male. There is no indication that the patient is pregnant or a nursing mother.\n  - [met] The patient has a ruptured liver abscess and hepatomegaly, but there is no mention of severe liver failure or Child class C cirrhosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient using Linezolid.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pheochromocytoma in the patient's history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hematologic malignancy in the patient's history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient using epinephrine.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient undergoing CVVH (continuous venovenous hemofiltration) treatment.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201422__NCT01376466", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl presenting with classic symptoms of acute appendicitis (abdominal pain migrating to the right lower quadrant, localized rebound tenderness, and ultrasound showing a m\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 15 years old, which is under the age of 18 years. For exclusion criteria, 'met' means the patient does NOT have the condition described. Since she IS under 18, this exclusion criterion \n  - [met] The patient denies having had sexual partners and her menses are regular, making pregnancy extremely unlikely.\n  - [met] There is no mention of uncooperativeness, senile dementia, or mental illness. The patient appears to be cooperative.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's language abilities or whether she speaks Danish.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the patient wishes to participate.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201410__NCT01600482", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 67-year-old woman, which is over 18 years of age.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about consent or willingness to participate.\n  - [not met] The patient underwent cardiac catheterization via the right femoral artery, which is an intra-arterial procedure involving access through the common femoral artery. However, the sheath size (6F-7F) is\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information about allergies to device materials.\n  - [met] No mention of severe acute non-cardiac systemic disease or terminal illness.\n  - [met] No evidence of systemic bacterial or cutaneous infection, including groin infection, is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of coagulopathy or low platelet count.\n  - [met] No mention of thrombolytic agent use or fibrinogen levels.\n  - [not met] Sheath size is not specified, so cannot confirm if it was smaller than 6F or greater than 7F.\n  - [met] No mention of participation in another investigational device or drug study.\n  - [met] No mention of severe claudication, significant stenosis, or prior bypass/stent at access site.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 27}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT02443389", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 6-month-old infant, but there is no information about whether he was born or admitted to a level 2 or 3 NICU.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the duration of intravenous fluid administration (>48 hours).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 6 months old, so if admitted to the NICU at 2 weeks of age or older, this would apply. However, there is no information about the age at NICU admission.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cardiovascular surgery for congenital heart lesion within 1 week of life.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a lethal anomaly diagnosed upon admission.\n  - [met] The patient is 6 months old, so did not die within 48 hours after birth.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201413__NCT02616991", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a woman who gave birth 3 weeks ago (within 6 weeks postpartum), presents with acute shortness of breath, tachypnea, tachycardia, and low oxygen saturation, which are suggestive of clini\n  - [met] There is no mention of any contraindication to iodinated contrast (no history of allergy, renal insufficiency, or hyperthyroidism).\n  - [met] The patient is 30 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no information about health insurance status.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the possibility of 3-month follow-up.\n  - [not met] There is no information about written informed consent or ability to give consent, but the patient is alert and apprehensive, suggesting capacity.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of anticoagulation therapy for any reason.\n  - [met] The patient gave birth 3 weeks ago and there is no mention of a new pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of contrast medium extravasation during injection.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of CTA or CTV being performed or not according to study requirements.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT00178711", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient suffered a non-penetrating brain injury (fall from bike, struck temple) and has a post-resuscitation GCS of 6/15 (which is <8). The motor score is not explicitly stated, but GCS 6/15 impli\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old, which is not between 16 and 45 years old.\n  - [met] The timeline indicates the child was transferred to the ED within 30 minutes after the fall, so the time of injury is within 2.5 hours of arrival.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has GCS 6, not 7 or 8, and no CT scan was performed. Thus, this exclusion does not apply.\n  - [met] The patient does not have GCS 3 (GCS is 6), so this exclusion does not apply.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any other body area injury or AIS > 4 for any body area except head.\n  - [met] No abdominal ultrasound or CT scan was performed, and there is no mention of abdominal injury.\n  - [met] On arrival, blood pressure was 155/98, which is not hypotensive. No mention of persistent hypotension.\n  - [met] No mention of hypoxia or O2 saturation < 94%.\n  - [met] The patient is an 8-year-old boy, so pregnancy is not possible.\n  - [met] The injury occurred less than 2.5 hours before hospital arrival.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT02559310", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 31-year-old male, which is at least 18 years of age.\n  - [not met] No information is provided regarding informed consent or willingness to adhere to study procedures.\n  - [met] Patient has an acute illness of 7 days duration with at least 3 symptoms consistent with lower respiratory tract infection: productive cough, chest pain, fever, chills, and worsening cough.\n  - [not met] No mention of dyspnea (shortness of breath) in the note.\n  - [met] Patient has a new or increased cough (productive and worsening).\n  - [met] Patient has productive cough, which suggests purulent sputum production.\n  - [met] Patient has chest pain aggravated by coughing, which is consistent with pneumonia-related chest pain.\n  - [met] Patient has at least 2 vital sign abnormalities: fever (103.4\u00b0F) and tachycardia (pulse 105).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information on prior antibacterial use is provided.\n  - [met] No information on requirement for concomitant systemic antibacterial therapy is provided.\n  - [met] No information on recent hospitalization or residence in a nursing home/long-term care facility is provided.\n  - [met] No evidence of infection with resistant or non-community acquired pathogens; presentation is consistent with community-acquired infection.\n  - [met] No evidence of noninfectious cause of pulmonary infiltrates; presentation is consistent with infection.\n  - [met] No mention of pleural empyema.\n  - [met] No mention of requirement for mechanical ventilation.", "n_inc_assessed": 18, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT01858194", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 82 years old, which is \u2265 18 years.\n  - [met] The patient has segmental left ventricular dysfunction and a history of MI-like presentation (chest pain, elevated troponin, wall motion abnormalities), which qualifies as structural heart disease.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a planned catheter-based ablation of VT.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of an existing ICD.\n  - [not met] The patient has renal-artery stenosis, but accessibility of renal vasculature is not directly addressed. Renal angiography was performed, but no explicit statement about accessibility.\n  - [not met] The patient has dementia, which likely impairs her ability to understand study requirements.\n  - [not met] The patient has dementia, which likely impairs her willingness/ability to adhere to study restrictions and follow-up.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presented with acute MI-like symptoms (chest pain, elevated troponin, ST elevations) and wall motion abnormalities, suggesting a recent MI, possibly within 30 days.\n  - [met] No mention of recent or prior CABG.\n  - [not met] The patient has known renal-artery stenosis, which is a renovascular abnormality that would preclude RSDN.\n  - [not met] The patient has chronic renal insufficiency, but GFR is not provided. Cannot determine if GFR <30 ml/min.\n  - [met] No explicit mention of life expectancy <1 year, but the patient is elderly with multiple comorbidities. However, no direct evidence for <1 year.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to anticoagulation.\n  - [not met] The patient has dementia, which likely impairs her ability to give informed consent.\n  - [met] The patient is an 82-year-old woman; no mention of pregnancy or recent HCG testing. Pregnancy is extremely unlikely.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT00524238", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms highly suggestive of hypothyroidism (cold intolerance, fatigue, constipation, hyporeflexia, dry skin, slow movements and speech). However, there is no explicit mention of a ne\n  - [not met] The patient is not a healthy control; she has multiple symptoms consistent with hypothyroidism.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy or breastfeeding. The patient is a 56-year-old female, which makes pregnancy or breastfeeding unlikely but not impossible. However, based on available information, the", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-20141__NCT01604655", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with episodic chest pain and mild dyspnea, and was admitted to the ER for evaluation. The description suggests she is being evaluated for possible acute coronary syndrome.\n  - [met] The patient is 58 years old, which is \u226545 years.\n  - [met] The EKG shows nonspecific changes, which is considered non-diagnostic for acute coronary syndrome.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of troponin I results in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence or mention of ST elevation myocardial infarction.\n  - [met] There is no evidence or mention of non-ST elevation myocardial infarction.\n  - [met] The patient denies a history of heart disease and there is no mention of known coronary artery disease.\n  - [not met] Serum creatinine is not mentioned in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of atrial fibrillation or marked irregular heart rhythm.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient's heart rate cannot be controlled.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of allergies to iodinated contrast agents.\n  - [met] The patient is a 58-year-old woman, but there is no mention of pregnancy. At this age, pregnancy is highly unlikely.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
