{"pair": "sigir-201514__NCT00842621", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has anemia (Hb < normal), elevated reticulocyte count, elevated LDH, presence of hemosiderin in urine, anisocytosis, poikilocytosis, polychromasia, and negative DAT. These findings are con\n  - [not met] There is no mention of sickle cell disease or any hemoglobinopathy consistent with SCD (e.g., HbSS, HbSC, HbS/\u03b2-thalassemia).\n  - [met] The patient has hemolysis, but the specific cause is not stated. There is no mention of RBC membranopathies, enzymopathies, unstable hemoglobinopathies, or PNH. However, the presence of hemolysis and \n  - [not met] This criterion is for SCD participants only. The patient does not have SCD.\n  - [met] The patient is 27 years old, which is above 5 years of age. This criterion is met.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous cardiac surgery in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of left ventricle dysfunction or shortening fraction < 28%.\n  - [met] There is no mention of right sided congenital heart defect such as atrial septal defect or pulmonary valve stenosis.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201523__NCT00458120", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about previous vaccination with rDEN1delta30, rDEN2/4delta30(ME), or rDEN4delta30 vaccine.\n  - [not met] The patient is presenting with acute illness (high fever, chills, etc.), which suggests he is not currently in general good health.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's availability for the duration of the study.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness to use contraception.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has abnormal laboratory findings (leukopenia, thrombocytopenia, increased hematocrit) and is acutely ill, but there is no mention of chronic or clinically significant neurologic, heart, lu\n  - [met] No mention of behavioral, cognitive, or psychiatric disease.\n  - [not met] The patient has abnormal laboratory values (leukopenia, thrombocytopenia, increased hematocrit).\n  - [met] No mention of medical, work, or family problems due to alcohol or illegal drug use.\n  - [met] No mention of history of severe allergy or anaphylaxis.\n  - [met] No mention of severe asthma or recent ER visits/hospitalizations for asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of HIV infection.\n  - [met] No mention of Hepatitis C infection.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 18}
{"pair": "sigir-201519__NCT01313494", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note regarding the patient's willingness to sign a written informed consent.\n  - [met] The patient has a significant smoking history, chronic cough, progressive shortness of breath, barrel chest, and wheezing, all of which are consistent with COPD according to GOLD guidelines.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ethnicity in the note.\n  - [met] The patient has had a chronic cough for the past two years, indicating COPD symptoms for at least 12 months.\n  - [not met] There is no spirometry data (FEV1/FVC ratio) provided in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no FEV1 value provided in the note.\n  - [met] The patient has smoked 1-2 packs per day for 47 years, which is well over 10 pack years. Current smoking status is not explicitly stated, but the history supports at least the pack-year requirement.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a recent COPD exacerbation or ongoing antibiotic treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a recent lower respiratory tract infection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of asthma diagnosed before age 40 or other relevant lung diseases besides COPD.\n  - [met] There is no mention of participation in a pulmonary rehabilitation program.\n  - [met] There is no mention of alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT00857701", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note states 'extremely limited range of motion' of the right knee, which implies reduced flexibility in active range of motion (AROM) of knee extension.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of pain being specifically worsened by bending over with straight legs. This detail is not provided.\n  - [not met] The note does not mention the patient's gait or any impairment in walking.\n  - [not met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy. Ability to understand informed consent and experiment responsibilities is not addressed, and at this age, it is unlikely he can provide informed consent himself.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no history of trauma and imaging shows an osteolytic lesion, not a fracture.\n  - [not met] The patient has fever, joint effusion, limited range of motion, and lethargy, all of which are highly suggestive of knee sepsis (septic arthritis).\n  - [not met] Imaging shows an osteolytic lesion, fever, and local symptoms, which are highly suggestive of osteomyelitis or orthopedic infection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of extensor mechanism dysfunction (e.g., patellar tendon rupture, quadriceps tendon rupture).\n  - [met] There is no mention of psoriasis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of knee joint neuropathy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous stroke or brain injury.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201528__NCT00065806", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of SLE (systemic lupus erythematosus) or meeting ACR criteria for SLE in the note. The patient presents with joint pain, fever, and a history of tick bite, but these are not suffic\n  - [met] The patient is an 8-year-old boy. While his exact weight is not given, the average weight for an 8-year-old boy is around 25-30 kg. It is reasonable to assume he likely meets this criterion.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inpatient admission or hospitalization. The context suggests an outpatient evaluation.\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old and likely able to complete self-report questionnaires in English, as the note is in English and there is no mention of language barriers.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness to comply with a recommended diet.\n  - [met] The patient is an 8-year-old boy, so contraception is not applicable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of drug-induced lupus.\n  - [met] There is no mention of liver disease or abnormal liver enzymes.\n  - [met] There is no mention of myositis or elevated CK.\n  - [met] There is no mention of IMT imaging or inability to obtain adequate images.\n  - [met] There is no mention of tacrolimus or cyclosporine use.\n  - [met] There is no mention of dialysis or elevated serum creatinine.\n  - [met] There is no mention of nephrotic syndrome, proteinuria, or low serum albumin.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cholesterol levels.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT00315549", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is 5 years old, which is less than 13 years.\n  - [not met] Patient is a boy (male), so female-specific criteria do not apply.\n  - [not met] Patient is male, so premenarchal or surgically incapable of bearing children does not apply.\n  - [not met] Patient is male, so childbearing potential criteria do not apply.\n  - [not met] Patient is male, so menstrual flow criteria do not apply.\n  - [not met] Patient is male, so pregnancy test criteria do not apply.\n  - [not met] Patient is male, so contraception criteria do not apply.\n  - [not met] No mention of clinical diagnosis of acute tonsillitis/pharyngitis caused by Streptococcus pyogenes. Presentation is more consistent with possible epiglottitis (leaning forward, drooling, muffled voice\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Symptoms do not suggest laryngitis, coryza, conjunctivitis, diarrhea, or cough. Presentation is more consistent with epiglottitis.\n  - [met] No history of positive throat culture for Streptococcus pyogenes in absence of clinical signs and symptoms.\n  - [not met] Symptoms (leaning forward, drooling, muffled voice, toxic appearance) are classic for epiglottitis, which is an infection of deep tissues of the upper respiratory tract. This is an exclusion criterion\n  - [met] No history of rheumatic heart disease mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital prolonged QT syndrome.\n  - [met] No mention of hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia, or bradycardia.\n  - [met] No mention of impaired renal function.\n  - [met] No mention of myasthenia gravis.", "n_inc_assessed": 13, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-201519__NCT01248507", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about signed informed consent.\n  - [met] Patient is 66 years old, which is \u2265 40 years.\n  - [met] Patient has chronic cough, significant smoking history, progressive shortness of breath, barrel-shaped chest, and wheezing, all classic signs of COPD. GOLD stage is not explicitly stated, but symptoms\n  - [met] Patient has smoked 1-2 packs per day for 47 years, which is well above 10 pack-years.\n  - [not met] The note describes progressive shortness of breath and moderate respiratory distress, but does not explicitly state an acute exacerbation of COPD (AECOPD).\n  - [not met] No information about hospital admission due to AECOPD.\n  - [not met] No information about confirmed AECOPD at GP or treatment with oral corticosteroids/antibiotics.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has a significant smoking history; has smoked for 47 years.\n  - [met] No evidence of other active long-term respiratory diseases (e.g., asthma, cystic fibrosis, malignancy, etc.) in the note.\n  - [met] No mention of exacerbation due to pneumothorax or acute decompensated congestive heart failure.\n  - [met] No mention of communication difficulties.\n  - [met] No evidence of severe disease with poor vital prognosis (life expectancy <1 year) in the note.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT00264901", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a diagnosis of diabetes mellitus and persistently elevated HbA1c. However, the exact HbA1c value is not provided, nor is it specified to be <= 12.0% within the past 12 months. Given th\n  - [not met] The patient is described as obese, but no BMI value is given. Obesity can include BMI > 45, but without specific data, we cannot confirm BMI <= 45.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of initiation, addition, change, or continuation of basal insulin therapy with insulin detemir. The patient is non-compliant with diabetes medication, but the specific medication i\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of anticipated changes in medications known to interfere with glucose metabolism.\n  - [met] There is no mention of proliferative retinopathy or maculopathy requiring acute treatment within the last 6 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being on any glucose lowering medication not indicated in combination with insulin, such as GLP-1 analogues.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypoglycemia unawareness or recurrent major hypoglycemia.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201412__NCT01276782", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 25-year-old woman, which fits the age range (18-45). There is no mention of pregnancy or gestational age, so it is unclear if she is pregnant or before 14 weeks of gestation. There is\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is already on levothyroxine. However, the patient is likely hypothyroid based on symptoms and exam, and if discovered to be hypothyroid, she would need levothyroxi", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT00630513", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is an adult (48 years old) who required surgical intervention (exploratory laparotomy and drainage) within 24 hours for a ruptured liver abscess, which is a localized intra-abdominal infec\n  - [not met] There is no mention of acute appendicitis or ruptured/perforated appendicitis with abscess.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of acute diverticulitis with perforation or abscess.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of acute cholecystitis or rupture/perforation of the gallbladder.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of acute gastric or duodenal perforation.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of traumatic perforation of the intestines.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of secondary peritonitis due to perforated viscus; the primary issue is a ruptured liver abscess.\n  - [met] The patient has an intra-abdominal abscess (liver abscess) that ruptured and was surgically drained.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of traumatic bowel perforation requiring surgery within 12 hours.\n  - [met] There is no mention of gastroduodenal ulcer perforation requiring surgery within 24 hours.\n  - [met] The primary etiology is infectious (liver abscess), not a non-infectious process.\n  - [met] The patient is a 48-year-old male, not pregnant or lactating.\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy, hypersensitivity, or severe reaction to study antibiotics.\n  - [met] There is no mention of rapidly progressive or terminal illness; the patient has CVID but no evidence of terminal disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe hepatic or renal disease (e.g., creatinine clearance < 0.5 ml/min/1.73 m2). Hepatomegaly is noted, but no evidence of severe hepatic dysfunction.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a concomitant infection that would interfere with evaluation of response to study antibiotics.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-20145__NCT02375919", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute onset of shortness of breath (dyspnea), which is a qualifying symptom.\n  - [met] There is no explicit mention of a high clinical pretest probability of PE; the patient has risk factors (recent surgery, immobility), but the note does not state a high suspicion or clinical gestalt. \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No other obvious cause for dyspnea or chest pain is mentioned. The surgical site is healing well, and there are no signs of infection or bleeding.\n  - [met] The presentation is not described as acute severe (e.g., no mention of shock, respiratory failure, or hemodynamic instability).\n  - [met] There is no mention of any contraindication to CTPA (e.g., contrast allergy, renal failure).\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being on anticoagulation treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a current diagnosed thrombo-embolic event.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting inability to follow up.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is a prisoner.\n  - [met] The patient is a 56-year-old female, but there is no mention of pregnancy.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT01689350", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient meets at least 4 of the 11 ACR criteria for SLE (malar rash, arthritis, hematologic disorder, renal disorder, positive ANA, positive anti-dsDNA).\n  - [met] The patient has a rash mainly distributed on the bridge of her nose and her cheeks, consistent with a malar rash.\n  - [not met] No mention of discoid rash (red, scaly patches causing scarring) in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of serositis, pleurisy, or pericarditis.\n  - [not met] No mention of oral or nasopharyngeal ulcers.\n  - [met] The patient has swelling and tenderness of wrists and ankles, consistent with nonerosive arthritis of two or more peripheral joints.\n  - [not met] No mention of photosensitivity or rash/symptoms triggered by UV light.\n  - [met] The patient has normocytic anemia and thrombocytopenia, both hematologic disorders seen in SLE.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of poor compliance.\n  - [met] No mention of lupus mental damage, epilepsy, or inability to express symptoms.\n  - [met] No mention of drugs affecting cytochrome P450 enzymes.\n  - [met] No mention of abnormal liver function.", "n_inc_assessed": 15, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT01666093", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 72 years old, which is above 18.\n  - [not met] No mention of admission to university hospitals of Geneva or non-healing lower limb ulcer.\n  - [not met] No mention of non-healing lower limb ulcers for more than 3 months.\n  - [not met] No mention of hospitalization in Dermatology inpatient clinic.\n  - [not met] No mention of thin skin autograft at ulcer level.\n  - [not met] No mention of complete angiological diagnostic work-up.\n  - [not met] No mention of baseline ABI, toe pressure, or tcPO2 measurements.\n  - [not met] No mention of non-invasive arterial imaging (angio-CT or angio-MRI).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of refusal to give written informed consent.\n  - [met] No angiological work-up results or evidence of CLI (no ankle pressure < 50mmHg, toe pressure < 30mmHg, tcPO2 < 20mmHg).\n  - [met] Patient has symptoms and signs suggestive of PAD (calf pain on exertion, diminished pulses, cool extremities), so likely does not have normal ABI, TP, or tcPO2.\n  - [met] No mention of another reversible cause of non-healing ulcer.\n  - [met] No mention of treatable venous insufficiency, inflammatory/infectious process, or mechanical factors.\n  - [met] Diminished pulses and cool extremities suggest significant arterial lesions.", "n_inc_assessed": 24, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201424__NCT02071290", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 33 years old, which is \u226516 years.\n  - [met] Patient suffered blunt trauma to the left hemi-abdomen from a bike fall.\n  - [met] Patient is in hemorrhagic shock: BP 60/30 mmHg, HR 140/min, pale, extended intraperitoneal hemorrhage.\n  - [met] Systolic BP is 60 mmHg, which is \u226490 mmHg.\n  - [met] Identified source of blood loss: spleen rupture with intraperitoneal hemorrhage.\n  - [not met] No explicit mention of blood products being ordered, but patient is in hemorrhagic shock and likely to require transfusion. Uncertain.\n  - [not met] No information about admission to St. Michael's Hospital or time since injury (injury was a week ago, not within 3 hours).\n  - [not met] No information about Remote Ischemic Conditioning (RIC) application or timing.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is male, not pregnant.\n  - [met] Shock is hemorrhagic, not non-hemorrhagic.\n  - [met] No mention of burns.\n  - [met] No mention of fractures or traumatic amputation of both lower extremities.\n  - [met] Patient has vital signs and is not dead or undergoing CPR.\n  - [met] No mention of injury in both legs.\n  - [met] Systolic BP is 60 mmHg, not above 200 mmHg.\n  - [met] No mention of anticoagulant, antiplatelet, steroid use, or bleeding disorder.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201527__NCT02631668", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl (female). Her Hb is 4.2 g/dL (42 g/L), which is well below 110 g/L. Her MCV is 61.8 fL (<80 fL). Serum ferritin is 2 ng/mL (well below 12 ng/mL). Serum iron is <1.8 u\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is not pregnant (no evidence of pregnancy in a 15-year-old girl, and not mentioned). No drug allergy is mentioned. No evidence of serious gastrorrhagia, peptic ulcers, active bleeding, hep", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT01748162", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 4 year old boy, which is within the 6 months to 15 years age range.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of 2 or more episodes of croup in a 12 month period. In fact, there is no history of wheezing prior to this episode.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of inspiratory stridor, barking cough, or respiratory distress. The patient had a brief cough and is now wheezing, but is playful and well-appearing with normal O2 sats.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of subglottic stenosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of subglottic hemangioma.\n  - [met] There is no mention of posterior laryngeal cleft.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recurrent respiratory papillomatosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of external compression or mediastinal mass.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of epiglottitis, bacterial tracheitis, or supraglottic foreign body. However, the sudden onset after playing in a sandbox raises the possibility of a foreign body, but this is not \n  - [met] There is no mention of tracheomalacia or bronchomalacia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current steroid therapy.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT00912990", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 4 years old, which is between 6 months and 17 years.\n  - [met] The patient is a 4 year old boy (male).\n  - [met] The note is in English and there is no indication of a language barrier.\n  - [met] There is no mention of abnormal airway or Mallampati classification issues.\n  - [met] The child is described as playful and well appearing, suggesting ASA I or II, but not explicitly stated.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of an elective surgical procedure; the patient presented to the ED for acute symptoms.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent/assent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 4 years old, which is not <6 months or >17 years.\n  - [met] No evidence of a difficult airway or abnormal Mallampati classification.\n  - [met] No history of difficult intubation or suspected abnormal airway.\n  - [met] No mention of facial trauma.\n  - [met] No mention of airway tumor.\n  - [met] No mention of epiglottitis.\n  - [met] No mention of retropharyngeal abscess.\n  - [met] No mention of foreign body, though sudden onset after coughing could suggest it, but not confirmed.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201415__NCT00190918", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a differential diagnosis of vesicular mole (a form of gestational trophoblastic disease), but there is no explicit mention of persistent or recurrent low risk GTT. The diagnosis is not\n  - [not met] There is no information about a WHO score or risk assessment for gestational trophoblastic disease.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of histologically confirmed complete or partial mole on initial evacuation. The diagnosis is only suspected based on ultrasound and clinical findings.\n  - [not met] There is no information about renal insufficiency, NSAID use, or pemetrexed administration.\n  - [not met] There is no information about NSAID use or pemetrexed administration.\n  - [not met] There is no information about folic acid supplementation or pemetrexed therapy.\n  - [not met] There is no information about Vitamin B12 supplementation or pemetrexed therapy.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous chemotherapy treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of metastatic lesions.\n  - [met] There is no mention of metastases to liver, spleen, brain, kidney, or GI tract.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT00104663", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 89 years old, which meets the age requirement (12+). The clinical note describes rapidly progressive dementia, myoclonus, paratonic rigidity, and behavioral changes, which are highly su\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is alert and oriented to self and city, though not year, and is interacting with the examiner. There is no mention of coma or pre-terminal phase, and the note does not suggest that prolong\n  - [met] There is no mention of quinacrine sensitivity or allergy in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking any other putative anti-prion therapy, so we assume this exclusion does not apply.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201411__NCT01653587", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with excruciating right arm pain, but there is no mention of chest pain, ischemic symptoms, ECG changes, or cardiac enzyme results. The presentation is not clearly compatible with\n  - [not met] There is no information about the intention to submit the patient to early invasive strategy (coronary angiography/PCI) within 72 hours.\n  - [not met] No information is provided regarding informed consent.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about eligibility for transradial/transfemoral coronary angiography or PCI, or the operator's familiarity/agreement.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 40 years old.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic use of anticoagulants.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to antiplatelet or anticoagulant drugs.\n  - [met] No evidence of active bleeding or high bleeding risk. No mention of liver failure, peptic ulcer, renal failure, or thrombocytopenia.\n  - [met] The patient's blood pressure is low (80/60), not hypertensive.\n  - [not met] The patient is hypotensive and tachycardic, which could suggest shock, but there is no explicit diagnosis of cardiogenic shock. The etiology of shock is unclear.\n  - [met] No history of previous myocardial revascularization surgery.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201429__NCT00301353", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note does not explicitly state the patient is 'healthy' as assessed by any method, but she is seeking advice on osteoporosis prevention and has hypertension and diet-controlled diabetes. Unclear i\n  - [not met] No health and lifestyle questionnaire results are provided.\n  - [not met] No physical examination results are provided.\n  - [not met] No pre-study laboratory test results are provided.\n  - [not met] The patient's ethnicity is not stated.\n  - [met] She is postmenopausal within the last year, which is within the 12-60 month window.\n  - [not met] Interview is not documented, but menopause status is confirmed.\n  - [not met] FSH level was measured and used to confirm menopause, but the actual value (\u226520 IU/l) is not provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of recent participation in clinical trials.\n  - [met] No mention of recent participation in non-invasive clinical trials.\n  - [met] She is seeking advice on osteoporosis prevention, not treatment; no diagnosis of osteoporosis.\n  - [met] No history of spontaneous bone fractures or use of osteoporosis medication is mentioned.\n  - [met] No DXA scan results are provided.\n  - [met] No mention of scoliosis.\n  - [not met] No history of medical or surgical events that may affect study outcome is mentioned, except hypertension and diabetes (see below).\n  - [met] Menopause was determined by labs, not surgery.", "n_inc_assessed": 14, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-20152__NCT02136797", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient must satisfy at least one of the following criteria. Assessment will depend on subsequent criteria.\n  - [met] Patient has interstitial pneumonia (suggested by cough, fever, and BAL findings) and is immunosuppressed. Owl's eye inclusion bodies in BAL fluid are classic for CMV infection.\n  - [met] BAL fluid examination reveals owl's eye inclusion bodies, which is microbiological evidence of CMV tissue invasion.\n  - [met] Patient must also satisfy at least one of the following criteria. Assessment will depend on subsequent criteria.\n  - [not met] No information provided about progression of CMV infection or persistence/increase of viremia despite two weeks induction therapy.\n  - [not met] No information provided about development of CMV viremia while receiving prophylactic antiviral drugs post transplant.\n  - [not met] No information provided about inability to sustain antiviral treatment due to drug toxicities.\n  - [met] Patient must meet clinical criteria for CMVpp65-CTL infusions. Assessment will depend on subsequent criteria.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is on prednisone, but dose is not specified. Cannot confirm if dose is \u2265 0.3 mg/kg.\n  - [met] Patient is admitted but not described as moribund.\n  - [met] No mention of other life-threatening conditions unrelated to CMV infection.\n  - [met] Patient is male, so cannot be pregnant.", "n_inc_assessed": 16, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT01197183", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with classic symptoms and physical findings of hypothyroidism (cold intolerance, fatigue, constipation, hyporeflexia, dry skin, slow movements/speech). However, there is no explic\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient giving oral consent for participation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information indicating the patient is currently or recently (last 3 months) participating in a clinical trial.\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note that the patient is at risk of being unable to follow up (no mention of moving, other study, or short-term life-threatening pathology).\n  - [met] There is no mention of any contraindications to L\u00e9vothyrox (levothyroxine).", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT02561208", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 32-year-old woman, which meets the age and gender requirement. There is no information about whether she lives in a household visited by Community Health Workers (CHWs), so this part \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous HPV test; the current note refers to her 'most recent pap smear' with HPV testing, but no prior HPV test is documented.\n  - [met] The patient had a cytology negative result and is in general good health, with no mention of precancerous lesions or cervical cancer.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of mental disability.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT01161849", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient being in the post operative period of abdominal surgery (elective surgery of colon-rectum, ileum, stomach, or pancreas). The patient was admitted after a car acciden\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient having undergone an urgent laparotomy. The patient is described as being in the ER after trauma, but no surgery is documented.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient being in the post operative period or having signs of sepsis. The patient is alert, with normal vital signs, and no fever or other signs of sepsis are described.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient being in the post operative period or having signs of systemic hypoperfusion. Blood pressure and pulse are within normal limits.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of liver surgery.\n  - [met] There is no mention of abdominal drainage or drainage of bile, blood, or dejection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of sepsis or systemic hypoperfusion due to an extraabdominal infection site.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201523__NCT01080989", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is described as presenting to the ER with acute symptoms, not as a healthy volunteer from the community. There is no information about willingness to join the study or informed consent.\n  - [met] The patient is a hospital case with symptoms (high fever, chills, headache, joint pain, leukopenia, thrombocytopenia) and recent travel to Asia, which are suspicious for malaria, leptospirosis, or fla\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of inadequate or missing blood or stool samples. The clinical note specifically mentions blood count results, implying adequate blood sampling.\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient's personal information is fake or unidentifiable. The patient is described with age, gender, and clinical details.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201527__NCT01757119", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl, not a woman aged 18-45 years old. She does have iron deficiency anaemia, but does not meet the age requirement.\n  - [not met] Her haemoglobin is 4.2 g/dL (42 g/L), which is below the required range of 85-105 g/L.\n  - [met] Her serum ferritin is 2 ng/mL (2 \u00b5g/L), which is less than 15 \u00b5g/L.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the timing of her menstruation cycle or pharmacokinetic evaluation.\n  - [met] Her mother assures she is well fed, which may suggest a standard diet, but this is not explicitly stated.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Anaemia is due to iron deficiency (low Hb, low MCV, low serum iron, low ferritin). No evidence of other causes such as inflammatory anaemia, marrow failure, haemopathy, haemoglobinopathies, haemolytic\n  - [met] No evidence of haemochromatosis or iron overload. No mention of blood transfusions.\n  - [met] No mention of long-term treatment known to modify iron absorption.\n  - [met] No mention of gastro duodenal ulcer.\n  - [met] No mention of inflammatory bowel disease or any digestive disease.\n  - [met] No mention of fructose intolerance, malabsorption syndromes, or sucrase-isomaltase deficiency.\n  - [met] No evidence of serious or progressive disease (cardiac, pulmonary, hepatic, renal, haematological, malignancy, autoimmune, infectious, or neuropsychiatric disorders) except for iron deficiency anaemia\n  - [met] No mention of recent or planned surgery.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201429__NCT00578981", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 51-year-old woman who was documented to be in menopause within the last year. This meets the criterion of being a female, post-menopausal woman aged 50 to 90.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a bone mineral density (BMD) evaluation or a T-Score in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about a follow-up appointment with a provider in Family Medicine, Primary Care Internal Medicine, or POM.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any major barriers to participation in shared decision-making (e.g., severe hearing impairment, dementia, need for interpreter). The patient is actively seeking advice and appea\n  - [met] Enrollment is open to females of diverse racial backgrounds. The patient is female; no information suggests she is excluded based on race.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is currently taking a bisphosphonate.\n  - [not met] There is no information regarding the patient's availability for a 6 month follow-up phone call.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT00915928", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the note of a diagnosis of chronic subdural hematoma or a need for surgical evacuation. The patient has altered consciousness and a history of trauma, but the only imaging menti\n  - [met] The patient is 85 years old, which is over 18 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting lack of compliance.\n  - [met] There is no mention of kidney artery stenosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of aortic stenosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of kidney function or renal impairment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy, intolerance, or contraindication to ACE inhibitors.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current ACE inhibitor treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of coagulopathies.\n  - [met] There is no mention of malignant disorders.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201530__NCT00398242", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has dislocation of both the ulna and radius at the elbow, but there is no mention of a fracture of both forearm bones (radius and ulna).\n  - [not met] The patient is 47 years old, which is older than 16 years.\n  - [met] The clinical note describes dislocation of both the ulna and radius from the humerus.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the stability of the injury.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention that the fracture/dislocation is older than 1 week; the presentation appears to be acute.\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent.\n  - [met] There is no mention of this being a refracture.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an open fracture; the note only describes dislocation and does not mention any open wounds.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT01231945", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note states the patient has no previous medical history and there is no mention of a prior cervical cancer diagnosis.\n  - [met] The patient is a 32-year-old female who had a pap smear, which requires a cervix.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy, and the patient reports no complaints and is in good health.\n  - [met] The patient is in general good health, had a recent pap smear, and there is no indication of physical inability to undergo screening or provide consent.\n  - [met] The criterion clarifies that previous cervical cancer screening is not an exclusion, and the patient had a recent pap smear.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient never having had sexual intercourse or having had a total hysterectomy. She had a pap smear, implying she has a cervix.\n  - [met] There is no history of cervical cancer reported.\n  - [met] The patient is in good health, had a recent pap smear, and there is no indication of inability to undergo screening or provide consent.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current or recent pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient currently menstruating.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201424__NCT02261584", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of liver cirrhosis in the clinical note. The patient presented with splenic rupture and intraperitoneal hemorrhage, but no evidence of chronic liver disease or cirrhosis.\n  - [not met] The patient has a ruptured spleen with hemorrhage, but there is no mention of hypersplenism (which is typically characterized by splenomegaly and cytopenias).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is an athlete and there is no mention of poor performance status. Despite acute illness, baseline performance is likely good.\n  - [met] No evidence of hepatic encephalopathy or ascites is mentioned in the note.\n  - [met] No mention of esophageal variceal bleeding; the bleeding is intraperitoneal due to splenic rupture.\n  - [met] No mention of bone marrow findings or cytopenias; nothing suggests hypocellular BM.\n  - [met] No mention of renal failure or abnormal renal function.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201427__NCT02113202", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a family history of hundreds of colonic adenomas in siblings and is found to have dozens of small colonic polyps (all benign adenomas) himself. However, the patient does NOT have more \n  - [met] The patient is 21 years old, which is within the 18 to 70 years age range.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about written informed consent.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's potential for follow-up.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any medical or psychiatric conditions that would compromise the patient's ability to give informed consent.\n  - [met] The patient has not undergone proctocolectomy; only his siblings have.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a MutYH mutation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any concurrent uncontrolled medical conditions.\n  - [met] The patient is a 21-year-old male college student, so this criterion does not apply.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201514__NCT00726544", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 27-year-old woman, so female.\n  - [met] The patient is 27 years old, which is between 18 and 75.\n  - [met] Diagnosis of TMA is not explicitly stated, but the patient has anemia, thrombocytopenia, elevated LDH, negative DAT, and schistocytes are not mentioned. There is evidence suggestive of TMA but not def\n  - [not met] Thrombocytopenia is defined as platelet count <100 x 10^9/L. The patient's platelet counts are 119 and 108, both above 100.\n  - [met] Microangiopathic hemolytic anemia: The patient has negative DAT, elevated LDH, elevated reticulocyte count, anisocytosis, poikilocytosis, polychromasia, and hemosiderinuria, all supporting hemolysis. \n  - [met] No alternative explanation for thrombocytopenia and anemia is given (DIC, eclampsia, HELLP, Evans syndrome are not mentioned).\n  - [not met] The patient is pregnant (11 weeks gestation), so she is not non-pregnant.\n  - [met] Not applicable, patient is female.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is pregnant (11 weeks gestation).\n  - [met] No history of bleeding diathesis or active abnormal bleeding is mentioned.\n  - [met] No disseminated malignancy or co-morbid illness limiting life expectancy is mentioned.\n  - [met] No alternative diagnosis (DIC, HELLP, Evans) is given.\n  - [met] Diagnosis of DIC is not verified by labs; clotting screen is normal.\n  - [met] No information about recent treatment and relapse.\n  - [met] No information about plasma exchange.\n  - [met] No information about splenectomy.", "n_inc_assessed": 15, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT02439996", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with classic signs and symptoms of Kawasaki Disease (KD): prolonged high fever, conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue, extremity changes, desquamation, cervical lymphadenopathy, and c\n  - [met] The patient is 2 years old, which is within the required age range of 1 month to 12 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the clinical note about informed consent being signed.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about whether the patient received treatment prior to this encounter.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient receiving hormones or other immunosuppressive agents.\n  - [met] There is no information about whether informed consent was refused.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT02116361", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient reports fatigue, increased sleep and appetite, difficulty concentrating, anhedonia (no longer enjoys spending time with friends), and feelings of guilt. These symptoms are consistent with \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior treatment with botulinum toxin of any serotype for any reason in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of use of antidepressant medication for depression within 2 weeks of study in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of Myasthenia gravis, Eaton-Lambert Syndrome, or Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis. The patient has no significant past medical history.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT02590653", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided regarding informed consent.\n  - [not met] Patient has dementia, which may impair mental ability to participate in the study.\n  - [not met] Patient is 82 years old, which is outside the 35-65 year age range.\n  - [met] Patient has ST-segment elevations on ECG and elevated troponin T and CK-MB, consistent with STEMI.\n  - [not met] Coronary angiography showed no stenosis or clinically significant disease, so there is no hemodynamically relevant stenosis of one artery.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No history of repeat or recurrent myocardial infarction is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of chronic heart failure (NYHA III-IV) is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of left ventricular hypertrophy on echocardiography.\n  - [met] No QRS duration is provided.\n  - [met] Ejection fraction is not specified, but overall LV systolic function is described as 'mildly impaired', suggesting EF is likely above 40%.\n  - [met] Coronary angiography showed no stenosis or clinically significant disease.\n  - [met] No mention of type 1 diabetes mellitus.\n  - [met] No mention of type 2 diabetes mellitus or insulin therapy.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 22}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT02357498", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has amenorrhea and elevated prolactin, which suggests a functioning pituitary adenoma (likely prolactinoma), not a nonfunctioning macroadenoma. There is no mention of a pituitary macroaden\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, which is within the 18-80 years range.\n  - [met] There is no mention of medical instability or contraindications to surgery. The patient appears medically stable.\n  - [met] There is no evidence to suggest the patient would not be able to complete the study or follow-up. She is motivated to become pregnant and is actively seeking care.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is a prisoner.\n  - [met] Urine hCG is negative, so the patient is not pregnant.\n  - [not met] The patient has elevated prolactin and galactorrhea, which are signs of a functioning pituitary adenoma (prolactinoma).\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability to obtain MRI or contraindications such as pacemaker, anaphylaxis to gadolinium, or low GFR.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pituitary apoplexy (acute symptoms, headache, vision changes, etc.).", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT02359643", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy with 5 days of high fever, conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue, inflammation and desquamation of hands/feet, and cervical lymphadenopathy, which fulfills the American Hea\n  - [met] The patient has had fever for exactly 5 days (not >5 days), but has 4 of 5 principal symptoms (conjunctivitis, mucosal changes, extremity changes, lymphadenopathy). The fever duration is borderline, b\n  - [met] The patient has a strawberry tongue, which is a sign of diffuse mucosal inflammation.\n  - [met] Physical exam reveals conjunctivitis, and there is no mention of purulent discharge, so bilateral non-purulent conjunctivitis is likely present.\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention of dysmorphous skin rashes, but desquamation of the skin of the fingers and toes is noted, which is a skin manifestation of KD. However, dysmorphous rash is not directly s\n  - [met] Inflammation of the hands and feet is described, which may correspond to indurative angioedema, but this is not explicitly stated.\n  - [met] Cervical lymphadenopathy is present with the smallest node at 1.5 cm, meeting the criterion.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient fulfills the Kawasaki Disease criteria.\n  - [met] The patient has had fever for 5 days, not <5 or >10 days.\n  - [met] The clinical note provides data for CBC, liver enzymes, albumin, ESR, CRP, and echocardiography, suggesting complete data collection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of IVIG treatment at another hospital before referral.\n  - [met] There is no mention of corticosteroid treatment in the previous 2 weeks.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any disease known to mimic Kawasaki disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous diagnosis of Kawasaki disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability to take aspirin.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201422__NCT00435032", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has clinical signs and imaging findings consistent with appendicitis (abdominal pain localizing to the right lower quadrant, rebound tenderness, and an edematous appendix on ultrasound). H\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is unable to have usual follow up care or is transient to the area. Therefore, the exclusion criterion is considered met.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201529__NCT01440075", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 4-year-old girl presenting with classic symptoms of Kawasaki Disease (KD): persistent fever, erythematous rash, strawberry tongue, red/cracked lips, swollen red hands, and conjunctiva\n  - [not met] The patient is 4 years old, not 18 or older.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's or parents' agreement to participate in all explorations of the study.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about acceptance of genotyping.\n  - [met] No cardiovascular risk factors are mentioned in the note. The patient is a 4-year-old with no relevant history provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with classic (not atypical) KD symptoms: fever, rash, conjunctivitis, oral changes, extremity changes. No evidence of atypical KD.\n  - [met] No documented or suspected coronary ischemia is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about refusal to participate or sign consent.\n  - [not met] No information about contraindication to iodinated contrast agents (allergy, renal failure).\n  - [not met] No information about hypersensitivity to dobutamine.\n  - [met] The patient is a 4-year-old girl, prepubertal, so contraception is not applicable.\n  - [met] The patient is a 4-year-old girl, so not breastfeeding or pregnant.\n  - [not met] No information about treatment modifying endothelial reactivity.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-20159__NCT02495909", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about whether the patient is a lifelong resident of the area.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient providing at least 2 urine and 2 stool samples for parasitological examination.\n  - [not met] There is no information about blood samples being given before and after each treatment episode.\n  - [not met] There is no evidence in the note that the patient has been tested for or is negative for schistosomes, hookworm, Trichuris, and Ascaris.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of frequent contact with infective water. The patient did visit a farm, but this does not confirm water contact.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There are no clinical signs of tuberculosis or malaria described in the note.\n  - [not met] The patient is currently febrile (T: 39.5 C).\n  - [not met] The patient had a recent illness (viral illness diagnosed two weeks ago).\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous antihelminthic treatment.\n  - [not met] There is no direct evidence of helminth infection, but the patient has eosinophilia and exposure to pigs, which raises suspicion. However, infection is not confirmed.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT02276170", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 6-month-old male infant. Inclusion criterion requires neonate < 3 months post natal age. 6 months is older than 3 months.\n  - [met] The patient has urine output < 0.2 mL/kg/hr, elevated BUN (33 mg/dL), elevated creatinine (1.3 mg/dL), and urinalysis findings consistent with AKI (granular casts, RBCs). These findings support a diag\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the clinical note of the patient receiving aminophylline for AKI treatment.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of anatomical renal anomalies such as hydronephrosis, multicystic kidney, renal agenesis, renal dysplasia, polycystic kidney, or obstructive uropathy in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being on renal replacement therapy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of major genetic abnormalities (trisomy 13, 18, or 21).", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20151__NCT00164905", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has severe upper GI bleeding, evidenced by 'coffee ground' vomiting (hematemesis) and hemodynamic instability. However, there is no mention of a clean base ulcer specifically.\n  - [met] Patient's SBP is 70/40 mmHg (\u226490 mmHg) and heart rate is 135 bpm (\u2265110 bpm), both criteria are met.\n  - [not met] Patient received packed red blood cell transfusion, but the number of units and timing (within 12 hrs) is not specified.\n  - [not met] No information about hematocrit drop is provided.\n  - [not met] No mention of endoscopic confirmation or specific ulcer type.\n  - [met] Patient has acute upper GI hemorrhage (hematemesis), which could be primary or secondary.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of bleeding site from lesion other than GU, DU, pyloric or anastomotic ulcer.\n  - [met] No mention of more than one type of significant bleeding lesion.\n  - [met] No documented history of cirrhosis or portal hypertension.\n  - [met] No mention of ESRF or dialysis.\n  - [met] No mention of coagulopathy or INR.\n  - [met] No mention of platelet count.\n  - [met] No mention of aspirin or Plavix (clopidogrel) use.\n  - [met] No mention of neoplastic ulcer.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT02604576", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about signed informed consent.\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old, which is within the 18-70 years range.\n  - [not met] The patient presents with diarrhea, abdominal cramping, flatulence, greasy stools, and malaise after drinking untreated water, which is more consistent with an infectious etiology (giardiasis) rather \n  - [not met] No information is provided about the PADYQ questionnaire score.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a clinical and laboratory diagnosis of giardiasis (ellipsoidal cysts in stool, compatible symptoms and exposure).\n  - [met] No information is provided about Helicobacter pylori diagnosis.\n  - [met] No information about high digestive endoscopy or organic diseases.\n  - [met] No history of esophageal, gastrointestinal, or intra-abdominal surgery is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to formulation components.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to tartrazine yellow dye.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to aspirin.\n  - [met] No mention of use of PPIs, H2 blockers, prokinetics, antibiotics, prostaglandins, or bismuth salts in the last week.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT02051088", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 72-year-old man, which is >18 years old. There is no information suggesting unwillingness to be randomized.\n  - [met] The patient has increasing calf pain when walking uphill, which is consistent with intermittent claudication, a symptom of PAD. Physical exam shows diminished pulses and cool extremities, supporting P\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of acute thromboembolic disease in the leg. The symptoms have gradually increased over 3 months, which is more consistent with chronic PAD.\n  - [met] There is no mention of infrainguinal aneurysmal disease in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no information about previous participation in this or other randomized interventional studies of infrainguinal lesions.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's Swedish personal identification number status. This cannot be assessed from the note.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201412__NCT00360074", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No evidence of hypopituitarism affecting at least 3 axes. Symptoms and findings (fatigue, weight gain, cold intolerance, hair loss, anterior cervical mass) are more consistent with hypothyroidism, pos\n  - [not met] No mention of prior surgical or radiation treatment of pituitary tumors.\n  - [not met] BMI is not provided. The patient is described as having weight gain, but no specific height or weight is given.\n  - [not met] No mention of smoking status. Cannot determine if the patient is a non-smoker.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No history of cardiovascular or pulmonary diseases is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No information about current thyroxin dosage or use.\n  - [met] No mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] No mention of epilepsy.\n  - [met] No mention of cerebrovascular diseases.\n  - [met] The patient has a prominent, soft, uniform anterior cervical mass at the midline, which is more consistent with a diffuse goiter (e.g., due to hypothyroidism) rather than a nodular goiter. No mention ", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT00507871", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 32-year-old male. The inclusion criterion requires children aged 9-36 months. The patient is an adult and does not meet this age requirement.\n  - [met] The patient presents with diarrhea, which is defined in the criteria. However, the criteria are specific to children, and the patient is an adult. If only considering the symptom, the criterion is met\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's parent/guardian or their language. Additionally, the patient is an adult, so this criterion is not applicable.\n  - [not met] There is no information about a parent/guardian providing consent, and the patient is an adult, not a child.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient's age is known (32 years old).\n  - [met] There is no mention of known cardiac, CNS, metabolic, or endocrine disorders in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient is moribund (at the point of death).\n  - [met] There is no mention of a recent history of choking or sudden onset of symptoms with suspected foreign body inhalation.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20145__NCT00413374", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with symptoms suggestive of DVT/PE (shortness of breath, right calf tenderness, elevated D-dimer), but there is no confirmation by venous ultrasound or CT scan mentioned.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a chest CT scan or right ventricular size assessment.\n  - [met] The patient is 56 years old, which is greater than 18.\n  - [not met] There is no information about anticipated discharge within 72 hours.\n  - [not met] There is no information about written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 56-year-old female, but there is no mention of pregnancy or intent to become pregnant.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the need for ongoing hospitalization > 72 hours.\n  - [not met] No mention of hypersensitivity to heparin, pork products, or enoxaparin.\n  - [not met] No creatinine value is provided.\n  - [met] No mention of recurrent DVT/PE or oral anticoagulation.\n  - [met] No mention of planned surgery or medical procedure during the study.\n  - [met] No mention of prior history of heparin-induced thrombocytopenia.\n  - [not met] No information about ability to participate in follow-up.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201424__NCT02535624", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient suffered blunt trauma to the abdomen with extended intraperitoneal hemorrhage due to spleen rupture, and is hemodynamically unstable (BP 60/30, HR 140). These findings suggest severe traum\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a pelvic fracture or any radiographic findings related to the pelvis. The trauma described is to the left hemi-abdomen and spleen.\n  - [not met] The patient is hemodynamically unstable (SBP 60/30), but there is no information about whether 4 units of PRBC have been administered or the response to transfusion.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has multiple injuries (blunt abdominal trauma, spleen rupture, hemorrhage) and is likely to have ISS > 17, so monotrauma or ISS \u2264 17 is not met.\n  - [met] The patient is 33 years old, which is less than 65 years.\n  - [met] The patient is 33 years old, which is more than 18 years.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT02489578", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, which is greater than or equal to 14 years.\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute onset of fever, productive cough, chest pain, and lung exam findings (egophany, decreased breath sounds, wheezing) consistent with community acquired pneumonia. There i\n  - [not met] There is no evidence in the note that the patient has had recent healthcare exposure or risk factors for healthcare-associated pneumonia.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, not less than 14 years.\n  - [met] There is no evidence that the patient has hospital acquired pneumonia; no recent hospitalization is mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active tuberculosis or current treatment for tuberculosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of non-infectious pulmonary diseases in the patient's history or current presentation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of HIV positivity.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20152__NCT00817908", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 62-year-old male, which fulfills the requirement of being a male or female patient.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note indicating the patient is a CMV D+/R- transplant recipient (liver, kidney, heart, pancreas, lung, or combined).\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient being scheduled to receive 3 months of valganciclovir, oral ganciclovir, or intravenous ganciclovir prophylaxis.\n  - [not met] The note does not state whether the patient is able to give written informed consent.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's willingness or ability to comply with the protocol.\n  - [met] The patient is 62 years old, which is >=18 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information indicating the patient is unwilling or unable to give informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT01242150", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] PaO2/FiO2 ratio is not directly provided. However, O2 saturation is 100% on room air, suggesting normal oxygenation and likely PaO2/FiO2 ratio >300.\n  - [not met] Respiratory rate is not documented in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of chest x-ray or findings compatible with pulmonary infection.\n  - [not met] No information about oxygen therapy or response; patient is on room air with normal O2 saturation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of endotracheal tube or tracheostomy.\n  - [met] No mention of facial deformities.\n  - [met] No mention of upper airway obstruction; wheezing is likely lower airway.\n  - [met] No mention of cyanotic congenital heart disease.\n  - [met] No mention of facial trauma.\n  - [met] No mention of recurrent apnea.\n  - [met] No mention of neuromuscular weakness.\n  - [met] No mention of pulmonary hypoplasia.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT01480414", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has increasing calf pain when walking uphill, diminished pulses at dorsalis pedis, and cool lower extremities, consistent with ischemic lower limb (peripheral arterial disease) per TASK guidel\n  - [met] Rutherford score 2-3 corresponds to moderate claudication. Patient has increasing calf pain on exertion and diminished pulses, likely consistent with Rutherford 2 or 3.\n  - [not met] ABI (Ankle-Brachial Index) is not provided in the note. Cannot determine if ABI < 0.6.\n  - [not met] Absolute ankle pressure is not provided in the note. Cannot determine if < 60 mmHg.\n  - [met] Patient is male. Both genders are eligible.\n  - [not met] Patient is 72 years old, which is above the inclusion age range of 20-62 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Ejection fraction (EF) is not mentioned. No evidence of severe heart failure.\n  - [met] HbA1c is not mentioned. No evidence of uncontrolled diabetes.\n  - [met] No mention of bone marrow disorders or leukemia.\n  - [met] No mention of cognitive disorders.\n  - [met] No mention of infections.\n  - [met] Patient had MI 2 years ago, not within the last month.\n  - [met] No mention of malignancy.\n  - [met] No mention of immunologic or rheumatologic disorders.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT00455468", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old, which is 96 months. The inclusion criterion is age 2 to 59 months (under 5 years).\n  - [met] The patient is male. Both boys and girls are eligible.\n  - [not met] The patient has cough, dyspnea, respiratory distress, and bilateral lung infiltrates, which are consistent with severe pneumonia. However, the age is outside the specified range for the WHO criteria p\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the patient attended the Radda Clinic or ICHSH or the time of attendance.\n  - [not met] There is no information about written informed consent from parents/guardians.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has severe pneumonia, not very severe or non-severe pneumonia.\n  - [met] There is no evidence that the pneumonia is nosocomial (hospital-acquired).\n  - [met] No history of taking antibiotics for pneumonia within 48 hours is mentioned.\n  - [met] No chronic illnesses like tuberculosis or cystic fibrosis are mentioned.\n  - [met] No congenital deformities or anomalies are mentioned.\n  - [met] No evidence of immunodeficiency is mentioned.\n  - [met] No trauma or burn is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of bronchiolitis.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-20152__NCT00034437", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 62 years old, which falls within the age range of 18-65.\n  - [met] BAL fluid examination reveals owl's eye inclusion bodies, which are characteristic of CMV infection, indicating CMV seropositivity.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about informed consent being given.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is CMV seropositive, not seronegative.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about blood counts.\n  - [met] No known history of heart, lung, kidney, liver, or bleeding disorder is mentioned.\n  - [met] No diagnosis of HIV infection is mentioned.\n  - [not met] Patient is on immunosuppressive medications, which suggests an immunodeficiency state.\n  - [met] No history of intravenous drug use is mentioned.\n  - [met] Patient is a 62-year-old male, so cannot be currently pregnant.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201529__NCT00305201", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is currently presenting with symptoms consistent with acute Kawasaki disease (persistent fever, erythematous rash, strawberry tongue, red/cracked lips, swollen red hands, conjunctival inje\n  - [not met] The patient is 4 years old, which is younger than 8 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of diabetes mellitus in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypertension or uncontrolled blood pressure in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of treatment with drugs that modify endothelial function.\n  - [met] The patient is a 4-year-old girl; it is extremely unlikely she is a smoker.\n  - [met] There is no mention of total cholesterol levels.\n  - [met] There is no mention of triglyceride levels.\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic statin treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic renal insufficiency or elevated creatinine.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201415__NCT00166790", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with 12 weeks of amenorrhea, vaginal spotting, enlarged uterus, and ultrasound showing multiple cystic areas. The differential diagnosis includes vesicular mole (another term for \n  - [not met] There is no mention of choriocarcinoma in the clinical note, nor are there findings such as metastatic disease or very high beta-HCG levels. The differential diagnosis does not include choriocarcinoma\n  - [met] Hydatidiform mole is a type of gestational trophoblastic neoplasm. Since the patient is highly suspected to have a hydatidiform mole, this criterion is likely met.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information in the note indicating that the patient is unwilling to participate.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
