{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT01219998", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 6-month-old infant who underwent major surgery. However, the note does not specify that the surgery was heart surgery with cardiopulmonary bypass. Therefore, it is unclear if this cri\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about whether the parents received written information.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of preoperative documented kidney injury. The kidney injury described appears to be postoperative.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the parents were informed or opposed. This criterion cannot be confidently assessed.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20159__NCT00138346", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The clinical note does not mention the patient's place of residence or whether they live in the study area (Cooperative Tupac Amaru).\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 10 year old child, which is older than five years old.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 10 year old child, and there is no indication that the patient is a pregnant woman.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT01470040", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about informed consent by the patient or a legally appointed guardian.\n  - [met] The patient is 85 years old, which is greater than or equal to 50 years.\n  - [not met] The patient had a car accident (mild head trauma) and visited the ER, but the visit described in the note is 3 weeks after the trauma, not within 24 hours. It is unclear if he visited the ER within 24\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient being on low-dose aspirin therapy at the time of head trauma.\n  - [met] The patient had a normal head CT at the time of trauma, with no evidence of intracranial hemorrhage or skull fracture.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no documentation or suspicion of myocardial infarction within the last 12 months.\n  - [met] There is no documentation or suspicion of transient ischemic event or cerebrovascular accident within the last 12 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of coronary intervention within the last 6 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of vascular stenting or bypass within the last 6 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of end-stage renal failure requiring dialysis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of aspirin use at any dose.\n  - [met] There is no mention of concomitant treatment with anti-coagulant or other anti-aggregant.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT01226134", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is an adult male (32 years old). However, there is no mention of a diagnosis of functional dyspepsia or fulfillment of Rome III criteria; symptoms described are more consistent with giardi\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about H. pylori status (gastric biopsy or Urea Breath Test).\n  - [not met] The stool smear revealed cysts consistent with giardiasis, and there is no mention of duodenal biopsy results. The patient likely has giardiasis, so this criterion is not met.\n  - [not met] There is no information about an upper abdominal ultrasound.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness to participate or consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old, which is >=18 years.\n  - [not met] There is no information about H. pylori status.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking medications that alter gastric motility like macrolides.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking anti-emetics or antibiotics.\n  - [met] The patient is a male, so not pregnant or breast-feeding.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT01296789", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has fever, tachycardia (HR 132), and acute abdominal pain. According to ACCP/SCCM, SIRS criteria include temperature abnormality, heart rate >90, respiratory rate >20 or PaCO2 <32, and WBC\n  - [met] The patient has a documented infection: a ruptured liver abscess, which was surgically drained. While antibiotic treatment is not explicitly mentioned, surgical drainage of an abscess typically includ\n  - [not met] Shock is defined as hypotension (BP <90/40) with need for vasopressors. The patient has hypotension (BP 80/40) and was taken to the ICU, but there is no explicit mention of vasopressor use.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of central nervous system diseases in the clinical note.\n  - [met] No mention of ST elevation myocardial infarction.\n  - [met] No mention of pulmonary embolism.\n  - [met] No mention of out of hospital cardiac arrest.\n  - [met] No mention of therapy limitations.\n  - [met] Patient is a 48-year-old male, so pregnancy is not possible.\n  - [met] No mention of inclusion in other interventional trials.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT02548715", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of head and neck cancer or biopsy in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of surgery or treatment location in Edmonton, Alberta.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of treatment with curative intent.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms suggestive of hypothyroidism (cold intolerance, fatigue, constipation, dry skin, hyporeflexia, slow movements), but there is no mention of sub-clinical hypothyroidism, TSH, fr\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of head and neck cancer of the thyroid gland or other subsite involving the thyroid gland.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous treatment for a different head and neck cancer.\n  - [met] There is no mention of history of radiation therapy or chemotherapy to the head and neck.\n  - [met] There is no explicit history of thyroid disease provided.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms highly suggestive of hypothyroidism (cold intolerance, fatigue, constipation, dry skin, hyporeflexia, slow movements), but there is no explicit diagnosis. However, the symptom\n  - [met] There is no mention or symptoms of hyperthyroidism.\n  - [met] There is no mention of autoimmune thyroid disease, Grave's disease, or Hashimoto's thyroiditis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of thyroiditis.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT01521403", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old, which is \u2265 18 years.\n  - [not met] The duration of gastrointestinal symptoms is not specified in the note. It is unclear if symptoms have lasted more than 10 days.\n  - [not met] The stool smear revealed ellipsoidal cysts, but there is no mention of B. hominis specifically. The cysts described could be Giardia or another protozoan.\n  - [not met] No other pathogenic micro-organism is mentioned as identified, but the specific organism is not named. Unclear if other pathogens were tested for.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No fever is mentioned.\n  - [met] No bloody diarrhea is mentioned; stools are described as greasy and foul-smelling.\n  - [met] Weight loss is not mentioned, only loss of appetite.\n  - [met] Significant decrease of general condition is not mentioned; malaise is present but not specified as significant.\n  - [met] No oncological diseases are mentioned.\n  - [met] No immune deficiencies are mentioned.\n  - [met] No known chronic intestinal diseases are mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of anti-protozoan drug use in the last 2 weeks.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201519__NCT02282436", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 66-year-old female. Both males and females are eligible.\n  - [not met] The patient has clinical features of COPD (chronic cough, barrel chest, wheezing, significant smoking history), but there is no FEV1 value provided to confirm it is under 60% of predicted.\n  - [not met] The patient has a significant smoking history (1-2 packs per day for 47 years), so is not a non-smoker.\n  - [met] The patient is 66 years old, which is between 50 and 75.\n  - [met] The patient is experiencing recent, progressive shortness of breath and moderate respiratory distress, consistent with an acute exacerbation of COPD, though the exact duration (24-48 hours) is not spe\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of HIV, cancer, renal or cardiac deficiency in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hormonal dysregulation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inferior limb pathology.\n  - [met] There is no mention of neuromuscular pathology.\n  - [not met] The patient has a history of tobacco use (significant smoking history), which counts as tobacco abuse.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is oxygen dependent.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20153__NCT02334007", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is above 18.\n  - [met] The patient is male. Either gender is allowed.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of resectable lung cancer or metastatic lung disease.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient undergoing segmentectomy, wedge resection, lobectomy, bilobectomy, or pneumonectomy. The only surgery mentioned is right total hip replacement.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is not competent to understand consent documents. No cognitive impairment is mentioned.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergic or anaphylactic reaction to contrast dye, heparin, or LMWH.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being on anticoagulation for VTE or other conditions.\n  - [met] No information is provided about renal function or GFR.\n  - [met] No information is provided about hepatic failure or INR.\n  - [met] No history or evidence of liver disease or ascites is mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient is male and therefore cannot be pregnant.\n  - [met] There is no mention of VTE diagnosis or treatment in the 3 months prior to surgery.\n  - [met] No known bleeding disorder is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT02229695", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 32-year-old woman (over 18 years old) who has sustained multiple injuries and has abdominal findings (tenderness, guarding, rebound, no bowel sounds) suggestive of intra-abdominal inj\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information in the note to suggest that the surgeon estimates she will not survive 24 hours. Her vital signs are stable (BP 134/74, pulse 87), and she is fully awake and alert.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201518__NCT00530426", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with classic symptoms and signs of decompensated heart failure, including worsening exertional dyspnea, orthopnea (difficulty breathing when lying flat, requiring extra pillows), \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Heart failure is not merely a co-morbid condition in this case; it is the principal focus of diagnosis and treatment, as evidenced by the detailed description of heart failure symptoms and physical fi", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201427__NCT02521727", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a first-degree relative (sibling) of individuals diagnosed with hundreds of colonic adenomas, but not specifically non-advanced adenoma. The siblings had advanced polyposis, not non-adv\n  - [not met] The patient is a first-degree relative of siblings with hundreds of colonic adenomas, not negative findings on colonoscopy. Therefore, this criterion is not met.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a first-degree relative with colorectal cancer (CRC); siblings had polyposis but no cancer.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a family history compatible with HNPCC (Amsterdam criteria: 3 relatives with CRC, across 2 generations, 1 diagnosed before age 50). The family history is of polyposis, not CRC.\n  - [not met] The family history and the patient's findings are highly suggestive of Familial Adenomatous Polyposis (FAP) syndrome (hundreds of adenomas in siblings, dozens in patient). Therefore, this exclusion cr\n  - [met] There is no mention of inflammatory bowel disease in the patient or siblings.\n  - [met] There is no information about prior colonoscopies in the past 5 years.\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe cardio-pulmonary or other medical co-morbidities.\n  - [met] The patient is a 21-year-old male college student, so pregnancy does not apply.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT01414322", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents to the ER with wheezing, which is a sign of respiratory distress and may be associated with shortness of breath, though shortness of breath is not explicitly stated.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether management is according to Hadassah Mt. Scopus pediatric emergency department protocols.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of asthma management protocol being used.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of bronchiolitis management protocol being used.\n  - [met] The patient is 4 years old, which is within the 0-15 age range.\n  - [met] The mother brought the child to the ED and is described as concerned, suggesting she is present and able to comprehend. No evidence she cannot give consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of the patient receiving inhaled bronchodilators prior to enrollment.\n  - [met] No mention of the patient receiving oral or IV steroids prior to enrollment.\n  - [met] The patient is playful, well-appearing, and has normal O2 saturation, indicating he is not ventilated.\n  - [met] No mention of chest skin lesions.\n  - [met] No mention or evidence of cystic fibrosis.\n  - [met] The patient is playful, well-appearing, and has normal O2 saturation, indicating hemodynamic stability.\n  - [met] No indication that the parent/guardian objects to the study protocol.\n  - [met] No mention of concurrent participation in any other clinical study.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT00747981", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 4 year old boy, which is between 6 months and 16 years.\n  - [met] The patient suddenly started coughing while playing in a sandbox, followed by persistent wheezing. This clinical scenario raises suspicion for foreign body aspiration.\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention of health care assurance in the note. This cannot be determined from the available information.\n  - [met] The mother is present and able to provide information about the patient\u2019s history and events leading up to presentation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The child is described as playful and well appearing, with normal oxygen saturation. This suggests the situation is not an emergency.\n  - [met] There is suspicion but not certainty of foreign body presence. The note does not confirm a foreign body.\n  - [not met] There is no information about CT scan timing. This cannot be determined from the note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the parents' language. This cannot be determined from the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of parental refusal. The mother brought the child to the ED, suggesting consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20143__NCT00049543", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a left lung mass, but there is no mention of histological proof of non-small cell lung cancer.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about post-operative staging or pathologic criteria.\n  - [not met] No information about mediastinal lymph node resection or sampling.\n  - [not met] No information about nodal tissue labeling or biopsy.\n  - [not met] No information about biopsy of right upper lobe nodal levels.\n  - [not met] No information about biopsy of right middle lobe nodal levels.\n  - [not met] No information about biopsy of right lower lobe nodal levels.\n  - [not met] No information about biopsy of left upper lobe nodal levels.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):", "n_inc_assessed": 30, "n_exc_assessed": 0}
{"pair": "sigir-201529__NCT01596335", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 4-year-old girl with persistent fever, erythematous rash, strawberry tongue, red/cracked lips, swollen red hands, and bilateral conjunctival injection (red eyes with no discharge). Th\n  - [not met] There is no mention of IVIG therapy being administered or the patient being refractory to it.\n  - [met] The patient has had a persistent fever with a reported spike to 104F (40C), which is above 37.5\u00baC.\n  - [met] The patient has had fever for the past week (7 days), so administration by day 8 is possible.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information about recent BCG vaccination.\n  - [met] There is no mention of serious infections requiring hospitalization in the past 6 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of opportunistic infections in the past 6 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active tuberculosis, hepatitis B or C, or history of hepatitis B.\n  - [met] There is no mention of HIV infection or family history of HIV.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior treatment with infliximab or other biological products.\n  - [met] There is no mention of participation in another clinical study or receiving a study drug in the past 12 weeks.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201422__NCT01068288", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a child (15 years old). The duration of symptoms is not explicitly stated, but the pain started 'gradually' and she has had no appetite since yesterday. This suggests symptoms for less \n  - [not met] Abdominal ultrasound shows a markedly edematous appendix, but there is no mention of an appendiceal abscess or phlegmon, nor explicit mention of perforation. The diagnosis of perforated appendicitis i\n  - [not met] Consent to participate is not mentioned in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The diagnosis appears to be appendicitis based on clinical and imaging findings, with no uncertainty expressed.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the need for laparotomy for another reason.\n  - [met] There is no mention of free intraperitoneal air on imaging.\n  - [met] There is no mention of diffuse abdominal fluid on imaging or a clinical picture of severe sepsis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of other medical conditions such as inflammatory bowel disease.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT01284218", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about any medication fills, including augmentation therapy medications from Table 1, or about the identification period.\n  - [not met] There is no information about insurance enrollment or pharmacy benefits coverage for the required periods.\n  - [not met] The note describes symptoms consistent with major depressive disorder (MDD), but there is no explicit mention of a medical claim or ICD-9-CM diagnosis code for MDD.\n  - [met] The patient is 20 years old, which is \u226518 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about pharmacy claims for atypical antipsychotics, mood stabilizers, anxiolytics, anticonvulsants, or stimulants during the pre-index period.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any medical claims or diagnoses for non-MDD episodic mood disorders or schizophrenia.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201427__NCT00641147", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a family history of familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP) and is found to have dozens of small colonic polyps (benign adenomas) in the rectosigmoid. This meets the criterion of 'patient\n  - [not met] The patient has FAP and lower tract adenomatous polyposis (dozens of colonic adenomas in rectosigmoid), but there is no mention of duodenal adenomatous polyposis or status/post ileostomy. Therefore, t\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 21-year-old college student, but gender is not explicitly stated. However, the use of 'his' and 'brother' indicates the patient is male. Thus, this exclusion criterion is met.\n  - [met] The patient is male, so cannot be pregnant. This exclusion criterion is met.\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's white blood cell count. Assume criterion is met unless otherwise stated.\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's platelet count. Assume criterion is met unless otherwise stated.\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's blood urea nitrogen. Assume criterion is met unless otherwise stated.\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's creatinine. Assume criterion is met unless otherwise stated.\n  - [met] No information is provided about the patient's use of NSAIDs, aspirin, curcumin, turmeric, calcium, vitamin D, green tea, or polyphenol E supplements. Assume criterion is met unless otherwise stated.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any malignancy in the patient. The polyps are benign adenomas. Assume criterion is met.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT00814307", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has 2 weeks of joint pain, swelling, and stiffness in multiple joints (knees, hips, right elbow, previously right ankle), as well as fatigue and intermittent fevers. However, there is no e\n  - [not met] The patient has pain, swelling, and stiffness in multiple joints, but the exact number of tender/swollen joints is not specified. There is no information about ESR or CRP values.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of prior DMARD use or inadequate response to DMARDs.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active, latent, or inadequately treated tuberculosis infection.\n  - [not met] There is no information about DMARD washout or use of antimalarials.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of blood dyscrasias or abnormal blood counts.\n  - [met] The patient has no previous medical problems and no history of other autoimmune rheumatic diseases is mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of malignancy or history of malignancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any infection requiring hospitalization or significant antimicrobial therapy in the past 6 months.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT02105714", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 32-year-old male presenting with diarrhea, abdominal cramping, and flatulence. The duration of diarrhea is not explicitly stated, but the symptoms are persistent enough to prompt a cl\n  - [not met] There is no mention of written informed consent being provided in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient is in need of immediate intensive or surgical care. The symptoms are gastrointestinal and not life-threatening.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is unable or unwilling to give written informed consent.\n  - [met] There is no mention of clinical jaundice or observation of jaundice in the conjunctivae.\n  - [met] There is no information to suggest the patient is unable to comply with study requirements.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is participating in other diagnostic studies or clinical trials.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20149__NCT00132327", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a patient presenting with skin lesions to a dermatologist.\n  - [met] The patient is 43 years old, which is >= 18 years.\n  - [not met] No evidence of an expanding annular lesion at least 5 cm in diameter or history of exposure to Lyme disease. Lesions are described as small (largest 4 mm), soft, and pedunculated.\n  - [not met] No mention of exposure to wooded, brushy, or grassy areas or Lyme endemic area.\n  - [met] A history of tick bite is not required, so this criterion is not applicable.\n  - [not met] Lesions are on the neck, which is an excluded site for biopsy.\n  - [not met] No information about RPR, HIV, HBsAg, or HCV status.\n  - [not met] No information about ability to give consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a patient presenting with lesions.\n  - [met] No mention of antibiotic therapy for Lyme disease.\n  - [met] No mention of oral corticosteroid use.\n  - [met] No mention of severe skin disease such as psoriasis or atopic dermatitis in the last year.\n  - [met] No mention of diabetes, active cancer, or autoimmune diseases.\n  - [met] No mention of investigational drug use in the past month.\n  - [met] No mention of history of forming large thick scars.\n  - [met] No mention of excessive bleeding or anticoagulation.", "n_inc_assessed": 12, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT02229812", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 72-year-old woman, thus is a female in-patient.\n  - [met] Patient is 72 years old, which is within the 18-80 years range.\n  - [met] Patient had a cryptogenic (ischemic) stroke, CT excluded hemorrhage, and received thrombolytic therapy. The note does not specify the exact neurological deficit, but the diagnosis and treatment imply \n  - [met] The note states she was given thrombolytic therapy after stroke, but does not specify the time from symptom onset to treatment. However, standard of care for thrombolysis is within 3 hours, so it is l\n  - [met] No mention of symptoms resolving before treatment; she received thrombolysis with resolution after treatment, suggesting symptoms persisted for at least 30 minutes and were not rapidly improving befor\n  - [met] No explicit mention of consent, but she received thrombolysis and is being followed up, suggesting willingness to participate.\n  - [met] No evidence of inability or unwillingness to comply; she is attending follow-up.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] CT was negative for brain hemorrhage.\n  - [met] No evidence that symptoms began more than 3 hours before infusion; standard practice and context suggest within window.\n  - [met] No mention of minor deficit or rapidly improving symptoms before infusion; symptoms resolved after thrombolysis.\n  - [met] No mention of severe stroke; symptoms resolved after thrombolysis and no imaging abnormalities.\n  - [met] No mention of seizure at onset.\n  - [met] No mention of symptoms suggestive of subarachnoid hemorrhage.\n  - [met] No mention of heparin administration or abnormal thromboplastin time.\n  - [met] Patient has type 2 diabetes and a history of stroke (the index event), but the criterion refers to 'any history of prior stroke and concomitant diabetes.' Since this is her first stroke, this exclusio", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 23}
{"pair": "sigir-20141__NCT01356992", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about ICF signature (informed consent form).\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's willingness to follow instructions or perform study procedures.\n  - [met] Patient is a 58-year-old woman, which is over 18 and under 75.\n  - [not met] Patient has had chest pain episodes for the first time in her life, starting two days ago, but there is no evidence of angina at rest for at least 20 minutes in the last 24 hours and for at least 10 d\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the timing of randomization relative to ER arrival.\n  - [not met] There is no clear evidence of NSTEMI or unstable angina based on the provided criteria. The EKG shows nonspecific changes, and there is no mention of cardiac biomarkers or other qualifying features.\n  - [not met] None of the specific findings (dynamic T-wave changes, ST-segment changes, biomarker elevation, pulmonary edema, angina with murmur, abnormal heart sounds, or hypotension) are documented. EKG only sho\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] EKG shows nonspecific changes, not persistent ST-segment elevation.\n  - [met] No evidence of secondary causes of angina (anemia, fever, hypovolemia, dehydration, cocaine use) is mentioned.\n  - [met] Patient is not taking any medications, so no heparin use.\n  - [met] No mention of severe renal failure, hepatic disease, or other significant comorbidities except hypertension and obesity.\n  - [met] No history of recent hemorrhagic cerebrovascular accident is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of scheduled cardiac surgery.\n  - [met] Patient denies drug use and there is no mention of alcohol abuse.\n  - [met] Patient is a 58-year-old woman, but there is no mention of pregnancy or lactation. At this age, pregnancy is highly unlikely.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT00228111", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is fully awake and alert (no neurological compromise), blood pressure is 134/74 mm Hg (not hypotensive), pulse is 87/min (not tachycardic), and no mention of respiratory compromise or majo\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the revised trauma score. Cannot determine from the note.\n  - [met] The patient has sustained multiple injuries including upper and lower extremity fractures, which suggests fractures of at least two long bones.\n  - [not met] No mention of flail chest or multiple rib fractures.\n  - [not met] No mention of a pelvic rim fracture.\n  - [not met] No mention of unstable vertebral fractures or neural cord compression.\n  - [met] The patient was involved in a car accident, which is considered a high-energy injury mechanism.\n  - [not met] No mention of a fall from height.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of shock Class IIIB/IV. Blood pressure and pulse are within normal limits.\n  - [met] No indication that the patient needs immediate neurosurgical intervention.\n  - [met] No mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] The patient was admitted directly to the ER, not referred from another hospital.\n  - [met] The patient is alive and alert in the emergency department.", "n_inc_assessed": 9, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT00880347", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is being considered for the AD group.\n  - [met] The patient is an 89-year-old man, which is \u2265 40 years old.\n  - [met] The patient has progressive cognitive decline, memory loss, language impairment, and functional decline, consistent with probable AD by DSM-IV TR and NINCDS-ADRDA criteria, though the note does not ex\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about brain imaging (CT or MRI) being performed.\n  - [not met] The neurological exam shows paratonic rigidity and myoclonic jerks, which are not typical for AD and may be considered focal or atypical signs.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's compliance with study procedures.\n  - [not met] This is for the non-AD demented group, not applicable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] This is for the AD group.\n  - [not met] The presence of myoclonic jerks and paratonic rigidity may suggest other diagnoses (e.g., CJD, FTD), which could make the AD diagnosis doubtful.\n  - [met] No evidence of drug or alcohol abuse or dependence.\n  - [met] The patient meets criteria for dementia, not just mild cognitive impairment.", "n_inc_assessed": 26, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT01177657", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header for cases, not an actual criterion.\n  - [met] The patient is a 5-year-old boy, born after 6 March 2006 and at least 12 weeks of age.\n  - [not met] The patient was admitted to the emergency department, but there is no mention of severe gastroenteritis; symptoms are dysphagia, drooling, fever, and vocal changes.\n  - [not met] No evidence of severe gastroenteritis, so onset timing is not applicable.\n  - [not met] No mention of laboratory confirmed rotavirus positive stool sample.\n  - [not met] No information about written informed consent.\n  - [not met] This is a header for controls, not an actual criterion.\n  - [met] The patient was admitted for non-gastroenteritis causes (dysphagia, drooling, fever, vocal changes), so this is met if considering control criteria.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header for cases, not an actual criterion.\n  - [met] No information about previous participation as case or control.\n  - [met] No evidence of severe gastroenteritis, so nosocomial infection timing is not applicable.\n  - [not met] This is a header for controls, not an actual criterion.\n  - [met] The patient does not have symptoms of gastroenteritis during current hospitalization; presenting symptoms are not gastroenteritis.\n  - [not met] The patient may have a vaccine-preventable disease (epiglottitis is possible given symptoms and delayed vaccines), but this is not confirmed in the note.\n  - [met] No information about past participation as case or control.\n  - [met] No information about living in the same house as a case.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-20145__NCT02334007", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 56 years old, which is above 18.\n  - [met] The patient is female. Either gender is allowed.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of resectable lung cancer or metastatic lung disease. The patient had a left mastectomy, which is typically for breast cancer.\n  - [not met] The patient underwent a left mastectomy, not a lung surgery such as segmentectomy, wedge resection, lobectomy, bilobectomy, or pneumonectomy.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's competence to understand consent documents.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of allergy or anaphylactic reaction to contrast dye, heparin, or LMWH.\n  - [met] No mention of current anticoagulation for VTE or other conditions.\n  - [met] No mention of renal impairment or GFR values.\n  - [met] No mention of hepatic failure or INR values.\n  - [met] No mention of history or ongoing liver disease, ascites, or peritoneal tapping.\n  - [met] No mention of pregnancy or plans to become pregnant. The patient is 56, which is likely post-menopausal.\n  - [met] No mention of VTE diagnosis or treatment in the 3 months prior to surgery.\n  - [met] No mention of a bleeding disorder.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT00430677", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has at least 4 of the 11 ACR criteria for SLE: malar rash (rash on bridge of nose and cheeks), non-scarring alopecia, arthritis (swelling and tenderness of wrists and ankles), hematologic \n  - [not met] There is no mention of a renal biopsy or its findings in the clinical note. Therefore, it cannot be determined if this criterion is met.\n  - [not met] Serum creatinine is not reported in the clinical note, so it is not possible to determine if the patient meets this criterion.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information about a rise in serum creatinine within 1 month prior to screening. Cannot confirm exclusion.\n  - [met] There is no mention of drug-induced SLE; the presentation is consistent with idiopathic SLE.\n  - [met] There is no mention of CNS lupus or related symptoms (e.g., seizures, psychosis, etc.).\n  - [met] There is no mention of another autoimmune disease as the main diagnosis; SLE is the primary diagnosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cyclophosphamide treatment within the last 3 months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of rituximab treatment within the last 6 months.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20151__NCT01292915", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 44-year-old male (adult) admitted to the hospital (ICU) after presenting with multiple bouts of coffee ground vomiting, which is a manifestation of overt non-variceal upper GI bleed.\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the clinical note of an upper GI endoscopy being performed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The clinical note describes GI bleeding consistent with non-variceal upper GI bleed (coffee ground vomiting), and there is no evidence that the bleeding is from another source.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT02064959", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient had a car accident (blunt trauma) 3 weeks ago, which is consistent with non-penetrating traumatic brain injury. However, there is no explicit mention of brain injury at that time, but the \n  - [met] The patient has a gradual decrease in consciousness and is no longer walking or eating by himself, suggesting significant impairment. However, there is no explicit GCS motor score provided. The descri\n  - [not met] The patient is 85 years old, which is outside the 22-65 year age range.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of an acute subdural hematoma or emergent craniotomy within 6 hours of injury.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the time to reach a temperature of 35\u00b0C or whether this was achieved within 6 hours.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's pupils or total GCS score.\n  - [met] The patient is not following commands and has not improved after coma.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a known pre-existing neurological deficit.\n  - [met] There is no mention of concomitant spinal cord injury.\n  - [not met] No information about arrival temperature.\n  - [not met] No information about hemodynamic instability.\n  - [not met] No information about cardiac dysrhythmia.\n  - [met] The patient is an 85-year-old man, so pregnancy is not possible.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201429__NCT02347865", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is postmenopausal, as documented by LH and FSH levels within the last year. She is seeking advice on osteoporosis prevention, but there is no explicit mention that a decision has been made\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note indicating that the patient has received her first prescription of Prolia in the last 4 weeks.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of informed consent being provided by the patient for study enrollment.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting that the patient is participating in ongoing or previous Denosumab clinical trials.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT02255487", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 32-year-old woman, which is 18 years of age or older.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about written informed consent or surrogate consent.\n  - [not met] The patient has experienced abdominal trauma (tender abdomen with guarding and rebound, no bowel sounds), but there is no mention of requiring or having undergone open abdominal laparotomy with primar\n  - [not met] The patient has signs of an acute surgical abdomen (tenderness, guarding, rebound, no bowel sounds), but there is no mention of requiring or having undergone open abdominal laparotomy with primary clo\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a known allergy to Chlorhexidine Gluconate (CHG).\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's Abbreviated Injury Scale (AIS) score.\n  - [met] There is no information about the patient's ASA score, but the patient is awake, alert, and hemodynamically stable, making an ASA score of 5 or greater unlikely.\n  - [not met] There is no information about pregnancy or breastfeeding status.\n  - [met] There is no mention of damage control laparotomy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an abdominal incision created prior to the operating room.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being enrolled in another clinical trial.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201527__NCT02341300", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 15-year-old girl with severe anemia (Hb 4.2 g/dL), but there is no mention of pregnancy or gestational status. Therefore, she does not meet the criterion of being a pregnant woman in \n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's or her family's willingness or ability to cook with a cast iron pot at least 3 times per week.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of pregnancy or gestational status, so singleton gestation cannot be confirmed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence of a secondary cause of anemia such as hemolytic anemia, sickle cell disease, thalassemia, or malaria. The anemia appears to be iron deficiency based on labs. Willingness to use a\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe chronic illness, high likelihood of preterm birth, long-term hospitalization, or multifetal gestation. However, the patient is not pregnant, so this is not directly appli", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201423__NCT01460082", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of heavy smoking, is over 40, presents with cough, shortness of breath, barrel-shaped chest, diffuse rales, cyanosis, tachypnea, and chest x-ray shows hyperinflation. These f\n  - [met] The patient has an acute worsening of respiratory symptoms (productive cough, purulent sputum, increased dyspnea) requiring increased oxygen use, which fits the definition of acute exacerbation of COP\n  - [met] The patient is 63 years old, which is over 40 years of age.\n  - [met] The patient has a history of heavy smoking, which likely exceeds 10 pack-years, though the exact number is not specified. Given the description, it is reasonable to assume at least 10 pack-years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Chest x-ray shows hyperinflation with no consolidation, and the patient denies fever. There is no evidence of pneumonia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of history or signs of congestive heart failure in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of acute myocardial infarction or related symptoms.\n  - [met] There is no mention of thoracotomy or lung tissue resection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of interstitial lung disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of acute or chronic renal failure.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active malignancy.\n  - [not met] The patient has mild psoriasis, which is an autoimmune disease, but the criterion is for exclusion if the patient has an autoimmune disease. Since psoriasis is present, this criterion is NOT met.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201510__NCT01601366", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has severe premenstrual and menstrual pelvic pain (dysmenorrhoea) and chronic pelvic pain. However, there is no explicit diagnosis of adenomyosis or statement that the pain is secondary to\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's plans for birth spacing.\n  - [met] The patient is 38 years old, which is within the 20-45 year range.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of ultrasonographic or Doppler findings suggestive of adenomyosis.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's place of residence or proximity for follow-up.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence that the patient is currently pregnant.\n  - [met] There is no evidence or history of defective coagulation.\n  - [met] There is no history or evidence of malignancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of endometrial biopsy or hyperplasia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of incidental adnexal abnormality on ultrasound.\n  - [met] There is no mention of contraindications to COCs.\n  - [met] There is no mention of absolute contraindication to LNG-IUS insertion.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous endometrial ablation or resection.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201412__NCT02190214", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The clinical note states the patient is a 25-year-old woman, which is equal to or more than 18 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about the patient's citizenship or nationality.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note regarding whether the patient gave consent or not.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT00873522", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute onset of productive cough, fever, chills, chest pain, and lung exam findings (egophany, decreased breath sounds) consistent with community-acquired pneumonia (CAP).\n  - [met] There is no mention of recent hospital admission within the past 14 days.\n  - [met] No evidence in the note that the patient meets HCAP criteria (no recent hospitalization, dialysis, infusion therapy, residence in nursing home, or outpatient chemo/radiation).\n  - [not met] No evidence of HCAP risk factors (no recent hospitalization, dialysis, infusion therapy, residence in nursing home, or outpatient chemo/radiation).\n  - [not met] No mention of dialysis, infusion therapy, or similar treatments.\n  - [not met] No mention of radiation therapy or chemotherapy.\n  - [not met] No mention of any hospital admission in the past 90 days.\n  - [not met] No mention of residence in a nursing home or long-term care facility.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence that pneumonia developed after hospital admission or within 14 days after discharge.\n  - [met] No evidence of mechanical ventilation or hospital-acquired pneumonia.\n  - [met] No mention of HIV or immunosuppression.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT02562040", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms suggestive of mild sleep-disordered breathing (nighttime snoring, pauses in breathing, restlessness, daytime sleepiness), but there is no explicit diagnosis or confirmation of\n  - [not met] Caregiver report of habitual snoring is present, but frequency and duration (most nights per week for at least three months) are not explicitly stated.\n  - [not met] No polysomnogram (PSG) data is provided in the note.\n  - [not met] No information about tonsillar hypertrophy is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about ENT evaluation or candidacy for AT is provided.\n  - [met] The primary indication appears to be nocturnal obstructive symptoms (snoring, pauses in breathing, sleepiness), not recurrent infections.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No history of previous tonsillectomy is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of recurrent tonsillitis.\n  - [met] No mention of severe obesity or BMI.\n  - [met] No mention of failure to thrive.\n  - [met] No mention of severe chronic health conditions.\n  - [met] No mention of severe cardiopulmonary disorders.\n  - [met] No mention of bleeding disorders.\n  - [met] No mention of sickle cell disease.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 19}
{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT01962779", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 62-year-old man, which meets the age requirement (>50 years). However, the criterion also requires normal cognition, and the patient has severe cognitive deficits and memory dysfuncti\n  - [not met] The patient has severe cognitive deficits and memory dysfunction confirmed on neurological examination, which means he is not within normal limits on neurological and psychiatric examinations. He woul\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's education level.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether an informed family member or life partner was interviewed, or about agreement to MRI, lumbar puncture, ApoE genotyping, and DNA banking.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has severe cognitive deficits, memory dysfunction, EEG abnormalities, cerebral atrophy, and biopsy findings consistent with a brain disease (likely a neurodegenerative disorder). Therefore\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of brain tumor.\n  - [met] There is no mention of radiation or chemotherapy in the past 3 years.\n  - [met] There is no mention of significant history of alcoholism or drug abuse.\n  - [met] There is no mention of psychiatric illness such as schizophrenia, mania, PTSD, or lifelong major depression.\n  - [met] No information about Hamilton Depression Scale or lifelong depressive episodes.\n  - [met] No evidence of clinically relevant and uncontrolled cardiac, pulmonary, hypothyroid, or hematological conditions is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of physical impairment affecting psychological testing.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 19}
{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT00183092", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a biopsy-confirmed diagnosis of sCJD (diffuse vacuolar changes of the gray matter with reactive astrocytosis, no inflammatory infiltration), which meets the 'definite' sCJD definition.\n  - [met] The patient is 62 years old, which is over 18.\n  - [not met] There is no information about swallowing ability in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to follow simple one-step commands. Severe cognitive deficits are noted, but this does not confirm or exclude ability.\n  - [met] The patient has had both an EEG and neuroimaging (MRI or similar) studies, but the timing (within 6 months for MRI, 3 months for EEG) is not specified. The findings are consistent with sCJD and rule o\n  - [not met] There is no information about consent to autopsy.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No history of cancer, end-stage liver or renal disease, or severe heart disease is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of other disease requiring regular supportive care is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of liver disease.\n  - [met] No mention of active alcoholism.\n  - [met] No mention of bone marrow suppression.\n  - [met] No mention of severe hypotension.\n  - [met] No mention of severe psoriasis.\n  - [met] No mention of poorly controlled diabetes.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT01145157", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, so he is not of legal age and is likely not skeletally mature.\n  - [not met] There is no mention that the patient requires primary total knee arthroplasty due to degenerative or inflammatory joint disease. The main issue is acute knee pain, fever, and an osteolytic lesion, pos\n  - [not met] There is no information about preoperative medical clearance or operative risk assessment.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's availability for follow-up.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability to have an MRI scan or any of the listed contraindications.\n  - [met] No cardiac pacemaker is mentioned.\n  - [met] No surgical clips in the head are mentioned.\n  - [met] No artificial heart valves are mentioned.\n  - [met] No electronic inner ear implants are mentioned.\n  - [met] No metal fragments in eyes are mentioned.\n  - [met] No electronic stimulators are mentioned.\n  - [met] No implanted pumps are mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201518__NCT01138683", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms and signs of heart failure (orthopnea, PND, bibasilar crackles, edema, JVD), but there is no explicit mention of ejection fraction or severity.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of hospitalization in the note.\n  - [met] The patient has significant symptoms with exertion and at rest (orthopnea, PND), which is consistent with NYHA III or IV, but not explicitly stated.\n  - [?] This is a header criterion; assessment depends on the following subcriteria.\n  - [met] Jugular venous distension is present, but the exact measurement is not provided.\n  - [not met] No echocardiographic or Doppler data is provided.\n  - [not met] No chest X-ray findings are mentioned.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of need for inotropic or vasopressive agents.\n  - [met] No mention of IV contrast media use.\n  - [met] No mention of acute coronary syndrome.\n  - [met] No mention of dialysis or renal failure.\n  - [met] No mention of severe co-morbidities.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindications for anticoagulation.\n  - [met] The patient is a 65-year-old male and cannot be pregnant.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT02018952", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy presenting with acute knee pain, fever, lethargy, edema, tenderness, effusion, and extremely limited range of motion. Imaging showed an osteolytic lesion. These findin\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any material (such as prosthesis or hardware) present in the targeted joint (knee).\n  - [not met] The patient is 10 years old, which is less than 18 years old.\n  - [met] The note mentions the child's guardians, but does not state that the patient is under legal guardianship (as in a court-appointed guardian for incapacity). This is likely referring to parental guardia\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, so pregnancy is not possible.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201424__NCT01103999", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presented to the ER with acute abdominal pain after blunt abdominal trauma and is being evaluated for extended intraperitoneal hemorrhage due to spleen rupture, which strongly suggests hos\n  - [met] Diagnosis of splenic contusion (spleen rupture) is confirmed by CT scan, and the patient is hemodynamically unstable (BP: 60/30, HR: 140).\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the patient signing a consent form.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the patient's affiliation with a social security program.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient refusing to participate.\n  - [met] The patient is a 33-year-old male, so he cannot be pregnant or breastfeeding.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being under guardianship.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201530__NCT00551668", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The clinical note describes a traumatic injury to the left arm with dislocation of the ulna and radius at the elbow joint, but there is no mention of a patellar (kneecap) dislocation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information in the note about any previous dislocation or subluxation of the patella.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any pre-existing knee pathology on either side in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous knee trauma or patellar fracture in the clinical note.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT00393913", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has nighttime snoring, pauses in breathing, and excessive sleepiness during class, which are symptoms of OSA.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any change in medical history or medications that could affect sleepiness.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of other sleep disorders such as periodic leg movements, narcolepsy, insomnia, central sleep apnea, or sleep hypoventilation syndrome. The symptoms described are consistent with OS\n  - [met] There is no mention of medically unstable health conditions such as heart attack or congestive heart failure.\n  - [met] There is no mention of use of psychotropic medications that cause sedation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recreational drug use or alcohol abuse.\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, so cannot be pregnant.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability to communicate verbally, write, or read.\n  - [met] There is no mention of visual, hearing, or cognitive impairment.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201530__NCT00707018", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 47 years old, which is outside the required age range of 14 to 30 years.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's willingness to participate in follow-up for at least two years.\n  - [not met] The patient has an acute, first-time, traumatic, isolated dislocation, but it is of the elbow (ulna and radius), not the shoulder. The criterion specifies anterior shoulder dislocation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous instability of the affected shoulder.\n  - [met] There is no mention of significant ligamentous laxity or multi-directional instability of the opposite shoulder.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability or willingness to comply with sling immobilization, rehabilitation, or follow-up.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's competence or willingness to consent.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a medical condition making the patient unable to wear a sling.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a significant associated fracture; only dislocations are described.\n  - [met] There is no mention of neurovascular compromise of the affected limb.\n  - [not met] The patient has a traumatic elbow dislocation, which is a significant ipsilateral upper extremity injury that would affect participation in a shoulder rehabilitation program.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201423__NCT02282436", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 63-year-old man, so he is male.\n  - [not met] The patient has clinical features of COPD (heavy smoking history, barrel chest, hyperinflation on x-ray, chronic symptoms), but there is no FEV1 value provided.\n  - [not met] The patient has a history of heavy smoking, so is not a non-smoker.\n  - [met] The patient is 63 years old, which is between 50 and 75.\n  - [met] The patient is experiencing an acute exacerbation of COPD (recent onset of increased cough, purulent sputum, dyspnea, requiring increased oxygen use). The time course is about a week, but symptoms req\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has diabetes and mild psoriasis (an inflammatory disease), but does not have HIV, cancer, renal or cardiac deficiency. Psoriasis is an inflammatory disease, so this criterion is NOT met.\n  - [not met] The patient has hypothyroidism, which is a hormonal dysregulation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inferior limb pathology.\n  - [not met] The patient has spinal stenosis, which can be considered a neuromuscular pathology.\n  - [not met] The patient has a history of heavy smoking (tobacco abuse).\n  - [not met] The patient is using home oxygen, indicating oxygen dependence.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201424__NCT02203968", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient suffered blunt trauma and is at risk of significant bleeding (spleen rupture with extended intraperitoneal hemorrhage). SBP is 60/30 mmHg, which is \u2264 100 mmHg. However, there is no explici\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is in shock, but the etiology is related to bleeding (spleen rupture and hemorrhage), not purely non-bleeding causes.\n  - [met] No evidence of cardiogenic, distributive, or obstructive shock. Shock is due to hemorrhage from trauma.\n  - [met] No mention of severe head injury or any findings suggestive of TBI.\n  - [met] No evidence of GCS 3, immediate neurosurgical intervention, or unsalvageable head injury.\n  - [met] No mention of spinal cord injury.\n  - [met] No mention of hereditary or acquired coagulopathies unrelated to trauma.\n  - [met] No mention of anticoagulant medication use.\n  - [met] No evidence of moribund state or withdrawal of care.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-201519__NCT00683722", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a significant smoking history, chronic cough, progressive shortness of breath, barrel-shaped chest, and wheezing, all classic signs of moderate or severe COPD. The note does not explic\n  - [not met] There is no spirometry data provided (no FEV1/FVC ratio), so it cannot be confirmed if the post-bronchodilator FEV1/FVC ratio is < 0.7.\n  - [not met] No post-bronchodilator FEV1 % predicted value is provided in the note.\n  - [met] The patient is 66 years old and female, which is within the 40-80 years age range and meets the sex criterion.\n  - [met] The patient has smoked 1-2 packs per day for 47 years, which is well over 10 years and 10 pack-years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of asthma or other clinically relevant lung diseases besides COPD.\n  - [met] No mention of \u03b11-antitrypsin deficiency.\n  - [not met] No information on body mass is provided.\n  - [met] No evidence of active infection is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of recent COPD exacerbation or mechanical ventilation within 4 weeks.\n  - [met] No mention of other uncontrolled medical conditions.\n  - [met] No documented history of uncontrolled heart failure.\n  - [met] No mention of pulmonary hypertension due to left heart condition.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-20147__NCT00063362", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of bipolar disorder. The note does not specify whether it is Bipolar I or II, but the use of lithium carbonate (a mood stabilizer commonly used for both types) and the diagno\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the number of mood episodes in the past 12 months. Rapid cycling is not mentioned, nor is there evidence of four or more episodes. Cannot confirm this criteri\n  - [met] The patient reports feeling depressed, difficulty sleeping, anxiety, agitation, suicidal thoughts, irritability, and psychomotor agitation. These symptoms are consistent with a major depressive episod\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of intolerability to lithium, divalproex, or lamotrigine. The patient is currently taking lithium carbonate, suggesting no intolerability to lithium.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT00394550", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy (within 1-18 years age range) with clinical signs and symptoms of obstructive sleep apnea: nighttime snoring, witnessed apneas (pauses in breathing), daytime somnolenc\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior laser supraglottoplasty, adenoidectomy, tonsillectomy, stridor with cyanosis or apnea, severe respiratory distress, recurrent pneumonia, laryngeal cyst, vocal cord paralys", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201424__NCT01540318", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient suffered blunt trauma to the left hemi-abdomen after falling off his bike, which is a significant mechanism of injury for blunt torso trauma.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a motor vehicle collision, ejection, or rollover in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] The patient fell off his bike, but there is no mention of an automobile versus bicycle collision or the speed of an automobile.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a fall greater than 20 feet in height; the patient fell off his bike.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a crush injury to the torso.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of physical assault involving the abdomen.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of decreased level of consciousness or Glasgow Coma Scale score < 15.\n  - [met] This is a general criterion for blunt traumatic event with any of the following, but the specifics are not listed. Based on the context, the patient had blunt trauma and intra-abdominal injury.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is clear concern for intra-abdominal injury and planned evaluation (ultrasound and CT scan performed).\n  - [not met] The patient is hypotensive (BP: 60/30 mmHg), which would normally be an exclusion, but the criterion is met if the patient does NOT have hypotension. Therefore, this criterion is NOT met.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a GCS score \u2264 8 or decreased consciousness.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an abdominal seat belt sign.\n  - [met] There is no mention of penetrating trauma (stab or gunshot wounds).\n  - [not met] The traumatic injury occurred a week earlier, which is more than 24 hours prior to presentation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of transfer from an outside facility or prior abdominal CT scan, diagnostic peritoneal lavage, or laparotomy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of known disease processes resulting in intraperitoneal fluid (e.g., liver failure, ventriculoperitonea", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
