{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT01881659", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old, which is within the 30-64 years age range.\n  - [met] The patient presents to clinic to discuss lab results, reports no complaints, and is in general good health. There is no indication of mental incompetence.\n  - [met] The patient is able to present to clinic and discuss lab results, indicating ability to communicate with staff.\n  - [met] The patient attended a clinic visit and had a pap smear, indicating she is physically able to have a pelvic exam.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient had a pap smear, which implies previous sexual activity. She does not report no previous sexual activity.\n  - [met] There is no history of cervical cancer mentioned, and the patient has no previous medical history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous treatment for cervical pre-cancer in the last six months, and the patient has no previous medical history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hysterectomy, and the patient had a pap smear, which would not be performed after hysterectomy.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of plans to move out of the study area in the next 12 months.\n  - [not met] The patient was screened for cervical cancer recently (pap smear), but the exclusion depends on local regulations. Without knowing the local rules, this is uncertain.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT01193803", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 10 years old, which is less than 18 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the patient declined to have his medical records reviewed for research.\n  - [not met] No evidence of spondylodiscitis or spinal involvement is mentioned; the case is about the knee.\n  - [not met] No suspicion of discitis or vertebral osteomyelitis; the lesion is in the knee.\n  - [met] Clinical presentation is described: fever, lethargy, knee pain, swelling, limited motion.\n  - [not met] No mention of spinal pain.\n  - [met] There is localized tenderness and extremely limited range of motion in the right knee.\n  - [met] Fever is 38.1\u00b0C, which is just above 38\u00b0C.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):", "n_inc_assessed": 30, "n_exc_assessed": 0}
{"pair": "sigir-201424__NCT00778362", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The clinical note describes a patient with splenic rupture and extended intraperitoneal hemorrhage, which typically requires splenectomy. However, the note does not explicitly state that the patient r\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information in the clinical note indicating that the patient rejected an interview. Therefore, it is reasonable to assume the patient did not reject an interview.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT02227927", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 31-year-old woman, so she is female.\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of GERD symptoms, gastrointestinal motility disorders, or related symptoms such as nausea, vomiting, severe dyspepsia, or severe chronic constipation. The main symptoms are amenorr\n  - [met] The patient has had a workup including urine hCG (to rule out pregnancy) and TSH (to rule out thyroid dysfunction), suggesting a comprehensive evaluation to eliminate other causes of her symptoms.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of informed consent for domperidone administration in the note.\n  - [met] The patient has elevated prolactin levels.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of extrapyramidal side effects.\n  - [met] The patient has breast changes (milky nipple discharge/galactorrhea).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no history or current arrhythmias mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of bradycardia, sinus node dysfunction, heart block, or prolonged QTc.\n  - [met] No mention of clinically significant electrolyte disorders.\n  - [met] No mention of gastrointestinal hemorrhage or obstruction.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a prolactinoma. The patient has elevated prolactin, but no diagnosis of prolactinoma is stated.\n  - [met] Urine hCG is negative, so the patient is not pregnant. There is no mention of breastfeeding.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to domperidone.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201429__NCT00000430", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 51 years old, which is less than the required 60 years of age.\n  - [met] The patient has hypertension and diet-controlled diabetes but no evidence of serious illness or poor general health. She is seeking preventive care and is living independently.\n  - [not met] There is no explicit statement about willingness to participate in a 3.5 year study.\n  - [met] There is no explicit statement about ability to give informed consent, but she is seeking advice and appears to be making her own medical decisions.\n  - [met] She is living independently and attending clinic visits, suggesting she can travel to the research center.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about her bone mineral density or T-scores.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No history of cancer is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of abnormal transvaginal ultrasound.\n  - [met] No history of low-trauma hip or spine fracture is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of cerebral vascular disease is mentioned.\n  - [met] She has diet-controlled diabetes mellitus, which is allowed if there is no significant microvascular or neuropathic disease. No such complications are mentioned.\n  - [met] No information about serum creatinine.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic liver disease or alcoholism.\n  - [met] No mention of treatment with bone active agents.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 21}
{"pair": "sigir-201510__NCT00361036", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the patient's consent or willingness to participate.\n  - [met] The patient is 38 years old, which is between 30 and 50.\n  - [not met] The patient has heavy, irregular periods and pelvic pain, which are symptoms that can be caused by uterine fibroids. However, the note does not confirm that these symptoms are due to fibroids.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of fibroids or MRI confirmation in the note.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about kidney function.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about willingness or ability to undergo follow-up imaging.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a history of infertility treatment and an ectopic pregnancy, suggesting possible desire for fertility, but there is no explicit statement about current pregnancy or desire for future f\n  - [met] No history of gynecologic malignancy is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of endometrial hyperplasia.\n  - [met] No mention of adenomyosis.\n  - [met] No mention of pelvic inflammatory disease.\n  - [not met] No information about uterine volume or gestational size.\n  - [met] No mention of pedunculated subserosal fibroids.\n  - [not met] The patient complains of severe pelvic pain, which may be the dominant syndrome. However, heavy bleeding is also present. Unclear if pain is dominant.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-20145__NCT02258958", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 56-year-old female, which is over 18 years of age.\n  - [met] The patient is female, and either gender is allowed.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of resectable lung cancer or metastatic lung disease. The patient had a left mastectomy, which is typically for breast cancer.\n  - [not met] The patient underwent a left mastectomy, not one of the specified lung surgeries (segmentectomy, wedge resection, lobectomy, bilobectomy, or pneumonectomy).\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's competence to understand and sign consent documents.\n  - [met] The patient is a patient presenting to the emergency department.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any allergic or anaphylactic reaction to contrast dye, heparin, or LMWH.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being under current anticoagulation for VTE or other conditions.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about renal function or creatinine clearance.\n  - [met] No history or evidence of liver disease, ascites, or peritoneal tapping is mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient is a 56-year-old female, but there is no mention of pregnancy or plans for pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a diagnosis or treatment for VTE in the past 3 months prior to surgery.\n  - [met] There is no mention of present or previous increased risk of hemorrhage.\n  - [met] No history of heparin induced thrombocytopenia (HIT) is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT00912990", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 5-year-old boy, which is within the age range of 6 months to 17 years.\n  - [met] The patient is male. Both male and female are eligible.\n  - [met] The note is written in English and there is no indication the patient or family cannot communicate in English.\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention of Mallampati classification or normal airway. However, the patient is described as having progressively worsening dysphagia, drooling, muffled voice, and toxic appearance\n  - [not met] No explicit mention of ASA classification. The patient is acutely ill and toxic-appearing, which may suggest ASA III or higher. Cannot confirm ASA I or II.\n  - [not met] The patient is presenting to the emergency department with acute symptoms, not for an elective surgical procedure.\n  - [not met] No information about written informed consent/assent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 5 years old, which is between 6 months and 17 years.\n  - [not met] The patient is described as having airway compromise (drooling, muffled voice, toxic appearance), which suggests a difficult airway.\n  - [met] No history of previous difficult intubation or micrognathia is mentioned.\n  - [met] Parents deny trauma; no facial trauma is reported.\n  - [met] No mention of airway tumor.\n  - [not met] The clinical presentation (drooling, muffled voice, leaning forward, toxic appearance) is classic for epiglottitis.\n  - [met] No mention of retropharyngeal abscess.\n  - [met] Parents deny possibility of foreign body ingestion.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-20153__NCT02596555", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is \u226518 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of an objectively confirmed diagnosis of acute PE by imaging (CT angiography, V/Q scan, or pulmonary angiography). Symptoms are suggestive, but confirmation is not documented.\n  - [met] The patient presents with tachypnea and shortness of breath but there is no mention of hemodynamic collapse or decompensation (e.g., hypotension, shock).\n  - [not met] sPESI score is not explicitly calculated, but the patient is 65 (age>80 not met), no history of cancer, no chronic cardiopulmonary disease, not hypotensive, not tachycardic (HR not given), but has tac\n  - [not met] No imaging (CT or echo) findings of RV pressure overload/dysfunction are provided.\n  - [not met] No troponin levels or mention of myocardial injury are provided.\n  - [not met] No NT-proBNP levels or mention of RV failure are provided.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's ability to consent or understanding of the trial.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 65-year-old male, so pregnancy and lactation do not apply.\n  - [met] The patient is male, so this criterion does not apply.\n  - [met] No history of hypersensitivity to investigational products is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of participation in another clinical trial.\n  - [met] No medical or psychological condition precluding consent or trial completion is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of use of fibrinolytic agents, thrombectomy, thrombus aspiration, lysis, or cava filter.\n  - [met] No mention of anticoagulant use prior to presentation.\n  - [met] No mention of need for long-term anticoagulation or antiplatelet agents for other indications.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT01848171", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 56 years old, which is less than 75 years old.\n  - [not met] The patient exhibits classic symptoms and physical findings of hypothyroidism (cold sensitivity, fatigue, constipation, hyporeflexia, dry skin, slow movement and speech), but there is no explicit ment\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a female, but there is no mention of pregnancy or lactation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe hepatic or renal dysfunction in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of psychiatric disabilities, acute cardiovascular or cerebrovascular diseases, chronic respiratory diseases, familial hypercholesterolemia, malignancy, cholelithiasis, pancreatitis\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking lipid-lowering agents or other drugs influencing thyroid function, lipid, or bile acid metabolism.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of obviously poor compliance in the clinical note.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT02627937", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy (within the age range of older than 2 and younger than 18) with symptoms of snoring, pauses in breathing, and restlessness at night, which are suggestive of obstructiv\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of substance abuse, long-term medication use affecting sleep, craniofacial abnormalities, neuromuscular disorders, Down syndrome, cerebral palsy, mucopolysaccharidoses, Prader-Will", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT02023567", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is being assessed for the MDD group. The note describes symptoms consistent with depression (fatigue, increased sleep and appetite, difficulty concentrating, anhedonia, guilt), but does no\n  - [met] The patient is a 20-year-old female, which is within the age range (18-55) and gender criteria.\n  - [not met] The note describes symptoms consistent with MDD per DSM-IV, but does not mention a formal diagnosis or use of M.I.N.I. instrument.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about whether this is a first episode or a relapse.\n  - [met] The patient is a college student, which implies sufficient reading and writing ability to complete questionnaires and assessments.\n  - [not met] There is no information about written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has no significant past medical history and no mention of current psychopathology or neurologic conditions, substance dependence, or cognitive impairment.\n  - [met] Physical exam and labs are normal, and there is no mention of severe somatic diseases.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about whether informed consent was signed.\n  - [met] No information is provided about participation in other studies.\n  - [met] This criterion is for the healthy control group, which does not apply as the patient is being considered for the MDD group.\n  - [met] The patient is 20 years old, which is within the age range (18-55).\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201530__NCT01110304", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 47 year old male, which is \u2265 18 years-old.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of an AC joint dislocation type III or Zanca X-ray view demonstrating CC distance of 200%. The described injury is a posterior dislocation of the ulna and radius at the elbow, not \n  - [not met] The note does not specify the trauma-surgery delay. This information is not available.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a consent form being signed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of AC joint dislocation type I, II, IV, V, or VI. The injury is not an AC joint dislocation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of associated neuro-vascular damage.\n  - [met] The patient is 47 years old, which is not > 60 years-old.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an open dislocation; the note does not specify whether the dislocation is open or closed.\n  - [met] There is no mention of local skin damage.\n  - [met] There is no mention of polytrauma; only a single injury is described.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a floating shoulder.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a fracture of the ipsilateral or contralateral arm or shoulder girdle.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201410__NCT02237430", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 67-year-old woman, which is over 18 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to provide valid informed signed consent.\n  - [met] The patient underwent cardiac catheterization (CAG) via the right femoral artery. There is no mention of intracoronary measurement or imaging, but CAG is confirmed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) or stent implantation; only cardiac catheterization is described.\n  - [met] There is no mention of ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (STEMI).\n  - [not met] There is no information about multiple punctures.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active infection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of groin hematoma before the closure procedure.\n  - [not met] The patient has a pulsatile mass and bruit in the right groin, which is suggestive of a pseudoaneurysm or AV fistula in the ipsilateral groin.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cardiogenic shock.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior peripheral arterial surgery in abdomen or lower extremities.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT01577017", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, which is between 18 and 40.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of PCOS in the clinical note. The patient's amenorrhea and galactorrhea are more consistent with hyperprolactinemia.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the husband's seminal fluid analysis.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has hyperprolactinemia (elevated prolactin and galactorrhea), which is specifically listed as a medical problem in the exclusion criterion.\n  - [not met] The patient has hyperprolactinemia, which is a known cause of anovulatory infertility. Therefore, she does have another cause.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT00832026", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, so he is not an adult over the age of 21.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms suggestive of obstructive sleep apnea (nighttime snoring, pauses in breathing, daytime sleepiness), but there is no explicit diagnosis in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of unstable cardiovascular disease.\n  - [met] No information about hypertension or blood pressure is provided.\n  - [met] No mention of severe intrinsic lung disease or supplemental oxygen use.\n  - [met] No history of chronic renal insufficiency is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of hepatic insufficiency is mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy and therefore cannot be pregnant.\n  - [met] No mention of bleeding disorders or Coumadin use.\n  - [met] No other sleep disorders are mentioned; symptoms are consistent with OSA.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201427__NCT00808743", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a strong family history of familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP) with siblings having hundreds of colonic adenomas and total proctocolectomy. The patient himself has 'dozens' of small c\n  - [not met] There is no mention of duodenal adenomas or a Spigelman score in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence that the patient is incapable of signing informed consent.\n  - [met] There is no mention of active gastric or duodenal ulcer or gastrointestinal bleeding.\n  - [met] No cardiovascular disease or risk is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of congestive cardiac failure.\n  - [met] No mention of ischemic heart disease or cerebrovascular disease.\n  - [met] No mention of hypertension, hyperlipidaemia, diabetes mellitus, or family history of cardiovascular events. The family history described is for polyps, not cardiovascular events.\n  - [met] No mention of renal dysfunction.\n  - [met] No mention of liver dysfunction.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT01603875", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is experiencing neck and shoulder pain, paresthesias, tremors, spasticity, agitation, hydrophobia, and was hospitalized for acute symptoms. These findings indicate she is not healthy.\n  - [met] There is no information indicating the patient cannot visit according to the protocol. She was able to attend a campaign and visit the ER.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient was hospitalized for acute symptoms including spastic movements, agitation, hydrophobia, and difficulty swallowing, indicating an acute illness.\n  - [met] There is no mention of rabies vaccination history in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any allergies to vaccine components.\n  - [met] No evidence in the note of immunosuppressive conditions or relevant drug/blood product history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy in the note.\n  - [not met] No information about urine pregnancy test results is provided.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201423__NCT00791505", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a history of heavy smoking, chronic symptoms (barrel chest, cyanosis, tachypnea, rales, hyperinflation on chest x-ray) consistent with COPD. He presents with an acute exacerbation (inc\n  - [not met] The patient has increased cough, increased volume and purulence of sputum, and increased dyspnea, meeting the definition of acute exacerbation. He is tachypneic, but the exact respiratory rate is not \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Chest x-ray shows hyperinflation with no consolidation, so there is no evidence of pneumonia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of antibiotic treatment in the previous ten days.\n  - [met] No information is provided about prior inclusion in the study.\n  - [met] No history of allergy to quinolones or trimethoprim sulfamethoxazole is mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient is a 63-year-old man, so pregnancy or breastfeeding does not apply.\n  - [met] The patient has diabetes and hypothyroidism, but there is no mention of severe heart, liver, or kidney disease.\n  - [met] No known immunodeficiency is mentioned.\n  - [met] No digestive disease affecting drug absorption is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-20156__NCT01227499", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has symptoms highly suggestive of hyperthyroidism (weight loss, sweating, increased appetite, palpitations, hyperreflexia, exophthalmia). There is no mention of prior diagnosis or treatmen\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's willingness to be enrolled.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information indicating the patient is unwilling.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking antithyroid drugs or beta blockers.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking foods or medicine rich in iodine in the past 8 weeks.\n  - [met] The patient is a woman, but there is no mention of pregnancy or lactation.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201512__NCT02457546", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 44 years old (\u226518), but there is no mention of undergoing craniotomy/craniectomy for pathological processes in the supratentorial region or posterior fossa.\n  - [not met] No information about willingness to participate or consent.\n  - [not met] No information about surgical wound classification.\n  - [not met] No information about the cuff of native dura or surgeon's judgment.\n  - [not met] Clear fluid dripping from the nose suggests CSF leakage, but there is no mention of intra-operative CSF leakage following primary dural closure or after Valsalva maneuver.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of recent surgery; the dural lesion is from trauma.\n  - [met] No mention of chemotherapy.\n  - [met] No mention of radiation therapy.\n  - [met] No mention of previous craniotomy/craniectomy.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to investigational product.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to FD&C Blue #1 dye.\n  - [not met] Patient has fever and nuchal rigidity, which are signs of infection, but unclear if infection is at surgical site.\n  - [not met] Patient has fever and nuchal rigidity, which strongly suggest infection (possibly meningitis).", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 24}
{"pair": "sigir-20147__NCT00602537", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of bipolar disorder, but the note does not specify bipolar II or whether DSM-IV criteria are met. However, lithium carbonate is commonly used for bipolar disorder, and there \n  - [met] The patient reports feeling depressed, difficulty sleeping, anxiety, agitation, irritability, and suicidal thoughts, which are consistent with a major depressive episode per DSM-IV. However, the note \n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's HAM-D score in the note.\n  - [met] The patient is taking lithium carbonate and zolpidem, with no mention of MAOI use.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness to use birth control.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of mania in the note.\n  - [met] The patient has bipolar disorder and depressive symptoms, with no mention of another primary Axis I diagnosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of alcohol or drug dependence.\n  - [met] The patient is currently taking lithium carbonate, suggesting no contraindication to lithium. No mention of venlafaxine contraindication.\n  - [met] The patient is obese, but there is no mention of unstable medical conditions such as thyroid disease, hypertension, or angina.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy or breastfeeding.\n  - [not met] The patient is experiencing suicidal thoughts, which is explicitly stated.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient requires hospitalization.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201512__NCT01522105", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is 44 years old, which is outside the age range (>3 months and <16 years).\n  - [met] Patient has symptoms consistent with bacterial meningitis (headache, fever, nuchal rigidity, clear fluid from nose after skull fracture).\n  - [not met] No information provided about written parental or legal consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information about Gram-negative bacteria in CSF.\n  - [met] No information about creatinine clearance.\n  - [met] No information about creatinine phosphokinase levels.\n  - [met] No information about allergy or hypersensitivity to daptomycin.\n  - [met] No mention of significant cardiovascular, pulmonary, renal, hepatic, gastrointestinal, endocrine, hematologic, autoimmune disease, or primary immunodeficiency.\n  - [met] No information about height and weight percentiles.\n  - [met] No history or current muscular disease mentioned.\n  - [met] Patient has a skull fracture and clear fluid from nose, suggesting disruption of blood brain barrier, but no underlying neurological disease is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201419__NCT00816634", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note describes progressive dysphagia and weight loss, which are suggestive of esophageal cancer, but there is no mention of histological confirmation or metastatic/recurrent squamous cell carcinom\n  - [met] The patient is 52 years old, which is greater than 18 years.\n  - [not met] ECOG performance status is not specified. The patient has significant weight loss and progressive dysphagia, but no explicit mention of performance status.\n  - [not met] No mention of measurable lesions by RECIST criteria in the note.\n  - [met] Life expectancy is not specified, but the patient has progressive symptoms. No evidence to suggest life expectancy < 3 months.\n  - [not met] No information about prior adjuvant chemotherapy.\n  - [not met] No information about previous palliative chemotherapy.\n  - [not met] No information about prior radiotherapy.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of other tumor types such as adenocarcinoma or small cell carcinoma. Esophageal cancer is suspected.\n  - [met] No evidence of CNS metastasis in the note.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to any drug in the chemotherapy regimen.\n  - [met] No information about previous adjuvant treatment with 5-FU, cisplatin, capecitabine or paclitaxel.\n  - [met] No evidence of serious gastrointestinal bleeding.\n  - [met] No mention of history of another malignancy within the last five years.\n  - [met] No mention of clinically significant cardiac disease or recent myocardial infarction.\n  - [met] No mention of serious pulmonary conditions or chronic lung disease.", "n_inc_assessed": 12, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT02177032", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 28-year-old female, which is \u2265 1 years of age.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about written consent.\n  - [not met] The patient is currently hospitalized with severe symptoms (spastic movements, hydrophobia, difficulty swallowing, agitation), indicating she is not in good health.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about compliance with study procedures; her current severe symptoms may impair compliance.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as having increasing agitation and anxiety, but no clear diagnosis of behavioral or cognitive impairment or psychiatric disease.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about inability to comprehend or follow study procedures, but her current severe symptoms may impair this.\n  - [not met] The patient has an ongoing illness (severe neurological symptoms, hydrophobia, likely rabies), which may pose additional risk.\n  - [met] The patient is 28 years old, so this criterion does not apply.\n  - [met] No history of malignancy is mentioned.\n  - [met] No known or suspected immune system impairment is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No information about contraceptive use is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about birth control refusal is provided.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 21}
{"pair": "sigir-201510__NCT02197936", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 38-year-old premenopausal woman (age 20-45). She has symptoms suggestive of adenomyosis (severe premenstrual and menstrual pelvic pain, heavy, irregular periods, and spotting), but th\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 38 years old and therefore not postmenopausal.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current pregnancy. Past ectopic pregnancy is noted, but not current.\n  - [met] There is no mention of gynecological cancer in the patient's history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of GnRH analog therapy or systemic hormone therapy in the last three months.\n  - [met] There is no mention of endometriosis in the patient's history.\n  - [met] There is no mention of uterine fibroids in the patient's history.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201528__NCT01145157", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is an 8-year-old boy, which means he is not of legal age and is likely not skeletally mature.\n  - [not met] No evidence of degenerative or inflammatory joint disease requiring total knee arthroplasty; patient presents with acute pain and swelling, likely due to infection or tick bite.\n  - [not met] No information provided about preoperative medical clearance or comorbidities; cannot assess.\n  - [not met] No information about availability for follow-up; cannot assess.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information about inability to have MRI scan; cannot assess.\n  - [met] No mention of cardiac pacemaker.\n  - [met] No mention of surgical clips in head.\n  - [met] No mention of artificial heart valves.\n  - [met] No mention of electronic inner ear implants.\n  - [met] No mention of metal fragments in eyes.\n  - [met] No mention of electronic stimulators.\n  - [met] No mention of implanted pumps.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201529__NCT02317913", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has persistent fever (>=5 days), bilateral conjunctival congestion (red eyes with no discharge), changes of lips and oral cavity (strawberry tongue, red and cracked lips), polymorphous exa\n  - [met] The patient has had a persistent fever for the past week (7 days), which meets the criterion of fever persisting 5 days or longer.\n  - [met] The patient has 'the whites of both eyes are red with no discharge,' which is consistent with bilateral conjunctival congestion.\n  - [met] Physical examination reveals strawberry red tongue and red and cracked lips, which are changes of lips and oral cavity.\n  - [met] The patient has an erythematous rash on the trunk, which is consistent with polymorphous exanthema.\n  - [met] The patient has swollen red hands, which is a change of peripheral extremities.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of acute nonpurulent cervical lymphadenopathy in the note. Cannot confirm this criterion.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient meets the recruited criteria (KD diagnostic criteria), so this exclusion criterion is NOT met (i.e., patient is not excluded).", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT00233194", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 10-year-old boy, which means he is over the age of 9 and likely able to provide assent if cognitively typical. No evidence of cognitive impairment is mentioned.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about whether a parent or guardian has signed informed consent.\n  - [not met] The patient is not described as a healthy volunteer, nor is there mention of being scheduled for an adenotonsillectomy.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about referral by an otolaryngologist or scheduling for adenotonsillectomy.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of mental or physical limitations that would prevent proper interpretation of neurobehavioral tests.\n  - [met] No medical history is described that could confound EEG or behavioral data (e.g., epilepsy, psychiatric diagnoses, head trauma, or chronic medication use).\n  - [met] There is no mention of current or past treatment by a physician or surgical treatment for SDB.\n  - [met] No known medical condition with high risk of SDB or excessive daytime sleepiness (e.g., Pierre Robin syndrome, Down syndrome, neuromuscular disorders, narcolepsy) is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about scheduling of polysomnography, MSLT, or neurobehavioral testing.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about physician determination that sleep testing is required before surgery.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about prior enrollment of a sibling.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about expected access to University of Michigan facilities or further surgery.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT02589925", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 89 years old, which is above the inclusion age range of 35-75 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of idiopathic Parkinson's disease (PD) or probable Parkinson's disease dementia (PDD). The symptoms described are consistent with dementia but not specifically PDD.\n  - [not met] No MMSE score is provided. The patient has severe cognitive impairment, but without a score, this cannot be confirmed.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a history of idiopathic PD or duration of motor symptoms.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about Hoehn and Yahr stage or severity of PD.\n  - [not met] No UPDRS subset III score or equivalent motor assessment is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about levodopa response or a levodopa challenge test.\n  - [not met] No information about timing of PDD symptom onset relative to PD symptoms.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has an acute confusional state and significant cognitive impairment, which may be consistent with delirium or other significant psychiatric problems.\n  - [met] No mention of current drug or alcohol abuse.\n  - [met] No history of recurrent or unprovoked seizures is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of prior movement disorder treatments involving intracranial surgery or device implantation.\n  - [met] No history of neurostimulation intolerance is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No significant medical condition likely to interfere with study procedures or terminal illness with survival <12 months is mentioned, but the patient's severe dementia and functional dependence may be\n  - [met] No mention of participation in another trial.\n  - [met] Patient is male, so pregnancy, breast-feeding, or contraception are not applicable.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201510__NCT02201719", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 38 year old woman, which falls within the 30-50 years age range and is likely premenopausal given her symptoms and age.\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the clinical note that the patient is scheduled for vaginal, abdominal, or laparoscopic total hysterectomy.\n  - [met] The patient reports heavy, irregular periods (bleeding disorders), severe premenstrual and menstrual pelvic pain (chronic pelvic pain, dysmenorrhoea), and occasional spotting between periods. She meet\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the junction zone being definable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 38 years old and has regular menstrual symptoms, indicating she is not postmenopausal.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current pregnancy; past ectopic pregnancy is noted but not current.\n  - [met] There is no mention of gynecological cancer in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of GnRH analog therapy or systemic hormone therapy in the last three months.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the junctional zone being unidentifiable.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT02139384", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the note that the patient has been intubated.\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old, which is within the 1 day to 21 years age range.\n  - [not met] The patient presents to the ER with symptoms and chest x-ray findings consistent with suspected pneumonia, but there is no mention of admission to the LLUCH PICU.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the patient has received antibiotics or for how long.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the patient has been intubated or for how long.\n  - [met] The note is in English and there is no indication that the patient or family cannot speak English or Spanish.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about antibiotic administration, so it cannot be determined if the patient has received antibiotics for greater than 12 hours.\n  - [not met] There is no information about intubation status or duration.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to tolerate non-bronchoscopic bronchoalveolar lavage.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT01773772", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 31-year-old woman, not in early to mid-puberty (Tanner 1-3).\n  - [not met] The patient had menarche at age 14 and has had normal periods since then, so she is not premenarcheal.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about BMI or weight percentile.\n  - [met] Urine hCG is negative, indicating the patient is not pregnant.\n  - [met] No evidence of inability to comprehend the study; patient is able to communicate and express desire for pregnancy.\n  - [met] No evidence of hyperandrogenism (no hirsutism or elevated testosterone mentioned).\n  - [met] No history of allergy to progesterone is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No information about hemoglobin or hematocrit.\n  - [not met] No information about sodium, potassium, or bicarbonate.\n  - [not met] No information about creatinine, hepatic transaminases, or alkaline phosphatase.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT02339896", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 28-year-old female, which is outside the 1-15 years age range specified for healthy children.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about signed informed consent from parents. Additionally, the patient is an adult, so parental consent is not applicable.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about willingness to participate, ability to receive vaccination, or blood sample collection. The patient is hospitalized for acute symptoms.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior rabies vaccination, equine/human serum administration, or vaccine allergy in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of immunosuppressive conditions, HIV infection, transplantation, chronic renal failure, or use of steroids/immunosuppressive drugs.\n  - [met] There is no mention of anti-malarial drug use within the previous two months or blood product administration within the previous three months.\n  - [met] The patient is a 28-year-old female, not an adolescent. There is no mention of a urine pregnancy test, but the criterion applies to female adolescents.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20149__NCT00288938", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 43-year-old woman, not an infant or child.\n  - [not met] The patient is 43 years old, which is older than 5 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a large congenital melanocytic nevus greater than 20 cm or 8 cm on the scalp. Lesions described are small, with the largest being 4 mm.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about an outside referring physician.\n  - [met] The patient is an adult (43 years old).\n  - [met] The patient is 43 years old, which is greater than 18 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient having 100 or more melanocytic nevi greater than 2 mm. Only 'multiple' lesions are described.\n  - [met] The patient has at least one lesion that is 4 mm in diameter, but it is not specified as a melanocytic nevus. However, given the context (dermatology, pigmented lesions), it is reasonable to assume at\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No diagnosis of a genetic syndrome associated with multiple lentigines or nevi is mentioned.\n  - [met] No information is provided about family history of melanoma or familial atypical mole-melanoma syndrome.\n  - [met] No diagnosis of cancer-associated syndrome is mentioned.\n  - [met] No information is provided about inability to tolerate surgical procedures.\n  - [met] No information is provided about willingness to consider elective biopsy.", "n_inc_assessed": 15, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201514__NCT01181154", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 27 years old, which is >18 years.\n  - [not met] Patient has Hb < 10 g/dL (9.0 and 8.9), reticulocyte count > 120 x 10^9/L (180 x 10^9/L), signs of hemolysis (elevated LDH, presence of hemosiderin in urine, polychromasia, anisocytosis, poikilocytosi\n  - [not met] No information about prior corticosteroid treatment or whether this is first episode of AIHA. The patient is already receiving iron supplementation, but no mention of corticosteroids.\n  - [met] Platelet count is 119 and 108 x 10^9/L, which is >30 x 10^9/L. No explicit mention of autoimmune thrombocytopenia (Evans' syndrome), but if present, platelet count would be eligible.\n  - [not met] No information about serum gammaglobulin levels.\n  - [not met] No information about lymph node status or CT scan.\n  - [not met] No information about contraception use.\n  - [not met] Patient is pregnant (11 weeks gestation), so cannot have a negative pregnancy test.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of previous rituximab treatment.\n  - [met] No mention of corticosteroid treatment or AIHA relapse. Patient is not treated with corticosteroids for more than 6 weeks as far as can be determined.\n  - [met] No mention of ongoing immunosuppressive therapy other than corticosteroids.\n  - [met] No mention of Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma or chronic lymphoid leukemia.\n  - [met] No mention of previous or concomitant malignancy.\n  - [met] No mention of SLE or other autoimmune disorder with extra-hematological manifestation.\n  - [met] No mention of other congenital or acquired hemolytic anemia (except thalassemia trait or heterozygous sickle cell anemia).\n  - [met] DAT is negative, which meets exclusion (should not have negative DAT).", "n_inc_assessed": 9, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT01540318", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient sustained blunt torso trauma from a car accident, which is a significant mechanism of injury.\n  - [not met] The note does not specify the speed of the collision, ejection, or rollover.\n  - [not met] No mention of automobile versus pedestrian/bicycle or speed > 25 mph.\n  - [not met] No mention of a fall from height.\n  - [not met] No mention of crush injury to the torso.\n  - [not met] No mention of physical assault involving the abdomen.\n  - [not met] Patient is fully awake and alert, so no decreased level of consciousness.\n  - [not met] This is a header criterion; specifics are covered in subsequent criteria.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is concern for intra-abdominal injury based on physical exam.\n  - [met] Blood pressure is 134/74 mm Hg, which is not hypotensive for age.\n  - [met] Patient is fully awake and alert, so GCS > 8.\n  - [met] No mention of abdominal seat belt sign; patient was not wearing a seat belt.\n  - [met] No mention of penetrating trauma (stab or gunshot wounds).\n  - [met] Traumatic injury occurred recently (car accident, admitted to ER), not >24 hours prior.\n  - [met] No mention of transfer from outside facility or prior abdominal CT, lavage, or laparotomy.\n  - [met] No mention of known disease processes resulting in intraperitoneal fluid (e.g., liver failure, VP shunt).", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT00282269", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a GCS of 6 (\u22648), but there is no CT scan performed, so we cannot confirm an abnormal CT scan (intracranial hemorrhage, cerebral edema, or diffuse axonal injury). The motor score is not\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old, which is between 1 and 16 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient being mechanically ventilated.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about randomization timing relative to injury.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a penetrating brain injury; the injury was due to a fall.\n  - [met] The patient does not have fixed dilated pupils (pupils were asymmetrical, not fixed/dilated) and GCS is 6, not 3.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cervical spinal cord injury.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pre-existing neurodevelopmental disability.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an acute isolated epidural hematoma or expectation of rapid recovery after surgical removal.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a post-traumatic seizure.\n  - [met] The patient's blood pressure is elevated (155/98), not hypotensive, and there is no mention of refractory shock.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201518__NCT00664339", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 65-year-old male, which meets the age and sex requirement. He has symptoms consistent with severe congestive heart failure (orthopnea, worsening exertional dyspnea, bibasilar crackles\n  - [met] The patient has definite evidence of underlying heart failure as shown by multiple symptoms (orthopnea, bibasilar crackles, pitting edema, JVD).\n  - [met] The patient has orthopnea (difficulty breathing when lying flat, uses extra pillows).\n  - [not met] No mention of X-ray findings or wedge pressure.\n  - [not met] No mention of recent prior hospitalization for CHF.\n  - [not met] No echocardiography data provided.\n  - [not met] No mention of non-invasive ventilation or SaO2.\n  - [met] Patient has bibasilar lung crackles, which may correspond to 'wet rales in at least the lower half of the lung fields.'\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of concomitant infective disease.\n  - [met] No evidence of multi-organ failure, terminal disease, or contraindications to follow-up/vaccination.\n  - [met] No evidence of unstable coronary artery disease, recent bypass, angioplasty, or CHF complicating MI requiring urgent intervention.\n  - [met] No evidence that mechanical ventilation was required on admission.\n  - [met] No mention of prior vaccinations.\n  - [met] Patient is male, so pregnancy does not apply.\n  - [met] No evidence that the patient is unable or refused to give written informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 9, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT02136654", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 64-year-old female, which is older than 19 years.\n  - [met] The patient has a diagnosis of diabetes mellitus and is non-compliant with diabetes medication, indicating she is prescribed at least one medication to control diabetes.\n  - [met] The note states 'persistently elevated HbA1c', which strongly suggests A1C \u22657% in the past year.\n  - [not met] The patient is 'reluctant to see a nutritionist' and 'not compliant', suggesting unwillingness or inability to attend education, dietician, and peer sessions.\n  - [met] There is no information about the patient's ability to provide informed consent; however, there is no evidence of cognitive impairment.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ethnicity or language ability.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a life-limiting illness with prognosis <12 months.\n  - [met] The patient is not compliant with exercise, but there is no evidence of physical inability to exercise.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recurrent severe hypoglycemia or hypoglycemic unawareness.\n  - [met] There is no information about family members or household status.\n  - [met] The patient is a 64-year-old female, but there is no mention of pregnancy or gestational diabetes.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201423__NCT01636401", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has clinical features highly suggestive of COPD (heavy smoking history, chronic symptoms, barrel chest, hyperinflation on chest x-ray). However, there is no spirometry data (postbronchodil\n  - [met] The patient is a current or former heavy smoker, which strongly suggests a smoking history of at least 10 pack-years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history or current diagnosis of asthma.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hospitalization for an acute COPD exacerbation within the past 3 months.\n  - [not met] The patient is currently presenting with symptoms consistent with a respiratory tract infection or COPD exacerbation (productive cough, purulent sputum, increased oxygen requirement) that began about \n  - [met] There is no mention of other clinically significant respiratory conditions besides COPD.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20145__NCT00077805", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of acute ischemic stroke or any neuroradiologic study (CT or MRI) showing non-hemorrhagic stroke. The patient's presentation is related to post-mastectomy status, shortness of brea\n  - [not met] No evidence of stroke symptoms or timing of stroke onset is provided. The patient's symptoms are not consistent with acute stroke.\n  - [not met] No mention of significant motor impairment of the leg or NIHSS score. The only leg-related finding is right calf tenderness, which may suggest DVT, not motor impairment.\n  - [not met] The patient has been bedridden for two weeks, but it is not specified whether this is due to inability to walk without assistance or due to post-surgical recovery. There is no explicit mention of inab\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 56-year-old female, but there is no information about pregnancy, breastfeeding, or contraception status.\n  - [not met] The patient has clinical evidence suggestive of VTE (right calf tenderness, shortness of breath, elevated D-dimer), which is consistent with possible DVT/PE.\n  - [met] No evidence of active bleeding is reported. The surgical incision shows no bleeding.\n  - [met] No history or evidence of intracranial hemorrhage is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of spinal or epidural analgesia or lumbar puncture within the preceding 24 hours.\n  - [met] No mention of thrombolytic therapy (tPA) or intra-arterial thrombolytic therapy.\n  - [met] No evidence of coma or altered mental status. No NIHSS score provided, but the patient is alert and presenting complaints.\n  - [met] No mention of cerebral aneurysm or arteriovenous malformation.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 22}
{"pair": "sigir-20149__NCT00476905", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 43-year-old woman, which means she is female and over 18 years of age.\n  - [met] The patient is visiting her dermatologist for lesions and is undergoing an examination of her skin.\n  - [met] The patient has multiple small, soft, pedunculated lesions, which are most consistent with benign lesions (likely skin tags).\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention that the lesions warrant a biopsy.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the patient signed an informed consent document.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has lesions that fit into the benign lesions category, so she does not have an absence of such lesions.\n  - [not met] It is not stated whether the lesions need a biopsy or not.\n  - [not met] There is no information about whether the patient signed informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT00823563", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient underwent coronary angiography, but it was performed emergently due to acute chest pain and suspicion of acute coronary syndrome, not as an elective procedure for clinical suspicion of chr\n  - [met] The patient presented with chest pain radiating to the left shoulder and jaw, and shortness of breath, which are anginal equivalents.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is symptomatic with chest pain and shortness of breath.\n  - [met] No evidence or mention of heart transplant.\n  - [met] No evidence or mention of coronary artery bypass grafting.\n  - [met] Patient is 82 years old, well above 18.\n  - [not met] Patient has chronic renal insufficiency, but creatinine is not provided. Chronic renal insufficiency suggests likely creatinine >1.5, but this is not certain.\n  - [not met] Patient has ST-segment elevations, elevated troponin, and segmental left ventricular dysfunction (EF mildly impaired), consistent with acute coronary syndrome (STEMI) and abnormal EF (<55%).\n  - [met] No mention of pulmonary hypertension or aortic stenosis as alternative explanations for chest pain.\n  - [met] No mention of adverse reactions to acetylcholine, nitroglycerin, adenosine, or heparin.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT01058161", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has 2 weeks of joint pain, swelling, and stiffness in multiple joints, which is suggestive of possible rheumatoid polyarthritis. However, there is no explicit mention of a GP's suspicion o\n  - [not met] The patient reports joint stiffness but there is no explicit mention of morning stiffness lasting at least 15 minutes.\n  - [not met] The patient has arthralgias/arthritis in at least three joints (knees, hips, right elbow, right ankle), but there is no mention of hand involvement.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about rheumatoid factor or anti-CCP antibodies.\n  - [not met] No radiological findings are mentioned.\n  - [not met] No evidence or mention of spondylitis or axial/peripheral involvement consistent with stiffening spondylitis.\n  - [not met] No mention of lumbago, lumbar stiffness, HLA allele, or sacroiliitis.\n  - [not met] No mention of positive ANA or specific antibodies, nor a diagnosis of connective tissue disease.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of claustrophobia.\n  - [met] No mention of metallic foreign bodies.\n  - [met] No mention of pacemaker or pregnancy.\n  - [met] No mention of being a parturient or breastfeeding.", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201427__NCT01483144", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has dozens of small colonic polyps (benign adenomas) in rectosigmoid and strong family history of FAP (siblings with hundreds of adenomas and proctocolectomy). This is consistent with phenotyp\n  - [not met] No mention of APC mutation testing or result in the note.\n  - [not met] Patient has 'dozens' of polyps, not 'hundreds to thousands' as required for classical FAP phenotype. Siblings had hundreds, but patient does not meet this threshold.\n  - [met] Patient underwent sigmoidoscopy and colonoscopy recently (timing not specified, but context suggests recent).\n  - [met] Patient has intact colon/rectum with polyposis; prophylactic surgery is being considered (implied by family history and findings).\n  - [met] Patient has rectosigmoid polyposis (dozens of polyps).\n  - [not met] Patient has not had colectomy or proctocolectomy; this criterion is not applicable.\n  - [met] Patient has 'dozens' of polyps, which may correspond to Stage 3 (>25 polyps), but size information is limited (all are small, <5mm).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):", "n_inc_assessed": 30, "n_exc_assessed": 0}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT01579942", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with symptoms consistent with major depressive disorder (fatigue, increased sleep and appetite, anhedonia, guilt, difficulty concentrating), but there is no explicit diagnosis of \n  - [met] The patient is a 20-year-old female, which is within the 18-55 age range.\n  - [not met] Symptoms are consistent with MDD, but there is no explicit mention of a structured diagnostic interview (SCID) or formal diagnosis.\n  - [not met] No HAM-D17 score is provided in the note.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's ability to provide informed consent.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about handedness, vision, or hearing.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence of other primary psychiatric diagnoses or psychotic features.\n  - [met] No mention of substance use disorder.\n  - [met] No mention of sensory deficits such as deafness or blindness.\n  - [met] No evidence of severe or unstable medical illness, neurological disorders, or history of head injury.\n  - [not met] The patient is a 20-year-old female, but there is no information about pregnancy, nursing, or contraception.\n  - [met] Physical exam and laboratory tests are within normal limits.\n  - [met] The patient is a 20-year-old female, which is within the 18-55 age range.\n  - [not met] The patient likely meets criteria for MDD, so this exclusion for healthy controls does not apply.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201411__NCT00823563", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention that the patient was referred for elective coronary angiography or that there is a reasonable clinical suspicion of coronary ischemia. The presentation is acute pain in the right a\n  - [not met] The patient presents with excruciating right arm pain, which could be considered an anginal equivalent if brought on by exertion or stress, but there is no mention of a trigger. The pain started sudde\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is symptomatic with excruciating right arm pain.\n  - [met] No history of heart transplant is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of coronary artery bypass grafting is mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient is 40 years old.\n  - [met] No mention of renal insufficiency or creatinine levels.\n  - [met] No evidence of acute coronary syndrome, Tako-tsubo, abnormal EF, cardiogenic shock, or recent VT/VF is provided. The patient is hypotensive and tachycardic, but there is no diagnosis of these conditio\n  - [met] No mention of another likely explanation for chest pain such as pulmonary hypertension or aortic stenosis.\n  - [met] No history of adverse reaction to study medications is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT01748162", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 5-year-old boy, which falls within the pediatric population age range of 6 months to 15 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient having 2 or more episodes of croup in a 12 month period. Only the current episode is described.\n  - [not met] The patient presents with progressively worsening dysphagia, drooling, fever, vocal changes, muffled 'hot potato' voice, and toxic appearance. There is no mention of inspiratory stridor, barking cough\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of grade 3 or 4 subglottic stenosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of subglottic hemangioma.\n  - [met] There is no mention of posterior laryngeal cleft.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recurrent respiratory papillomatosis.\n  - [met] There is no mention of external compression such as innominate artery compression, mediastinal mass, or double aortic arch.\n  - [not met] The patient's symptoms (progressive dysphagia, drooling, fever, muffled voice, toxic appearance, leaning forward) are classic for epiglottitis, which is specifically listed as an exclusion. These symp\n  - [met] There is no mention of tracheomalacia or bronchomalacia severe enough to cause respiratory distress.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current steroid therapy for a previously diagnosed condition.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201518__NCT02347722", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with symptoms consistent with heart failure (shortness of breath on exertion, orthopnea, bibasilar crackles, pitting edema, jugular venous distension). However, there is no explic\n  - [met] The patient has symptoms and signs consistent with congestive heart failure and meets modified Framingham criteria (see below).\n  - [met] Patient has at least 2 major criteria (orthopnea/paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea, neck vein distention, rales/crackles) and at least 2 minor criteria (bilateral ankle edema, dyspnea on exertion).\n  - [not met] This is a header criterion; see individual major criteria below.\n  - [met] Patient reports orthopnea (difficulty breathing when lying flat, uses extra pillows).\n  - [met] Physical exam shows jugular venous distension (neck vein distention).\n  - [met] Bibasilar lung crackles are present; however, the note does not specify >10 cm from base, but crackles are a major criterion.\n  - [not met] No mention of acute pulmonary edema.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence that the patient is unable to provide a blood sample.\n  - [met] No evidence that the patient is unable to provide consent.\n  - [met] No mention of life expectancy <6 months or major co-morbidities.\n  - [met] No mention of other significant disease or disorder that would put the patient at risk or influence trial participation.\n  - [met] No mention of participation in another research trial in the past 30 days.", "n_inc_assessed": 20, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201518__NCT02620384", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [not met] The note does not explicitly state that the patient is currently hospitalized for chronic congestive heart failure or the timing of admission.\n  - [not met] There is no information about duration of heart failure treatment, NYHA class, or ejection fraction/echocardiogram findings.\n  - [met] The patient has symptoms and signs of decompensated heart failure (orthopnea, bibasilar crackles, pitting edema, JVD), which are consistent with clinical decompensated heart failure and extracellular \n  - [not met] No information is provided about timing of study medication or IV diuretics.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information about mean arterial pressure or hypotension.\n  - [met] No information about creatinine clearance or serum creatinine.\n  - [met] No information about serum sodium.\n  - [met] No information about serum potassium.\n  - [met] No mention of adverse reaction to metolazone.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to take oral medications.\n  - [met] No mention of severe aortic stenosis.\n  - [met] No mention of hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201422__NCT00674726", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with abdominal pain that localizes to the right lower quadrant, has rebound tenderness, and ultrasound shows a markedly edematous appendix. These findings are classic for acute ap\n  - [not met] There is no mention of diarrhea or vomiting, and the clinical findings and imaging are consistent with appendicitis, not gastroenteritis.\n  - [not met] The patient is 15 years old, not older than 15 years. The criterion requires patients to be older than 15, so this is not met.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient does not have other acute abdominal diseases; the findings are specific for acute appendicitis.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201519__NCT01314807", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 66 years old, which is within the 40-80 years old range.\n  - [not met] The patient has a significant smoking history (1-2 packs/day for 47 years = 47-94 pack-years) and symptoms consistent with COPD (chronic cough, progressive shortness of breath, barrel chest, wheezing)\n  - [not met] This criterion is for smoking controls with no COPD. The patient likely has COPD based on symptoms and exam, so this is not met.\n  - [not met] This criterion is for non-smoking controls with <1 pack year. The patient has a heavy smoking history, so this is not met.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of a respiratory disorder other than COPD is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of \u03b11-antitrypsin deficiency.\n  - [met] No known history of significant inflammatory disease other than COPD is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of a COPD exacerbation within the last 4 weeks. The patient has progressive symptoms but no acute exacerbation described.\n  - [met] No mention of lung surgery.\n  - [met] No mention of recent cancer diagnosis.\n  - [met] No mention of oral corticosteroid therapy in the last 6 weeks.\n  - [met] No mention of significant cardiovascular comorbidity.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201522__NCT01866020", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is greater than 18.\n  - [met] Sputum culture revealed an organism with septated, low-angle branching hyphae and straight, parallel walls, which is characteristic of Aspergillus species.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a galactomannan test or result in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about informed consent.\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is not less than 18.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT00540527", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient was hospitalized for cryptogenic stroke with sudden focal neurological deficit, as implied by the need for thrombolytic therapy and resolution of symptoms.\n  - [met] The note states thrombolytic therapy was given with resolution of symptoms, implying treatment was initiated within the recommended time window. Exact timing is not specified, but clinical practice su\n  - [met] Patient is 72 years old, which is between 18 and 80 years.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of pre-existing disability or modified Rankin scale score of 2-4 prior to stroke.\n  - [met] No mention of coma at onset.\n  - [met] No mention of severe stroke or NIHSS>25; symptoms resolved after thrombolytic therapy.\n  - [met] Patient had resolution of symptoms after thrombolytic therapy, but at presentation had a stroke requiring treatment. The current symptoms are minor and transient, but the initial event was not describ\n  - [met] No mention of seizure at onset.\n  - [met] CT scan was negative for brain hemorrhage and no mention of subarachnoid hemorrhage.\n  - [met] No history or suspicion of intracranial hemorrhage; CT scan was negative.\n  - [met] No mention of previous CNS damage, neoplasm, aneurysm, or intracranial/spinal surgery.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 27}
{"pair": "sigir-201526__NCT01860690", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note states the patient is admitted for a non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy.\n  - [met] The patient has obesity and a history of infertility, but no acute illnesses or significant comorbidities are mentioned. However, 'healthy' is subjective; in clinical trials, it often means no major c\n  - [met] There is no mention of hemodynamic instability (e.g., no hypotension, tachycardia, or shock). The patient is admitted for a non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy, which is typically stable.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior ectopic pregnancies. This appears to be her first (G1P0A0, first pregnancy).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of hemodynamic instability is present in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of abnormal liver or kidney function in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any allergy to MTX (methotrexate) or any drug allergies.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201522__NCT01430663", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 65-year-old male with a history of tuberculosis and current symptoms/signs suggestive of pulmonary aspergillosis (productive cough with blood, chest X-ray and CT findings, and sputum \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about informed consent, so we cannot determine whether the patient lacks informed consent. In the absence of evidence to the contrary, we assume the exclusion crite", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201522__NCT02234739", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a history of tuberculosis and now presents with a productive cough with blood, a round mass in a lung cavity, and sputum culture showing septated, low-angle branching hyphae (suggestiv\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient using voriconazole, itraconazole, amphotericin B, caspofungin, or micafungin within the last 4 weeks.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a known allergy to voriconazole.\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe impairment of liver or kidney function.\n  - [met] There is no mention of septic shock.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness to sign informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201522__NCT01615809", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 65 years old, which is outside the 3-18 year age range.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of myeloblastic or lymphoblastic acute leukemia or chemotherapy.\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent or assent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has probable or proven invasive pulmonary fungal infection: radiology shows a mass in a cavity, and sputum culture shows septated, low-angle branching hyphae (suggestive of Aspergillus).\n  - [met] No mention of chronic renal impairment or serum creatinine levels.\n  - [met] No mention of severe hepatic impairment.\n  - [met] No mention of moderate-severe asthma or pharmacological treatment for asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of antifungal treatment for filamentous fungi in the last 4 weeks.\n  - [met] No mention of participation in a clinical trial in the last 4 weeks.\n  - [met] No mention of mental retardation.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy or hypersensitivity to the study drug or its excipients.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-201526__NCT00194272", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is admitted for a non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy, which is a confirmed diagnosis.\n  - [not met] No mention of D&E (dilation and evacuation) or frozen pathology in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of VABRA (vacuum aspiration) or pathologic evaluation in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of ultrasound findings or visualization of gestational sac, yolk sac, or fetal pole.\n  - [met] No mention of hemodynamic instability or hemoperitoneum; patient is admitted for non-ruptured ectopic pregnancy, suggesting stability.\n  - [met] Laparoscopy has been performed in the past for adhesions, but not for the current ectopic pregnancy. The note says laparoscopy has not yet been performed for this episode.\n  - [not met] No information about ability to return for follow-up care.\n  - [not met] No laboratory data provided regarding renal or liver function.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of breastfeeding.\n  - [met] No laboratory evidence or mention of immunodeficiency.\n  - [met] No mention of alcoholism or chronic liver disease.\n  - [met] No mention of NSAID use.\n  - [met] No mention of blood dyscrasia, leukopenia, thrombocytopenia, or severe anemia.\n  - [met] No mention of active pulmonary disease.\n  - [met] No mention of hepatic, renal, or hematological dysfunction.\n  - [met] No mention of adnexal mass size.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-20147__NCT02491307", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The clinical note states the patient is a 26-year-old woman, which is older than 18.\n  - [met] The patient has a history of bipolar disorder and is currently experiencing depressive symptoms, anxiety, and agitation. Bipolar disorder and depression are mood disorders listed in the inclusion crit\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about whether the patient possesses a smartphone with Android or iOS.\n  - [not met] The clinical note is written in English and the patient is able to communicate her symptoms, but there is no explicit statement about her ability to read and write in English.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about whether the patient has a designated primary behavioral health care provider who is using the app or issuing surveys.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 0}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT01013662", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 48-year-old male, which falls within the age range of 18 to 80 years old.\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute abdominal pain, fever, dehydration, hypotension (BP 80/40), tachycardia (HR 132 bpm), and a ruptured liver abscess requiring ICU admission. These findings are consisten\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a male; there is no mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous diagnosis of any cancer in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of leptospirosis in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of AIDS in the clinical note. The patient has common variable immunodeficiency (CVID), which is distinct from AIDS.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT01463475", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 62 years old, which is outside the age range of 18 to 35 years.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about the patient's willingness to provide written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has clinical evidence consistent with Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (progressive memory loss, EEG findings, biopsy findings), which is a human transmissible spongiform encephalopathy.\n  - [not met] The patient has a communicable disease risk associated with xenotransplantation due to likely Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease.\n  - [not met] The patient likely tests positive for human transmissible spongiform encephalopathy (Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease), but there is no information about other listed infections.\n  - [met] There is no information about investigational drug or device use in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of malignancy in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The patient is a 62-year-old man, so pregnancy is not applicable.\n  - [not met] The patient has severe cognitive deficits and likely Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease, which would compromise the ability to safely provide BM donation.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-20147__NCT02604277", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The clinical note is written in English and the patient is described as communicating her symptoms clearly, indicating she is English speaking.\n  - [met] The patient has a documented history of bipolar disorder.\n  - [met] There is no evidence in the note suggesting the patient is unable to provide written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of cognitive impairments; patient is able to describe her symptoms and history.\n  - [met] No evidence of acute psychosis; symptoms described are mood-related (depression, anxiety, agitation) but not psychotic.\n  - [met] No mention of medical instability; obesity is noted but does not imply instability.\n  - [met] No history of schizophrenia spectrum disorder is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of mood incongruent psychotic symptoms; only mood symptoms are described.\n  - [met] No mention of a primary substance disorder.\n  - [met] No mention of primary organic disease or dementia.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT02491541", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 28 years old, which is within the 10-60 years age range.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about compliance with protocol requirements.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about ability to understand or sign informed consent.\n  - [not met] Patient is not healthy, as she is hospitalized with neurological symptoms and hydrophobia, likely consistent with a serious illness (possibly rabies).\n  - [not met] No information about temperature is provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information about lactation, pregnancy, or plans for pregnancy is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about allergic history to vaccines or medicines is provided.\n  - [met] Patient attended a stray animal recovery campaign, which may involve exposure to animals, but there is no mention of injury by dogs or mammals or rabies vaccination.\n  - [not met] No information about serious adverse reaction history after vaccination.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital malformation, developmental disorder, or serious chronic disease.\n  - [met] No mention of autoimmune diseases or immunodeficiency.\n  - [met] No mention of asthma or recent instability.\n  - [met] No mention of diabetes.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 24}
{"pair": "sigir-201422__NCT01022567", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 15 years old, which is below the required age range of 18 to 60 years.\n  - [not met] The patient has an abdominal ultrasound showing an edematous appendix, consistent with acute appendicitis, but there is no mention of a CT scan diagnosis.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is under 18 years old (15 years), so this exclusion criterion is met.\n  - [met] The patient denies sexual activity and has regular menses, making pregnancy or breast-feeding highly unlikely.\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy to contrast media or iodine.\n  - [met] There is no mention of renal insufficiency.\n  - [met] There is no mention of metformin use or diabetes mellitus.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of peritonitis or a perforated appendix; only localized rebound tenderness is noted.\n  - [met] There is no mention of lack of cooperation or inability to give consent.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any severe other medical condition.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-20156__NCT00796913", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with symptoms and signs highly suggestive of active hyperthyroidism (weight loss, sweating, insomnia, diarrhea, increased appetite, tachycardia, hyperreflexia, exophthalmia). Ther\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 46 years old (not under 18) and there is no mention of any severe concomitant disease in the note.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT00725881", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 72-year-old man, which is aged 40 or older.\n  - [not met] Patient has increasing calf pain when walking uphill, gradually worsening over 3 months. However, the severity has changed in the past 3 months, not stable. Fontaine Stage II PAD is likely given dimin\n  - [met] Diagnosis of PAD secondary to atherosclerosis is likely given history of MI, TIA, diminished pulses, and claudication.\n  - [not met] No information about ABI or TBI values is provided.\n  - [not met] Claudication severity has changed in the past 3 months, and blood pressure has worsened recently. Clinical stability for 3 months is not confirmed.\n  - [not met] No information about exercise treadmill test (ETT) or peak walking time (PWT) is provided.\n  - [met] No mention of Pletal or Trental use; patient is on isosorbide dinitrate, hydrochlorothiazide, and aspirin.\n  - [not met] Blood pressure has worsened over the past month, so antihypertensive therapy is not stable for 30 days prior to screening.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is male, not pregnant or lactating.\n  - [met] No evidence of critical limb ischemia; only intermittent claudication and diminished pulses.\n  - [met] PAD is likely secondary to atherosclerosis, not acute limb ischemia or non-atherosclerotic disorder.\n  - [met] Walking impairment is due to intermittent claudication, not other co-morbid conditions.\n  - [met] No mention of recent surgical or endovascular intervention within 3 months.\n  - [met] Walking is limited by claudication, not other reasons.\n  - [met] No mention of other conditions that could confound PWT.\n  - [met] No evidence of severe congestive heart failure.", "n_inc_assessed": 12, "n_exc_assessed": 18}
{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT00416169", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has progressive changes in cognition and personality, poor memory, difficulty expressing himself, and unusual behaviors, which are consistent with frontotemporal dementia. However, there i\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a recent MRI or CT confirming frontotemporal lobar atrophy.\n  - [met] The patient is unable to dress, bathe, use the toilet, or walk independently, which implies that he has the opportunity to perform activities of daily living (even if he cannot do them independently).\n  - [met] The patient was brought to the emergency department by his wife and son, suggesting he lives with or is regularly visited by caregivers.\n  - [met] There is no Mini Mental State Examination (MMSE) score provided, but the patient is alert and oriented to self and city, can recall some words immediately, and can communicate. However, he cannot foll\n  - [met] The patient is able to see, hear, and communicate (speech is fluent, though with word substitutions), and is able to participate in an interview, suggesting he could complete neuropsychometric tests.\n  - [met] The patient is an 89-year-old man, so this criterion is not applicable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a neurodegenerative disorder (dementia), so this exclusion criterion is NOT met (i.e., he should be excluded if he has a non-neurodegenerative cause, but he does have a neurodegenerati\n  - [met] The patient has both memory disturbance and behavioral changes, but the memory disturbance is not clearly primary or amnestic as in Alzheimer's disease. The clinical picture is more compatible with fr\n  - [met] There is no mention of uncontrolled epilepsy, psychiatric disease, or significant comorbidities such as cardiovascular, hepatic, renal, pulmonary, metabolic, or endocrine disturbances, or peptic ulcer\n  - [met] There is no mention of the use of any agent for the treatment of dementia or c", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT00104663", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 62 years old (aged >12). The clinical note describes progressive memory loss, severe cognitive deficits, periodic sharp waves on EEG, cerebral atrophy, and cortical biopsy showing diffu\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being in a coma or in a pre-terminal phase. The patient is seeing a neurologist and undergoing diagnostic workup, suggesting he is not in a pre-terminal phase.\n  - [met] There is no information provided about sensitivity to quinacrine.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient taking any anti-prion therapy, so it is assumed he has not been taking any for less than 8 weeks.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20141__NCT01084239", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient had episodic chest pain radiating to the back, with associated symptoms (nausea, diaphoresis, mild dyspnea) that began two days prior and the latest episode ended half an hour before arrival. \n  - [not met] Patient has hypertension and obesity. She denies diabetes, hypercholesterolemia, smoking, and family history of heart disease. Only one cardiac risk factor (hypertension) is present, as obesity is not\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's ability to provide written informed consent.\n  - [met] Patient is 58 years old, which is between 40 and 75 years.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's ability to hold breath for at least 10 seconds.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's cardiac rhythm. EKG shows nonspecific changes, but sinus rhythm is not explicitly mentioned.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] EKG shows nonspecific changes, with no mention of new diagnostic ischemic changes or left bundle branch block.\n  - [met] Patient denies history of CAD, MI, PCI, CABG, or known significant coronary stenosis.\n  - [met] Patient presented to the ED within 30 minutes of her latest episode of pain, so it is not greater than 6 hours since presentation.\n  - [not met] Patient is obese, but BMI is not specified. Cannot confirm if BMI >40 kg/m2.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about renal function or serum creatinine.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about troponin-T levels.\n  - [met] Physical examination is normal, and there is no mention of hemodynamic or clinical instability.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about allergy to iodinated contrast agent.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 15}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT01280292", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has amenorrhea and elevated prolactin, but there is no mention of a history of pituitary surgery or radiotherapy, nor is there laboratory documentation of central hypothyroidism. In fact, \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Primary hypothyroidism is excluded by the patient's normal TSH. There is no evidence in the note to suggest primary hypothyroidism.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-20159__NCT00486863", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No specific information about screening is provided, but the patient is being assessed.\n  - [not met] Patient is a 10 year old child, not female, and not age 18 or over.\n  - [not met] No evidence the patient is presenting to a study midwife with suspected pregnancy.\n  - [not met] No information about living in a study village.\n  - [not met] No specific information about main study eligibility.\n  - [not met] No evidence of S. japonicum infection; symptoms and exposure history suggest possible parasitic infection, but not schistosomiasis.\n  - [not met] Patient is a 10 year old child, not pregnant.\n  - [not met] Patient is 10 years old, not 18 or older.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient has acute illness (fever, myalgia, cyanosis, high WBC, eosinophilia), so presence of significant disease/illness is met (should NOT have for exclusion to be met).\n  - [met] No history of seizures or chronic medical problems is documented.\n  - [not met] WBC is 25,000, which is a grade 3 or higher abnormality; exclusion criterion is NOT met.\n  - [met] Patient is not a woman, and no mention of myoma.\n  - [met] Patient is not a woman, and no mention of congenital anomalies of reproductive tract.\n  - [not met] Patient has acute illness that significantly alters ability to perform activities of daily living and causes symptoms more than two days per week.\n  - [met] No mention of cysts in the eye or neurocysticercosis.\n  - [met] No mention of regular use of medication for chronic medical condition.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201530__NCT00251160", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 47 years old, which is greater than 14 years.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of MDI (multidirectional instability) or MDL-AII. The patient has an elbow dislocation, not a shoulder instability diagnosis.\n  - [not met] The patient has pain and inability to bend the arm, but these are due to an elbow dislocation, not symptomatic translation in the shoulder (anterior, inferior, or posterior).\n  - [not met] No information is provided about glenohumeral translation or results of any shoulder instability tests.\n  - [not met] No mention of a positive sulcus sign or shoulder instability findings.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms of instability (dislocation), but this is at the elbow, not the shoulder.\n  - [not met] No information about written informed consent.\n  - [not met] No information about prior non-operative treatment or its duration.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of any neurologic disorder such as axillary nerve injury or syringomyelia.\n  - [met] No mention of third party compensation cases.\n  - [met] No mention of primary posterior instability (shoulder). The patient's issue is an elbow dislocation.\n  - [met] No mention of bony abnormalities such as Hill Sachs or bony Bankart lesions on shoulder x-rays.\n  - [met] No mention of a Bankart lesion on arthroscopic exam.\n  - [met] No mention of an unstable biceps anchor or SLAP lesion.\n  - [met] No mention of a full-thickness rotator cuff tear.", "n_inc_assessed": 9, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201418__NCT02306642", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the infant being born prematurely.\n  - [not met] No mention of UVA NICU admission prior to 2 days of life.\n  - [not met] Birth weight is not provided in the note.\n  - [met] The patient has acute kidney injury: urine output <0.2 mL/kg/hr, elevated BUN and creatinine, granular casts, and fractional excretion of sodium >2%. This fits KDIGO modified criteria for AKI.\n  - [not met] The patient has AKI, so does not meet the 'no AKI' control group criteria.\n  - [not met] No information about term birth, and the patient has AKI, so does not meet this criterion.\n  - [not met] No information about parental or legal guardian consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of congenital anomalies of the kidney and urinary tract.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201424__NCT00769873", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note does not mention whether the patient is scheduled for laparoscopic splenectomy or the location (University of Alberta or Grey Nun's Community Hospitals).\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's capacity to understand the study or willingness to sign informed consent.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's willingness to undergo daily Lovenox\u00ae injections.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 33-year-old male, so is not pregnant or nursing.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about inability or unwillingness to provide informed consent.\n  - [met] No history of bleeding diathesis or anticoagulation therapy is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of hemorrhagic cerebral vascular accident.\n  - [met] The patient is hypotensive (BP: 60/30 mmHg), not hypertensive.\n  - [met] No mention of diabetic or hemorrhagic retinopathy.\n  - [not met] The patient has splenectomy due to trauma, which is listed as a contraindication to anticoagulation in the exclusion criteria.\n  - [not met] No mention of conversion to open splenectomy.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201415__NCT00288938", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 36-year-old woman, not an infant or child.\n  - [not met] The patient is 36 years old.\n  - [not met] No mention of congenital melanocytic nevus or any nevus in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] No information about an outside referring physician.\n  - [met] The patient is 36 years old, thus an adult.\n  - [met] The patient is 36 years old.\n  - [not met] No mention of melanocytic nevi in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] No mention of melanocytic nevi in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of any such genetic syndrome.\n  - [met] No mention of family history of melanoma or related syndrome.\n  - [met] No mention of any cancer-associated syndrome.\n  - [met] No mention of bleeding diathesis or inability to tolerate surgery; blood counts are normal.\n  - [met] No information about willingness for biopsy.", "n_inc_assessed": 15, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT02029339", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 48 years old (age \u2265 18), has a complicated intra-abdominal infection (ruptured liver abscess), and underwent exploratory laparotomy. However, it is not explicitly stated that the patien\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about consent or whether the patient or their legal representative provided consent.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the Bjorck classification of the open abdomen. The patient had a ruptured liver abscess and exploratory laparotomy, but no details about OA grade.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 48 years old, which is \u2265 18 years.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a pre-existing large ventral hernia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of frozen OA with adherent bowel (grade 4 OA).\n  - [met] The patient had a ruptured liver abscess (contaminated wound), not a clean wound.\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic wound infection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of critical wound ischemia.\n  - [not met] The patient has acute infection (ruptured liver abscess with sepsis signs), but 'severe systemic infection' is not clearly defined. However, the patient is hypotensive and tachycardic, suggesting poss\n  - [met] There is no mention of end-stage renal disease.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT01970332", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient reports increasing calf pain when walking uphill, which has gradually increased over 3 months. This is consistent with a positive history of chronic claudication.\n  - [not met] The patient has exercise-limiting calf pain by history, but there is no mention of direct observation during a screening walking test by a vascular surgeon.\n  - [not met] There is no ankle/brachial index (ABI) value provided in the note, so it cannot be determined if ABI < 0.90 at rest.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has symptoms and signs consistent with Peripheral Arterial Disease (PAD), such as claudication, diminished pulses, and cool extremities. Therefore, absence of PAD is NOT present.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of an acute lower extremity ischemic event due to thromboembolic disease or trauma. The symptoms are chronic and progressive.\n  - [met] The exercise limitation is attributed to claudication, not to other conditions such as joint, neurologic, heart, or lung disease.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT02024373", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is an 85-year-old man, which is \u226518 and <90 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a CT scan revealing a chronic subdural hematoma. The only information is that a head CT was normal 3 weeks ago. No new imaging results are provided.\n  - [not met] Markwalder's Grading Scale and Glasgow Coma Scale are not explicitly mentioned. The patient has a gradual decrease in consciousness and stopped walking/eating, but no specific grade is given.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the attending physician's judgment regarding cerebral hernia risk or surgical timing. Conservative treatment is not mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient having undergone surgery on a hematoma.\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent or the patient's understanding of the study.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to statins or their ingredients.\n  - [met] No mention that cerebral herniation might occur at any time.\n  - [met] No mention that hematoma leads to herniation or warrants surgical operation.\n  - [met] No mention that hematoma is caused by tumors, blood disorders, or other comorbidities.\n  - [met] No mention of abnormal liver function.\n  - [met] No mention of uncontrolled hepatitis, other liver diseases, or other interfering diseases.\n  - [met] No mention of long-term oral statin treatment.\n  - [met] No mention of long-term oral steroid treatment.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-20141__NCT01682096", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note does not explicitly state the patient's rhythm, but there is no mention of arrhythmia, and the EKG shows only nonspecific changes. In the absence of evidence to the contrary, it is reasonable\n  - [met] The patient had episodic chest pain that began two days earlier and the latest episode ended half an hour prior to arrival. The pain is described as pressing/burning and lasted more than 5 minutes (si\n  - [met] The patient is a 58-year-old woman with hypertension and obesity, presenting with new-onset chest pain. These factors suggest a pre-test probability of significant CAD >15%.\n  - [met] The EKG shows 'nonspecific changes' and does not mention ST-segment deviation >1 mm or T wave inversion >4 mm in at least two contiguous leads.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about troponin I levels at admission.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to iodinated contrast.\n  - [met] No mention of renal insufficiency or elevated creatinine.\n  - [met] No history of coronary artery disease or prior myocardial revascularization; in fact, this is the first episode of chest pain in her life.\n  - [met] No evidence of hemodynamic instability, persistent chest pain, or low systolic blood pressure. Physical exam is normal.\n  - [met] No mention of cardiac arrhythmia; EKG shows only nonspecific changes.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to perform an exercise test; patient is ambulatory and was walking when pain started.\n  - [met] No mention of incapacity to provide informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT00162032", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy. The inclusion criterion requires age between 4 and 16 years. The patient is younger than 4 years.\n  - [met] The patient has classic signs of Kawasaki Disease (fever, conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue, extremity changes, desquamation, lymphadenopathy) and evidence of coronary artery disease (moderate dilatio\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the patient's ability to exercise or achieve 85% age predicted maximum heart rate. The patient is acutely ill, so it is uncertain if he can exercise adequatel\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a terminal illness or expected survival < 6 months. The patient has Kawasaki Disease, which is not a terminal illness.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-20156__NCT02373995", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with classic symptoms and signs of untreated Graves' hyperthyroidism (weight loss, sweating, diarrhea, palpitations, exophthalmia). There is no mention of prior treatment with ant\n  - [met] The definition of hyperthyroidism includes decreased TSH and increased FT4/FT3. While labs are not provided, the clinical presentation (weight loss, increased appetite, sweating, palpitations, diarrhe\n  - [not met] Graves' disease is suggested by the presence of hyperthyroidism and mild exophthalmia. However, there is no explicit mention of thyroid gland enlargement, imaging, or TSHRAb positivity.\n  - [met] This appears to be the patient's first episode of hyperthyroidism, as there is no mention of prior episodes.\n  - [not met] The patient has mild exophthalmia, but there is no mention of lid retraction or lid lag specifically. Mild exophthalmia may or may not fit the definition of 'minimal or no eye signs' as per the criter\n  - [not met] There is no information about planned treatment with antithyroid drugs or the regimen.\n  - [met] The patient has untreated Graves' hyperthyroidism and overt signs of Graves' orbitopathy (mild exophthalmia), which may fit EUGOGO1 criteria for overt GO.\n  - [met] The patient has mild exophthalmia, which could be considered mild GO if it has only minor impact on daily life and no other severe features. There is no mention of diplopia or corneal exposure.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous or planned treatment with 131I or thyroidectomy, sight-threatening GO, use of excluded drugs, acute diarrhea illness, drug/alcohol abuse, lack of consent, age <18, or p", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201523__NCT02134652", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 18 years old. The criterion requires age >3 months and <16 years. Therefore, the patient does not meet this criterion.\n  - [met] The patient presents with high fever, chills, facial flushing, epistaxis, severe headache, joint pain, leukopenia, increased hematocrit, and thrombocytopenia after travel to Asia. These are consistent\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is a prisoner or ward of the state.\n  - [met] The patient is 18 years old, so parental consent and child assent are not applicable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy to ultrasound gel.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is a prisoner or ward of the state.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being unstable (e.g., hypotension, shock, respiratory distress).\n  - [met] There is no mention of known pleural effusion, ascites, or gallbladder wall thickening.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT02605122", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient has documented fever up to 39\u00b0C, which meets the threshold for fever.\n  - [met] Chest x-ray shows bilateral lung infiltrates, consistent with pneumonia.\n  - [met] Patient has at least two symptoms: fever, dyspnea, cough, and respiratory distress.\n  - [met] Patient is in respiratory distress and has dyspnea, indicating difficulty breathing.\n  - [not met] No mention of purulent sputum production in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of chest pain in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of grunting in the note.\n  - [not met] No mention of hypotension in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of ventilator-associated or hospital-acquired pneumonia; patient presented to ER after vacation.\n  - [met] No mention of prior antibacterial therapy; likely not received >48 hours.\n  - [met] No evidence or mention of bacterial meningitis.\n  - [met] Patient is an 8-year-old male, not a breast-feeding female.\n  - [met] Patient is an 8-year-old male, not pregnant.", "n_inc_assessed": 22, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20158__NCT02053012", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The clinical note does not explicitly state whether the patient can understand or perform a reaction time test without assistance. However, the patient is a 10-year-old boy attending school, which gen\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information in the note indicating that the child is unable to understand or perform the test, nor is there mention of parental refusal. The absence of such information suggests the exclus", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201528__NCT00313365", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has had symptoms (limping, pain, fever) for the past two days, which is less than or equal to two weeks.\n  - [met] The infection appears to be localized to the right knee, which is one of the specified joints.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a positive gram stain or culture of synovial fluid, nor is there a synovial fluid WBC count provided. Only peripheral WBC and SRP are mentioned.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of synovial fluid cultures, blood cultures, or prior antibiotic therapy. This information is not available.\n  - [met] Only the right knee is described as affected, indicating monoarticular arthritis.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of gonococcal infection.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prosthetic joints.\n  - [met] There is no mention of adjacent osteomyelitis preceding the joint infection.\n  - [met] There is no indication that this is an incidental event late in a fatal illness; the patient was previously healthy.\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old, which is less than 17.\n  - [met] Only one joint (right knee) is affected, so polyarticular arthritis is not present.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT01438060", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is non-institutionalized (brought in by family), has progressive cognitive decline consistent with Alzheimer's disease, and exhibits unusual behaviors. However, there is no mention of delu\n  - [not met] No MMSE score is provided in the note. However, the patient's cognitive deficits are severe, possibly consistent with an MMSE in the 6-24 range, but this cannot be confirmed.\n  - [not met] The patient is unable to walk independently, and there is no mention of use of an assistive device. Therefore, self-locomotion or locomotion with aid is not confirmed.\n  - [met] The patient has an identified caregiver or proxy (wife and son).\n  - [not met] No information about Extension Phase.\n  - [not met] No information about completion of the 10-week Acute Phase, NPI score, or investigator judgment.\n  - [not met] No information about treatment beyond 140 weeks.\n  - [not met] No information about completion of the extension phase of CN138-006.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of any Axis I (DSM IV) diagnosis other than dementia is provided.\n  - [met] No evidence of delirium (patient is alert and oriented to self and city, not year, but no acute onset or fluctuating course).\n  - [met] The patient has amnestic symptoms, but these are part of the dementia syndrome, not a separate amnestic disorder.\n  - [met] No evidence of bipolar disorder.\n  - [met] No evidence of schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder.\n  - [met] No evidence of mood disorder with psychotic features.\n  - [met] No evidence of reversible causes of dementia is mentioned.\n  - [met] No evidence that psychotic symptoms were present prior to dementia onset.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT01083563", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about informed consent.\n  - [met] Patient is a 31-year-old woman, which is over 18 years old.\n  - [not met] No explicit diagnosis of RA or DAS28 assessment is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No explicit diagnosis of RA, no information about MTX use, DAS28, or evidence of knee synovitis on exam.\n  - [not met] No information about TNF antagonist response, DAS score, flare, or DMARD use.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information suggesting exclusion for investigator discretion reasons.\n  - [met] No evidence of active systemic disorders or inflammatory conditions other than the condition being studied.\n  - [not met] No information about plasma creatinine.\n  - [not met] No information about corticosteroid allergy.\n  - [not met] No information provided for these questions.\n  - [not met] No information provided for these questions.\n  - [met] No mention of cardiac pacemaker or defibrillator.\n  - [met] No mention of cardiac valve replacement or prosthesis.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 20}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT02282228", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention that the patient is admitted for surgery of chronic subdural hematoma. The note only describes decreased consciousness and a history of trauma, but does not specify the diagnosis o\n  - [not met] The note states that a head CT was performed 3 weeks prior to admission, but there is no evidence of a CT scan within the last 96 hours.\n  - [not met] The patient has a gradual decrease in level of consciousness and has stopped walking and eating by himself. This suggests he is not able to have a normal conversation or score a 5 on the Glasgow Coma \n  - [met] The patient is 85 years old, which is \u2265 18 years.\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent being signed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is an 85-year-old man, so he is not a pregnant or breastfeeding woman.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a shunt or other foreign object implanted in the brain.\n  - [met] There is no information about participation in other clinical studies.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20153__NCT00740883", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with symptoms suggestive of pulmonary embolism (acute shortness of breath, tachypnea, pleuritic chest pain, recent immobility after surgery, and right calf pain suggestive of DVT)\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is above 18.\n  - [met] There is no mention of warfarin hypersensitivity.\n  - [not met] There is no information about willingness or ability to give written informed consent.\n  - [not met] The patient has right calf pain, which may suggest DVT, but there is no confirmed diagnosis of distal or proximal DVT.\n  - [not met] The pulmonary embolism (if present) would be provoked by a reversible major risk factor (recent major surgery and immobility).\n  - [met] No mention of major thrombophilia.\n  - [met] No history of previous DVT or pulmonary embolism is mentioned.\n  - [met] No other indication for anticoagulant therapy is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-201410__NCT02241642", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 67-year-old woman, which is over 18 years of age.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about informed consent or willingness to participate.\n  - [not met] The patient underwent cardiac catheterization via the right femoral artery, which is an endovascular procedure involving femoral access. However, the access puncture size (18-24F) is not specified.\n  - [met] The patient is female and 67 years old. There is no information about pregnancy, lactation, or plans to become pregnant, but at this age, pregnancy is highly unlikely.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of severe acute non-cardiac systemic disease or terminal illness with life expectancy <1 year.\n  - [met] No evidence of systemic bacterial or cutaneous infection is described.\n  - [met] No evidence of MRSA or VRE colonization is mentioned.\n  - [met] Arterial access was via the right femoral artery, which is appropriate.\n  - [met] No mention of coagulopathy or low platelet count.\n  - [met] No mention of haematocrit levels.\n  - [met] No mention of ACT levels.\n  - [met] No information about post-procedure anticoagulation therapy.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 26}
{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT01280292", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with symptoms consistent with hypothyroidism (cold intolerance, fatigue, constipation, hyporeflexia, dry skin, slow movement and speech). However, there is no mention of pituitary\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient's symptoms (cold intolerance, fatigue, constipation, hyporeflexia, dry skin, slow movement and speech) are classic for primary hypothyroidism. There is no evidence in the note to suggest c", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT02362321", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 85 years old, which is older than 18 years.\n  - [not met] There is no evidence in the note of subacute or chronic supratentorial subdural hematoma by CT or MRI. The only imaging mentioned is a normal head CT 3 weeks ago.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the Markwalder grading scale or a classification between 0 and 2. The patient's symptoms (decreased consciousness, stopped walking/eating) may suggest a higher grade, but this i\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of contraindications or intolerance to corticosteroid therapy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient already undergoing steroid treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous neurological surgery in the past year.\n  - [met] There is no mention of concomitant cerebral pathology of neoplastic or presumed infectious origin.\n  - [met] There is no mention of anticoagulant therapy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of refusal to participate.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-20146__NCT00519935", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The note states the patient has 'persistently elevated HbA1c', which strongly suggests a current HbA1c >8.0%. However, the exact value is not provided.\n  - [met] The note mentions 'persistently elevated HbA1c', implying that the average HbA1c over the past year is likely >8.0%. No specific values or time frame are given.\n  - [not met] The patient is diagnosed with diabetes mellitus, but the type (Type 1 or Type 2) is not specified. Most older, obese patients have Type 2 diabetes, so this criterion is likely not met.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's residence or location in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of severe mental impairment or thought disorder in the note.\n  - [met] The note is written in English and there is no indication that the patient or parent is non-English speaking.\n  - [met] There is no mention of co-morbid major medical conditions such as cystic fibrosis.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20151__NCT02105532", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 44-year-old male (adult aged 18 or over) presenting with multiple bouts of vomiting with a 'coffee ground' appearance, which is indicative of haematemesis and thus acute upper gastroi\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient received a rapid infusion of crystalloid solution followed by packed red blood cell transfusion due to severe bleeding and shock (heart rate 135 bpm, BP 70/40 mmHg, decreased mental status\n  - [met] The patient was brought to the emergency room, indicating he was not an existing hospital in-patient who developed AUGIB.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT01463475", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 89 years old, which is outside the required age range of 18 to 35 years.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's willingness or ability to provide written informed consent. Given his severe cognitive impairment, it is unlikely he can provide informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient having risk factors for or clinical evidence of HIV, Hepatitis B or C, HTLV, transmissible spongiform encephalopathy, or treponema pallidum. However, the clinical pi\n  - [met] There is no mention of communicable disease risk associated with xenotransplantation.\n  - [met] There is no information about testing positive for any of the listed infections.\n  - [met] There is no mention of investigational drug use or implanted devices.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of malignancy.\n  - [met] The patient is male and therefore cannot be pregnant.\n  - [not met] The patient has severe cognitive and functional impairment, is unable to perform activities of daily living, and likely cannot safely provide BM donation.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201429__NCT00485953", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 51-year-old woman. The criterion requires age 55 or older. She is younger than 55.\n  - [not met] There is no information about DXA T-score or diagnosis of osteopenia or osteoporosis. The patient is seeking advice on osteoporosis prevention, but no BMD data is provided.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of breast cancer or aromatase inhibitor therapy.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of breast cancer, metastatic disease, or osteoporosis by BMD or clinical history.\n  - [not met] No surgical procedure or radiation therapy is mentioned, but the criterion is not exclusionary.\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No history of breast cancer or metastatic disease is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No DXA results are provided, so it is unknown if she has normal bone density.\n  - [met] No history of illnesses affecting bone/mineral metabolism (renal failure, hepatic failure, malignancy, etc.) is mentioned. Hypertension and diabetes are present, but not listed as exclusions.\n  - [met] No mention of oral glucocorticoid or anti-seizure medication use.\n  - [met] No mention of active peptic ulcer disease.\n  - [met] No evidence of osteoporosis by BMD or history of fragility fracture is provided.\n  - [met] No mention of bisphosphonate or calcitonin use.\n  - [met] The patient is a woman.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-201522__NCT01178177", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is not described as a solid organ transplant recipient or as having a hematologic disease. There is no mention of transplantation or hematologic malignancy/disorder in the note.\n  - [met] The patient has clinical, radiological, and microbiological evidence highly suggestive of proven or probable invasive pulmonary aspergillosis (IPA): history of tuberculosis (risk factor), hemoptysis, \nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is over 16 years old.\n  - [met] The case is not described as a 'possible' IPA, but rather as probable or proven based on clinical, radiological, and microbiological findings.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20153__NCT02375919", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute onset of shortness of breath (dyspnea) and left-sided chest pain that worsens with inspiration.\n  - [not met] The patient has risk factors for PE (recent surgery, immobility, calf pain), but the note does not explicitly state a high or low pretest probability by gestalt. However, the presence of multiple risk\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No other obvious cause for dyspnea or chest pain is mentioned in the note.\n  - [not met] The patient has a respiratory rate of 35 (tachypnea) and acute symptoms, which may suggest a severe presentation, but there is no mention of hemodynamic instability or shock. The severity is unclear.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to CTPA (e.g., contrast allergy, renal failure).\n  - [met] No mention of concurrent anticoagulation treatment.\n  - [met] No mention of a current diagnosed thrombo-embolic event.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to follow up.\n  - [met] No mention of the patient being a prisoner.\n  - [met] Patient is a 65-year-old male, so not pregnant.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201529__NCT00162032", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 4-year-old girl, which fits the age range of 4 to 16 years and includes both males and females.\n  - [met] The patient presents with persistent fever, erythematous rash, strawberry tongue, red/cracked lips, swollen red hands, and bilateral conjunctival injection (red eyes with no discharge). These findings\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note regarding the patient's ability to exercise or achieve 85% of age-predicted maximum heart rate. This cannot be determined from the available data.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a terminal illness or limited life expectancy (<6 months) in the clinical note.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT00111735", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 56-year-old female, which is older than 18 years.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms highly suggestive of hypothyroidism (cold intolerance, fatigue, constipation, hyporeflexia, dry skin, slow movements/speech), but there is no explicit mention of primary hypot\n  - [not met] There is no information about thyroxine dose.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about changes in thyroxine dose.\n  - [not met] No laboratory data (TSH) is provided.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about contraceptive measures.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence of a major systemic illness affecting quality of life or participation, aside from possible hypothyroidism.\n  - [met] No mention of T3 treatment currently or in the past 2 months.\n  - [met] No history of thyroid cancer or TSH suppression is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of ischaemic heart disease, myocardial infarction, angina, or coronary artery revascularisation.\n  - [met] No mention of renal failure or serum creatinine levels.\n  - [met] No mention of liver disease or abnormal liver function tests.\n  - [met] No mention of recent bony fracture or Paget's disease.\n  - [met] Symptoms are consistent with primary hypothyroidism, not secondary (central) hypothyroidism or hypopituitarism, but this is not explicitly stated.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT02269644", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 31-year-old male, which is within the 18 to 85 age range.\n  - [not met] No information is provided regarding written, informed consent.\n  - [met] Patient developed acute illness with onset within the previous 7 days (cold symptoms started one week ago, worsened two days ago).\n  - [met] Patient has at least 2 symptoms: productive cough, chest pain, fever, chills.\n  - [not met] No mention of difficulty breathing or shortness of breath.\n  - [not met] Patient has a productive cough, but no explicit mention of purulent sputum.\n  - [met] Patient has chest pain aggravated by coughing, which is consistent with pleuritic chest pain.\n  - [met] Patient has at least 2 vital sign abnormalities: fever (103.4\u00b0F = 39.7\u00b0C), tachycardia (pulse 105).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of contraindications to study treatments or relevant drug use.\n  - [met] No mention of recent antibiotic therapy.\n  - [met] No evidence or mention of aspiration pneumonia.\n  - [met] No evidence of hospital-acquired, ventilator-associated, or healthcare-associated pneumonia, or recent hospitalization.\n  - [met] No mention of cystic fibrosis, Pneumocystis pneumonia, or tuberculosis.\n  - [met] Patient is male.\n  - [met] No mention of lung cancer.\n  - [met] No mention of bronchial obstruction or post-obstructive pneumonia.", "n_inc_assessed": 18, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
