{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT01962779", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is an 89-year-old man, which is >50 years of age. However, he does not have normal cognition, as he has significant cognitive impairment.\n  - [not met] The patient has significant cognitive impairment, abnormal neurological findings (paratonic rigidity, myoclonic jerks), and would not have a Clinical Dementia Rating of 0 or Global Deterioration Scale\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's years of education.\n  - [not met] The patient was brought by his wife and son, suggesting an informed family member is available. There is no information about agreement to MRI, lumbar puncture, ApoE genotyping, or DNA banking.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has significant cognitive impairment, abnormal neurological findings (paratonic rigidity, myoclonic jerks), and likely a neurodegenerative disorder. This would be considered a serious neur\n  - [met] No history of brain tumor is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of radiation or chemotherapy in the past 3 years.\n  - [met] No significant history of alcoholism or drug abuse is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of psychiatric illness (schizophrenia, mania, PTSD, lifelong major depression) is mentioned.\n  - [met] No information about Hamilton Depression Scale or lifelong depressive episodes.\n  - [met] No evidence of uncontrolled cardiac, pulmonary, hypothyroid, or hematological conditions. Blood pressure is 144/78 mm Hg (slightly above normal systolic), but not clearly uncontrolled.\n  - [not met] The patient is unable to walk independently and has severe cognitive impairment, which would adversely affect the validity of psychological testing.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 19}
{"pair": "sigir-201522__NCT01576315", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of cystic fibrosis in the patient's history; instead, the patient has a history of tuberculosis.\n  - [met] The patient is a 65-year-old male, so this criterion is met.\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is greater than 12 years.\n  - [not met] The patient has a positive sputum culture for a fungus with septated, low-angle branching hyphae (suggestive of Aspergillus), but there is no information about confirmation twice within 6 months.\n  - [not met] There is no information about written informed consent in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about contraindications to antifungal agents.\n  - [met] The patient is male, so cannot be a pregnant woman or nursing mother.\n  - [met] The patient is male, so this criterion does not apply.\n  - [met] There are no signs or symptoms of invasive aspergillosis described; the findings are more consistent with aspergilloma (fungal ball in a cavity).\n  - [not met] The patient has a round mass in a cavity that moves with position and a positive sputum culture for Aspergillus, which is classic for aspergilloma.\n  - [met] The patient has a history of tuberculosis but no mention of Burkholderia complex Cepacia or mycobacterial infection (other than TB, which is not specified as active).\n  - [met] No mention of lung transplant, being on a transplant list, or imminent registration.\n  - [not met] No information about prior systemic antifungal therapy.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT01917721", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy (within 1 month to 21 years) with clinical features consistent with Kawasaki Disease (KD): 5 days of high fever, conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue, extremity changes, d\n  - [not met] The patient has moderate dilation of the coronary arteries with possible aneurysm on echocardiogram. However, there is no mention of a z-score > +2.5 specifically for the right or left anterior descen\n  - [not met] The echocardiogram shows possible coronary artery aneurysm, but it is not explicitly stated that the aneurysm is in the right or left main coronary arteries. The finding is suggestive but not definiti\n  - [not met] There is no information about prior IVIG treatment or refractory KD. The patient is presenting acutely, and no mention is made of prior therapy or refractory status.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the right or left anterior descending coronary artery measurements being below a z-score of +2.5. In fact, the patient has moderate dilation, which may suggest a higher z\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header criterion and not applicable for assessment.\n  - [met] The patient has classic, complete KD (meets all clinical criteria: fever, conjunctivitis, oral changes, extremity changes, rash/desquamation, lymphadenopathy).\n  - [met] There is no mention of parental refusal to administer doxycycline.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of acute renal failure in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The patient has elevated liver enzymes and low albumin, but there is no mention of chronic liver or kidney disease. The findings are likely acute and related to KD.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
