{"pair": "sigir-201528__NCT02218580", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of JIA (Juvenile Idiopathic Arthritis) according to ILAR classification. The patient presents with joint pain, swelling, and fever, but these could be due to other c\n  - [met] The patient is 8 years old, which is within the 5 to 17 years age range.\n  - [met] The note is in English, and there is no indication that the patient or caregiver cannot speak/read English. One caregiver is present.\n  - [met] The patient reports pain, limping, and the joint is tender and swollen on examination. This meets the pain criterion.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an anticipated change in treatment.\n  - [not met] There is no information about current medications or intra-articular corticosteroid injections.\n  - [not met] Eligibility confirmation by a rheumatologist is not mentioned.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] It is unclear what 'MT' refers to. No information is provided.\n  - [not met] The patient has fever, but there is no mention of systemic arthritis with quotidian (daily) fevers. The fever could be due to infection.\n  - [not met] The patient presents with fever, elevated WBC, and joint swelling, which are suggestive of an acute infection (e.g., septic arthritis or Lyme disease).\n  - [met] There is no mention of open skin lesions.\n  - [met] There is no mention of fibromyalgia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of sleep apnea.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about current medications.\n  - [met] The patient is an 8-year-old boy, so pregnancy is not possible.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201419__NCT01054274", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note describes progressive dysphagia and weight loss, which are suggestive of esophageal cancer, but there is no mention of endoscopic or histological confirmation.\n  - [met] The patient has progressive dysphagia, starting with meat and progressing to all foods and liquids, which is consistent with grade III or IV dysphagia. However, the cause is presumed esophageal cancer\n  - [not met] There is no information about a barium meal or radiological findings.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of CT imaging or three-dimensional reconstruction.\n  - [met] The patient is described as able to locate the obstruction and is communicating clearly, suggesting clear consciousness and cooperation. ECOG status is not specified, but no evidence of poor performan\n  - [not met] No information about informed consent or authorization/signature.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of poor general status or ECOG 4; patient is able to describe symptoms and history.\n  - [met] Dysphagia is presumed to be caused by esophageal cancer based on history, but not confirmed.\n  - [met] Patient appears cooperative; no evidence of noncooperation or lack of authorization/signature, but this is not explicitly stated.\n  - [met] No information about the superior border of the cancer or its relation to the seventh cervical vertebra.\n  - [met] No mention of ulcerative esophageal carcinoma.\n  - [met] No mention of esophageal fistulas.\n  - [met] No information about WBC count.\n  - [met] No information about hepatic or renal function.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT00762086", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 72-year-old man, which is within the 18-90 year age range.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms and signs suggestive of PAD (calf pain on exertion, diminished pulses, cool extremities), but there is no mention of Doppler Ultrasound or ABPI measurement.\n  - [not met] Symptoms have been present and gradually increasing over 3 months, but it is not clear if PAD has been stable for >3 months or if Fontaine Stage II is confirmed.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about aortoiliac vessel hemodynamics or recent clinical examination specific to this.\n  - [met] The patient has intermittent claudication and calf pain on exertion.\n  - [not met] There is no treadmill test or claudication distance reported.\n  - [not met] No information about consent is provided.\n  - [met] The patient is currently taking aspirin, but duration is not specified.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No ABI values are provided.\n  - [met] The patient can walk, as he experiences calf pain when walking uphill.\n  - [met] No mention of chronic respiratory insufficiency.\n  - [met] History of myocardial infarction, but no mention of current angina.\n  - [met] The patient had a TIA 6 months ago and MI 2 years ago, but no acute vascular events in the last 3 months.\n  - [met] No mention of congestive heart failure.\n  - [met] No mention of joint lesions interfering with walking.\n  - [met] No mention of spinal stenosis or disc lesions.", "n_inc_assessed": 9, "n_exc_assessed": 21}
