{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT02258763", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a child presenting with severe pneumonia: fever, cough, dyspnea, respiratory distress, and abnormal CXR (bilateral infiltrates). The note does not explicitly state 'admitted', but ER pr\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old (96 months), which is older than the 3-59 months (approx 0.25-5 years) required.\n  - [met] The patient has a history of cough and dyspnea (shortness of breath).\n  - [met] The patient has been unwell for 2 days (<=7 days) and is in respiratory distress. Age-specific respiratory rate is not provided, but retractions/distress are present.\n  - [met] The patient is in respiratory distress, which would necessitate admission.\n  - [met] Fever up to 39\u00b0C is documented.\n  - [met] Chest x-ray shows bilateral lung infiltrates, which are abnormal.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about response to IV antibiotics or clinical course after admission.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence in the note for any exclusion: not transferred, no refusal of blood, no asthma/recurrent wheeze, not bronchiolitis, illness is acute, no mention of inability to follow-up, appears to be co", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
