{"pair": "sigir-201522__NCT00263315", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 65-year-old male, which is over 18 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a hematologic malignancy or bone-marrow transplant in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about chemotherapy or neutropenia in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the expected duration of neutropenia.\n  - [not met] No mention of oral antibiotic prophylaxis or fluconazole use.\n  - [not met] No information about written informed consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has a pulmonary fungal infection, as evidenced by the clinical description and sputum culture showing septated, low-angle branching hyphae (suggestive of Aspergillus).\n  - [met] No mention of concomitant use of systemic anti-aspergillus treatment.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to amphotericin B.\n  - [not met] There is evidence of pneumonia or a pulmonary mass, which may be considered pneumonia or pneumonitis.\n  - [met] No information about the ability to use a nebulizer.\n  - [met] No information about expected survival.\n  - [met] The patient is male, so pregnancy is not possible.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201512__NCT01747369", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient\u2019s clinical note describes symptoms consistent with meningitis (headache, fever, nuchal rigidity) following a skull fracture, but there is no mention of pneumonia or pneumonia surveillance.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient being a resident of T\u00f4ne sanitary district or being hospitalised for clinical pneumonia syndrome.\n  - [not met] The note states the patient was in the emergency room and had physical examination, but does not specify hospitalisation in a study site during the study period.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about informed consent status in the note.\n  - [not met] This criterion is for meningitis surveillance. The patient has symptoms consistent with meningitis (headache, fever, nuchal rigidity), so the condition described is present.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient being a resident of T\u00f4ne sanitary district.\n  - [not met] The patient presents clinical signs of acute bacterial meningitis (headache, fever, nuchal rigidity).\n  - [not met] The note does not specify hospitalisation in a study site during the study period.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-20143__NCT01803542", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of histological confirmation of malignancy or biopsy. However, the patient has a lung mass and a solitary brain mass, which are highly suspicious for malignancy, but no explicit co\n  - [met] Staging studies (chest x-ray, CT scan of head) have been performed, identifying a lung mass and a brain mass.\n  - [not met] The patient has a lung mass and a solitary brain mass, which suggests metastatic disease (M1), not stage I or II non-metastatic NSCLC.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a non-lung primary tumor that is controlled and has metastasized to the lungs alone.\n  - [not met] The patient has a lung mass and a solitary brain metastasis, which may fit the definition of limited (low) volume metastatic NSCLC. However, there is no information about whether other sites of metast\n  - [not met] There is no information about resectability or surgical candidacy.\n  - [met] The number of parenchymal lung lesions is not specified, only a 'left lung mass' is mentioned. No evidence of >1 lung lesion.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about hilar or mediastinal lymph node status.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No evidence of active systemic, pulmonary, or pericardial infection.\n  - [met] No mention of concurrent systemic therapy.\n  - [met] No history of active autoimmune diseases is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No information about candidacy for concurrent chemo-radiation therapy.\n  - [met] No mention of enrollment on other studies.", "n_inc_assessed": 15, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201429__NCT01677637", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 51-year-old woman.\n  - [met] She was documented by previous LH and FSH levels to be in menopause within the last year.\n  - [met] She is seen in clinic for advice on osteoporosis and is seeking advice on osteoporosis prevention, suggesting she is being screened.\n  - [met] She is 51 years old.\n  - [not met] She is 51 years old, so this criterion does not apply.\n  - [met] There is no explicit mention of consent, but she is seeking advice and attending the clinic voluntarily, which implies likely consent.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] She is postmenopausal as documented by LH and FSH levels.\n  - [met] She is documented to be in menopause.\n  - [met] There is no explicit mention of lack of consent; her voluntary attendance suggests implied consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20151__NCT02017379", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 44 years old, which is within the 18-80 age range.\n  - [met] The patient was admitted to the ICU for coffee ground emesis (hematemesis).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 44 years old, not younger than 18 or older than 80.\n  - [met] There is no information about refusal to consent.\n  - [met] The patient is male, so cannot be pregnant.\n  - [met] No information is provided about prior use of prokinetics in the last 48 hours.\n  - [met] No history of cardiac arrhythmia is mentioned.\n  - [met] No allergy to erythromycin or metoclopromide is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of QT prolongation.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201513__NCT00938353", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information in the clinical note about written informed consent obtained by parents/legal representative.\n  - [not met] The patient is a 5-year-old boy, which is outside the specified age range (6 months to 3 years).\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of moderate croup or a Westley score (3-8). The symptoms described (dysphagia, drooling, fever, muffled voice, toxic appearance, leaning forward) are more consistent\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has symptoms and signs suggestive of another cause of stridor (epiglottitis), not croup.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous acute angioneurotic oedema.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of severe croup (Westley score >8).\n  - [not met] The patient has a diagnosis suggestive of epiglottitis, which is explicitly listed as an exclusion criterion.\n  - [not met] The patient appears toxic and has a severe acute medical condition (likely epiglottitis), which may increase risk and interfere with study interpretation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of treatment with corticosteroids or epinephrine prior to enrollment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous ER visit due to croup during this episode.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the parent's ability to understand the study.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-20148__NCT02589925", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 62 years old, which falls within the required age range of 35-75 years.\n  - [not met] The patient has progressive memory loss and severe cognitive deficits, but there is no mention of idiopathic Parkinson's disease or probable Parkinson's disease dementia. The described symptoms and fi\n  - [not met] The patient has severe cognitive deficits and memory dysfunction, but there is no MMSE score provided. Severity is described as 'severe,' which may be outside the 'mild to moderately severe' range (MM\n  - [not met] There is no mention of idiopathic Parkinson's disease or duration of motor symptoms. The motor symptoms described are jerking movements, not typical PD motor symptoms.\n  - [not met] No information about Hoehn and Yahr stage or PD severity is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about UPDRS subset III score or PD diagnosis.\n  - [not met] No information about levodopa response or UPDRS scores; no evidence of PD diagnosis.\n  - [not met] No evidence of PDD or timing of dementia relative to PD onset.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has severe cognitive deficits and memory dysfunction, but there is no mention of acute confusional state, ongoing psychosis, or clinically significant depression.\n  - [met] No mention of current drug or alcohol abuse.\n  - [met] No mention of history of recurrent or unprovoked seizures.\n  - [met] No mention of prior movement disorder treatments involving intracranial surgery or device implantation.\n  - [met] No mention of neurostimulation intolerance.\n  - [not met] No mention of significant medical conditions likely to interfere with study procedures or terminal illness with survival <12 months, but the described findings (severe dementia, advanced cerebral atro\n  - [met] No mention of participation in another trial.\n  - [met] Patient is a 62-year-old man, so pregnancy, breast-feeding, or contraception are not applica", "n_inc_assessed": 10, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT00116584", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 4 years old, which is older than 12 months. This criterion is not met.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a clinical bronchiolitis score or a modified Wood's Clinical Bronchiolitis Score in the note.\n  - [not met] The patient has cough and wheezing, but there is no mention of tachypnea, prolonged expiratory phase, rales, chest retractions, or hyperinflation of lungs on chest radiograph. RSV testing is not menti\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information suggests exclusion based on race or gender.\n  - [not met] The patient is 4 years old, which is greater than 12 months. This exclusion criterion is NOT met (i.e., the patient should be excluded).\n  - [met] No history or findings of cyanotic heart disease are mentioned.\n  - [met] No chest radiograph findings or diagnosis of lobar pneumonia are mentioned.\n  - [met] This criterion states that interstitial disease or atelectasis does not exclude patients. No such findings are mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of croup.\n  - [not met] The history is suggestive of possible foreign body aspiration (sudden onset cough and persistent wheezing after playing in sandbox), but not confirmed. Suspicion is high.\n  - [met] No history of cystic fibrosis, bronchopulmonary dysplasia, or other chronic lung disease.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 17}
{"pair": "sigir-201419__NCT01745107", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's pathological stage, TESCC diagnosis, or whether they received R0 operations at the specified hospital.\n  - [not met] KPS (Karnofsky Performance Status) is not mentioned. However, the patient is described as having progressive dysphagia and significant weight loss, but no explicit mention of functional status.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about neoadjuvant or adjuvant treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recurrent or metastatic lesions before radiotherapy.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the use of IMRT.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about regular follow-up.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of exploratory thoracotomy or palliative surgery.\n  - [met] No clear recurrent or metastatic sites are described.\n  - [met] No evidence of recurrence or metastasis is mentioned.\n  - [met] The patient is alive; no mention of death.\n  - [not met] No information about follow-up regularity.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201529__NCT01917721", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 4-year-old girl (within 1 month to 21 years) with clinical features highly suggestive of Kawasaki Disease (KD): persistent fever, erythematous rash, strawberry tongue, red/cracked lip\n  - [not met] There is no mention of coronary artery dilation or z-score measurements in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of aneurysms of the right or left main coronary arteries in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about prior IVIG treatment, refractory KD, or echocardiogram findings.\n  - [not met] There is no information about coronary artery measurements or z-scores in the clinical note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [met] The patient has classic features of complete KD (fever, rash, conjunctivitis, oral changes, extremity changes). There is no evidence of incomplete KD.\n  - [met] There is no mention of parental refusal to administer doxycycline.\n  - [met] There is no mention of acute renal failure.\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic liver or kidney disease.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT02447172", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient having diabetes mellitus or meeting ADA criteria for diabetes.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of any skin ulcer located on or below the malleolus. The patient presents with knee pain, edema, and an osteolytic lesion, but no ulcer is described.\n  - [not met] The patient has local swelling (edema), tenderness, and possibly induration, but there is no mention of a skin ulcer or purulent discharge. The manifestations are not clearly related to a skin ulcer.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of erythema >2cm, or involvement of structures deeper than skin and subcutaneous tissues in the context of a skin ulcer. Osteolytic lesion is present, but not in the context of a d\n  - [not met] There is no documentation of arterial perfusion in the affected limb(s).\n  - [not met] There is no mention of surgical intervention to remove necrotic or infected bone.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of surgical debridement to remove gangrenous tissue.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypersensitivity to gentamicin or other aminoglycosides.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypersensitivity to bovine collagen.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an ulcer infection or antibiotic regimen issues.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an ulcer associated with prosthetic material or an implanted device.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recent systemic or topical antibiotic therapy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a need for concomitant topical product or wound therapy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being severely immunocompromised.\n  - [met] There is no mention of myasthenia gravis or other neurological conditions where gentamicin is contraindicated.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT00077805", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient had a cryptogenic stroke, CT was negative for hemorrhage, and was treated with thrombolytic therapy, indicating an acute ischemic (non-hemorrhagic) stroke confirmed by imaging.\n  - [not met] Stroke occurred two weeks ago, not within 48 hours prior to randomization. No evidence that study drug is being started within 48 hours of symptom onset.\n  - [not met] No mention of significant motor impairment of the leg or NIHSS score. No evidence provided.\n  - [not met] No mention of inability to walk without assistance.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 72-year-old woman, unlikely to be of childbearing potential. No mention of pregnancy or breastfeeding.\n  - [met] No evidence or mention of VTE at screening.\n  - [met] No evidence or mention of active bleeding.\n  - [met] CT was negative for brain hemorrhage and no prior history of intracranial hemorrhage mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of spinal/epidural analgesia or lumbar puncture within preceding 24 hours.\n  - [met] Thrombolytic therapy was given two weeks ago, not within the preceding 24 hours.\n  - [met] No mention of coma or NIHSS item 1a score. Patient is alert and able to report symptoms.\n  - [met] No evidence of cerebral aneurysm or AVM on imaging.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 22}
{"pair": "sigir-201511__NCT00535561", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms consistent with hypothyroidism (cold sensitivity, fatigue, constipation, hyporeflexia, dry skin, slow movement and speech), but there is no mention of laboratory confirmation \n  - [met] There is no mention of swallowing difficulties. The patient is described as moving and talking slowly, but nothing suggests inability to swallow tablets.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of multifactorial anemia or anemia due to other reasons. Anemia is not discussed in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of iron deficiency anemia requiring urgent intervention, cardiac ischemia, severe anemia, or GI/GU losses. The note does not indicate any acute or severe conditions.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior thyroid disorder or treatment history. The symptoms described are current, and no history of thyroid treatment is provided.\n  - [met] There is no mention of co-morbid diseases such as renal insufficiency/failure, coronary heart disease, hypertension, diabetes mellitus, or other endocrine diseases. Only symptoms of hypothyroidism are", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT02492646", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a 4 year old boy, which is outside the required age range of 20-80 years. There is no mention of scheduled surgery or need for orotracheal intubation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of congenital or acquired abnormalities of the upper airway such as tumor, polyp, trauma, abscess, inflammation, infection, or foreign bodies. The wheezing is likely acute onset af\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous airway surgery or increased risk of aspiration.\n  - [met] There is no mention of coagulation disorders.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous history of difficult intubation or conditions with expected difficult airway.\n  - [met] There is no mention of using other intubation devices beyond direct laryngoscopy.\n  - [met] The patient had sudden onset coughing and current wheezing, but there is no mention of sore throat or upper respiratory tract infection symptoms.\n  - [met] There is no mention of expected placement of a nasogastric tube during the perioperative period.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT00492726", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is a 48-year-old male hospitalized after surgery and taken to ICU.\n  - [met] Patient has a ruptured liver abscess, which typically requires IV antibiotics for at least 5 days. Exact duration not specified, but clinical context supports this.\n  - [not met] Ability to provide consent is not specified in the note.\n  - [met] Confirmed intra-abdominal infection: ruptured liver abscess.\n  - [met] Exploratory laparotomy performed and revealed ruptured liver abscess.\n  - [met] Gross peritoneal inflammation is likely given abundant free intraperitoneal fluid and surgical findings, but not explicitly stated.\n  - [met] Intra-abdominal abscess confirmed (liver abscess).\n  - [not met] No mention of intestinal perforation.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to antibiotics.\n  - [met] Patient is male.\n  - [met] No history of tendon disease/disorder related to quinolone treatment mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of QT prolongation, hypokalemia, bradycardia, heart failure, or arrhythmias.\n  - [met] No mention of concomitant use of QT-prolonging drugs.\n  - [met] No mention of severe end stage liver disease.\n  - [met] Creatinine clearance not mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of prior systemic antibacterial therapy.", "n_inc_assessed": 18, "n_exc_assessed": 12}
{"pair": "sigir-20144__NCT01440075", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy with clinical features and echocardiogram findings consistent with Kawasaki Disease (KD), including fever, conjunctivitis, strawberry tongue, extremity changes, lymphad\n  - [not met] The patient is 2 years old, which is less than 18 years old.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient's or guardian's agreement to participate in all explorations of the study.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about acceptance of genotyping.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cardiovascular risk factors such as hypertension, diabetes, dyslipidemia, or smoking. The patient is 2 years old, making such risk factors highly unlikely.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient meets the classic criteria for KD (fever >5 days, conjunctivitis, oral changes, extremity changes, rash/desquamation, lymphadenopathy). There is no evidence of atypical KD.\n  - [met] There is no documentation or suspicion of coronary ischemia; only coronary artery dilation/aneurysm is noted.\n  - [not met] There is no information about refusal to participate or consent.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy or renal failure or other contraindication to iodinated contrast agents.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to dobutamine.\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy, so this criterion does not apply.\n  - [met] The patient is a 2-year-old boy, so this criterion does not apply.\n  - [met] No mention of treatment modifying endothelial reactivity.", "n_inc_assessed": 5, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-201420__NCT01594385", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is a trauma patient admitted after a car accident with multiple injuries. However, there is no explicit mention of DC/OA (damage control/open abdomen) management being performed.\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient has a life expectancy less than 48 hours. She is awake, alert, and hemodynamically stable.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is a prisoner.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old, which is not younger than 18.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20149__NCT02260180", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 43 years old, which is at least 18.\n  - [not met] Fitzpatrick skin type is not specified in the note.\n  - [not met] The lesions are described as small, soft, pedunculated, and on the neck. These features are more consistent with skin tags (acrochordons) than seborrheic keratosis. No mention of seborrheic keratosis.\n  - [not met] No mention of a seborrheic keratosis lesion on the face; lesions are on the neck.\n  - [not met] Lesions are described as clinically typical for skin tags, but not for seborrheic keratosis.\n  - [met] No mention of prior treatment; likely treatment na\u00efve.\n  - [not met] No Physician's Lesion Assessment (PLA) score is provided.\n  - [not met] Largest lesion is 4 mm in diameter, which is less than the required \u22657mm.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of atypical or rapidly growing lesions.\n  - [met] Multiple lesions are present, but no mention of eruptive onset or Sign of Leser-Trelat.\n  - [met] No mention of systemic malignancy.\n  - [met] No mention of keloid formation or hypertrophic scarring.\n  - [met] No mention of recent systemic therapy.\n  - [met] No mention of retinoid use.\n  - [met] No mention of glucocortico-steroid use.\n  - [met] No mention of anti-metabolite use.", "n_inc_assessed": 22, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201410__NCT00481741", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 67-year-old woman, which is \u2265 18 years old.\n  - [met] The patient underwent cardiac catheterization via the right femoral artery, which is a coronary or peripheral vascular intervention.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about the size of the arterial sheath used.\n  - [not met] There is no information about overnight hospitalization following the procedure.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a pulsatile mass and loss of distal pulses, but there is no mention of hematoma or persistent bleeding around the vascular sheath.\n  - [met] There is no mention of previous AV fistula or pseudoaneurysm in the ipsilateral femoral artery.\n  - [met] There is no mention of history of bleeding diathesis or coagulopathy.\n  - [met] No information about hemoglobin level is provided.\n  - [met] No information about baseline ambulation ability is provided.\n  - [met] No information about allergy to materials used in SafeSeal.\n  - [met] The patient is a 67-year-old woman; there is no mention of pregnancy or lactation, and age makes pregnancy unlikely.\n  - [met] No evidence of ongoing systemic or cutaneous infection is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT00443313", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 32-year-old female (within 26-65 age range), not pregnant, no history of hysterectomy, and is attending clinic for pap smear results. There is no evidence she is excluded by any of th\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 32 years old, which is between 26 and 65 years of age.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy or recent childbirth. She is described as in general good health and no complaints.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of hysterectomy. She is attending for pap smear results, which implies she has a cervix.\n  - [met] There is no mention of an overt cancerous lesion visible on exam. The pap smear was cytology negative.\n  - [met] There is no mention of inability to speak English, mental incompetence, or refusal to participate. The note is in English and the patient is attending clinic and discussing results.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201410__NCT01001663", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is described as a 67-year-old woman, which is over 18 years old.\n  - [met] The patient underwent cardiac catheterization via the right femoral artery, which is consistent with femoral access coronary angiography.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's competence for providing informed, written consent.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the sheath size used during the procedure.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of percutaneous coronary intervention; only diagnostic catheterization is described.\n  - [met] No mention of intra coronary measurements (FFR, IVUS, OCT, NIR) in the note.\n  - [met] No mention of groin hematoma before closure; the note describes a pulsatile mass, which may indicate a vascular complication but not specifically a hematoma before closure.\n  - [not met] The patient has a pulsatile mass in the right groin with loss of distal pulses and a bruit, which is highly suggestive of a pseudoaneurysm or AV fistula.\n  - [met] No explicit mention of significant stenosis of ilial or femoral artery.\n  - [met] No mention of prior peripheral artery surgery.\n  - [met] No information about INR.\n  - [met] No information about platelet count.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-201521__NCT00002248", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the patient's current medications.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about allowed concurrent medications.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about use of antidiarrheal compounds.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about HIV therapy.\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms of diarrhea after drinking untreated water, but the stool smear revealed ellipsoidal cysts with 2+ nuclei, which is characteristic of Giardia, not Cryptosporidium. No evidence\n  - [not met] The patient presents with diarrhea, but chronicity (duration >2-4 weeks) is not specified.\n  - [met] No evidence of life-threatening illness; patient is a 32-year-old male with GI symptoms. Presumed to have life expectancy >4 weeks.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [not met] The patient has Giardia (ellipsoidal cysts with 2+ nuclei), which is an enteric pathogen other than C. parvum. Thus, this exclusion criterion is NOT met.\n  - [met] No evidence of other acute infections or life-threatening crisis; Giardia is not immediately life-threatening.\n  - [met] No mention of bloody diarrhea; stools are described as greasy and foul-smelling.\n  - [met] No mention of milk allergy.\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [not met] This is a header, not a criterion.", "n_inc_assessed": 14, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201423__NCT02340702", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The clinical note does not mention a diagnosis of heart failure. The patient's symptoms (cough, shortness of breath, cyanosis, tachypnea, barrel-shaped chest, diffuse rales, hyperinflation on chest x-\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient required admission due to worsening respiratory symptoms and has been using home oxygen for the past 24 hours. This suggests he is not ambulatory and is currently hospitalized.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT01869855", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 85 years old (over 18) and presents with neurological symptoms (gradual decrease in consciousness, stopped walking/eating). However, there is no explicit mention of a chronic subdural h\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a chronic subdural hematoma being verified on cranial CT or MRI. The only imaging mentioned is a normal head CT 3 weeks ago.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no information about the surgeon deciding to perform a craniotomy or intraoperative findings.\n  - [met] There is no evidence that the chronic subdural hematoma (if present) is caused by another underlying illness such as over-drainage of a VP shunt.\n  - [not met] There is no information regarding informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20152__NCT00411645", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention in the clinical note of the patient having received an allogeneic stem cell transplant.\n  - [not met] The patient's CMV serostatus (recipient or donor) is not mentioned in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about transplant engraftment in the note.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to swallow tablets.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has evidence of CMV organ disease: 'owl's eye inclusion bodies' in BAL fluid are classic for CMV pneumonia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of HIV infection in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the use of other anti-CMV therapy post-transplant; however, there is also no mention of transplant.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT00948610", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 31 years old (within age range). She has had 2 weeks of joint pain and fatigue, with pain, swelling, and stiffness in multiple joints (knees, hips, right elbow, previously right ankle).\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient receiving DMARDs.\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient receiving TNF antagonists or other biologic medications.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient currently taking steroids.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient using opioid agents.\n  - [met] The patient has no previous medical problems and no mention of co-morbid medical disorders or other autoimmune/inflammatory diseases.\n  - [met] There is no mention of chronic infections.\n  - [met] There is no mention of co-morbid pain disorders such as fibromyalgia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of psychiatric disorders.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy or breast-feeding.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT02440815", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with symptoms consistent with major depressive disorder (fatigue, increased sleep and appetite, difficulty concentrating, anhedonia, guilt), but the note does not explicitly state\n  - [not met] No Hamilton Depression Rating Scale (HDRS) score is provided. Symptoms suggest moderate depression, but without a score, this cannot be confirmed.\n  - [met] The patient is a female college student and the note is in English, indicating she is English speaking.\n  - [not met] The patient is 20 years old, not 65 or older.\n  - [met] Physical exam and laboratory tests are within normal limits, and there is no mention of any significant medical history. This suggests good general health.\n  - [met] No explicit statement about ability to give informed consent, but as a college student with no cognitive impairment, it is reasonable to assume she can.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of antidepressant use, psychotherapy, or electroconvulsive therapy.\n  - [met] No mention of substance or alcohol abuse or dependence.\n  - [met] No mention of cognitive enhancing medications.\n  - [met] No mention of PTSD or other Axis 1 psychiatric disorders besides possible depression.\n  - [met] No mention of neurological diseases or dementia.\n  - [met] No mention of surgical procedures affecting study outcomes.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindications for MR exam, claustrophobia, metal implants, or BMI. As a 20-year-old college student, likely able to fit in MRI comfortably.\n  - [met] Physical exam and labs are normal, no mention of acute or uncontrolled medical illness or medication use impacting cognitive function.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT02192320", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 85 years old, which is \u226518 and <90 years old. Gender is male, which is included.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of the patient being on long-term antiplatelet or anticoagulant drugs or having coagulation disorders.\n  - [not met] The note mentions a normal head CT 3 weeks ago and does not mention any CT showing chronic subdural hematoma.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about midline shift on imaging.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about the attending physician's judgment or treatment plan.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient having undergone surgery on a hematoma.\n  - [not met] No information is provided about informed consent or the patient's understanding.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to statin or dexamethasone.\n  - [met] No mention of hematoma caused by tumors, blood, or other comorbidities.\n  - [met] No mention of abnormal liver function.\n  - [met] No mention of hepatitis, liver disease, or other interfering diseases.\n  - [met] No mention of oral statin treatment in the past four weeks.\n  - [met] No mention of long-term oral steroid treatment.\n  - [met] No mention of diabetes or poorly controlled blood glucose.\n  - [met] No mention of participation in clinical trials in the past four weeks.", "n_inc_assessed": 7, "n_exc_assessed": 11}
{"pair": "sigir-201522__NCT01259336", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has started to complain of productive cough with tinges of blood, but the duration of symptoms is not specified. Chronic symptoms lasting \u2265 six weeks are not explicitly mentioned.\n  - [met] Radiological findings are present: Chest X-ray reveals a round opaque mass within a cavity in the left upper lobe, and CT imaging shows the mass moves within the cavity.\n  - [not met] There is evidence of a cavity with a mass, but the note does not specify 'slowly progressive pulmonary lesions over weeks-months' or mention surrounding inflammation.\n  - [not met] There is an intracavitary mass described, but the presence of a surrounding crescent of air or pleural thickening is not mentioned.\n  - [met] Sputum culture revealed an organism with septated, low-angle branching hyphae with straight, parallel walls, which is characteristic of Aspergillus species. This meets the criterion for demonstration \n  - [met] The diagnosis of CCPA is not explicitly stated, but the findings are highly suggestive of chronic cavitary pulmonary aspergillosis.\n  - [met] Patient satisfies radiological findings (1) and microbiological findings (4), which aligns with the requirement to satisfy at least 1, 2a or 2b and/or any of the 3rd criteria.\n  - [not met] FNAC from the cavity wall is only considered in atypical cases; there is no mention of FNAC being performed or needed.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no evidence of invasive aspergillosis (no mention of acute, rapidly progressive disease or systemic involvement).\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA) or related symptoms (e.g., asthma, eosinophilia).\n  - [met] The patient has a history of tuberculosis, but there is no evidence of active tuberculosis or malignancy in the current presentation.\n  - [met] The patient is a 65-year-old male, so cannot be a pregnant female.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20152__NCT00002025", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No co-existing conditions are specified in the clinical note.\n  - [met] No specific conditions are listed in the note that would exclude the patient.\n  - [met] Patient does not have AIDS or peripheral CMV retinitis, nor is there mention of meeting IND protocol criteria.\n  - [met] Severity of CMV infection is not fully described, but patient is hospitalized and immunosuppressed, suggesting more than mild/moderate disease.\n  - [met] No mention of transplant status; patient is on immunosuppressive drugs but not identified as a transplant patient.\n  - [met] Patient is a 62-year-old male, not a child.\n  - [met] No mention of hypersensitivity to these drugs.\n  - [met] No mention of antimetabolite treatment.", "n_inc_assessed": 0, "n_exc_assessed": 27}
{"pair": "sigir-201518__NCT01529463", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, which is greater than or equal to 18.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms and physical findings consistent with acute decompensated heart failure (shortness of breath, orthopnea, bibasilar crackles, pitting edema, jugular venous distension), but it \n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about referral to the Congestive Heart Failure Disease Management Program.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 65 years old, so he is not under 18.\n  - [met] There is no mention of mental incapacitation in the note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of discharge to a skilled nursing facility.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201517__NCT00458562", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient underwent Pap smear and HPV testing, as evidenced by the results discussed. There is no mention of HIV testing.\n  - [not met] No mention of biopsy or colposcopy, nor diagnosis of CIN or ICC.\n  - [not met] No mention of CIN grade 2-3 or higher.\n  - [not met] No mention of repeated CIN1.\n  - [not met] Pap smear cytology was negative, so no abnormal Pap smear (ASCUS or worse).\n  - [not met] No mention of HIV seropositivity.\n  - [met] Cytology was negative and HPV was positive.\n  - [not met] Cytology was negative but HPV was positive, so does not meet negative HPV requirement.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] Patient is 32 years old.\n  - [met] No mention of pregnancy.\n  - [met] No mention of cervix not intact; Pap smear performed.\n  - [met] No evidence of inability to provide informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 13, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201530__NCT01562535", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The criterion is for children with suspected pulled elbow. The patient is a 47-year-old male, not a child, and the diagnosis is elbow dislocation, not pulled elbow.\n  - [not met] This criterion requires a history of an adult or bigger person pulling a child's elbow. The patient is an adult and there is no mention of someone pulling his arm.\n  - [met] The patient presents with intense pain, swelling, bruising, and inability to bend the arm, which fits the criterion of intense pain and unwillingness to move the arm.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention or suspicion of intentional injury or child abuse.\n  - [not met] The patient has obvious deformity, ecchymoses, edema, and the mechanism was a fall, not pulling. This matches the exclusion criterion for suspected fracture or non-pulling mechanism.\n  - [met] The mechanism was a fall on an outstretched arm, not multiple trauma.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any chronic disease affecting bone mineralization.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-20156__NCT02107794", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 46-year-old woman, which is \u2265 18 years.\n  - [met] The patient presents with classic symptoms and signs of Graves Disease (weight loss, sweating, insomnia, diarrhea, increased appetite, palpitations, warm/sweaty hands, tachycardia, hyperreflexia, mild\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention of an appointment with an endocrinologist to discuss treatment options for Graves Disease in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of dementia, severe hearing or visual impairment, or other major barriers to shared decision making or informed consent.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 1}
{"pair": "sigir-201510__NCT01588899", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 38 year old woman, which is between 18 and 55 years.\n  - [not met] No information about the patient's weight is provided.\n  - [met] The patient is 38 years old and is having regular periods, indicating she is pre- or peri-menopausal.\n  - [not met] No information about uterine size is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about cervical cell assessment is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about fibroids is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about planned ablation volume or fibroids is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about the number of fibroids is provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a history of pelvic pain and infertility, but there is no mention of other pelvic disease such as endometriosis, ovarian tumor, acute pelvic disease, or significant adenomyosis.\n  - [not met] The patient has a history of two years of infertility treatment and an ectopic pregnancy, but there is no explicit statement about her current desire for future pregnancy.\n  - [met] No significant systemic disease is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No information about pregnancy test results is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about hematocrit is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about abdominal wall scarring is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about surgical clips is provided.\n  - [not met] No information about MRI contraindications is provided.", "n_inc_assessed": 13, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201417__NCT01161849", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is in the post-operative period of abdominal surgery, but the surgery was not elective and not specifically of colon-rectum, ileum, stomach, or pancreas. It was an urgent laparotomy for a \n  - [met] The patient underwent an urgent laparotomy for a non-traumatic acute abdomen (ruptured liver abscess).\n  - [met] The patient has signs of sepsis in the post-operative period: fever, tachycardia, hypotension, and acute abdominal pain.\n  - [met] The patient has signs of systemic hypoperfusion in the post-operative period: hypotension (BP 80/40), tachycardia (HR 132), and dehydration.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient underwent surgery involving the liver (drainage of ruptured liver abscess), which qualifies as liver surgery.\n  - [met] There is mention of surgical drainage of a liver abscess, but no explicit mention of drainage of bile, blood, or dejection from abdominal drainage.\n  - [met] Sepsis and hypoperfusion are due to intra-abdominal infection (ruptured liver abscess), not extra-abdominal infection.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT00908063", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old, which is younger than the required 18-70 years.\n  - [not met] No information about the patient's weight is provided.\n  - [met] The patient was transferred to the ED and received immediate treatment within a short time after injury, likely within 12 hours.\n  - [not met] The patient has a severe non-penetrating TBI (fall, GCS 6/15, clinical deterioration). However, there is no CT scan performed, so definite anatomic signs of injury on CT are not confirmed.\n  - [met] At the scene, both pupils were reactive. Upon arrival, pupils were asymmetrical but reactivity at that time is not specified.\n  - [not met] No information about consent or surrogate decision maker is provided.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [met] This is a header, not a criterion.\n  - [met] No indication that the patient is not expected to survive the next 24 hours.\n  - [met] No information about BMI or morbid obesity.\n  - [met] The patient had impaired movement on the right side but was moving all limbs initially. No mention of complete absence of motor response.\n  - [met] No mention of hyperthermia.\n  - [met] Pupils were asymmetrical, not bilaterally fixed and dilated.\n  - [met] Injury was non-penetrating (fall from bike, struck temple).", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 24}
{"pair": "sigir-201430__NCT00311805", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 72-year-old man, which is greater than 21 years old.\n  - [not met] The patient has symptoms consistent with infra-inguinal atherosclerosis (calf pain, diminished dorsalis pedis pulses, cool extremities). However, the note does not specify the exact arteries involved \n  - [not met] The patient has increasing calf pain when walking uphill (intermittent claudication), but the symptoms have been present for 3 months, not 6 months as required.\n  - [not met] The patient has a diagnosis consistent with Peripheral Arterial Disease (PAD) in at least one lower limb (diminished pulses, cool extremities, claudication), but the duration is only 3 months, not 6 m\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of recent (within 3 months) aortic or lower extremity arterial surgery, angioplasty, or lumbar sympathectomy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of iliac disease or that it is amenable to revascularization.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is a suitable candidate for surgical or percutaneous revascularization.\n  - [met] The patient has intermittent claudication (Rutherford Class 3), not Critical Limb Ischemia (Rutherford 4, 5, or 6).\n  - [met] The arterial insufficiency appears to be due to atherosclerosis, not a non-atherosclerotic disorder.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT00118651", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 31-year-old male, which is older than 18 years.\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute respiratory symptoms including productive cough, chest pain, fever, chills, and worsening cough.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of chest radiographs or their results in the clinical note.\n  - [met] The note does not specify the setting, but there is no indication the patient is hospitalized; outpatient or emergency department presentation is likely.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, not under 18.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recent hospitalization or hospital discharge, so hospital-acquired pneumonia is unlikely.\n  - [met] There is no mention of aspiration risk factors or events (e.g., altered mental status, swallowing difficulties), so aspiration pneumonia is unlikely.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 3}
{"pair": "sigir-20142__NCT01192789", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 8 years old, which is 96 months, and thus outside the specified age range of 2 to 59 months. The note does not mention presentation to LHWs, only to the ER.\n  - [not met] There is no information in the note about informed consent being given by a legal guardian.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note describes respiratory distress, but does not specify 'very severe disease' as defined by the study. The severity is unclear.\n  - [met] There is no mention of persistent vomiting in the clinical note.\n  - [met] There is no mention of parental or caretaker refusal to participate.\n  - [met] There is no mention of the child being treated for non-severe pneumonia who advanced to severe pneumonia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of suspected or known kerosene oil ingestion.\n  - [met] There is no mention of prior enrollment in the study within 2 weeks of last follow up.\n  - [met] The patient had loose stools prior to onset of fever and cough, but there is no mention of severe diarrhea with signs of dehydration or severe malnutrition.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
{"pair": "sigir-201516__NCT00851487", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 4 year old boy (age 48 months), which falls within the 2 to 59 months range. He is attending the emergency room, which is not an outpatient clinic, but the note does not specify if th\n  - [not met] WHO defined non-severe pneumonia requires cough or difficulty breathing with no signs of severe pneumonia (no chest indrawing, no cyanosis, etc). The patient has wheezing and a brief episode of coughi\n  - [met] The patient was brought to the ED by his mother, suggesting accessibility for follow-up. No evidence suggests otherwise.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of written informed consent by a parent or legal guardian in the note.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of lower chest wall retraction or indrawing, and no signs of very severe disease/pneumonia are described. The child is playful and well appearing.\n  - [met] O2 sats are 100% on room air, so no cyanosis.\n  - [met] No mention of inability to drink; the child is playful and well appearing.\n  - [met] No mention of convulsions.\n  - [met] The child is playful and well appearing, so not abnormally sleepy or difficult to wake.\n  - [met] No mention of severe malnutrition, weight, or oedema.\n  - [met] No history of wheezing prior to this episode, and no diagnosis of asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of congenital heart disease, cyanosis, congestive heart failure, or cardiomegaly.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 16}
{"pair": "sigir-20157__NCT00339066", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient reports fatigue, increased sleep and appetite, difficulty concentrating, anhedonia, and guilt. These symptoms are consistent with DSM-IV criteria for major depressive disorder (MDD), thoug\n  - [not met] No MADRS score is provided. The patient has symptoms consistent with depression, possibly atypical depression, but without a score, this cannot be confirmed.\n  - [not met] No MMSE score is provided. There is no evidence of cognitive impairment, but the criterion requires a specific score.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of any condition that would make MRI medically inadvisable.\n  - [met] The patient has no significant past medical history and physical exam/labs are normal. No severe or unstable medical conditions are reported.\n  - [met] No known primary neurological disorders or history of stroke are mentioned.\n  - [met] No other simultaneous Axis I disorder is mentioned. Only depressive symptoms are described.\n  - [met] No history of substance or alcohol abuse disorder is mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of suicidal ideation or risk.\n  - [met] No history of failed prior adequate trials of two antidepressants for the current depressive episode is mentioned.\n  - [met] No history of failed prior adequate trial of sertraline is mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 9}
{"pair": "sigir-201413__NCT02375919", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with acute onset of shortness of breath (dyspnea) that started 2 hours before admission.\n  - [met] The patient is described as generally healthy, with no significant past health problems, and the presentation is not described as high risk for PE. The gestalt (clinical impression) would likely be lo\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No other obvious cause for dyspnea or chest pain is mentioned in the note. Physical exam, chest x-ray, and CBC are normal.\n  - [met] Although the patient is tachypneic and tachycardic, her blood pressure is stable and there is no mention of shock, respiratory failure, or other acute severe presentation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any contraindication to CTPA (e.g., contrast allergy, renal failure, etc.).\n  - [met] There is no mention of the patient being on anticoagulation treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a current diagnosed thrombo-embolic event.\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient would be unable to follow up.\n  - [met] There is no mention that the patient is a prisoner.\n  - [met] The patient gave birth 3 weeks ago, so she is postpartum, not currently pregnant.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-20155__NCT00339157", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of SO-JIA is mentioned. Patient is 31 years old, which is outside the 2-20 years age range. No information on corticosteroid resistance or prior IL-1ra treatment.\n  - [not met] No diagnosis of SO-JIA (Edmonton's revision) is mentioned in the note.\n  - [not met] Patient is 31 years old, which is outside the required age range (2-20 years).\n  - [not met] Disease duration is 2 weeks, which is less than the required 6 months.\n  - [not met] No information about corticosteroid treatment or failure/requirement.\n  - [not met] Active arthritis is described (multiple joints with pain, swelling, stiffness), but no information on Giannini's core-set items, physician/parent assessments, CHAQ score, or ESR.\n  - [not met] No information on CRP or ESR values.\n  - [not met] Patient has polyarthritis (multiple joints involved), but no information on radiological evidence of irreversible damage.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of previous treatment with IL-1Ra.\n  - [met] No mention of intra-articular injection or recent changes in NSAIDs/corticosteroids.\n  - [met] No mention of treatment with other immunosuppressive or disease-modifying drugs.\n  - [met] No mention of contraindication to anakinra, active infection, or allergy.\n  - [met] No previous history of malignancy or heart insufficiency is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of asthma.\n  - [met] No mention of need for therapeutic intervention before study completion.\n  - [not met] No lab values are provided, so cannot assess for cytopenias or abnormal liver/renal function.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201525__NCT00679835", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about written parental consent.\n  - [not met] The patient is 10 years old, which is outside the 2-6 year age range.\n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's ability to comply with the protocol.\n  - [met] The patient is clinically stable: normal blood pressure, no mention of pharmacological intervention for BP, and no evidence or history of renal or hepatic compromise.\n  - [not met] The patient has fever, lethargy, and an osteolytic lesion, suggesting possible infection, but there is no explicit mention of a suspected or diagnosed Gram-positive infection or antibiotic therapy.\n  - [not met] No information about creatinine clearance or renal function labs.\n  - [not met] No information about CPK levels.\n  - [not met] No information about intravenous lines or venous access.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of investigational drug use or participation in experimental procedures.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy or hypersensitivity to daptomycin.\n  - [met] No history of clinically significant cardiovascular, renal, hepatic, pulmonary, GI, endocrine, hematologic, autoimmune disease, or primary immune deficiency is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of pneumonia.\n  - [met] No mention of abnormal laboratory test results or ECGs.\n  - [met] No mention of rifampin administration.\n  - [not met] No information about BMI.\n  - [not met] No information about risk from blood volume collection.", "n_inc_assessed": 8, "n_exc_assessed": 13}
{"pair": "sigir-201524__NCT00540072", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No information is provided about informed consent.\n  - [met] Patient is a 31-year-old male, which meets the age and gender requirements. No information about weight, but no evidence to suggest >150 kg. Not female, so pregnancy/lactation/birth control not applic\n  - [not met] No mention of chest radiograph or pulmonary infiltrate.\n  - [met] Patient has fever, productive cough, chest pain, and chills, which are clinical symptoms of pneumonia.\n  - [met] Patient has productive cough, which likely indicates production of purulent sputum or change in character of sputum.\n  - [met] Lung exam reveals egophany (evidence of consolidation) and decreased breath sounds.\n  - [not met] No mention of dyspnea or tachypnea. Respiratory rate is 15 (normal).\n  - [met] Temperature is 103.4\u00b0F (>38\u00b0C), so documented fever is present.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No information about Fine Score or Grade V pneumonia.\n  - [met] No evidence of respiratory failure; respiratory rate is normal and no mention of distress.\n  - [met] No mention of other pulmonary conditions that would preclude interpretation.\n  - [met] No mention or history of cystic fibrosis.\n  - [met] No mention or history of lung cancer or metastatic malignancy.\n  - [met] No mention of bronchial obstruction or post-obstructive pneumonia.\n  - [met] No mention or suspicion of active tuberculosis.\n  - [met] Blood pressure is 120/80, so no severe shock.", "n_inc_assessed": 12, "n_exc_assessed": 18}
{"pair": "sigir-20154__NCT00990262", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presented with chest pain lasting more than five minutes and was admitted to rule out acute coronary syndrome.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient had elevated initial troponin (0.40 ng/ml) and CK-MB (10.9 ng/ml), both of which are considered positive.\n  - [not met] The ECG showed ST-segment elevations up to 3 mm in V1, V2, and V3, which are diagnostic ECG changes.\n  - [met] The patient was hypertensive but not described as hemodynamically unstable, no ventricular tachycardia, and no persistent chest pain despite therapy is mentioned.\n  - [not met] The patient has chronic renal insufficiency, but no creatinine clearance value is provided. However, chronic renal insufficiency often implies reduced clearance, possibly <50 mL/min.\n  - [met] No mention of allergy to iodinated contrast agents.\n  - [met] No mention of metformin therapy.\n  - [met] No mention of asthma or reactive airway disease.\n  - [met] The ECG showed sinus tachycardia, not atrial fibrillation.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 10}
{"pair": "sigir-20151__NCT00838682", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient presents with hematemesis (vomiting with 'coffee ground' appearance), hypotension, and signs of shock, which are consistent with upper GI bleeding. However, there is no mention of a peptic\n  - [not met] There is no information provided about the patient undergoing an endoscopic hemostasis procedure or achieving primary hemostasis via upper GI endoscopy.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no indication that the patient refused an endoscopic procedure.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of complications from gastric ulcer requiring operative treatment prior to endoscopy (e.g., no mention of perforation or obstruction).\n  - [met] The patient is a 44-year-old male, so pregnancy is not applicable.\n  - [met] There is no mention of serious concurrent diseases such as malignant tumors or end-stage diseases.\n  - [met] There is no history provided of previous gastrectomy or vagotomy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of hypersensitivity to proton pump inhibitors.\n  - [met] The patient is 44 years old, which does not qualify as elderly.\n  - [met] There is no mention of epilepsy.", "n_inc_assessed": 2, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201515__NCT00861133", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient was hospitalized for cryptogenic stroke two weeks ago, which is within 30 days. The note describes sudden onset of focal neurological deficits presumed vascular etiology and lasting more t\n  - [met] Computed tomography was negative for brain hemorrhage, indicating no evidence of hemorrhagic stroke.\n  - [met] The patient is currently in normal sinus rhythm on a 12-lead electrocardiogram.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a known history of atrial fibrillation. The patient reports occasional palpitations, but this does not confirm atrial fibrillation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a previous implanted cardiac device (ppM or ICD).\n  - [met] There is no mention of a serious illness making it unlikely for the patient to survive one year. The patient has hypertension and diabetes, but these are not immediately life-threatening.\n  - [met] The stroke is described as cryptogenic, and workup found no evidence of abnormalities or secondary cause.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201528__NCT01193803", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient is 8 years old, not more than 18 years old.\n  - [not met] No information about consent for medical record review.\n  - [not met] No evidence or mention of spondylodiscitis.\n  - [not met] No mention of discitis or vertebral osteomyelitis or need for spinal biopsy.\n  - [met] Clinical presentation is described (pain, fever, limping, swollen knee).\n  - [not met] No mention of spinal pain.\n  - [met] Localized tenderness and limited range of motion (limping, tender/swollen knee) are present.\n  - [not met] Fever is present, but temperature not specified (>38\u00b0C not confirmed).\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):", "n_inc_assessed": 30, "n_exc_assessed": 0}
{"pair": "sigir-201414__NCT01624545", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of chronic subdural hematoma by CT or MRI, nor any mention of surgery within the last 48 hours.\n  - [met] The patient is 85 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [not met] There is no information about written informed consent from the patient.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a gradual decrease in consciousness and stopped walking/eating, but there is no explicit statement that he is moribund or that surgery is prohibited.\n  - [met] No information is provided about geographic barriers to follow-up.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recurrent hematoma or prior surgery for hematoma.\n  - [met] There is no mention of CSH due to spontaneous spinal CSF fistula or meningeosis carcinomatosa.\n  - [met] The patient is male, so pregnancy is not possible.\n  - [met] There is no mention of metastatic disease or a high likelihood of death in 6 months.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201416__NCT01827917", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The note does not mention informed consent or willingness/ability to understand protocol requirements, but as the patient is an adult, it is likely she could provide consent. However, this is not expl\n  - [not met] The patient is described as having neck and shoulder pain, paresthesias, tremors, spasticity, and later severe symptoms (spastic movements, hydrophobia, agitation, etc.), indicating she is not in good\n  - [not met] There is no information about the 'man-killer' (presumably the animal responsible for injury) being found or tested for virus carriage.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of a known bleeding disorder, immunologic impairment, or receipt of immunosuppressive therapy or immunoglobulin since birth.\n  - [met] There is no mention of passive immunity preparation being applied.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-201428__NCT02551367", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 31 years old, which is within the 20-35 age range.\n  - [met] The patient has secondary amenorrhea (no periods for 7 months) and is trying to conceive, which suggests secondary infertility.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a diagnosis of PCOS or Rotterdam criteria being met. The patient has amenorrhea and hyperprolactinemia, but no evidence of polycystic ovaries, oligo/anovulation, or hyperandroge\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has elevated prolactin, which is hyperprolactinemia.\n  - [met] No mention of male factor infertility; patient is female and no partner information is provided.\n  - [met] No information about seminal fluid analysis is provided.\n  - [met] No information about seminal fluid volume is provided.\n  - [met] No information about seminal fluid pH is provided.\n  - [met] No information about liquefaction time is provided.\n  - [met] No information about sperm concentration is provided.\n  - [met] No information about total motility is provided.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 14}
{"pair": "sigir-20145__NCT01164046", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has cancer (recent mastectomy for breast cancer) and symptoms/signs suggestive of PE or DVT (shortness of breath, right calf tenderness, elevated D-dimer), but there is no confirmation of \n  - [not met] There is no mention of written informed consent in the clinical note.\n  - [not met] There is no explicit mention of an indication for long-term anticoagulant therapy such as metastasized disease or ongoing chemotherapy. The patient is post-mastectomy and bedridden, which may increase\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 56 years old, which is above the minimum age of 18.\n  - [met] There is no indication for anticoagulant therapy other than DVT or PE mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any contraindication to LMWH or VKA in the note.\n  - [not met] The patient is a 56-year-old female, but there is no information about childbearing potential, contraceptive measures, pregnancy, or breastfeeding.\n  - [met] There is no mention of life expectancy, but nothing in the note suggests a life expectancy less than 3 months.", "n_inc_assessed": 3, "n_exc_assessed": 5}
{"pair": "sigir-201519__NCT00202176", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient has a significant smoking history, chronic cough, progressive shortness of breath, and physical findings (barrel chest, wheezes) consistent with COPD. There is no evidence that she is a he\n  - [met] The patient is 66 years old, which is within the 40-80 year age range.\n  - [met] There is no information suggesting the patient is unable to perform study procedures. She was able to walk from the waiting room to the exam room, though with distress. Assume able unless stated other\n  - [met] The patient has smoked 1-2 packs per day for 47 years, which is at least 47 pack-years, well above the >10 pack-year threshold for mild COPD.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of an allergy to atrovent.\n  - [met] There is no mention of a history of asthma, atopy, or nasal polyps.\n  - [met] There is no information about oxygen desaturation during exercise.\n  - [met] There is no mention of recent CAD or other significant diseases besides COPD that could contribute to dyspnea or exercise limitation.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 4}
{"pair": "sigir-201421__NCT01689025", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 21-year-old female. There is no mention of pregnancy or nursing.\n  - [not met] The patient has clinical and laboratory features consistent with SLE (arthralgias, malar rash, alopecia, anemia, thrombocytopenia, positive ANA and anti-dsDNA, proteinuria, RBC casts). However, diseas\n  - [met] The patient has clinically active SLE (multiple organ involvement, positive ANA and anti-dsDNA). While the exact SELENA-SLEDAI score is not given, the described findings would likely result in a score\n  - [not met] There is no information about background medication or its stability.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has active lupus nephritis (proteinuria and RBC casts), which is an exclusion if present within the last 4 months. The note describes current findings, so this criterion is NOT met (i.e., \n  - [not met] There is no information about the patient's BMI.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 2}
{"pair": "sigir-20156__NCT00150124", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient has classic symptoms and signs of hyperthyroidism (weight loss, sweating, insomnia, diarrhea, increased appetite, tachycardia, hyperreflexia, exophthalmia). However, there is no explicit m\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 46 years old, which is above 18 years.\n  - [met] There is no mention of allergy to anti-thyroid drugs.\n  - [met] There is no mention of substernal or large goiter.\n  - [met] The patient has mild exophthalmia, but there is no evidence of severe endocrine ophthalmopathy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of pregnancy or lactation.\n  - [met] There is no suspicion of thyroid malignancy mentioned.\n  - [met] There is no mention of unsafe contra-conception.\n  - [met] There is no mention of any physical or mental condition that would hinder cooperation.", "n_inc_assessed": 1, "n_exc_assessed": 8}
{"pair": "sigir-201425__NCT02119533", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient was transferred to the emergency department after trauma, which is consistent with recruitment from the Emergency Department or Trauma Bay. There is no information about consent, but this \n  - [not met] There is no CT scan result provided in the note, so there is no evidence of hemorrhage, contusion, or skull fracture. Cannot confirm structural TBI by imaging.\n  - [not met] No imaging was performed, so structural injury cannot be confirmed or excluded. The patient has symptoms (vomiting, drowsiness, impaired movement, GCS 6), but these are not sufficient to confirm non-s\n  - [not met] The note explicitly states there was no immediate loss of consciousness.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of loss of memory for events before or after the accident.\n  - [met] The patient became drowsy and pale, which is an alteration in mental state.\n  - [met] The patient has focal neurological deficits (impaired movement of right upper and lower extremities). The severity of injury is not fully clear, but GCS is 6, which is severe TBI (not mild/moderate).\n  - [not met] There was no loss of consciousness, so this criterion is not met.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient did not suffer minor penetrating trauma; the trauma was blunt.\n  - [not met] The patient has a low heart rate (52/min) and high blood pressure (155/98), and a GCS of 6, which may indicate hemodynamic or neurological instability. This suggests possible exclusion.\n  - [met] The patient is not blind, is able to open eyes, and has both eyes.\n  - [met] The patient can detect light and has both eyes.\n  - [not met] The patient has a GCS of 6 and impaired movement, which may render task completion difficult.\n  - [met] No evidence the patient is pregnant or a prisoner.", "n_inc_assessed": 11, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201413__NCT00077805", "eligibility": "ineligible", "global_decision": 0, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] No evidence of acute ischemic stroke or neuroradiologic study consistent with non-hemorrhagic stroke is mentioned.\n  - [not met] No mention of stroke symptoms or qualifying stroke onset within 48 hours.\n  - [not met] No mention of significant motor impairment of the leg or NIHSS score.\n  - [not met] No mention of inability to walk without assistance.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] Patient gave birth 3 weeks ago, so she is likely not pregnant but may be breast-feeding. No explicit mention of contraception or breast-feeding status.\n  - [met] No clinical evidence of VTE (venous thromboembolism) at screening is described.\n  - [met] No evidence of active bleeding is mentioned.\n  - [met] No prior history of intracranial hemorrhage is mentioned.\n  - [met] No mention of spinal or epidural analgesia or lumbar puncture within the preceding 24 hours.\n  - [met] No mention of thrombolytic therapy.\n  - [met] No evidence of coma; patient is apprehensive and responsive.\n  - [met] No mention of cerebral aneurysm or arteriovenous malformation.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 22}
{"pair": "sigir-20156__NCT01247077", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 2, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient presents with classic symptoms and signs of thyrotoxicosis (weight loss, sweating, diarrhea, palpitations, hyperreflexia, exophthalmia). The presence of exophthalmia suggests Graves' disea\n  - [not met] There is no biochemical data (thyroxin levels) provided in the note.\n  - [not met] No laboratory data (TSH, TRAb, scintigraphy) is provided in the note.\n  - [met] The patient is 46 years old, which is within the age range. Willingness to participate is not mentioned.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] No mention of previous head trauma in the note.\n  - [not met] No information about language proficiency is provided.\n  - [met] No mention of medications in the note.\n  - [met] No mention of pregnancy status.\n  - [met] No evidence of intellectual impairment is mentioned.\n  - [met] Patient has mild exophthalmia, not severe ophthalmopathy. No other severe diseases mentioned.", "n_inc_assessed": 4, "n_exc_assessed": 6}
{"pair": "sigir-201514__NCT02389231", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is a 27-year-old woman, which is older than 18 years.\n  - [not met] wAHAI (warm autoimmune hemolytic anemia) is defined by hemolysis and a positive Coombs test. The patient has evidence of hemolysis (anemia, elevated LDH, elevated reticulocyte count, hemosiderinuria, \n  - [met] There is no mention of infection or another hematologic disease in the note. The anemia appears to be hemolytic, and there is mild iron deficiency, but no other hematologic disease is described.\n  - [not met] There is no information about steroid treatment or response to steroids.\n  - [met] There is no mention of rituximab treatment.\n  - [not met] There is no mention of a signed informed consent form.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] The patient is 27 years old, which is older than 18.\n  - [met] There is no mention of cold AHAI. The hemolysis is not described as cold-mediated.\n  - [met] There is no mention of IL2 allergy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of chemotherapy or immunosuppressive treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of rituximab treatment.\n  - [met] There is no mention of neoplasia or hematologic malignancy.\n  - [met] There is no mention of aplastic anemia. The patient has elevated reticulocyte count, which argues against aplastic anemia.\n  - [met] The patient's WBC count is above 1000/mm3 (6.3 and 7.1 x 10^9/L). Neutropenia is not described.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 19}
{"pair": "sigir-201520__NCT02055092", "eligibility": "eligible", "global_decision": 1, "rationale": "Inclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [not met] The patient is 89 years old and the debut of dementia symptoms was 6 months ago, so symptoms began at age 88. This is well above the required debut before age 65.\n  - [met] The patient has progressive changes in cognition and personality, poor memory, difficulty expressing himself, unusual behaviors (disinhibition, apathy, loss of empathy, perseverative/compulsive behavi\n  - [not met] The patient has difficulty expressing himself and fluent speech with paraphasias, but the overall syndrome is dominated by behavioral changes and global cognitive decline, not isolated language impair\n  - [met] The patient has progressive memory impairment, functional decline, and cognitive deficits in multiple domains, which are consistent with DSM-IV criteria for Alzheimer's disease. However, the prominent\n  - [met] The note does not mention that the patient lives in a dementia-specific facility manned 24/7. He was brought in by family, suggesting community living.\n  - [met] The patient was brought to the ED by his wife and son, indicating he has family members with regular contact.\nExclusion criteria (per-criterion Stanford verdict):\n  - [met] There is no mention of lack of informed consent.\n  - [met] The patient has a wife and son involved in his care.\n  - [met] There is no evidence of non-progressive injury such as cerebral infarction causing the frontal lobe dysfunction. The presentation is progressive.\n  - [met] There is no mention of ALS or motor neuron disease.\n  - [met] There is no mention of Huntington's, HIV, Down syndrome, or alcoholic dementia.\n  - [met] There is no mention of mental retardation.\n  - [met] There is no mention of current substance abuse or excessive alcohol consumption.", "n_inc_assessed": 6, "n_exc_assessed": 7}
